		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification defines a set of elements that can be used in HTML, along with rules about\n  the ways in which the elements can be nested."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Elements can have attributes, which control how the elements work. In the example below, there\n  is a "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="a-quick-introduction-to-html:hyperlink" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- ", formed using the "
			code id="a-quick-introduction-to-html:the-a-element" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " element and its "
			code id="a-quick-introduction-to-html:attr-hyperlink-href" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
