			a href="#refsENCODING" {
				- "[ENCODING]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Since the "
			code id="resource-metadata-management:dom-document-cookie" {
				a href="#dom-document-cookie" {
					- "cookie"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is accessible\n  across frames, the path restrictions on cookies are only a tool to help manage which cookies are\n  sent to which parts of the site, and are not in any way a security feature."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="warning" {
			- "The "
			code id="resource-metadata-management:dom-document-cookie-2" {
				a href="#dom-document-cookie" {
					- "cookie"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's getter and\n  setter synchronously access shared state. Since there is no locking mechanism, other browsing\n  contexts in a multiprocess user agent can modify cookies while scripts are running. A site could,\n  for instance, try to read a cookie, increment its value, then write it back out, using the new\n  value of the cookie as a unique identifier for the session; if the site does this twice in two\n  different browser windows at the same time, it might end up using the same \"unique\" identifier for\n  both sessions, with potentially disastrous effects."
		}
