		- "\n\n  "
		p id="no-browsing-context" {
			- "DOM nodes whose "
			a id="semantics-2:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-document-bc" id="semantics-2:concept-document-bc" {
				- "browsing context"
			}
			- " is null are exempt from all document\n  conformance requirements other than the "
			a href="#writing" {
				- "HTML syntax"
			}
			- " requirements and "
			a href="#writing-xhtml-documents" {
				- "XML syntax"
			}
			- " requirements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "In particular, the "
				code id="semantics-2:the-template-element" {
					a href="#the-template-element" {
						- "template"
					}
				}
				- " element's "
				a href="#template-contents" id="semantics-2:template-contents" {
					- "template contents"
				}
				- "'s "
				a id="semantics-2:node-document-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
					- "node\n   document"
				}
				- "'s "
				a href="#concept-document-bc" id="semantics-2:concept-document-bc-2" {
					- "browsing context"
				}
				- " is null. For\n   example, the "
				a href="#concept-element-content-model" id="semantics-2:concept-element-content-model" {
					- "content model"
				}
				- " requirements and\n   attribute value microsyntax requirements do not apply to a "
				code id="semantics-2:the-template-element-2" {
					a href="#the-template-element" {
						- "template"
					}
				}
				- " element's\n   "
				a href="#template-contents" id="semantics-2:template-contents-2" {
					- "template contents"
				}
				- ". In this example an "
				code id="semantics-2:the-img-element" {
					a href="#the-img-element" {
						- "img"
					}
				}
				- " element has attribute values\n   that are placeholders that would be invalid outside a "
				code id="semantics-2:the-template-element-3" {
					a href="#the-template-element" {
						- "template"
					}
				}
				- " element."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "template"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "article"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "img"
					}
					- " "
					mark {
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"{{src}}\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"{{alt}}\""
						}
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "article"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "template"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, if the above markup were to omit the "
				code {
					- "</h1>"
				}
				- " end tag, that\n   would be a violation of the "
				a href="#writing" {
					- "HTML syntax"
				}
				- ", and would thus be flagged as an\n   error by conformance checkers."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Through scripting and using other mechanisms, the values of attributes, text, and indeed the\n  entire structure of the document may change dynamically while a user agent is processing it. The\n  semantics of a document at an instant in time are those represented by the state of the document\n  at that instant in time, and the semantics of a document can therefore change over time. User\n  agents must update their presentation of the document as this\n  occurs."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "HTML has a "
			code id="semantics-2:the-progress-element" {
				a href="#the-progress-element" {
					- "progress"
				}
			}
			- " element that describes a progress bar. If its\n  \"value\" attribute is dynamically updated by a script, the UA would update the rendering to show\n  the progress changing."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="elements-in-the-dom" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.2"
			}
			- " Elements in the DOM"
			a href="#elements-in-the-dom" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The nodes representing "
			a href="#html-elements" id="elements-in-the-dom:html-elements" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " in the DOM must\n  implement, and expose to scripts, the interfaces listed for them in the relevant sections of this\n  specification. This includes "
			a href="#html-elements" id="elements-in-the-dom:html-elements-2" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="elements-in-the-dom:xml-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-document" data-x-internal="xml-documents" {
				- "XML documents"
			}
			- ", even when\n  those documents are in another context (e.g. inside an XSLT transform)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Elements in the DOM "
			dfn id="represents" {
				- "represent"
			}
			- " things; that is, they have\n  intrinsic "
			em {
				- "meaning"
			}
			- ", also known as semantics."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, an "
			code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-ol-element" {
				a href="#the-ol-element" {
					- "ol"
				}
			}
			- " element represents an ordered list."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Elements can be "
			dfn id="referenced" {
				- "referenced"
			}
			- " (referred to) in some way, either\n  explicitly or implicitly. One way that an element in the DOM can be explicitly referenced is by\n  giving an "
			code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-id-attribute" {
				a href="#the-id-attribute" {
					- "id"
				}
			}
			- " attribute to the element, and then creating a\n  "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="elements-in-the-dom:hyperlink" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- " with that "
			code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-id-attribute-2" {
				a href="#the-id-attribute" {
					- "id"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value as the "
			a href="#navigate-fragid" id="elements-in-the-dom:navigate-fragid" {
				- "fragment"
			}
			- " for the "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="elements-in-the-dom:hyperlink-2" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- "'s "
			code id="elements-in-the-dom:attr-hyperlink-href" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute value. Hyperlinks are not necessary for a\n  reference, however; any manner of referring to the element in question will suffice."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider the following "
				code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-figure-element" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " element, which is given an "
				code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-id-attribute-3" {
					a href="#the-id-attribute" {
						- "id"
					}
				}
				- " attribute:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "figure"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "id"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"module-script-graph\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "img"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "src"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"module-script-graph.svg\""
					}
					- "\n       "
					c- e="" {
						- "alt"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"Module A depends on module B, which depends"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- s="" {
						- "            on modules C and D.\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "figcaption"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Figure 27: a simple module graph"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "figcaption"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "figure"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "A "
				a href="#hyperlink" id="elements-in-the-dom:hyperlink-3" {
					- "hyperlink"
				}
				- "-based "
				a href="#referenced" id="elements-in-the-dom:referenced" {
					- "reference"
				}
				- " could be created\n   using the "
				code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-a-element" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element, like so:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					- "As we can see in "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "a"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "href"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"#module-script-graph\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "figure 27"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "a"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- ", ..."
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, there are many other ways of "
				a href="#referenced" id="elements-in-the-dom:referenced-2" {
					- "referencing"
				}
				- " the\n   "
				code id="elements-in-the-dom:the-figure-element-2" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " element, such as:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			ul {
				li {
					p {
						- "\"As depicted in the figure of modules A, B, C, and D...\""
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "\"In Figure 27...\" (without a hyperlink)"
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "\"From the contents of the 'simple module graph' figure...\""
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "\"In the figure below...\" (but "
						a href="#figure-note-about-references" {
							- "this is\n    discouraged"
						}
						- ")"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The basic interface, from which all the "
			a href="#html-elements" id="elements-in-the-dom:html-elements-3" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- "' interfaces inherit, and which must be used by elements that have no additional requirements, is\n  the "
			code id="elements-in-the-dom:htmlelement" {
				a href="#htmlelement" {
					- "HTMLElement"
				}
			}
			- " interface."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
