		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="element-definitions" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.4"
			}
			- " Element definitions"
			a href="#element-definitions" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each element in this specification has a definition that includes the following\n  information:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-categories" {
					- "Categories"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A list of "
					a href="#content-categories" id="element-definitions:content-categories" {
						- "categories"
					}
					- " to which the element belongs.\n   These are used when defining the "
					a href="#content-models" id="element-definitions:content-models" {
						- "content models"
					}
					- " for each element."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-contexts" {
					- "Contexts in which this element can be used"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "A "
					em {
						- "non-normative"
					}
					- " description of where the element can be used. This information is\n    redundant with the content models of elements that allow this one as a child, and is provided\n    only as a convenience."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="note" {
					- "\n     "
					p {
						- "For simplicity, only the most specific expectations are listed."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "For example, all "
						a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="element-definitions:phrasing-content-2" {
							- "phrasing content"
						}
						- " is "
						a href="#flow-content-2" id="element-definitions:flow-content-2" {
							- "flow content"
						}
						- ". Thus, elements\n     that are "
						a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="element-definitions:phrasing-content-2-2" {
							- "phrasing content"
						}
						- " will only be listed as \"where "
						a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="element-definitions:phrasing-content-2-3" {
							- "phrasing\n     content"
						}
						- " is expected\", since this is the more-specific expectation. Anywhere that expects\n     "
						a href="#flow-content-2" id="element-definitions:flow-content-2-2" {
							- "flow content"
						}
						- " also expects "
						a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="element-definitions:phrasing-content-2-4" {
							- "phrasing content"
						}
						- ", and thus also meets this\n     expectation."
					}
					- "\n    "
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-content-model" {
					- "Content model"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A normative description of what content must be included as children and descendants of\n   the element."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-tag-omission" {
					- "Tag omission in text/html"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A "
					em {
						- "non-normative"
					}
					- " description of whether, in the "
					code id="element-definitions:text/html" {
						a href="#text/html" {
							- "text/html"
						}
					}
					- " syntax, the\n   "
					a href="#syntax-start-tag" id="element-definitions:syntax-start-tag" {
						- "start"
					}
					- " and "
					a href="#syntax-end-tag" id="element-definitions:syntax-end-tag" {
						- "end"
					}
					- " tags can\n   be omitted. This information is redundant with the normative requirements given in the "
					a href="#syntax-tag-omission" id="element-definitions:syntax-tag-omission" {
						- "optional tags"
					}
					- " section, and is provided in the element\n   definitions only as a convenience."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-attributes" {
					- "Content attributes"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A normative list of attributes that may be specified on the element (except where\n   otherwise disallowed), along with non-normative descriptions of those attributes. (The content to\n   the left of the dash is normative, the content to the right of the dash is not.)"
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-accessibility-considerations" {
					- "Accessibility considerations"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "For authors: Conformance requirements for use of "
					cite {
						- "ARIA"
					}
					- " "
					code id="element-definitions:attr-aria-role" {
						a href="#attr-aria-role" {
							- "role"
						}
					}
					- " and "
					code id="element-definitions:attr-aria-*" {
						a href="#attr-aria-*" {
							- "aria-*"
						}
					}
					- " attributes are\n    defined in "
					cite {
						- "ARIA in HTML"
					}
					- ". "
					a href="#refsARIA" {
						- "[ARIA]"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#refsARIAHTML" {
						- "[ARIAHTML]"
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "For implementers: User agent requirements for implementing accessibility API semantics are\n    defined in "
					cite {
						- "HTML Accessibility API Mappings"
					}
					- ". "
					a href="#refsHTMLAAM" {
						- "[HTMLAAM]"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-element-dom" {
					- "DOM interface"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A normative definition of a DOM interface that such elements must implement."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This is then followed by a description of what the element "
			a href="#represents" id="element-definitions:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- ", along with\n  any additional normative conformance criteria that may apply to authors and implementations. Examples are sometimes also included."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="attributes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.4.1"
			}
			- " Attributes"
			a href="#attributes" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="attribute-text" {
			- "An attribute value is a string. Except where otherwise specified,\n  attribute values on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="attributes:html-elements" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " may be any string value, including the empty\n  string, and there is no restriction on what text can be specified in such attribute values."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="content-models" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				- "Content models"
			}
			a href="#content-models" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each element defined in this specification has a content model: a description of the element's\n  expected "
			a href="#concept-html-contents" id="content-models:concept-html-contents" {
				- "contents"
			}
			- ". An "
			a href="#html-elements" id="content-models:html-elements" {
				- "HTML\n  element"
			}
			- " must have contents that match the requirements described in the element's content\n  model. The "
			dfn id="concept-html-contents" {
				- "contents"
			}
			- " of an element are its children in the\n  DOM."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a id="content-models:space-characters" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="space-characters" {
				- "ASCII whitespace"
			}
			- " is always allowed between elements. User agents represent these\n  characters between elements in the source markup as "
			code id="content-models:text" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " nodes in the DOM. Empty "
			code id="content-models:text-2" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " nodes and\n  "
			code id="content-models:text-3" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " nodes consisting of just sequences of those characters are considered\n  "
			dfn id="inter-element-whitespace" {
				- "inter-element whitespace"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#inter-element-whitespace" id="content-models:inter-element-whitespace" {
				- "Inter-element whitespace"
			}
			- ", comment nodes, and processing instruction nodes must be\n  ignored when establishing whether an element's contents match the element's content model or not,\n  and must be ignored when following algorithms that define document and element semantics."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Thus, an element "
			var {
				- "A"
			}
			- " is said to be "
			i {
				- "preceded or followed"
			}
			- "\n  by a second element "
			var {
				- "B"
			}
			- " if "
			var {
				- "A"
			}
			- " and "
			var {
				- "B"
			}
			- " have\n  the same parent node and there are no other element nodes or "
			code id="content-models:text-4" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " nodes (other than\n  "
			a href="#inter-element-whitespace" id="content-models:inter-element-whitespace-2" {
				- "inter-element whitespace"
			}
			- ") between them. Similarly, a node is the "
			i {
				- "only child"
			}
			- " of\n  an element if that element contains no other nodes other than "
			a href="#inter-element-whitespace" id="content-models:inter-element-whitespace-3" {
				- "inter-element\n  whitespace"
			}
			- ", comment nodes, and processing instruction nodes."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Authors must not use "
			a href="#html-elements" id="content-models:html-elements-2" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " anywhere except where they are explicitly\n  allowed, as defined for each element, or as explicitly required by other specifications. For XML\n  compound documents, these contexts could be inside elements from other namespaces, if those\n  elements are defined as providing the relevant contexts."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			cite {
				- "The Atom Syndication Format"
			}
			- " defines a "
			code {
				- "content"
			}
			- " element. When its "
			code {
				- "type"
			}
			- " attribute has the value\n  "
			code {
				- "xhtml"
			}
			- ", "
			cite {
				- "The Atom Syndication Format"
			}
			- " requires that it contain a\n  single HTML "
			code id="content-models:the-div-element" {
				a href="#the-div-element" {
					- "div"
				}
			}
			- " element. Thus, a "
			code id="content-models:the-div-element-2" {
				a href="#the-div-element" {
					- "div"
				}
			}
			- " element is allowed in that context,\n  even though this is not explicitly normatively stated by this specification. "
			a href="#refsATOM" {
				- "[ATOM]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In addition, "
			a href="#html-elements" id="content-models:html-elements-3" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " may be orphan nodes (i.e. without a parent node)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, creating a "
				code id="content-models:the-td-element" {
					a href="#the-td-element" {
						- "td"
					}
				}
				- " element and storing it in a global variable in a\n   script is conforming, even though "
				code id="content-models:the-td-element-2" {
					a href="#the-td-element" {
						- "td"
					}
				}
				- " elements are otherwise only supposed to be used\n   inside "
				code id="content-models:the-tr-element" {
					a href="#the-tr-element" {
						- "tr"
					}
				}
				- " elements."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="js" {
					c- a="" {
						- "var"
					}
					- " data "
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n  name"
					c- o="" {
						- ":"
					}
					- " "
					c- u="" {
						- "\"Banana\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ","
					}
					- "\n  cell"
					c- o="" {
						- ":"
					}
					- " document"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "createElement"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					c- t="" {
						- "'td'"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "),"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "};"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="the-nothing-content-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.1"
			}
			- " The \"nothing\" content model"
			a href="#the-nothing-content-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an element's content model is "
			dfn id="concept-content-nothing" {
				- "nothing"
			}
			- ", the\n  element must contain no "
			code id="the-nothing-content-model:text" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " nodes (other than "
			a href="#inter-element-whitespace" id="the-nothing-content-model:inter-element-whitespace" {
				- "inter-element whitespace"
			}
			- ")\n  and no element nodes."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Most HTML elements whose content model is \"nothing\" are also, for convenience,\n  "
			a href="#void-elements" id="the-nothing-content-model:void-elements" {
				- "void elements"
			}
			- " (elements that have no "
			a href="#syntax-end-tag" id="the-nothing-content-model:syntax-end-tag" {
				- "end tag"
			}
			- " in\n  the "
			a href="#syntax" {
				- "HTML syntax"
			}
			- "). However, these are entirely separate concepts."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="kinds-of-content" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.2"
			}
			- " Kinds of content"
			a href="#kinds-of-content" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each element in HTML falls into zero or more "
			dfn id="content-categories" {
				- "categories"
			}
			- "\n  that group elements with similar characteristics together. The following broad categories are used\n  in this specification:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul class="brief" {
			li {
				a href="#metadata-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:metadata-content-2" {
					- "Metadata content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#flow-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:flow-content-2" {
					- "Flow content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#sectioning-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:sectioning-content-2" {
					- "Sectioning content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#heading-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:heading-content-2" {
					- "Heading content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:phrasing-content-2" {
					- "Phrasing content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#embedded-content-category" id="kinds-of-content:embedded-content-category" {
					- "Embedded content"
				}
			}
			li {
				a href="#interactive-content-2" id="kinds-of-content:interactive-content-2" {
					- "Interactive content"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Some elements also fall into other categories, which are defined in other parts of\n  this specification."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "These categories are related as follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			iframe src="/images/content-venn.svg" width="1000" height="288"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Sectioning content, heading content, phrasing content, embedded content, and interactive\n  content are all types of flow content. Metadata is sometimes flow content. Metadata and\n  interactive content are sometimes phrasing content. Embedded content is also a type of phrasing\n  content, and sometimes is interactive content."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Other categories are also used for specific purposes, e.g. form controls are specified using a\n  number of categories to define common requirements. Some elements have unique requirements and do\n  not fit into any particular category."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="metadata-content" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.2.1"
			}
			- " Metadata content"
			a href="#metadata-content" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			dfn id="metadata-content-2" data-export="" {
				- "Metadata content"
			}
			- " is content that sets up the presentation or behavior of the\n  rest of the content, or that sets up the relationship of the document with other documents, or\n  that conveys other \"out of band\" information."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  "
		ul class="brief category-list" {
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-base-element" {
					a href="#the-base-element" {
						- "base"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-link-element" {
					a href="#the-link-element" {
						- "link"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-meta-element" {
					a href="#the-meta-element" {
						- "meta"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-noscript-element" {
					a href="#the-noscript-element" {
						- "noscript"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-script-element" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-style-element" {
					a href="#the-style-element" {
						- "style"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-template-element" {
					a href="#the-template-element" {
						- "template"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="metadata-content:the-title-element" {
					a href="#the-title-element" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Elements from other namespaces whose semantics are primarily metadata-related (e.g. RDF) are\n  also "
			a href="#metadata-content-2" id="metadata-content:metadata-content-2" {
				- "metadata content"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Thus, in the XML serialization, one can use RDF, like this:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "html"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "xmlns"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\""
					}
					- "\n      "
					c- e="" {
						- "xmlns:r"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "xml:lang"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"en\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "head"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "title"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Hedral's Home Page"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "title"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "r:RDF"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "Person"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "xmlns"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/pim/contact#\""
					}
					- "\n           "
					c- e="" {
						- "r:about"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"https://hedral.example.com/#\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "fullName"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Cat Hedral"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "fullName"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "mailbox"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "r:resource"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"mailto:hedral@damowmow.com\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "/>"
					}
					- "\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "personalTitle"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Sir"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "personalTitle"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "Person"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "r:RDF"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "head"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "body"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "My home page"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "I like playing with string, I guess. Sister says squirrels are fun\n  too so sometimes I follow her to play with them."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "body"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "html"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This isn't possible in the HTML serialization, however."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="flow-content" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.2.2"
			}
			- " Flow content"
			a href="#flow-content" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Most elements that are used in the body of documents and applications are categorized as\n  "
			dfn id="flow-content-2" data-export="" {
				- "flow content"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  "
		ul class="brief category-list" {
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-a-element" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-abbr-element" {
					a href="#the-abbr-element" {
						- "abbr"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-address-element" {
					a href="#the-address-element" {
						- "address"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-area-element" {
					a href="#the-area-element" {
						- "area"
					}
				}
				- " (if it is a descendant of a "
				code id="flow-content:the-map-element" {
					a href="#the-map-element" {
						- "map"
					}
				}
				- " element)"
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-article-element" {
					a href="#the-article-element" {
						- "article"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-aside-element" {
					a href="#the-aside-element" {
						- "aside"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-audio-element" {
					a href="#the-audio-element" {
						- "audio"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-b-element" {
					a href="#the-b-element" {
						- "b"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-bdi-element" {
					a href="#the-bdi-element" {
						- "bdi"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-bdo-element" {
					a href="#the-bdo-element" {
						- "bdo"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="flow-content:the-blockquote-element" {
					a href="#the-blockquote-element" {
						- "blockquote"
					}
				}
			}
