		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="script-supporting-elements" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.2.9"
			}
			- " Script-supporting elements"
			a href="#script-supporting-elements" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			dfn id="script-supporting-elements-2" {
				- "Script-supporting elements"
			}
			- " are those that do not "
			a href="#represents" id="script-supporting-elements:represents" {
				- "represent"
			}
			- " anything themselves (i.e. they are not rendered), but are\n  used to support scripts, e.g. to provide functionality for the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following elements are script-supporting elements:"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  "
		ul class="brief category-list" {
			li {
				code id="script-supporting-elements:the-script-element" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				code id="script-supporting-elements:the-template-element" {
					a href="#the-template-element" {
						- "template"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="transparent-content-models" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.5.3"
			}
			- " Transparent content models"
			a href="#transparent-content-models" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some elements are described as "
			dfn id="transparent" {
				- "transparent"
			}
			- "; they have \"transparent\" in the\n  description of their content model. The content model of a "
			a href="#transparent" id="transparent-content-models:transparent" {
				- "transparent"
			}
			- " element is\n  derived from the content model of its parent element: the elements required in the part of the\n  content model that is \"transparent\" are the same elements as required in the part of the content\n  model of the parent of the transparent element in which the transparent element finds itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For instance, an "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-ins-element" {
					a href="#the-ins-element" {
						- "ins"
					}
				}
				- " element inside a "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-ruby-element" {
					a href="#the-ruby-element" {
						- "ruby"
					}
				}
				- " element cannot contain an\n   "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-rt-element" {
					a href="#the-rt-element" {
						- "rt"
					}
				}
				- " element, because the part of the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-ruby-element-2" {
					a href="#the-ruby-element" {
						- "ruby"
					}
				}
				- " element's content model that\n   allows "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-ins-element-2" {
					a href="#the-ins-element" {
						- "ins"
					}
				}
				- " elements is the part that allows "
				a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="transparent-content-models:phrasing-content-2" {
					- "phrasing content"
				}
				- ", and the\n   "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-rt-element-2" {
					a href="#the-rt-element" {
						- "rt"
					}
				}
				- " element is not "
				a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="transparent-content-models:phrasing-content-2-2" {
					- "phrasing content"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In some cases, where transparent elements are nested in each other, the process\n  has to be applied iteratively."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider the following markup fragment:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "object"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "ins"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "map"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "a"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "href"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"/\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Apples"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "a"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "map"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "ins"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "object"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "To check whether \"Apples\" is allowed inside the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-a-element" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element, the content models are\n   examined. The "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-a-element-2" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element's content model is transparent, as is the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-map-element" {
					a href="#the-map-element" {
						- "map"
					}
				}
				- "\n   element's, as is the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-ins-element-3" {
					a href="#the-ins-element" {
						- "ins"
					}
				}
				- " element's, as is the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-object-element" {
					a href="#the-object-element" {
						- "object"
					}
				}
				- " element's. The\n   "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-object-element-2" {
					a href="#the-object-element" {
						- "object"
					}
				}
				- " element is found in the "
				code id="transparent-content-models:the-p-element" {
					a href="#the-p-element" {
						- "p"
					}
				}
				- " element, whose content model is\n   "
				a href="#phrasing-content-2" id="transparent-content-models:phrasing-content-2-3" {
					- "phrasing content"
				}
				- ". Thus, \"Apples\" is allowed, as text is phrasing content."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a transparent element has no parent, then the part of its content model that is\n  \"transparent\" must instead be treated as accepting any "
			a href="#flow-content-2" id="transparent-content-models:flow-content-2" {
				- "flow content"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
