			a href="#refsDOM" {
				- "[DOM]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="global-attributes:classes" {
				a href="#classes" {
					- "class"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="global-attributes:the-id-attribute" {
				a href="#the-id-attribute" {
					- "id"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attributes may be specified on all "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-3" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When specified on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-4" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- ", the "
			code id="global-attributes:classes-2" {
				a href="#classes" {
					- "class"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute must have a value that is a "
			a href="#set-of-space-separated-tokens" id="global-attributes:set-of-space-separated-tokens" {
				- "set of space-separated tokens"
			}
			- " representing the\n  various classes that the element belongs to."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n\n  "
			p {
				- "Assigning classes to an element affects class matching in selectors in CSS, the "
				code id="global-attributes:dom-document-getelementsbyclassname" {
					a data-x-internal="dom-document-getelementsbyclassname" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-getelementsbyclassname" {
						- "getElementsByClassName()"
					}
				}
				- " method in the DOM,\n  and other such features."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
			p {
				- "There are no additional restrictions on the tokens authors can use in the "
				code id="global-attributes:classes-3" {
					a href="#classes" {
						- "class"
					}
				}
				- " attribute, but authors are encouraged to use values that describe\n  the nature of the content, rather than values that describe the desired presentation of the\n  content."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When specified on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-5" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- ", the "
			code id="global-attributes:the-id-attribute-2" {
				a href="#the-id-attribute" {
					- "id"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  value must be unique amongst all the "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="global-attributes:concept-id" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
				- "IDs"
			}
			- " in the element's\n  "
			a id="global-attributes:tree" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" data-x-internal="tree" {
				- "tree"
			}
			- " and must contain at least one character. The value must not contain any\n  "
			a id="global-attributes:space-characters" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="space-characters" {
				- "ASCII whitespace"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n\n  "
			p {
				- "The "
				code id="global-attributes:the-id-attribute-3" {
					a href="#the-id-attribute" {
						- "id"
					}
				}
				- " attribute specifies its element's "
				a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="global-attributes:concept-id-2" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
					- "unique identifier (ID)"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
			p {
				- "There are no other restrictions on what form an ID can take; in particular, IDs can consist of\n  just digits, start with a digit, start with an underscore, consist of just punctuation, etc."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
			p {
				- "An element's "
				a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="global-attributes:concept-id-3" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
					- "unique identifier"
				}
				- " can be used for a variety of\n  purposes, most notably as a way to link to specific parts of a document using "
				a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="global-attributes:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
					- "fragments"
				}
				- ", as a way to target an element when scripting, and\n  as a way to style a specific element from CSS."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Identifiers are opaque strings. Particular meanings should not be derived from the value of the\n  "
			code id="global-attributes:the-id-attribute-4" {
				a href="#the-id-attribute" {
					- "id"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "There are no conformance requirements for the "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot-2" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  specific to "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-6" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot-3" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is used to "
			a id="global-attributes:assign-a-slot" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#assign-a-slot" data-x-internal="assign-a-slot" {
				- "assign a\n  slot"
			}
			- " to an element: an element with a "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot-4" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is\n  "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#assign-a-slot" id="global-attributes:assign-a-slot-2" data-x-internal="assign-a-slot" {
				- "assigned"
			}
			- " to the "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-slot" id="global-attributes:concept-slot" data-x-internal="concept-slot" {
				- "slot"
			}
			- "\n  created by the "
			code id="global-attributes:the-slot-element" {
				a href="#the-slot-element" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " element whose "
			a href="#attr-slot-name" id="global-attributes:attr-slot-name" {
				- "name"
			}
			- "\n  attribute's value matches that "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot-5" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value — but only\n  if that "
			code id="global-attributes:the-slot-element-2" {
				a href="#the-slot-element" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " element finds itself in the "
			a id="global-attributes:shadow-tree" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-tree" data-x-internal="shadow-tree" {
				- "shadow tree"
			}
			- " whose\n  "
			a id="global-attributes:root" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-root" data-x-internal="root" {
				- "root"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-documentfragment-host" id="global-attributes:concept-documentfragment-host" data-x-internal="concept-documentfragment-host" {
				- "host"
			}
			- " has the corresponding\n  "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-slot-6" {
				a href="#attr-slot" {
					- "slot"
				}
			}
			- " attribute value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To enable assistive technology products to expose a more fine-grained interface than is\n  otherwise possible with HTML elements and attributes, a set of "
			a href="#wai-aria" {
				- "annotations\n  for assistive technology products"
			}
			- " can be specified (the ARIA "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-aria-role" {
				a href="#attr-aria-role" {
					- "role"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-aria-*" {
				a href="#attr-aria-*" {
					- "aria-*"
				}
			}
			- " attributes).\n  "
			a href="#refsARIA" {
				- "[ARIA]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following "
			a href="#event-handler-content-attributes" id="global-attributes:event-handler-content-attributes" {
				- "event handler content attributes"
			}
			- " may be specified on any "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-7" {
				- "HTML element"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul class="brief" {
			li {
				code id="global-attributes:handler-onauxclick" {
					a href="#handler-onauxclick" {
						- "onauxclick"
					}
				}
