		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The attributes marked with an asterisk have a different meaning when specified on\n  "
			code id="global-attributes:the-body-element" {
				a href="#the-body-element" {
					- "body"
				}
			}
			- " elements as those elements expose "
			a href="#event-handlers" id="global-attributes:event-handlers" {
				- "event handlers"
			}
			- " of the\n  "
			code id="global-attributes:window" {
				a href="#window" {
					- "Window"
				}
			}
			- " object with the same names."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "While these attributes apply to all elements, they are not useful on all elements.\n  For example, only "
			a href="#media-element" id="global-attributes:media-element" {
				- "media elements"
			}
			- " will ever receive a "
			code id="global-attributes:event-media-volumechange" {
				a href="#event-media-volumechange" {
					- "volumechange"
				}
			}
			- " event fired by the user agent."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#custom-data-attribute" id="global-attributes:custom-data-attribute" {
				- "Custom data attributes"
			}
			- " (e.g. "
			code {
				- "data-foldername"
			}
			- " or "
			code {
				- "data-msgid"
			}
			- ") can be specified on any\n  "
			a href="#html-elements" id="global-attributes:html-elements-8" {
				- "HTML element"
			}
			- ", to store custom data, state, annotations, and\n  similar, specific to the page."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In "
			a id="global-attributes:html-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML documents"
			}
			- ", elements in the "
			a id="global-attributes:html-namespace-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace" data-x-internal="html-namespace-2" {
				- "HTML namespace"
			}
			- " may have an "
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- " attribute specified, if, and only if, it has the exact value \""
			code {
				- "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
			}
			- "\". This does not apply to "
			a id="global-attributes:xml-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-document" data-x-internal="xml-documents" {
				- "XML\n  documents"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In HTML, the "
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- " attribute has absolutely no effect. It\n  is basically a talisman. It is allowed merely to make migration to and from XML mildly easier.\n  When parsed by an "
			a href="#html-parser" id="global-attributes:html-parser" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- ", the attribute ends up in no namespace, not the \""
			code {
				- "http://www.w3.org/2000/xmlns/"
			}
			- "\" namespace like namespace declaration attributes in\n  XML do."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In XML, an "
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- " attribute is part of the namespace\n  declaration mechanism, and an element cannot actually have an "
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- "\n  attribute in no namespace specified."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- " also allows the use of the "
			code id="global-attributes:attr-xml-space" {
				a data-x-internal="attr-xml-space" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-white-space" {
					- "xml:space"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute in the "
			a id="global-attributes:xml-namespace" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-namespace" data-x-internal="xml-namespace" {
				- "XML namespace"
			}
			- " on any element in an "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-document" id="global-attributes:xml-documents-2" data-x-internal="xml-documents" {
