		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="html-global" id="attr-title" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  "
			a href="#represents" id="the-title-attribute:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " advisory information for the element, such as would be appropriate for a\n  tooltip. On a link, this could be the title or a description of the target resource; on an image,\n  it could be the image credit or a description of the image; on a paragraph, it could be a footnote\n  or commentary on the text; on a citation, it could be further information about the source; on\n  "
			a href="#interactive-content-2" id="the-title-attribute:interactive-content-2" {
				- "interactive content"
			}
			- ", it could be a label for, or instructions for, use of the\n  element; and so forth.  The value is text."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Relying on the "
			code id="the-title-attribute:attr-title-2" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is currently\n  discouraged as many user agents do not expose the attribute in an accessible manner as required by\n  this specification (e.g., requiring a pointing device such as a mouse to cause a tooltip to\n  appear, which excludes keyboard-only users and touch-only users, such as anyone with a modern\n  phone or tablet)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If this attribute is omitted from an element, then it implies that the "
			code id="the-title-attribute:attr-title-3" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute of the nearest ancestor "
			a href="#html-elements" id="the-title-attribute:html-elements" {
				- "HTML element"
			}
			- " with a "
			code id="the-title-attribute:attr-title-4" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute set is also\n  relevant to this element. Setting the attribute overrides this, explicitly stating that the\n  advisory information of any ancestors is not relevant to this element. Setting the attribute to\n  the empty string indicates that the element has no advisory information."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id="the-title-attribute:attr-title-5" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value contains U+000A LINE FEED (LF)\n  characters, the content is split into multiple lines. Each U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character\n  represents a line break."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Caution is advised with respect to the use of newlines in "
				code id="the-title-attribute:attr-title-6" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attributes."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For instance, the following snippet actually defines an abbreviation's expansion "
				em {
					- "with a\n   line break in it"
				}
				- ":"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre class="bad" {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "My logs show that there was some interest in "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "abbr"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "title"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"Hypertext"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- s="" {
						- "Transport Protocol\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "HTTP"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "abbr"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " today."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- " \n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some elements, such as "
			code id="the-title-attribute:the-link-element" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-title-attribute:the-abbr-element" {
				a href="#the-abbr-element" {
