			- "\n\n\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Given a suitable style sheet and the default alignment styles for the "
				code id="the-dir-attribute:the-p-element" {
					a href="#the-p-element" {
						- "p"
					}
				}
				- " element,\n   namely to align the text to the "
				i {
					- "start edge"
				}
				- " of the paragraph, the resulting rendering could\n   be as follows:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				img width="366" src="/images/im.png" height="157" alt="Each paragraph rendered as a separate block, with the paragraphs left-aligned except the second paragraph and the last one, which would be right aligned, with the usernames ('Student' and 'Teacher' in this example) flush right, with a colon to their left, and the text first to the left of that."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "As noted earlier, the "
				code id="the-dir-attribute:attr-dir-auto" {
					a href="#attr-dir-auto" {
						- "auto"
					}
				}
				- " value is not a panacea. The\n   final paragraph in this example is misinterpreted as being right-to-left text, since it begins\n   with an Arabic character, which causes the \"right?\" to be to the left of the Arabic text."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
