		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All "
			a href="#html-elements" id="the-style-attribute:html-elements" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " may have the "
			dfn data-dfn-for="html-global" id="attr-style" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "style"
				}
			}
			- " content attribute set. This is a "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-style-attr/#style-attribute" id="the-style-attribute:css-styling-attribute" data-x-internal="css-styling-attribute" {
				- "style attribute"
			}
			- " as defined by "
			cite {
				- "CSS Style\n  Attributes"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsCSSATTR" {
				- "[CSSATTR]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "In user agents that support CSS, the attribute's value must be parsed when the attribute is\n  added or has its value changed,\n  according to the rules given for "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-style-attr/#style-attribute" id="the-style-attribute:css-styling-attribute-2" data-x-internal="css-styling-attribute" {
				- "style attributes"
			}
			- ".\n  "
			a href="#refsCSSATTR" {
				- "[CSSATTR]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "However, if the "
			a id="the-style-attribute:should-element's-inline-behavior-be-blocked-by-content-security-policy" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#should-block-inline" data-x-internal="should-element's-inline-behavior-be-blocked-by-content-security-policy" {
				- "Should element's inline behavior be blocked by Content Security\n  Policy?"
			}
			- " algorithm returns \""
			code {
				- "Blocked"
			}
			- "\" when executed upon the\n  attribute's "
			a id="the-style-attribute:element" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-element" data-x-internal="element" {
				- "element"
			}
			- ", \""
			code {
				- "style attribute"
			}
			- "\", and the attribute's\n  value, then the style rules defined in the attribute's value must not be applied to the\n  "
			a id="the-style-attribute:element-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-element" data-x-internal="element" {
				- "element"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsCSP" {
				- "[CSP]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Documents that use "
			code id="the-style-attribute:attr-style-2" {
				a href="#attr-style" {
					- "style"
				}
			}
			- " attributes on any of their elements\n  must still be comprehensible and usable if those attributes were removed."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In particular, using the "
			code id="the-style-attribute:attr-style-3" {
				a href="#attr-style" {
					- "style"
				}
			}
			- " attribute to hide\n  and show content, or to convey meaning that is otherwise not included in the document, is\n  non-conforming. (To hide and show content, use the "
			code id="the-style-attribute:attr-hidden" {
				a href="#attr-hidden" {
					- "hidden"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
					a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#dom-elementcssinlinestyle-style" id="dom-style-dev" data-x-internal="dom-style" {
						- "style"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns a "
					code id="the-style-attribute:cssstyledeclaration" {
						a data-x-internal="cssstyledeclaration" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#the-cssstyledeclaration-interface" {
							- "CSSStyleDeclaration"
						}
					}
					- " object for the element's "
					code id="the-style-attribute:attr-style-4" {
						a href="#attr-style" {
							- "style"
						}
					}
					- " attribute."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-style-attribute:dom-style" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-style" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#dom-elementcssinlinestyle-style" {
					- "style"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute is defined in "
			cite {
				- "CSS Object\n  Model"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsCSSOM" {
				- "[CSSOM]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In the following example, the words that refer to colors are marked up using the\n   "
				code id="the-style-attribute:the-span-element" {
					a href="#the-span-element" {
						- "span"
					}
				}
				- " element and the "
				code id="the-style-attribute:attr-style-5" {
					a href="#attr-style" {
						- "style"
					}
				}
				- " attribute to make those\n   words show up in the relevant colors in visual media."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "My sweat suit is "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "style"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"color: green; background:"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- s="" {
						- "transparent\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "green"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " and my eyes are "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "style"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"color: blue;"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- s="" {
						- "background: transparent\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "blue"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "3.2.6.6"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				- "Embedding custom non-visible data"
			}
			- " with the "
			code id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:attr-data-*" {
				a href="#attr-data-*" {
					- "data-*"
				}
			}
			- " attributes"
			a href="#embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/data-*" title="The data-* global attributes form a class of attributes called custom data attributes, that allow proprietary information to be exchanged between the HTML and its DOM representation by scripts." {
						- "Global_attributes/data-*"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "6+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "5.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "7+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id="custom-data-attribute" {
				- "custom data attribute"
			}
			- " is an attribute in no namespace whose name starts with the\n  string \""
			dfn id="attr-data-*" {
				code {
					- "data-"
				}
			}
			- "\", has at least one character after the\n  hyphen, is "
			a href="#xml-compatible" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:xml-compatible" {
				- "XML-compatible"
			}
			- ", and contains no "
			a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-upper-alpha" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:uppercase-ascii-letters" data-x-internal="uppercase-ascii-letters" {
				- "ASCII\n  upper alphas"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "All attribute names on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:html-elements" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:html-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML documents"
			}
			- "\n  get ASCII-lowercased automatically, so the restriction on ASCII uppercase letters doesn't affect\n  such documents."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#custom-data-attribute" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:custom-data-attribute" {
				- "Custom data attributes"
			}
			- " are intended to store custom\n  data, state, annotations, and similar, private to the page or application, for which there are no\n  more appropriate attributes or elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "These attributes are not intended for use by software that is not known to the administrators\n  of the site that uses the attributes. For generic extensions that are to be used by multiple\n  independent tools, either this specification should be extended to provide the feature explicitly,\n  or a technology like "
			a href="#microdata" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:microdata" {
				- "microdata"
			}
			- " should be used (with a standardized vocabulary)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For instance, a site about music could annotate list items representing tracks in an album\n   with custom data attributes containing the length of each track. This information could then be\n   used by the site itself to allow the user to sort the list by track length, or to filter the list\n   for tracks of certain lengths."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "ol"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "li"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "data-length"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"2m11s\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Beyond The Sea"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "li"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n ...\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "ol"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "It would be inappropriate, however, for the user to use generic software not associated with\n   that music site to search for tracks of a certain length by looking at this data."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This is because these attributes are intended for use by the site's own scripts, and are not a\n   generic extension mechanism for publicly-usable metadata."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Similarly, a page author could write markup that provides information for a translation tool\n   that they are intending to use:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "The third "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "data-mytrans-de"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"Anspruch\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "claim"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " covers the case of "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- e="" {
						- "translate"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"no\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "HTML"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "span"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " markup."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In this example, the \""
				code {
					- "data-mytrans-de"
				}
				- "\" attribute gives specific text\n   for the MyTrans product to use when translating the phrase \"claim\" to German. However, the\n   standard "
				code id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:attr-translate" {
					a href="#attr-translate" {
						- "translate"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is used to tell it that in all\n   languages, \"HTML\" is to remain unchanged. When a standard attribute is available, there is no\n   need for a "
				a href="#custom-data-attribute" id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:custom-data-attribute-2" {
					- "custom data attribute"
				}
				- " to be used."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In this example, custom data attributes are used to store the result of a feature detection\n   for "
				code id="embedding-custom-non-visible-data-with-the-data-*-attributes:paymentrequest" {
					a data-x-internal="paymentrequest" href="https://w3c.github.io/payment-request/#dom-paymentrequest" {
						- "PaymentRequest"
					}
				}
				- ", which could be used in CSS to style a checkout page\n   differently."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- k="" {
						- "if"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					c- t="" {
						- "'PaymentRequest'"
					}
					- " "
					c- k="" {
						- "in"
					}
					- " window"
					c- p="" {
						- ")"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n   document"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "documentElement"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "dataset"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "hasPaymentRequest "
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					- " "
					c- t="" {
						- "''"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ";"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "}"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
