				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Many search engines do not consider such keywords, because this feature has\n    historically been used unreliably and even misleadingly as a way to spam search engine results\n    in a way that is not helpful for users."
				}
				- "\n\n    \n\n    "
				p {
					- "To obtain the list of keywords that the author has specified as applicable to the page, the\n    user agent must run the following steps:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "keywords"
							}
							- " be an empty list."
						}
					}
					li {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "For each "
							code id="standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-8" {
								a href="#the-meta-element" {
									- "meta"
								}
							}
							- " element with a "
							code id="standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-6" {
								a href="#attr-meta-name" {
									- "name"
								}
							}
							- "\n      attribute and a "
							code id="standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-2" {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" {
									- "content"
								}
							}
							- " attribute and where the "
							code id="standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-7" {
								a href="#attr-meta-name" {
									- "name"
								}
							}
							- " attribute value is an "
							a id="standard-metadata-names:ascii-case-insensitive-6" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
								- "ASCII case-insensitive"
							}
							- "\n      match for "
							code id="standard-metadata-names:meta-keywords" {
								a href="#meta-keywords" {
									- "keywords"
								}
							}
							- ":"
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-commas" id="standard-metadata-names:split-a-string-on-commas" data-x-internal="split-a-string-on-commas" {
										- "Split the value of the element's "
										code {
											- "content"
										}
										- " attribute on commas"
									}
									- "."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Add the resulting tokens, if any, to "
									var {
										- "keywords"
									}
									- "."
								}
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Remove any duplicates from "
							var {
								- "keywords"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Return "
							var {
								- "keywords"
							}
							- ". This is the list of keywords that the author has\n     specified as applicable to the page."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "User agents should not use this information when there is insufficient confidence in the\n    reliability of the value."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="example" {
					- "For instance, it would be reasonable for a content management system to use\n    the keyword information of pages within the system to populate the index of a site-specific\n    search engine, but a large-scale content aggregator that used this information would likely find\n    that certain users would try to game its ranking mechanism through the use of inappropriate\n    keywords."
				}
				- "\n\n    \n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="meta/name" id="meta-referrer" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
					code {
						- "referrer"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The value must be a "
					a id="standard-metadata-names:referrer-policy" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#referrer-policy" data-x-internal="referrer-policy" {
						- "referrer policy"
					}
					- ", which defines the default "
