				- "\n\n     "
				p {
					- "If any "
					code id="standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-19" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " elements are "
					a href="#insert-an-element-into-a-document" id="standard-metadata-names:insert-an-element-into-a-document-3" {
						- "inserted into the document"
					}
					- " or "
					a href="#remove-an-element-from-a-document" id="standard-metadata-names:remove-an-element-from-a-document-2" {
						- "removed from the document"
					}
					- ", or existing "
					code id="standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-20" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " elements have their\n     "
					code id="standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-15" {
						a href="#attr-meta-name" {
							- "name"
						}
					}
					- " or "
					code id="standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-11" {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" {
							- "content"
						}
					}
					- "\n     attributes changed, user agents must re-run the above algorithm."
				}
				- "\n\n    \n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Because these rules check successive elements until they find a match, an\n    author can provide multiple such values to handle fallback for legacy user agents. Opposite to\n    how CSS fallback works for properties, the multiple meta elements needs to be arranged with the\n    legacy values after the newer values."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="other-metadata-names" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.2.5.2"
			}
			- " Other metadata names"
			a href="#other-metadata-names" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Anyone can create and use their own "
			dfn id="concept-meta-extensions" {
				- "extensions to the\n  predefined set of metadata names"
			}
			- ". There is no requirement to register such extensions."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "However, a new metadata name should not be created in any of the following cases:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "If either the name is a "
					a id="other-metadata-names:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "URL"
					}
					- ", or the value of its accompanying "
					code id="other-metadata-names:attr-meta-content" {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" {
							- "content"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is a "
					a id="other-metadata-names:url-2" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "URL"
					}
					- "; in those cases,\n   registering it as an "
					a href="#concept-rel-extensions" id="other-metadata-names:concept-rel-extensions" {
						- "extension to the predefined set of\n   link types"
					}
					- " is encouraged (rather than creating a new metadata name)."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the name is for something expected to have processing requirements in user agents; in\n   that case it ought to be standardized."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Also, before creating and using a new metadata name, consulting the "
			a href="https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/MetaExtensions" {
				- "WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page"
			}
			- " is\n  encouraged — to avoid choosing a metadata name that's already in use, and to avoid duplicating the\n  purpose of any metadata names that are already in use, and to avoid new standardized names\n  clashing with your chosen name. "
			a href="#refsWHATWGWIKI" {
				- "[WHATWGWIKI]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Anyone is free to edit the WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page at any time to add a metadata name.\n  New metadata names can be specified with the following information:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Keyword"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The actual name being defined. The name should not be confusingly similar to any other\n   defined name (e.g. differing only in case)."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Brief description"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A short non-normative description of what the metadata name's meaning is, including the\n   format the value is required to be in."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Specification"
			}
			dd {
				- "A link to a more detailed description of the metadata name's semantics and requirements. It\n   could be another page on the wiki, or a link to an external page."
			}
			dt {
				- "Synonyms"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A list of other names that have exactly the same processing requirements. Authors should\n   not use the names defined to be synonyms (they are only intended to allow user agents to support\n   legacy content). Anyone may remove synonyms that are not used in practice; only names that need to\n   be processed as synonyms for compatibility with legacy content are to be registered in this\n   way."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Status"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "One of the following:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Proposed"
					}
					dd {
						- "The name has not received wide peer review and approval. Someone has proposed it and is, or\n     soon will be, using it."
					}
					dt {
						- "Ratified"
					}
					dd {
						- "The name has received wide peer review and approval. It has a specification that\n     unambiguously defines how to handle pages that use the name, including when they use it in\n     incorrect ways."
					}
					dt {
						- "Discontinued"
					}
					dd {
						- "The metadata name has received wide peer review and it has been found wanting. Existing\n     pages are using this metadata name, but new pages should avoid it. The \"brief description\" and\n     \"specification\" entries will give details of what authors should use instead, if anything."
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If a metadata name is found to be redundant with existing values, it should be removed and\n    listed as a synonym for the existing value."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If a metadata name is added in the \"proposed\" state for a period of a month or more without\n    being used or specified, then it may be removed from the WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If a metadata name is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be redundant with\n    existing values, it should be removed and listed as a synonym for the existing value. If a\n    metadata name is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be harmful, then it should be\n    changed to \"discontinued\" status."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Anyone can change the status at any time, but should only do so in accordance with the\n    definitions above."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="pragma-directives" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.2.5.3"
			}
			- " Pragma directives"
			a href="#pragma-directives" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meta" id="attr-meta-http-equiv" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "http-equiv"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is specified on a\n  "
			code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element, the element is a pragma directive."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv" {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
					- "http-equiv"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is an "
			a href="#enumerated-attribute" id="pragma-directives:enumerated-attribute" {
				- "enumerated\n  attribute"
			}
			- " with the following keywords and states:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table id="table-http-equiv" class="yesno" {
			thead {
				tr {
					th {
						- "Keyword\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "Conforming\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "State\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "Brief description\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "content-language"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td class="no" {
						- "No\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language" {
							- "Content language"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Sets the "
						a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id="pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language" {
							- "pragma-set default language"
						}
						- ".\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "content-type"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" {
							- "Encoding declaration"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "An alternative form of setting the "
						code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-charset" {
							a href="#attr-meta-charset" {
								- "charset"
							}
						}
						- ".\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-default-style" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "default-style"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-default-style" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-default-style" {
							- "Default style"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Sets the "
						a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#css-style-sheet-set-name" id="pragma-directives:css-style-sheet-set-name" data-x-internal="css-style-sheet-set-name" {
							- "name"
						}
						- " of the default\n     "
						a id="pragma-directives:css-style-sheet-set" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#css-style-sheet-set" data-x-internal="css-style-sheet-set" {
							- "CSS style sheet set"
						}
						- ".\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-refresh" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "refresh"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" {
							- "Refresh"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Acts as a timed redirect.\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-set-cookie" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "set-cookie"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td class="no" {
						- "No\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-set-cookie" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-set-cookie" {
							- "Set-Cookie"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Has no effect.\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-x-ua-compatible" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "x-ua-compatible"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-x-ua-compatible" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-x-ua-compatible" {
							- "X-UA-Compatible"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "In practice, encourages Internet Explorer to more closely follow the specifications.\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" id="attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-security-policy" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "content-security-policy"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" {
							- "Content security policy"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#enforced" id="pragma-directives:enforce-the-policy" data-x-internal="enforce-the-policy" {
							- "Enforces"
						}
						- " a "
						a id="pragma-directives:content-security-policy" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#content-security-policy-object" data-x-internal="content-security-policy" {
							- "Content Security\n     Policy"
						}
						- " on a "
						code id="pragma-directives:document" {
							a href="#document" {
								- "Document"
							}
						}
						- ".\n  "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-2" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element is "
			a href="#insert-an-element-into-a-document" id="pragma-directives:insert-an-element-into-a-document" {
				- "inserted\n  into the document"
			}
			- ", if its "
			code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-2" {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
					- "http-equiv"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is\n  present and represents one of the above states, then the user agent must run the algorithm\n  appropriate for that state, as described in the following list:"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language" {
					- "Content language state"
				}
				- "\n   ("
				code {
					- "http-equiv=\""
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language" {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language" {
							- "content-language"
						}
					}
					- "\""
				}
				- ")\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This feature is non-conforming. Authors are encouraged to use the "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-lang" {
						a href="#attr-lang" {
							- "lang"
						}
					}
					- " attribute instead."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This pragma sets the "
					dfn id="pragma-set-default-language" {
						- "pragma-set default language"
					}
					- ". Until such a pragma is\n    successfully processed, there is no "
					a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id="pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language-2" {
						- "pragma-set default language"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    \n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-3" {
								a href="#the-meta-element" {
									- "meta"
								}
							}
							- " element has no "
							code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-content" {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" {
									- "content"
								}
							}
							- "\n     attribute, then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If the element's "
							code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-2" {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" {
									- "content"
								}
							}
							- " attribute contains a\n     U+002C COMMA character (,) then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "input"
							}
							- " be the value of the element's "
							code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-3" {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" {
									- "content"
								}
							}
							- " attribute."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "position"
							}
							- " point at the first character of "
							var {
								- "input"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a id="pragma-directives:skip-ascii-whitespace" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#skip-ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="skip-ascii-whitespace" {
								- "Skip ASCII whitespace"
							}
							- " within "
							var {
								- "input"
							}
							- " given\n     "
							var {
								- "position"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a id="pragma-directives:collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" data-x-internal="collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" {
								- "Collect a sequence of code points"
							}
							- " that are not "
							a id="pragma-directives:space-characters" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="space-characters" {
								- "ASCII\n     whitespace"
							}
							- " from "
							var {
								- "input"
							}
							- " given "
							var {
								- "position"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "candidate"
							}
							- " be the string that resulted from the previous\n     step."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var {
								- "candidate"
							}
							- " is the empty string, return."
						}
					}
					li {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "Set the "
							a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id="pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language-3" {
								- "pragma-set default language"
							}
							- " to "
							var {
								- "candidate"
							}
							- "."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "If the value consists of multiple space-separated tokens, tokens after the\n      first are ignored."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This pragma is almost, but not quite, entirely unlike the HTTP `"
					code id="pragma-directives:http-content-language" {
						a data-x-internal="http-content-language" href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7231.html#header.content-language" {
							- "Content-Language"
						}
					}
					- "` header of the same name.\n    "
					a href="#refsHTTP" {
						- "[HTTP]"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" {
					- "Encoding declaration state"
				}
				- " ("
				code {
					- "http-equiv=\""
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type" {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type" {
							- "content-type"
						}
					}
					- "\""
				}
				- ")\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type-2" {
						- "Encoding declaration state"
					}
					- " is\n    just an alternative form of setting the "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-charset-2" {
						a href="#attr-meta-charset" {
							- "charset"
						}
					}
					- "\n    attribute: it is a "
					a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="pragma-directives:character-encoding-declaration" {
						- "character encoding declaration"
					}
					- ". This state's user\n    agent requirements are all handled by the parsing section of the specification."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "For "
					code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-4" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " elements with an "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-3" {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
							- "http-equiv"
						}
					}
					- "\n    attribute in the "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type-3" {
						- "Encoding declaration\n    state"
					}
					- ", the "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-4" {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" {
							- "content"
						}
					}
					- " attribute must have a value\n    that is an "
					a id="pragma-directives:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
						- "ASCII case-insensitive"
					}
					- " match for a string that consists of:\n    \""
					code {
						- "text/html;"
					}
					- "\", optionally followed by any number of "
					a id="pragma-directives:space-characters-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="space-characters" {
						- "ASCII\n    whitespace"
					}
					- ", followed by \""
					code {
						- "charset=utf-8"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "A document must not contain both a "
					code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-5" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " element with an "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-4" {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
							- "http-equiv"
						}
					}
					- " attribute in the "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type-4" {
						- "Encoding declaration state"
					}
					- " and a\n    "
					code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-6" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " element with the "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-charset-3" {
						a href="#attr-meta-charset" {
							- "charset"
						}
					}
