					- ", or "
					code id="pragma-directives:sandbox-directive-2" {
						a data-x-internal="sandbox-directive" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#sandbox" {
							- "sandbox"
						}
					}
					- " "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#directives" id="pragma-directives:content-security-policy-directive-2" data-x-internal="content-security-policy-directive" {
						- "directives"
					}
					- ".\n    The "
					a id="pragma-directives:content-security-policy-3" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#content-security-policy-object" data-x-internal="content-security-policy" {
						- "Content Security Policy"
					}
					- " given in the "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-14" {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" {
							- "content"
						}
					}
					- " attribute will be "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#enforced" id="pragma-directives:enforce-the-policy-4" data-x-internal="enforce-the-policy" {
						- "enforced"
					}
					- " upon the current document. "
					a href="#refsCSP" {
						- "[CSP]"
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "At the time of inserting the "
					code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-18" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- " element to the document, it is\n    possible that some resources have already been fetched. For example, images might be stored in\n    the "
					a href="#list-of-available-images" id="pragma-directives:list-of-available-images" {
						- "list of available images"
					}
					- " prior to dynamically inserting a "
					code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-19" {
						a href="#the-meta-element" {
							- "meta"
						}
					}
					- "\n    element with an "
					code id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-9" {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
							- "http-equiv"
						}
					}
					- " attribute in the "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" id="pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy-3" {
						- "Content security policy state"
					}
					- ".\n    Resources that have already been fetched are not guaranteed to be blocked by a "
					a id="pragma-directives:content-security-policy-4" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#content-security-policy-object" data-x-internal="content-security-policy" {
						- "Content\n    Security Policy"
					}
					- " that's "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#enforced" id="pragma-directives:enforce-the-policy-5" data-x-internal="enforce-the-policy" {
						- "enforced"
					}
					- " late."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "A page might choose to mitigate the risk of cross-site scripting attacks by preventing the\n     execution of inline JavaScript, as well as blocking all plugin content, using a policy such\n     as the following:\n\n     "
					}
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "meta"
							}
							- " "
							c- e="" {
								- "http-equiv"
							}
							c- o="" {
								- "="
							}
							c- s="" {
								- "\"Content-Security-Policy\""
							}
							- " "
							c- e="" {
								- "content"
							}
							c- o="" {
								- "="
							}
							c- s="" {
								- "\"script-src 'self'; object-src 'none'\""
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "There must not be more than one "
			code id="pragma-directives:the-meta-element-20" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element with any particular state in the\n  document at a time."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="charset" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.2.5.4"
			}
			- " Specifying the document's character encoding"
			a href="#charset" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id="character-encoding-declaration" {
				- "character encoding declaration"
			}
			- " is a mechanism by which the "
			a href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#encoding" id="charset:encoding" data-x-internal="encoding" {
				- "character encoding"
			}
			- " used to store or transmit a document is specified."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The Encoding standard requires use of the "
			a id="charset:utf-8" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8" data-x-internal="utf-8" {
				- "UTF-8"
			}
			- " "
			a href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#encoding" id="charset:encoding-2" data-x-internal="encoding" {
				- "character\n  encoding"
			}
			- " and requires use of the \""
			code {
				- "utf-8"
			}
			- "\" "
			a id="charset:encoding-label" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#label" data-x-internal="encoding-label" {
				- "encoding label"
			}
			- "\n  to identify it. Those requirements necessitate that the document's "
			a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="charset:character-encoding-declaration" {
				- "character encoding\n  declaration"
			}
			- ", if it exists, specifies an "
			a id="charset:encoding-label-2" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#label" data-x-internal="encoding-label" {
				- "encoding label"
			}
			- " using an "
			a id="charset:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
				- "ASCII\n  case-insensitive"
			}
			- " match for \""
			code {
				- "utf-8"
			}
			- "\". Regardless of whether a\n  "
			a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="charset:character-encoding-declaration-2" {
				- "character encoding declaration"
			}
			- " is present or not, the actual "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id="charset:document's-character-encoding" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
				- "character encoding"
			}
			- " used to encode the document must be\n  "
			a id="charset:utf-8-2" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8" data-x-internal="utf-8" {
				- "UTF-8"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsENCODING" {
				- "[ENCODING]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To enforce the above rules, authoring tools must default to using "
			a id="charset:utf-8-3" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8" data-x-internal="utf-8" {
				- "UTF-8"
			}
			- "\n  for newly-created documents."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following restrictions also apply:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "The character encoding declaration must be serialized without the use of "
				a href="#syntax-charref" id="charset:syntax-charref" {
					- "character references"
				}
				- " or character escapes of any kind."
			}
			li id="charset1024" {
				span id="charset512" {
					- "The element containing the character encoding\n   declaration must be serialized completely within the first 1024 bytes of the\n   document."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In addition, due to a number of restrictions on "
			code id="charset:the-meta-element" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " elements, there can only be\n  one "
			code id="charset:the-meta-element-2" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- "-based character encoding declaration per document."
		}
		- " \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If an "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" id="charset:html-documents" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML document"
			}
			- " does not start with a BOM, and its\n  "
			a id="charset:encoding-3" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#encoding" data-x-internal="encoding" {
				- "encoding"
			}
			- " is not explicitly given by "
			a href="#content-type" id="charset:content-type" {
				- "Content-Type\n  metadata"
			}
			- ", and the document is not "
			a href="#an-iframe-srcdoc-document" id="charset:an-iframe-srcdoc-document" {
				- "an "
				code {
					- "iframe"
				}
				- " "
				code {
					- "srcdoc"
				}
				- " document"
			}
			- ", then the encoding must be specified\n  using a "
			code id="charset:the-meta-element-3" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element with a "
			code id="charset:attr-meta-charset" {
				a href="#attr-meta-charset" {
					- "charset"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  or a "
			code id="charset:the-meta-element-4" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element with an "
			code id="charset:attr-meta-http-equiv" {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
					- "http-equiv"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute in the "
			a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id="charset:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" {
				- "Encoding declaration\n  state"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "A character encoding declaration is required (either in the "
				a href="#content-type" id="charset:content-type-2" {
					- "Content-Type metadata"
				}
				- " or explicitly in the file) even when all\n   characters are in the ASCII range, because a character encoding is needed to process non-ASCII\n   characters entered by the user in forms, in URLs generated by scripts, and so forth."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Using non-UTF-8 encodings can have unexpected results on form submission and URL encodings,\n   which use the "
				a id="charset:document's-character-encoding-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
					- "document's character encoding"
				}
				- " by default."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the document is "
			a href="#an-iframe-srcdoc-document" id="charset:an-iframe-srcdoc-document-2" {
				- "an "
				code {
					- "iframe"
				}
				- " "
				code {
					- "srcdoc"
				}
				- "\n  document"
			}
			- ", the document must not have a "
			a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="charset:character-encoding-declaration-3" {
				- "character encoding declaration"
			}
			- ". (In\n  this case, the source is already decoded, since it is part of the document that contained the\n  "
			code id="charset:the-iframe-element" {
				a href="#the-iframe-element" {
					- "iframe"
				}
			}
			- ".)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In XML, the XML declaration should be used for inline character encoding information, if\n  necessary."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In HTML, to declare that the character encoding is "
				a id="charset:utf-8-4" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8" data-x-internal="utf-8" {
					- "UTF-8"
				}
				- ", the author could\n   include the following markup near the top of the document (in the "
				code id="charset:the-head-element" {
					a href="#the-head-element" {
						- "head"
					}
				}
				- " element):"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "meta"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "charset"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"utf-8\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In XML, the XML declaration would be used instead, at the very top of the markup:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- cp="" {
						- "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-style-element" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.2.6"
			}
			- " The "
			dfn data-dfn-type="element" {
				code {
					- "style"
				}
			}
			- " element"
			a href="#the-style-element" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/style" title="The <style> HTML element contains style information for a document, or part of a document. It contains CSS, which is applied to the contents of the document containing the <style> element." {
						- "Element/style"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "3.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "10.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
