				- "represents"
			}
			- " a footer for its nearest ancestor\n  "
			a href="#sectioning-content-2" id="the-footer-element:sectioning-content-2-2" {
				- "sectioning content"
			}
			- " element, or for "
			a href="#the-body-element-2" id="the-footer-element:the-body-element-2" {
				- "the body element"
			}
			- " if there is no such\n  ancestor. A footer typically contains information about its section such as who wrote it, links\n  to related documents, copyright data, and the like."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			code id="the-footer-element:the-footer-element-3" {
				a href="#the-footer-element" {
					- "footer"
				}
			}
			- " element contains entire sections, they "
			a href="#represents" id="the-footer-element:represents-2" {
				- "represent"
			}
			- " appendices, indices, long colophons, verbose license\n  agreements, and other such content."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Contact information for the author or editor of a section belongs in an\n  "
			code id="the-footer-element:the-address-element" {
				a href="#the-address-element" {
					- "address"
				}
			}
			- " element, possibly itself inside a "
			code id="the-footer-element:the-footer-element-4" {
				a href="#the-footer-element" {
					- "footer"
				}
			}
			- ". Bylines and other\n  information that could be suitable for both a "
			code id="the-footer-element:the-header-element-2" {
				a href="#the-header-element" {
					- "header"
				}
			}
			- " or a "
			code id="the-footer-element:the-footer-element-5" {
				a href="#the-footer-element" {
					- "footer"
				}
			}
			- " can be\n  placed in either (or neither). The primary purpose of these elements is merely to help the author\n  write self-explanatory markup that is easy to maintain and style; they are not intended to impose\n  specific structures on authors."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
