						c- f="" {
							- "hr"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "The Carlton AllLander drove Dudley home just after dawn. Like the\nastronomer, the vehicle was old and worn, but perfectly capable of\ndoing its job. It had a cheap diesel engine, common enough on a\nsemi-frontier world like Gralmond, although its drive array was a\nthoroughly modern photoneural processor. With its high suspension and\ndeep-tread tyres it could plough along the dirt track to the\nobservatory in all weather and seasons, including the metre-deep snow\nof Gralmond's winters."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
