		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should render the items of the list in a manner consistent with the state of the\n  "
			code id="the-ol-element:attr-ol-type-3" {
				a href="#attr-ol-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute of the "
			code id="the-ol-element:the-ol-element-6" {
				a href="#the-ol-element" {
					- "ol"
				}
			}
			- " element. Numbers less than\n  or equal to zero should always use the decimal system regardless of the "
			code id="the-ol-element:attr-ol-type-4" {
				a href="#attr-ol-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "For CSS user agents, a mapping for this attribute to the\n  "
			a id="the-ol-element:'list-style-type'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-lists/#propdef-list-style-type" data-x-internal="'list-style-type'" {
				- "'list-style-type'"
			}
			- " CSS property is given "
			a href="#decohints" {
				- "in the Rendering\n  section"
			}
			- " (the mapping is straightforward: the states above have the same names as their\n  corresponding CSS values)."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "It is possible to redefine the default CSS list styles used to implement this\n  attribute in CSS user agents; doing so will affect how list items are rendered."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLOListElement" id="dom-ol-reversed" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "reversed"
				}
			}
			- "\n  and "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLOListElement" id="dom-ol-type" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " IDL\n  attributes must "
			a href="#reflect" id="the-ol-element:reflect" {
				- "reflect"
			}
			- " the respective content attributes of the same name."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLOListElement" id="dom-ol-start" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "start"
				}
			}
			- " IDL\n  attribute must "
			a href="#reflect" id="the-ol-element:reflect-2" {
				- "reflect"
			}
			- " the content attribute of the same name, with a "
			a href="#default-value" id="the-ol-element:default-value" {
				- "default\n  value"
			}
			- " of 1."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This means that the "
			code id="the-ol-element:dom-ol-start-2" {
				a href="#dom-ol-start" {
					- "start"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute does\n  not necessarily match the list's "
