		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="the-figure-element:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " some "
			a href="#flow-content-2" id="the-figure-element:flow-content-2-6" {
				- "flow content"
			}
			- ",\n  optionally with a caption, that is self-contained (like a complete sentence) and is typically\n  "
			a href="#referenced" id="the-figure-element:referenced" {
				- "referenced"
			}
			- " as a single unit from the main flow of the document."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "\"Self-contained\" in this context does not necessarily mean independent. For\n  example, each sentence in a paragraph is self-contained; an image that is part of a sentence would\n  be inappropriate for "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-2" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- ", but an entire sentence made of images would be\n  fitting."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The element can thus be used to annotate illustrations, diagrams, photos, code listings,\n  etc."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div id="figure-note-about-references" class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "When a "
				code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-3" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " is referred to from the main content of the document by identifying\n   it by its caption (e.g., by figure number), it enables such content to be easily moved away from\n   that primary content, e.g., to the side of the page, to dedicated pages, or to an appendix,\n   without affecting the flow of the document."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If a "
				code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-4" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " element is "
				a href="#referenced" id="the-figure-element:referenced-2" {
					- "referenced"
				}
				- " by its relative position, e.g.,\n   \"in the photograph above\" or \"as the next figure shows\", then moving the figure would disrupt the\n   page's meaning. Authors are encouraged to consider using labels to refer to figures, rather than\n   using such relative references, so that the page can easily be restyled without affecting the\n   page's meaning."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The first "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figcaption-element-3" {
				a href="#the-figcaption-element" {
					- "figcaption"
				}
			}
			- " element child of the element, if any,\n  represents the caption of the "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-5" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- " element's contents. If there is no child\n  "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figcaption-element-4" {
				a href="#the-figcaption-element" {
					- "figcaption"
				}
			}
			- " element, then there is no caption."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-6" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- " element's contents are part of the surrounding flow. If the purpose of\n  the page is to display the figure, for example a photograph on an image sharing site, the\n  "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-7" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figcaption-element-5" {
				a href="#the-figcaption-element" {
					- "figcaption"
				}
			}
			- " elements can be used to explicitly provide a\n  caption for that figure. For content that is only tangentially related, or that serves a separate\n  purpose than the surrounding flow, the "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-aside-element" {
				a href="#the-aside-element" {
					- "aside"
				}
			}
			- " element should be used (and can itself\n  wrap a "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-8" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- "). For example, a pull quote that repeats content from an\n  "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-article-element" {
				a href="#the-article-element" {
					- "article"
				}
			}
			- " would be more appropriate in an "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-aside-element-2" {
				a href="#the-aside-element" {
					- "aside"
				}
			}
			- " than in a\n  "
			code id="the-figure-element:the-figure-element-9" {
				a href="#the-figure-element" {
					- "figure"
				}
			}
			- ", because it isn't part of the content, it's a repetition of the content for\n  the purposes of enticing readers or highlighting key topics."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
