					- "em"
				}
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="the-em-element:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " stress emphasis of its contents."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The level of stress that a particular piece of content has is given by its number of ancestor\n  "
			code id="the-em-element:the-em-element-2" {
				a href="#the-em-element" {
					- "em"
				}
			}
			- " elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The placement of stress emphasis changes the meaning of the sentence. The element thus forms an\n  integral part of the content. The precise way in which stress is used in this way depends on the\n  language."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "These examples show how changing the stress emphasis changes the meaning. First, a general\n   statement of fact, with no stress:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Cats are cute animals."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "By emphasizing the first word, the statement implies that the kind of animal under discussion\n   is in question (maybe someone is asserting that dogs are cute):"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "em"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Cats"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "em"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " are cute animals."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Moving the stress to the verb, one highlights that the truth of the entire sentence is in\n   question (maybe someone is saying cats are not cute):"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Cats "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "em"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "are"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "em"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
