		p {
			- "Abbreviations do not have to be marked up using this element. It is expected to be useful in\n  the following cases:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "Abbreviations for which the author wants to give expansions, where using the\n   "
				code id="the-abbr-element:the-abbr-element-4" {
					a href="#the-abbr-element" {
						- "abbr"
					}
				}
				- " element with a "
				code id="the-abbr-element:attr-title" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is an\n   alternative to including the expansion inline (e.g. in parentheses)."
			}
			li {
				- "Abbreviations that are likely to be unfamiliar to the document's readers, for which authors\n   are encouraged to either mark up the abbreviation using an "
				code id="the-abbr-element:the-abbr-element-5" {
					a href="#the-abbr-element" {
						- "abbr"
					}
				}
				- " element with a "
				code id="the-abbr-element:attr-title-2" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attribute or include the expansion inline in the text the first\n   time the abbreviation is used."
			}
			li {
				- "Abbreviations whose presence needs to be semantically annotated, e.g. so that they can be\n   identified from a style sheet and given specific styles, for which the "
				code id="the-abbr-element:the-abbr-element-6" {
					a href="#the-abbr-element" {
						- "abbr"
					}
				}
				- " element\n   can be used without a "
				code id="the-abbr-element:attr-title-3" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attribute."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Providing an expansion in a "
			code id="the-abbr-element:attr-title-4" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute once\n  will not necessarily cause other "
			code id="the-abbr-element:the-abbr-element-7" {
				a href="#the-abbr-element" {
					- "abbr"
				}
			}
			- " elements in the same document with the same\n  contents but without a "
			code id="the-abbr-element:attr-title-5" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute to behave as if they had\n  the same expansion. Every "
			code id="the-abbr-element:the-abbr-element-8" {
				a href="#the-abbr-element" {
					- "abbr"
				}
			}
			- " element is independent."
		}
