					}
				}
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "2011-11-18 14:54:39.929"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Times with dates but without a time zone offset are useful for specifying events\n    that are observed at the same specific time in each time zone, throughout a day. For example,\n    the 2020 new year is celebrated at 2020-01-01 00:00 in each time zone, not at the same precise\n    moment across all time zones. For events that occur at the same time across all time zones, for\n    example a videoconference meeting, a "
					a href="#valid-global-date-and-time-string" id="the-time-element:valid-global-date-and-time-string" {
						- "valid global date and time string"
					}
					- " is likely\n    more useful."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				a href="#valid-time-zone-offset-string" id="the-time-element:valid-time-zone-offset-string" {
					- "valid time-zone offset string"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "Z"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "+0000"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "+00:00"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "-0800"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "-08:00"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "For times without dates (or times referring to events that recur on multiple\n    dates), specifying the geographic location that controls the time is usually more useful than\n    specifying a time zone offset, because geographic locations change time zone offsets with\n    daylight saving time. In some cases, geographic locations even change time zone, e.g. when the\n    boundaries of those time zones are redrawn, as happened with Samoa at the end of 2011. There\n    exists a time zone database that describes the boundaries of time zones and what rules apply\n    within each such zone, known as the "
					i {
						- "time zone database"
					}
					- ". "
					a href="#refsTZDATABASE" {
						- "[TZDATABASE]"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				a href="#valid-global-date-and-time-string" id="the-time-element:valid-global-date-and-time-string-2" {
					- "valid global date and time string"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				pre class="example" {
					code class="html" {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "2011-11-18T14:54Z"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "time"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
