				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Times with dates and a time zone offset are useful for specifying specific\n    events, or recurring virtual events where the time is not anchored to a specific geographic\n    location. For example, the precise time of an asteroid impact, or a particular meeting in a\n    series of meetings held at 1400 UTC every day, regardless of whether any particular part of the\n    world is observing daylight saving time or not. For events where the precise time varies by the\n    local time zone offset of a specific geographic location, a "
					a href="#valid-local-date-and-time-string" id="the-time-element:valid-local-date-and-time-string-2" {
						- "valid local date and time\n    string"
					}
					- " combined with that geographic location is likely more useful."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
