		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="links" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.6"
			}
			- " Links"
			a href="#links" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="introduction-2" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.6.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-2" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Links are a conceptual construct, created by "
			code id="introduction-2:the-a-element" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="introduction-2:the-area-element" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:the-form-element" {
				a href="#the-form-element" {
					- "form"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="introduction-2:the-link-element" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- " elements, that "
			a href="#represents" id="introduction-2:represents" {
				- "represent"
			}
			- "\n  a connection between two resources, one of which is the current "
			code id="introduction-2:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- ". There are\n  three kinds of links in HTML:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="external-resource-link" data-lt="external resource link" data-export="" {
					- "Links to\n   external resources"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "These are links to resources that are to be used to augment the current document,\n   generally automatically processed by the user agent. All "
					a href="#external-resource-link" id="introduction-2:external-resource-link" {
						- "external resource links"
					}
					- " have a "
					a href="#fetch-and-process-the-linked-resource" id="introduction-2:fetch-and-process-the-linked-resource" {
						- "fetch and process the linked resource"
					}
					- "\n   algorithm which describes how the resource is obtained."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="hyperlink" data-lt="hyperlink" data-export="" {
					- "Hyperlinks"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "These are links to other resources that are generally exposed to the user by the user\n   agent so that the user can cause the user agent to "
					a href="#navigate" id="introduction-2:navigate" {
						- "navigate"
					}
					- " to those resources, e.g.\n   to visit them in a browser or download them."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="internal-resource-link" data-export="" {
					- "Internal resource links"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "These are links to resources within the current document, used to give those resources\n   special meaning or behavior."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For "
			code id="introduction-2:the-link-element-2" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- " elements with an "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-link-href" {
				a href="#attr-link-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute and a\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-link-rel" {
				a href="#attr-link-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, links must be created for the keywords of the\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-link-rel-2" {
				a href="#attr-link-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, as defined for those keywords in the "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "link types"
			}
			- " section."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, for "
			code id="introduction-2:the-a-element-2" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="introduction-2:the-area-element-2" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements with an "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-href" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute and a "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-rel" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, links must be created for the keywords of the\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-rel-2" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute as defined for those keywords in the "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "link types"
			}
			- " section. Unlike "
			code id="introduction-2:the-link-element-3" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- " elements, however,\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:the-a-element-3" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="introduction-2:the-area-element-3" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements with an "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-href-2" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute that either do not have a "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-rel-3" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, or\n  whose "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-rel-4" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute has no keywords that are defined as\n  specifying "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="introduction-2:hyperlink" {
				- "hyperlinks"
			}
			- ", must also create a "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="introduction-2:hyperlink-2" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- ".\n  This implied hyperlink has no special meaning (it has no "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "link type"
			}
			- ")\n  beyond linking the element's "
			a id="introduction-2:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- " to the resource given by the element's "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-hyperlink-href-3" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, for "
			code id="introduction-2:the-form-element-2" {
				a href="#the-form-element" {
					- "form"
				}
			}
			- " elements with a "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-form-rel" {
				a href="#attr-form-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, links must be created for the keywords of the "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-form-rel-2" {
				a href="#attr-form-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute as defined for those keywords in the "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "link types"
			}
			- " section.\n  "
			code id="introduction-2:the-form-element-3" {
				a href="#the-form-element" {
					- "form"
				}
			}
			- " elements that do not have a "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-form-rel-3" {
				a href="#attr-form-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute,\n  or whose "
			code id="introduction-2:attr-form-rel-4" {
				a href="#attr-form-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute has no keywords that are defined as\n  specifying "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="introduction-2:hyperlink-3" {
				- "hyperlinks"
			}
			- ", must also create a "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="introduction-2:hyperlink-4" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- ".\n\n  "
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="introduction-2:hyperlink-5" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- " can have one or more "
			dfn id="hyperlink-annotation" {
				- "hyperlink\n  annotations"
			}
			- " that modify the processing semantics of that hyperlink."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.6.2"
			}
			- " Links created by "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements"
			a href="#links-created-by-a-and-area-elements" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-href" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute on "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-2" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-2" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:valid-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" {
				- "valid\n  URL potentially surrounded by spaces"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-href" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attribute on "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-3" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and\n  "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-3" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements is not required; when those elements do not have "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-href-2" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
					- "href"
				}
			}
			- " attributes they do not create hyperlinks."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-target" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "target"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, if present, must be a "
			a href="#valid-navigable-target-name-or-keyword" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:valid-navigable-target-name-or-keyword" {
				- "valid navigable target name or keyword"
			}
			- ". It gives the\n  name of the "
			a href="#navigable" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:navigable" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- " that will be used. User agents use this\n  name when "
			a href="#following-hyperlinks-2" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:following-hyperlinks-2" {
				- "following hyperlinks"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-download" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "download"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, if present, indicates that the author intends the hyperlink to be used for "
			a href="#downloading-hyperlinks" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:downloading-hyperlinks" {
				- "downloading a resource"
			}
			- ". The attribute may have a value; the\n  value, if any, specifies the default filename that the author recommends for use in labeling the\n  resource in a local file system. There are no restrictions on allowed values, but authors are\n  cautioned that most file systems have limitations with regard to what punctuation is supported in\n  filenames, and user agents are likely to adjust filenames accordingly."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/a#attr-ping" title="The <a> HTML element (or anchor element), with its href attribute, creates a hyperlink to web pages, files, email addresses, locations in the same page, or anything else a URL can address." {
						- "Element/a#attr-ping"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span title="Requires setting a user preference or runtime flag." {
							- "🔰 1+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "6+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "17+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "No"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "≤37+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="ping" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "ping"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, if present, gives the URLs of the\n  resources that are interested in being notified if the user follows the hyperlink. The value must\n  be a "
			a href="#set-of-space-separated-tokens" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:set-of-space-separated-tokens" {
				- "set of space-separated tokens"
			}
			- ", each of which must be a "
			a href="#valid-non-empty-url" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:valid-non-empty-url" {
				- "valid non-empty\n  URL"
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-scheme" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:concept-url-scheme" data-x-internal="concept-url-scheme" {
				- "scheme"
			}
			- " is an "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:http(s)-scheme" href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#http-scheme" data-x-internal="http(s)-scheme" {
				- "HTTP(S)\n  scheme"
			}
			- ". The value is used by the user agent for "
			a href="#hyperlink-auditing" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:hyperlink-auditing" {
				- "hyperlink\n  auditing"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-rel" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute on "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-4" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-4" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- "\n  elements controls what kinds of links the elements create. The attribute's value must be an\n  "
			a href="#unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens" {
				- "unordered set of unique space-separated tokens"
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "allowed\n  keywords and their meanings"
			}
			- " are defined below."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-rel" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-supported-tokens" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:concept-supported-tokens" data-x-internal="concept-supported-tokens" {
				- "supported tokens"
			}
			- " are the keywords defined in "
			a href="#linkTypes" {
				- "HTML link types"
			}
			- " which are allowed on "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-5" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-5" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- "\n  elements, impact the processing model, and are supported by the user agent. The possible "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-supported-tokens" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:concept-supported-tokens-2" data-x-internal="concept-supported-tokens" {
				- "supported tokens"
			}
			- " are "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:link-type-noreferrer" {
				a href="#link-type-noreferrer" {
					- "noreferrer"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:link-type-noopener" {
				a href="#link-type-noopener" {
					- "noopener"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:link-type-opener" {
				a href="#link-type-opener" {
					- "opener"
				}
			}
			- ". "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-rel-2" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-supported-tokens" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:concept-supported-tokens-3" data-x-internal="concept-supported-tokens" {
				- "supported tokens"
			}
			- " must only include the tokens from this\n  list that the user agent implements the processing model for."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-rel-3" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute has no default value. If the\n  attribute is omitted or if none of the values in the attribute are recognized by the user agent,\n  then the document has no particular relationship with the destination resource other than there\n  being a hyperlink between the two."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-hreflang" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "hreflang"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute on "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-6" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " elements that create "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:hyperlink" {
				- "hyperlinks"
			}
			- ", if\n  present, gives the language of the linked resource. It is purely advisory. The value must be a\n  valid BCP 47 language tag. "
			a href="#refsBCP47" {
				- "[BCP47]"
			}
			- " User agents must not consider this\n  attribute authoritative — upon fetching the resource, user agents must use only language\n  information associated with the resource to determine its language, not metadata included in the\n  link to the resource."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-type" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, if present, gives the "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:mime-type" href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" data-x-internal="mime-type" {
				- "MIME type"
			}
			- " of the linked resource. It is purely\n  advisory. The value must be a "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:valid-mime-type-string" href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#valid-mime-type" data-x-internal="valid-mime-type-string" {
				- "valid MIME type string"
			}
			- ". User agents must\n  not consider the "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-type" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute authoritative —\n  upon fetching the resource, user agents must not use metadata included in the link to the resource\n  to determine its type."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="a,area" id="attr-hyperlink-referrerpolicy" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "referrerpolicy"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#referrer-policy-attribute" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:referrer-policy-attribute" {
				- "referrer\n  policy attribute"
			}
			- ". Its purpose is to set the "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:referrer-policy" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#referrer-policy" data-x-internal="referrer-policy" {
				- "referrer policy"
			}
			- " used when\n  "
			a href="#following-hyperlinks-2" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:following-hyperlinks-2-2" {
				- "following hyperlinks"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsREFERRERPOLICY" {
				- "[REFERRERPOLICY]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-7" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " or "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-6" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:activation-behaviour" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#eventtarget-activation-behavior" data-x-internal="activation-behaviour" {
				- "activation behavior"
			}
			- " is\n  invoked, the user agent may allow the user to indicate a preference regarding whether the\n  hyperlink is to be used for "
			a href="#navigate" id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:navigate" {
				- "navigation"
			}
			- " or whether the resource it\n  specifies is to be downloaded."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In the absence of a user preference, the default should be navigation if the element has no\n  "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-download" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-download" {
					- "download"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, and should be to download the\n  specified resource if it does."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:activation-behaviour-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#eventtarget-activation-behavior" data-x-internal="activation-behaviour" {
				- "activation behavior"
			}
			- " of an "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-a-element-8" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " or "
			code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:the-area-element-7" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " element\n  "
			var {
				- "element"
			}
			- " given an event "
			var {
				- "event"
			}
			- " is:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " has no "
					code id="links-created-by-a-and-area-elements:attr-hyperlink-href-3" {
						a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
							- "href"
						}
					}
					- " attribute,\n   then return."
				}
			}
