		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In some cases, resources are intended for later use rather than immediate viewing. To indicate\n  that a resource is intended to be downloaded for use later, rather than immediately used, the\n  "
			code id="downloading-resources:attr-hyperlink-download" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-download" {
					- "download"
				}
			}
			- " attribute can be specified on the\n  "
			code id="downloading-resources:the-a-element" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- " or "
			code id="downloading-resources:the-area-element" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " element that creates the "
			a href="#hyperlink" id="downloading-resources:hyperlink" {
				- "hyperlink"
			}
			- " to that\n  resource."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The attribute can furthermore be given a value, to specify the filename that user agents are\n  to use when storing the resource in a file system. This value can be overridden by the `"
			code id="downloading-resources:http-content-disposition" {
				a data-x-internal="http-content-disposition" href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc6266.html" {
					- "Content-Disposition"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP header's filename parameters.\n  "
			a href="#refsRFC6266" {
				- "[RFC6266]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In cross-origin situations, the "
			code id="downloading-resources:attr-hyperlink-download-2" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-download" {
					- "download"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute has to be combined with the `"
			code id="downloading-resources:http-content-disposition-2" {
				a data-x-internal="http-content-disposition" href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc6266.html" {
					- "Content-Disposition"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP header, specifically with the\n  "
			code {
				- "attachment"
			}
			- " disposition type, to avoid the user being warned of possibly\n  nefarious activity. (This is to protect users from being made to download sensitive personal or\n  confidential information without their full understanding.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
