				- "\n\n    "
				div class="warning" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "If the algorithm reaches this step, then a download was begun from a different origin than\n     the resource being downloaded, and the origin did not mark the file as suitable for\n     downloading, and the download was not initiated by the user. This could be because a "
						code id="downloading-resources:attr-hyperlink-download-7" {
							a href="#attr-hyperlink-download" {
								- "download"
							}
						}
						- " attribute was used to trigger the download, or\n     because the resource in question is not of a type that the user agent supports."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "This could be dangerous, because, for instance, a hostile server could be trying to get a\n     user to unknowingly download private information and then re-upload it to the hostile server,\n     by tricking the user into thinking the data is from the hostile server."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Thus, it is in the user's interests that the user be somehow notified that the resource in\n     question comes from quite a different source, and to prevent confusion, any suggested filename\n     from the potentially hostile "
						var {
							- "interface origin"
						}
						- " should be ignored."
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					i {
						- "Sanitize"
					}
					- ": Optionally, allow the user to influence "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- ". For\n   example, a user agent could prompt the user for a filename, potentially providing the value of\n   "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- " as determined above as a default value."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Adjust "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- " to be suitable for the local file system."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="example" {
					- "For example, this could involve removing characters that are not legal in\n    filenames, or trimming leading and trailing whitespace."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the platform conventions do not in any way use "
					a href="#concept-extension" id="downloading-resources:concept-extension" {
						- "extensions"
					}
					- " to determine the types of file on the file system,\n   then return "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- " as the filename."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "claimed type"
					}
					- " be the type given by the resource's "
					a href="#content-type" id="downloading-resources:content-type" {
						- "Content-Type metadata"
					}
					- ", if any is known. Let "
					var {
						- "named\n   type"
					}
					- " be the type given by "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-extension" id="downloading-resources:concept-extension-2" {
						- "extension"
					}
					- ", if any is known. For the purposes of this step, a\n   "
					i {
						- "type"
					}
					- " is a mapping of a "
					a id="downloading-resources:mime-type" href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" data-x-internal="mime-type" {
						- "MIME type"
					}
					- " to an "
					a href="#concept-extension" id="downloading-resources:concept-extension-3" {
						- "extension"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "named type"
					}
					- " is consistent with the user's preferences (e.g., because the\n   value of "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- " was determined by prompting the user), then return\n   "
					var {
						- "filename"
					}
					- " as the filename."
