				- "\n\n    "
				dl class="switch" {
					dt {
						- "If the "
						a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url" id="hyperlink-auditing:the-document's-address" data-x-internal="the-document's-address" {
							- "URL"
						}
						- " of the "
						code id="hyperlink-auditing:document" {
							a href="#document" {
								- "Document"
							}
						}
						- " object\n     containing the hyperlink being audited and "
						var {
							- "ping URL"
						}
						- " have the "
						a href="#same-origin" id="hyperlink-auditing:same-origin" {
							- "same\n     origin"
						}
					}
					dt {
						- "If the origins are different, but the "
						a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-scheme" id="hyperlink-auditing:concept-url-scheme-2" data-x-internal="concept-url-scheme" {
							- "scheme"
						}
						- " of\n     the "
						a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url" id="hyperlink-auditing:the-document's-address-2" data-x-internal="the-document's-address" {
							- "URL"
						}
						- " of the "
						code id="hyperlink-auditing:document-2" {
							a href="#document" {
								- "Document"
							}
						}
						- " containing the\n     hyperlink being audited is not \""
						code {
							- "https"
						}
						- "\""
					}
					dd {
						var {
							- "request"
						}
						- " must include a `"
						code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-from" {
							a href="#ping-from" {
								- "Ping-From"
							}
						}
						- "` header with, as its value, the\n     "
						a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url" id="hyperlink-auditing:the-document's-address-3" data-x-internal="the-document's-address" {
							- "URL"
						}
						- " of the document containing the hyperlink, and a\n     `"
						code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-to" {
							a href="#ping-to" {
								- "Ping-To"
							}
						}
						- "` HTTP header with, as its value, the "
						var {
							- "target URL"
						}
						- "."
					}
					dt {
						- "Otherwise"
					}
					dd {
						var {
							- "request"
						}
						- " must include a `"
						code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-to-2" {
							a href="#ping-to" {
								- "Ping-To"
							}
						}
						- "` HTTP header with, as its value,\n     "
						var {
							- "target URL"
						}
						- ". "
						span class="note" {
							var {
								- "request"
							}
							- " does not include a\n     `"
							code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-from-2" {
								a href="#ping-from" {
									- "Ping-From"
								}
							}
							- "` header."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id="hyperlink-auditing:concept-fetch" data-x-internal="concept-fetch" {
						- "Fetch"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "request"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This may be done "
			a href="#in-parallel" id="hyperlink-auditing:in-parallel" {
				- "in parallel"
			}
			- " with the primary fetch, and is independent of the\n  result of that fetch."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should allow the user to adjust this behavior, for example in conjunction with a\n  setting that disables the sending of HTTP `"
			code id="hyperlink-auditing:http-referer" {
				a data-x-internal="http-referer" href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7231.html#header.referer" {
					- "Referer"
				}
			}
			- "` (sic)\n  headers. Based on the user's preferences, UAs may either "
			a href="#ignore" id="hyperlink-auditing:ignore" {
				- "ignore"
			}
			- " the "
			code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-3" {
				a href="#ping" {
					- "ping"
				}
			}
			- " attribute altogether, or selectively ignore URLs in the\n  list (e.g. ignoring any third-party URLs); this is explicitly accounted for in the steps\n  above."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents must ignore any entity bodies returned in the responses. User agents may close the\n  connection prematurely once they start receiving a response body."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-4" {
				a href="#ping" {
					- "ping"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is present, user agents\n  should clearly indicate to the user that following the hyperlink will also cause secondary\n  requests to be sent in the background, possibly including listing the actual target URLs."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, a visual user agent could include the hostnames of the target ping\n  URLs along with the hyperlink's actual URL in a status bar or tooltip."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The "
				code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-5" {
					a href="#ping" {
						- "ping"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is redundant with pre-existing\n   technologies like HTTP redirects and JavaScript in allowing web pages to track which off-site\n   links are most popular or allowing advertisers to track click-through rates."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, the "
				code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-6" {
					a href="#ping" {
						- "ping"
					}
				}
				- " attribute provides these advantages\n   to the user over those alternatives:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			ul {
				li {
					- "It allows the user to see the final target URL unobscured."
				}
				li {
					- "It allows the UA to inform the user about the out-of-band notifications."
				}
				li {
					- "It allows the user to disable the notifications without losing the underlying link\n    functionality."
				}
				li {
					- "It allows the UA to optimize the use of available network bandwidth so that the target page\n    loads faster."
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Thus, while it is possible to track users without this feature, authors are encouraged to use\n   the "
				code id="hyperlink-auditing:ping-7" {
					a href="#ping" {
						- "ping"
					}
				}
				- " attribute so that the user agent can make the\n   user experience more transparent."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="the-ping-headers" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.6.6.1"
			}
			- " The `"
			code id="the-ping-headers:ping-from" {
				a href="#ping-from" {
					- "Ping-From"
				}
			}
			- "` and `"
			code id="the-ping-headers:ping-to" {
				a href="#ping-to" {
					- "Ping-To"
				}
			}
			- "` headers"
			a href="#the-ping-headers" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The `"
			dfn id="ping-from" data-dfn-type="http-header" {
				code {
					- "Ping-From"
				}
			}
			- "` and `"
			dfn id="ping-to" data-dfn-type="http-header" {
				code {
					- "Ping-To"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP request headers are included in "
			a href="#hyperlink-auditing" id="the-ping-headers:hyperlink-auditing" {
				- "hyperlink\n  auditing"
			}
			- " requests. Their value is a "
			a id="the-ping-headers:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-serializer" id="the-ping-headers:concept-url-serializer" data-x-internal="concept-url-serializer" {
				- "serialized"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="linkTypes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.6.7"
			}
			- " Link types"
			a href="#linkTypes" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Link_types" title="The rel attribute defines the relationship between a linked resource and the current document. Valid on <link>, <a>, <area>, and <form>, the supported values depend on the element on which the attribute is found." {
						- "Link_types"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "1+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "10.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Link_types" title="The rel attribute defines the relationship between a linked resource and the current document. Valid on <link>, <a>, <area>, and <form>, the supported values depend on the element on which the attribute is found." {
						- "Link_types"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following table summarizes the link types that are defined by this specification, by their\n  corresponding keywords. This table is non-normative; the actual definitions for the link types are\n  given in the next few sections."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In this section, the term "
			i {
				- "referenced document"
			}
			- " refers to the resource identified by the\n  element representing the link, and the term "
			i {
				- "current document"
			}
			- " refers to the resource within\n  which the element representing the link finds itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "To determine which link types apply to a "
			code id="linkTypes:the-link-element" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="linkTypes:the-a-element" {
				a href="#the-a-element" {
					- "a"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="linkTypes:the-area-element" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  or "
			code id="linkTypes:the-form-element" {
				a href="#the-form-element" {
					- "form"
				}
			}
			- " element, the element's "
			code {
				- "rel"
			}
			- " attribute must be "
			a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id="linkTypes:split-a-string-on-spaces" data-x-internal="split-a-string-on-spaces" {
				- "split on ASCII whitespace"
			}
			- ". The resulting tokens\n  are the keywords for the link types that apply to that element."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Except where otherwise specified, a keyword must not be specified more than once per "
			code id="linkTypes:attr-hyperlink-rel" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-rel" {
					- "rel"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some of the sections that follow the table below list synonyms for certain keywords. The\n  indicated synonyms are to be handled as specified by user agents, but must\n  not be used in documents (for example, the keyword \""
			code {
				- "copyright"
			}
			- "\")."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Keywords are always "
			a id="linkTypes:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
				- "ASCII case-insensitive"
			}
			- ", and must be\n  compared as such."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "Thus, "
			code {
				- "rel=\"next\""
			}
			- " is the same as "
			code {
				- "rel=\"NEXT\""
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Keywords that are "
			dfn id="body-ok" {
				- "body-ok"
			}
			- " affect whether "
			code id="linkTypes:the-link-element-2" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- " elements are\n  "
			a href="#allowed-in-the-body" id="linkTypes:allowed-in-the-body" {
				- "allowed in the body"
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#body-ok" id="linkTypes:body-ok" {
				- "body-ok"
			}
			- " keywords are\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-dns-prefetch" {
				a href="#link-type-dns-prefetch" {
					- "dns-prefetch"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-modulepreload" {
				a href="#link-type-modulepreload" {
					- "modulepreload"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-pingback" {
				a href="#link-type-pingback" {
					- "pingback"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-preconnect" {
				a href="#link-type-preconnect" {
					- "preconnect"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-prefetch" {
				a href="#link-type-prefetch" {
					- "prefetch"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-preload" {
				a href="#link-type-preload" {
					- "preload"
				}
			}
			- ", and\n  "
			code id="linkTypes:link-type-stylesheet" {
				a href="#link-type-stylesheet" {
					- "stylesheet"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "New link types that are to be implemented by web browsers are to be added to this standard. The\n  remainder can be "
			a href="#concept-rel-extensions" id="linkTypes:concept-rel-extensions" {
				- "registered as extensions"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table id="table-link-relations" class="yesno" {
			thead {
				tr {
					th rowspan="2" {
						- "Link type"
					}
					th colspan="3" {
						- "Effect on..."
					}
					th rowspan="2" {
						a href="#body-ok" id="linkTypes:body-ok-2" {
							- "body-ok"
						}
					}
					th rowspan="2" {
						- "Has `"
						code id="linkTypes:http-link" {
							a data-x-internal="http-link" href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8288.html#header" {
								- "Link"
							}
						}
						- "` processing"
					}
					th rowspan="2" {
						- "Brief description"
					}
				}
				tr {
					th {
						code id="linkTypes:the-link-element-3" {
							a href="#the-link-element" {
								- "link"
							}
						}
					}
