		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="rel-icon:rel-icon" {
				a href="#rel-icon" {
					- "icon"
				}
			}
			- " keyword may be used with "
			code id="rel-icon:the-link-element" {
				a href="#the-link-element" {
					- "link"
				}
			}
			- " elements.\n  This keyword creates an "
			a href="#external-resource-link" id="rel-icon:external-resource-link" {
				- "external resource link"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The specified resource is an icon representing the page or site, and should be used by the user\n  agent when representing the page in the user interface."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Icons could be auditory icons, visual icons, or other kinds of icons. If\n  multiple icons are provided, the user agent must select the most appropriate icon according to the\n  "
			code id="rel-icon:attr-link-type" {
				a href="#attr-link-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="rel-icon:attr-link-media" {
				a href="#attr-link-media" {
					- "media"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="rel-icon:attr-link-sizes" {
				a href="#attr-link-sizes" {
					- "sizes"
				}
			}
			- " attributes. If there are multiple equally appropriate icons,\n  user agents must use the last one declared in "
			a id="rel-icon:tree-order" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" data-x-internal="tree-order" {
				- "tree order"
			}
			- " at the time that the user\n  agent collected the list of icons. If the user agent tries to use an icon but that icon is\n  determined, upon closer examination, to in fact be inappropriate (e.g. because it uses an\n  unsupported format), then the user agent must try the next-most-appropriate icon as determined by\n  the attributes."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "User agents are not required to update icons when the list of icons changes, but\n  are encouraged to do so."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "There is no default type for resources given by the "
			code id="rel-icon:rel-icon-2" {
				a href="#rel-icon" {
					- "icon"
				}
			}
			- " keyword.\n  However, for the purposes of "
			a href="#concept-link-type-sniffing" {
				- "determining the type of the\n  resource"
			}
			- ", user agents must expect the resource to be an image."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="rel-icon:attr-link-sizes-2" {
				a href="#attr-link-sizes" {
					- "sizes"
				}
			}
			- " keywords represent icon sizes in raw pixels (as\n  opposed to "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="rel-icon:'px'" data-x-internal="'px'" {
				- "CSS pixels"
			}
			- ")."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "An icon that is 50 "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="rel-icon:'px'-2" data-x-internal="'px'" {
				- "CSS pixels"
			}
			- " wide intended for\n  displays with a device pixel density of two device pixels per "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="rel-icon:'px'-3" data-x-internal="'px'" {
				- "CSS pixel"
			}
			- "\n  (2x, 192dpi) would have a width of 100 raw pixels. This feature does not support indicating that a\n  different resource is to be used for small high-resolution icons vs large low-resolution icons\n  (e.g. 50×50 2x vs 100×100 1x)."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "To parse and process the attribute's value, the user agent must first "
			a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id="rel-icon:split-a-string-on-spaces" data-x-internal="split-a-string-on-spaces" {
				- "split the attribute's value on ASCII whitespace"
			}
			- ", and must then\n  parse each resulting keyword to determine what it represents."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="attr-link-sizes-any" {
				code {
					- "any"
				}
			}
			- " keyword represents that the\n  resource contains a scalable icon, e.g. as provided by an SVG image."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Other keywords must be further parsed as follows to determine what they represent:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the keyword doesn't contain exactly one U+0078 LATIN SMALL LETTER X or U+0058 LATIN\n   CAPITAL LETTER X character, then this keyword doesn't represent anything. Return for\n   that keyword."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "width string"
					}
					- " be the string before the \""
					code {
						- "x"
					}
					- "\" or\n   \""
					code {
						- "X"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "height string"
					}
					- " be the string after the \""
					code {
						- "x"
					}
					- "\" or\n   \""
					code {
						- "X"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If either "
					var {
						- "width string"
					}
					- " or "
					var {
						- "height string"
					}
					- " start with\n   a U+0030 DIGIT ZERO (0) character or contain any characters other than "
					a id="rel-icon:ascii-digits" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit" data-x-internal="ascii-digits" {
						- "ASCII digits"
					}
					- ",\n   then this keyword doesn't represent anything. Return for that keyword."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Apply the "
					a href="#rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers" id="rel-icon:rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers" {
						- "rules for parsing non-negative integers"
					}
					- " to "
					var {
						- "width\n   string"
					}
					- " to obtain "
					var {
						- "width"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Apply the "
					a href="#rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers" id="rel-icon:rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers-2" {
						- "rules for parsing non-negative integers"
					}
					- " to "
					var {
						- "height\n   string"
					}
					- " to obtain "
					var {
						- "height"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The keyword represents that the resource contains a bitmap icon with a width of "
					var {
						- "width"
					}
					- " device pixels and a height of "
					var {
						- "height"
					}
					- " device\n   pixels."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The keywords specified on the "
			code id="rel-icon:attr-link-sizes-3" {
				a href="#attr-link-sizes" {
					- "sizes"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must not\n  represent icon sizes that are not actually available in the linked resource."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#linked-resource-fetch-setup-steps" id="rel-icon:linked-resource-fetch-setup-steps" {
				- "linked resource fetch setup steps"
