		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.7.3"
			}
			- " Attributes common to "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:the-ins-element" {
				a href="#the-ins-element" {
					- "ins"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:the-del-element" {
				a href="#the-del-element" {
					- "del"
				}
			}
			- " elements"
			a href="#attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="ins,del" id="attr-mod-cite" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "cite"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  may be used to specify the "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:the-document's-address" data-x-internal="the-document's-address" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- " of a document that\n  explains the change. When that document is long, for instance the minutes of a meeting, authors\n  are encouraged to include a "
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "fragment"
			}
			- " pointing to the\n  specific part of that document that discusses the change."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:attr-mod-cite" {
				a href="#attr-mod-cite" {
					- "cite"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is present, it must be a "
			a href="#valid-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:valid-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" {
				- "valid\n  URL potentially surrounded by spaces"
			}
			- " that explains the change. To obtain\n  the corresponding citation link, the value of the attribute must be "
			a href="#encoding-parsing-a-url" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:encoding-parsing-a-url" {
				- "parsed"
			}
			- " relative to the element's "
			a id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- ". User agents may\n  allow users to follow such citation links, but they are primarily intended for private use (e.g.,\n  by server-side scripts collecting statistics about a site's edits), not for readers."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="ins,del" id="attr-mod-datetime" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "datetime"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute may be used to specify the time and date of the change."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If present, the "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:attr-mod-datetime" {
				a href="#attr-mod-datetime" {
					- "datetime"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value must be a\n  "
			a href="#valid-date-string-with-optional-time" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:valid-date-string-with-optional-time" {
				- "valid date string with optional time"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents must parse the "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:attr-mod-datetime-2" {
				a href="#attr-mod-datetime" {
					- "datetime"
				}
			}
			- " attribute according\n  to the "
			a href="#parse-a-date-or-time-string" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:parse-a-date-or-time-string" {
				- "parse a date or time string"
			}
			- " algorithm. If that doesn't return a "
			a href="#concept-date" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-date" {
				- "date"
			}
			- " or a "
			a href="#concept-datetime" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-datetime" {
				- "global date and time"
			}
			- ",\n  then the modification has no associated timestamp (the value is non-conforming; it is not a\n  "
			a href="#valid-date-string-with-optional-time" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:valid-date-string-with-optional-time-2" {
				- "valid date string with optional time"
			}
			- "). Otherwise, the modification is marked as\n  having been made at the given "
			a href="#concept-date" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-date-2" {
				- "date"
			}
			- " or "
			a href="#concept-datetime" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-datetime-2" {
				- "global date and time"
			}
			- ". If the given value is a "
			a href="#concept-datetime" id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:concept-datetime-3" {
				- "global date and time"
			}
			- " then user agents should use the associated\n  time-zone offset information to determine which time zone to present the given datetime in."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "This value may be shown to the user, but it is primarily intended for\n  private use."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:the-ins-element-2" {
				a href="#the-ins-element" {
					- "ins"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:the-del-element-2" {
				a href="#the-del-element" {
					- "del"
				}
			}
			- " elements must implement the\n  "
			code id="attributes-common-to-ins-and-del-elements:htmlmodelement" {
				a href="#htmlmodelement" {
					- "HTMLModElement"
				}
			}
			- " interface:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLModElement" title="The HTMLModElement interface provides special properties (beyond the regular methods and properties available through the HTMLElement interface they also have available to them by inheritance) for manipulating modification elements, that is <del> and <ins>." {
						- "HTMLModElement"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
