				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Otherwise"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The element "
					a href="#represents" id="the-img-element:represents-8" {
						- "represents"
					}
					- " the text given by the "
					code id="the-img-element:attr-img-alt-13" {
						a href="#attr-img-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- " attribute."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-img-element:attr-img-alt-14" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute does not represent advisory information.\n  User agents must not present the contents of the "
			code id="the-img-element:attr-img-alt-15" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  in the same way as content of the "
			code id="the-img-element:attr-title-2" {
				a href="#attr-title" {
					- "title"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents may always provide the user with the option to display any image, or to prevent any\n  image from being displayed. User agents may also apply heuristics to help the user make use of the\n  image when the user is unable to see it, e.g. due to a visual disability or because they are using\n  a text terminal with no graphics capabilities. Such heuristics could include, for instance,\n  optical character recognition (OCR) of text found within the image."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="warning" {
			- "While user agents are encouraged to repair cases of missing "
			code id="the-img-element:attr-img-alt-16" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attributes, authors must not rely on such behavior. "
			a href="#alt" {
				- "Requirements for providing text to act as an alternative for images"
			}
			- " are described\n  in detail below."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
