						}
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "The user agent will calculate the effective pixel density of each image from the specified\n     "
						code {
							- "w"
						}
						- " descriptors and the specified rendered size in the "
						code id="introduction-3:attr-img-sizes-2" {
							a href="#attr-img-sizes" {
								- "sizes"
							}
						}
						- " attribute. It can then choose any of the given resources\n     depending on the user's screen's pixel density, zoom level, and possibly other factors such as\n     the user's network conditions."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "If the user's screen is 320 "
						a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="introduction-3:'px'-2" data-x-internal="'px'" {
							- "CSS pixels"
						}
						- " wide, this is equivalent\n     to specifying "
						code {
							- "wolf-400.jpg 1.25x, wolf-800.jpg 2.5x, wolf-1600.jpg 5x"
						}
						- ".\n     On the other hand, if the user's screen is 1200 "
						a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="introduction-3:'px'-3" data-x-internal="'px'" {
							- "CSS pixels"
						}
						- " wide,\n     this is equivalent to specifying "
						code {
							- "wolf-400.jpg 0.33x, wolf-800.jpg 0.67x, wolf-1600.jpg 1.33x"
						}
						- ". By using the\n     "
						code {
							- "w"
						}
						- " descriptors and the "
						code id="introduction-3:attr-img-sizes-3" {
							a href="#attr-img-sizes" {
								- "sizes"
							}
						}
						- "\n     attribute, the user agent can choose the correct image source to download regardless of how\n     large the user's device is."
