			- " A phrase or paragraph with an alternative graphical representation: charts, diagrams, graphs, maps, illustrations"
			a href="#a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Sometimes something can be more clearly stated in graphical form, for example as a flowchart, a\n  diagram, a graph, or a simple map showing directions. In such cases, an image can be given using\n  the "
			code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:the-img-element" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element, but the lesser textual version must still be given, so that users\n  who are unable to view the image (e.g. because they have a very slow connection, or because they\n  are using a text-only browser, or because they are listening to the page being read out by a\n  hands-free automobile voice web browser, or simply because they are blind) are still able to\n  understand the message being conveyed."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The text must be given in the "
			code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, and must convey\n  the same message as the image specified in the "
			code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:attr-img-src" {
				a href="#attr-img-src" {
					- "src"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "It is important to realize that the alternative text is a "
			em {
				- "replacement"
			}
			- " for the image,\n  not a description of the image."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In the following example we have "
				a href="/images/parsing-model-overview.svg" {
					- "a flowchart"
				}
				- "\n   in image form, with text in the "
				code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:attr-img-alt-2" {
					a href="#attr-img-alt" {
						- "alt"
					}
				}
				- " attribute rephrasing the\n   flowchart in prose form:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "In the common case, the data handled by the tokenization stage\ncomes from the network, but it can also come from script."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"images/parsing-model-overview.svg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"The Network"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- s="" {
							- "passes data to the Input Stream Preprocessor, which passes it to the"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- s="" {
							- "Tokenizer, which passes it to the Tree Construction stage. From there,"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- s="" {
							- "data goes to both the DOM and to Script Execution. Script Execution is"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- s="" {
							- "linked to the DOM, and, using document.write(), passes data to the"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- s="" {
							- "Tokenizer.\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Here's another example, showing a good solution and a bad solution to the problem of including\n   an image in a description."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "First, here's the good solution. This sample shows how the alternative text should just be\n   what you would have put in the prose if the image had never existed."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- c="" {
						- "<!-- This is the correct way to do things. -->"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n You are standing in an open field west of a house.\n "
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"house.jpeg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"The house is white, with a boarded front door.\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- "\n There is a small mailbox here.\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Second, here's the bad solution. In this incorrect way of doing things, the alternative text\n   is simply a description of the image, instead of a textual replacement for the image. It's bad\n   because when the image isn't shown, the text doesn't flow as well as in the first example."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre class="bad" {
				code class="html" {
					c- c="" {
						- "<!-- "
					}
					em {
						c- c="" {
							- "This is the wrong way to do things."
						}
					}
					c- c="" {
						- " -->"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n You are standing in an open field west of a house.\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "img"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "src"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"house.jpeg\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "alt"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"A white house, with a boarded front door.\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n There is a small mailbox here.\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Text such as \"Photo of white house with boarded door\" would be equally bad alternative text\n   (though it could be suitable for the "
				code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:attr-title" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attribute or in the\n   "
				code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:the-figcaption-element" {
					a href="#the-figcaption-element" {
						- "figcaption"
					}
				}
				- " element of a "
				code id="a-phrase-or-paragraph-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-charts,-diagrams,-graphs,-maps,-illustrations:the-figure-element" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " with this image)."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.4"
			}
			- " A short phrase or label with an alternative graphical representation: icons, logos"
			a href="#a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A document can contain information in iconic form. The icon is intended to help users of visual\n  browsers to recognize features at a glance."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In some cases, the icon is supplemental to a text label conveying the same meaning. In those\n  cases, the "
			code id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be present but must be empty."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
