		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Many pages include logos, insignia, flags, or emblems, which stand for a particular entity such\n  as a company, organization, project, band, software package, country, or some such."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the logo is being used to represent the entity, e.g. as a page heading, the "
			code id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos:attr-img-alt-4" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must contain the name of the entity being represented by\n  the logo. The "
			code id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos:attr-img-alt-5" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must "
			em {
				- "not"
			}
			- " contain text like\n  the word \"logo\", as it is not the fact that it is a logo that is being conveyed, it's the entity\n  itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the logo is being used next to the name of the entity that it represents, then the logo is\n  supplemental, and its "
			code id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos:attr-img-alt-6" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must instead be empty."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the logo is merely used as decorative material (as branding, or, for example, as a side\n  image in an article that mentions the entity to which the logo belongs), then the entry below on\n  purely decorative images applies. If the logo is actually being discussed, then it is being used\n  as a phrase or paragraph (the description of the logo) with an alternative graphical\n  representation (the logo itself), and the first entry above applies."
		}
