			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This example shows how the alternative text should be written such that if the image isn't "
				i id="a-short-phrase-or-label-with-an-alternative-graphical-representation:-icons,-logos:img-available" {
					a href="#img-available" {
						- "available"
					}
				}
				- ", and the text is used instead, the text flows seamlessly into\n   the surrounding text, as if the image had never been there in the first place."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="text-that-has-been-rendered-to-a-graphic-for-typographical-effect" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.5"
			}
			- " Text that has been rendered to a graphic for typographical effect"
			a href="#text-that-has-been-rendered-to-a-graphic-for-typographical-effect" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Sometimes, an image just consists of text, and the purpose of the image is not to highlight the\n  actual typographic effects used to render the text, but just to convey the text itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In such cases, the "
			code id="text-that-has-been-rendered-to-a-graphic-for-typographical-effect:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be present but must\n  consist of the same text as written in the image itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider a graphic containing the text \"Earth Day\", but with the letters all decorated with\n   flowers and plants. If the text is merely being used as a heading, to spice up the page for\n   graphical users, then the correct alternative text is just the same text \"Earth Day\", and no\n   mention need be made of the decorations:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"earthdayheading.png\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"Earth Day\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "An illuminated manuscript might use graphics for some of its images. The alternative text in\n   such a situation is just the character that the image represents."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "img"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "src"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"initials/o.svg\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "alt"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"O\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "nce upon a time and a long long time ago, late at\nnight, when it was dark, over the hills, through the woods, across a great ocean, in a land far\naway, in a small house, on a hill, under a full moon..."
				}
			}
			- " \n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an image is used to represent a character that cannot otherwise be represented in Unicode,\n  for example gaiji, itaiji, or new characters such as novel currency symbols, the alternative text\n  should be a more conventional way of writing the same thing, e.g. using the phonetic hiragana or\n  katakana to give the character's pronunciation."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In this example from 1997, a new-fangled currency symbol that looks like a curly E with two\n   bars in the middle instead of one is represented using an image. The alternative text gives the\n   character's pronunciation."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Only "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "img"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "src"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"euro.png\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "alt"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"euro \""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "5.99!"
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An image should not be used if characters would serve an identical purpose. Only when the text\n  cannot be directly represented using text, e.g., because of decorations or because there is no\n  appropriate character (as in the case of gaiji), would an image be appropriate."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If an author is tempted to use an image because their default system font does not\n  support a given character, then web fonts are a better solution than images."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.6"
			}
			- " A graphical representation of some of the surrounding text"
			a href="#a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In many cases, the image is actually just supplementary, and its presence merely reinforces the\n  surrounding text. In these cases, the "
			code id="a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be\n  present but its value must be the empty string."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In general, an image falls into this category if removing the image doesn't make the page any\n  less useful, but including the image makes it a lot easier for users of visual browsers to\n  understand the concept."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "A flowchart that repeats the previous paragraph in graphical form:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "The Network passes data to the Input Stream Preprocessor, which\npasses it to the Tokenizer, which passes it to the Tree Construction\nstage. From there, data goes to both the DOM and to Script Execution.\nScript Execution is linked to the DOM, and, using document.write(),\npasses data to the Tokenizer."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "p"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- "><"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"images/parsing-model-overview.svg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- "></"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "p"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In these cases, it would be wrong to include alternative text that consists of just a caption.\n   If a caption is to be included, then either the "
				code id="a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text:attr-title" {
					a href="#attr-title" {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " attribute\n   can be used, or the "
				code id="a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text:the-figure-element" {
					a href="#the-figure-element" {
						- "figure"
					}
				}
				- " and "
				code id="a-graphical-representation-of-some-of-the-surrounding-text:the-figcaption-element" {
					a href="#the-figcaption-element" {
						- "figcaption"
					}
				}
				- " elements can be used. In the\n   latter case, the image would in fact be a phrase or paragraph with an alternative graphical\n   representation, and would thus require alternative text."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- c="" {
						- "<!-- Using the title=\"\" attribute -->"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "The Network passes data to the Input Stream Preprocessor, which\npasses it to the Tokenizer, which passes it to the Tree Construction\nstage. From there, data goes to both the DOM and to Script Execution.\nScript Execution is linked to the DOM, and, using document.write(),\npasses data to the Tokenizer."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"images/parsing-model-overview.svg\""
						}
						- " "
