		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="ancillary-images" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.7"
			}
			- " Ancillary images"
			a href="#ancillary-images" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Sometimes, an image is not critical to the content, but is nonetheless neither purely\n  decorative nor entirely redundant with the text. In these cases, the "
			code id="ancillary-images:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be present, and its value should either be the\n  empty string, or a textual representation of the information that the image conveys. If the image\n  has a caption giving the image's title, then the "
			code id="ancillary-images:attr-img-alt-2" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute's value must not be empty (as that would be quite confusing for non-visual readers)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider a news article about a political figure, in which the individual's face was shown in\n   an image. The image is not purely decorative, as it is relevant to the story. The image is not\n   entirely redundant with the story either, as it shows what the politician looks like. Whether\n   any alternative text need be provided is an authoring decision, decided by whether the image\n   influences the interpretation of the prose."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In this first variant, the image is shown without context, and no alternative text is\n   provided:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"president.jpeg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- " Ahead of today's referendum,\nthe President wrote an open letter to all registered voters. In it, she admitted that the country was\ndivided."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the picture is just a face, there might be no value in describing it. It's of no interest\n   to the reader whether the individual has red hair or blond hair, whether the individual has white\n   skin or black skin, whether the individual has one eye or two eyes."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, if the picture is more dynamic, for instance showing the politician as angry, or\n   particularly happy, or devastated, some alternative text would be useful in setting the tone of\n   the article, a tone that might otherwise be missed:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"president.jpeg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"The President is sad.\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- "\nAhead of today's referendum, the President wrote an open letter to all\nregistered voters. In it, she admitted that the country was divided.\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"president.jpeg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"The President is happy!\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- "\nAhead of today's referendum, the President wrote an open letter to all\nregistered voters. In it, she admitted that the country was divided.\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Whether the individual was \"sad\" or \"happy\" makes a difference to how the rest of the\n   paragraph is to be interpreted: is she likely saying that she is unhappy with the country\n   being divided, or is she saying that the prospect of a divided country is good for her\n   political career? The interpretation varies based on the image."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the image has a caption, then including alternative text avoids leaving the non-visual user\n   confused as to what the caption refers to."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Ahead of today's referendum, the President wrote an open letter to\nall registered voters. In it, she admitted that the country was divided."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "figure"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "\n "
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"president.jpeg\""
						}
						- "\n      "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"A high forehead, cheerful disposition, and dark hair round out the President's face.\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "\n "
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "figcaption"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- " The President of Ruritania. Photo © 2014 PolitiPhoto. "
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "figcaption"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "figure"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="a-purely-decorative-image-that-doesn't-add-any-information" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.8"
			}
			- " A purely decorative image that doesn't add any information"
			a href="#a-purely-decorative-image-that-doesn't-add-any-information" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If an image is decorative but isn't especially page-specific — for example an image that\n  forms part of a site-wide design scheme — the image should be specified in the site's CSS,\n  not in the markup of the document."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "However, a decorative image that isn't discussed by the surrounding text but still has some\n  relevance can be included in a page using the "
			code id="a-purely-decorative-image-that-doesn't-add-any-information:the-img-element" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element. Such images are\n  decorative, but still form part of the content. In these cases, the "
			code id="a-purely-decorative-image-that-doesn't-add-any-information:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be present but its value must be the empty\n  string."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Examples where the image is purely decorative despite being relevant would include things like\n   a photo of the Black Rock City landscape in a blog post about an event at Burning Man, or an\n   image of a painting inspired by a poem, on a page reciting that poem. The following snippet shows\n   an example of the latter case (only the first verse is included in this snippet):"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "The Lady of Shalott"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					strong {
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "p"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- "><"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "img"
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "src"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"shalott.jpeg\""
						}
						- " "
						c- e="" {
							- "alt"
						}
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						c- s="" {
							- "\"\""
						}
						c- p="" {
							- "></"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "p"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "On either side the river lie"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nLong fields of barley and of rye,"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nThat clothe the wold and meet the sky;"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nAnd through the field the road run by"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nTo many-tower'd Camelot;"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nAnd up and down the people go,"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nGazing where the lilies blow"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nRound an island there below,"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "br"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\nThe island of Shalott."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="a-group-of-images-that-form-a-single-larger-picture-with-no-links" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.9"
			}
			- " A group of images that form a single larger picture with no links"
			a href="#a-group-of-images-that-form-a-single-larger-picture-with-no-links" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a picture has been sliced into smaller image files that are then displayed together to\n  form the complete picture again, one of the images must have its "
			code id="a-group-of-images-that-form-a-single-larger-picture-with-no-links:attr-img-alt" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute set as per the relevant rules that would be appropriate\n  for the picture as a whole, and then all the remaining images must have their "
			code id="a-group-of-images-that-form-a-single-larger-picture-with-no-links:attr-img-alt-2" {
				a href="#attr-img-alt" {
					- "alt"
				}
			}
			- " attribute set to the empty string."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In the following example, a picture representing a company logo for "
				span {
					- "XYZ\n   Corp"
				}
				- " has been split into two pieces, the first containing the letters \"XYZ\" and the second\n   with the word \"Corp\". The alternative text (\"XYZ Corp\") is all in the first image."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
