		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="a-key-part-of-the-content" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.4.4.11"
			}
			- " A key part of the content"
			a href="#a-key-part-of-the-content" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In some cases, the image is a critical part of the content. This could be the case, for\n  instance, on a page that is part of a photo gallery. The image is the whole "
			em {
				- "point"
			}
			- " of the\n  page containing it."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "How to provide alternative text for an image that is a key part of the content depends on the\n  image's provenance."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "The general case"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When it is possible for detailed alternative text to be provided, for example if the image is\n    part of a series of screenshots in a magazine review, or part of a comic strip, or is a\n    photograph in a blog entry about that photograph, text that can serve as a substitute for the\n    image must be given as the contents of the "
					code id="a-key-part-of-the-content:attr-img-alt" {
						a href="#attr-img-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- " attribute."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "A screenshot in a gallery of screenshots for a new OS, with some alternative text:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							strong {
								c- p="" {
									- "<"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "img"
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "src"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"KDE%20Light%20desktop.png\""
								}
								- "\n      "
								c- e="" {
									- "alt"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"The desktop is blue, with icons along the left hand side in"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           two columns, reading System, Home, K-Mail, etc. A window is"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           open showing that menus wrap to a second line if they"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           cannot fit in the window. The window has a list of icons"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           along the top, with an address bar below it, a list of"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           icons for tabs along the left edge, a status bar on the"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           bottom, and two panes in the middle. The desktop has a bar"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           at the bottom of the screen with a few buttons, a pager, a"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "           list of open applications, and a clock.\""
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "Screenshot of a KDE desktop."
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n"
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "A graph in a financial report:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							strong {
								c- p="" {
									- "<"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "img"
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "src"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"sales.gif\""
								}
								- "\n     "
								c- e="" {
									- "title"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"Sales graph\""
								}
								- "\n     "
								c- e="" {
									- "alt"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"From 1998 to 2005, sales increased by the following percentages"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "     with each year: 624%, 75%, 138%, 40%, 35%, 9%, 21%\""
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Note that \"sales graph\" would be inadequate alternative text for a sales graph. Text that\n     would be a good "
						em {
							- "caption"
						}
						- " is not generally suitable as replacement text."
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Images that defy a complete description"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "In certain cases, the nature of the image might be such that providing thorough alternative\n    text is impractical. For example, the image could be indistinct, or could be a complex fractal,\n    or could be a detailed topographical map."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "In these cases, the "
					code id="a-key-part-of-the-content:attr-img-alt-2" {
						a href="#attr-img-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- " attribute must contain some\n    suitable alternative text, but it may be somewhat brief."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Sometimes there simply is no text that can do justice to an image. For example, there is\n     little that can be said to usefully describe a Rorschach inkblot test. However, a description,\n     even if brief, is still better than nothing:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							strong {
								c- p="" {
									- "<"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "img"
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "src"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"/commons/a/a7/Rorschach1.jpg\""
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "alt"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"A shape with left-right"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- " symmetry with indistinct edges, with a small gap in the center, two"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- " larger gaps offset slightly from the center, with two similar gaps"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- " under them. The outline is wider in the top half than the bottom"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- " half, with the sides extending upwards higher than the center, and"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- " the center extending below the sides.\""
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "A black outline of the first of the ten cards\n in the Rorschach inkblot test."
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n"
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Note that the following would be a very bad use of alternative text:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre class="bad" {
						code class="html" {
							c- c="" {
								- "<!-- This example is wrong. Do not copy it. -->"
							}
							- "\n"
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "img"
							}
							- " "
							c- e="" {
								- "src"
							}
							c- o="" {
								- "="
							}
							c- s="" {
								- "\"/commons/a/a7/Rorschach1.jpg\""
							}
							- " "
							c- e="" {
								- "alt"
							}
							c- o="" {
								- "="
							}
							c- s="" {
								- "\"A black outline"
							}
							- "\n"
							c- s="" {
								- " of the first of the ten cards in the Rorschach inkblot test.\""
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "A black outline of the first of the ten cards\n in the Rorschach inkblot test."
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figcaption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n"
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "figure"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Including the caption in the alternative text like this isn't useful because it effectively\n     duplicates the caption for users who don't have images, taunting them twice yet not helping\n     them any more than if they had only read or heard the caption once."
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Another example of an image that defies full description is a fractal, which, by definition,\n     is infinite in detail."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "The following example shows one possible way of providing alternative text for the full view\n     of an image of the Mandelbrot set."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							strong {
								c- p="" {
									- "<"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "img"
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "src"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"ms1.jpeg\""
								}
								- " "
								c- e="" {
									- "alt"
								}
								c- o="" {
									- "="
								}
								c- s="" {
									- "\"The Mandelbrot set appears as a cardioid with"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "its cusp on the real axis in the positive direction, with a smaller"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "bulb aligned along the same center line, touching it in the negative"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "direction, and with these two shapes being surrounded by smaller bulbs"
								}
								- "\n"
								c- s="" {
									- "of various sizes.\""
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n    "
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="example" {
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Similarly, a photograph of a person's face, for example in a biography, can be considered\n     quite relevant and key to the content, but it can be hard to fully substitute text for:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "section"
							}
							- " "
							c- e="" {
								- "class"
							}
							c- o="" {
								- "="
							}
							c- s="" {
								- "\"bio\""
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "h1"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "A Biography of Isaac Asimov"
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
