		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In "
			a href="#syntax" id="the-iframe-element:syntax-2" {
				- "the HTML syntax"
			}
			- ", authors need only remember to use U+0022\n  QUOTATION MARK characters (\") to wrap the attribute contents and then to escape all U+0026\n  AMPERSAND (&) and U+0022 QUOTATION MARK (\") characters, and to specify the "
			code id="the-iframe-element:attr-iframe-sandbox-3" {
				a href="#attr-iframe-sandbox" {
					- "sandbox"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, to ensure safe embedding of content. (And\n  remember to escape ampersands before quotation marks, to ensure quotation marks become &quot;\n  and not &amp;quot;.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In XML the U+003C LESS-THAN SIGN character (<) needs to be escaped as well. In\n  order to prevent "
			a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#AVNormalize" {
				- "attribute-value\n  normalization"
			}
			- ", some of XML's whitespace characters — specifically U+0009 CHARACTER\n  TABULATION (tab), U+000A LINE FEED (LF), and U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) — also need to be\n  escaped. "
			a href="#refsXML" {
