		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element is used for playing videos or movies, and audio files with\n  captions."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Content may be provided inside the "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-2" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element. User agents\n  should not show this content to the user; it is intended for older web browsers which do\n  not support "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-3" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- ", so that text can be shown to the users of these older browsers\n  informing them of how to access the video contents."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In particular, this content is not intended to address accessibility concerns. To\n  make video content accessible to the partially sighted, the blind, the hard-of-hearing, the deaf,\n  and those with other physical or cognitive disabilities, a variety of features are available.\n  Captions can be provided, either embedded in the video stream or as external files using the\n  "
			code id="the-video-element:the-track-element-3" {
				a href="#the-track-element" {
					- "track"
				}
			}
			- " element. Sign-language tracks can be embedded in the video stream. Audio\n  descriptions can be embedded in the video stream or in text form using a "
			a id="the-video-element:webvtt-file" href="https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#webvtt-file" data-x-internal="webvtt-file" {
				- "WebVTT file"
			}
			- "\n  referenced using the "
			code id="the-video-element:the-track-element-4" {
				a href="#the-track-element" {
					- "track"
				}
			}
			- " element and synthesized into speech by the user agent.\n  WebVTT can also be used to provide chapter titles. For users who would rather not use a media\n  element at all, transcripts or other textual alternatives can be provided by simply linking to\n  them in the prose near the "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-4" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element. "
			a href="#refsWEBVTT" {
				- "[WEBVTT]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-5" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element is a "
			a href="#media-element" id="the-video-element:media-element-3" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#media-data" id="the-video-element:media-data" {
				- "media data"
			}
			- " is\n  ostensibly video data, possibly with associated audio data."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-src-4" {
				a href="#attr-media-src" {
					- "src"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-crossorigin-2" {
				a href="#attr-media-crossorigin" {
					- "crossorigin"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-preload-2" {
				a href="#attr-media-preload" {
					- "preload"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-autoplay-2" {
				a href="#attr-media-autoplay" {
					- "autoplay"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-loop-2" {
				a href="#attr-media-loop" {
					- "loop"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-muted-2" {
				a href="#attr-media-muted" {
					- "muted"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-media-controls-3" {
				a href="#attr-media-controls" {
					- "controls"
				}
			}
			- " attributes are "
			a href="#media-element-attributes" id="the-video-element:media-element-attributes" {
				- "the attributes common to all media elements"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="video" id="attr-video-poster" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "poster"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute gives the "
			a id="the-video-element:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- " of an image file that the user agent can show while no video\n  data is available.  The attribute, if present, must contain a "
			a href="#valid-non-empty-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" id="the-video-element:valid-non-empty-url-potentially-surrounded-by-spaces" {
				- "valid non-empty URL\n  potentially surrounded by spaces"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the specified resource is to be used, then, when the element is created or when the "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-video-poster-2" {
				a href="#attr-video-poster" {
					- "poster"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is set, changed, or removed, the user agent must\n  run the following steps to determine the element's "
			dfn id="poster-frame" {
				- "poster frame"
			}
			- " (regardless of the\n  value of the element's "
			a href="#show-poster-flag" id="the-video-element:show-poster-flag" {
				- "show poster flag"
			}
			- "):"
		}
		- " \n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If there is an existing instance of this algorithm running for this "
					code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-6" {
						a href="#the-video-element" {
							- "video"
						}
					}
					- "\n   element, abort that instance of this algorithm without changing the "
					a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame" {
						- "poster\n   frame"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id="the-video-element:attr-video-poster-3" {
						a href="#attr-video-poster" {
							- "poster"
						}
					}
					- " attribute's value is the empty string\n   or if the attribute is absent, then there is no "
					a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-2" {
						- "poster frame"
					}
					- "; return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "url"
					}
					- " be the result of "
					a href="#encoding-parsing-a-url" id="the-video-element:encoding-parsing-a-url" {
						- "encoding-parsing a URL"
					}
					- " given the "
					code id="the-video-element:attr-video-poster-4" {
						a href="#attr-video-poster" {
							- "poster"
						}
					}
					- " attribute's value, relative to the element's "
					a id="the-video-element:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
						- "node\n   document"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "url"
					}
					- " is failure, then return. "
					span class="note" {
						- "There is no "
						a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-3" {
							- "poster\n   frame"
						}
						- "."
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "request"
					}
					- " be a new "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request" id="the-video-element:concept-request" data-x-internal="concept-request" {
						- "request"
					}
					- " whose "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-url" id="the-video-element:concept-request-url" data-x-internal="concept-request-url" {
						- "URL"
					}
					- " is "
					var {
						- "url"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-client" id="the-video-element:concept-request-client" data-x-internal="concept-request-client" {
						- "client"
					}
					- " is the element's "
					a id="the-video-element:node-document-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
						- "node document"
					}
					- "'s\n   "
					a href="#relevant-settings-object" id="the-video-element:relevant-settings-object" {
						- "relevant settings object"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-destination" id="the-video-element:concept-request-destination" data-x-internal="concept-request-destination" {
						- "destination"
					}
					- " is \""
					code {
						- "image"
					}
					- "\", "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#request-initiator-type" id="the-video-element:concept-request-initiator-type" data-x-internal="concept-request-initiator-type" {
						- "initiator type"
					}
					- " is \""
					code {
						- "video"
					}
					- "\",\n   "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-credentials-mode" id="the-video-element:concept-request-credentials-mode" data-x-internal="concept-request-credentials-mode" {
						- "credentials mode"
					}
					- " is \""
					code {
						- "include"
					}
					- "\", and whose "
					a id="the-video-element:use-url-credentials-flag" href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-use-url-credentials-flag" data-x-internal="use-url-credentials-flag" {
						- "use-URL-credentials flag"
					}
					- " is set.\n\n   "
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id="the-video-element:concept-fetch" data-x-internal="concept-fetch" {
						- "Fetch"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "request"
					}
					- ". This must\n   "
					a href="#delay-the-load-event" id="the-video-element:delay-the-load-event" {
						- "delay the load event"
					}
					- " of the element's "
					a id="the-video-element:node-document-3" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
						- "node document"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If an image is thus obtained, the "
					a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-4" {
						- "poster frame"
					}
					- " is that image. Otherwise,\n   there is no "
					a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-5" {
						- "poster frame"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The image given by the "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-video-poster-5" {
				a href="#attr-video-poster" {
					- "poster"
				}
			}
			- " attribute,\n  the "
			i id="the-video-element:poster-frame-6" {
				a href="#poster-frame" {
					- "poster frame"
				}
			}
			- ", is intended to be a representative frame of the\n  video (typically one of the first non-blank frames) that gives the user an idea of what the video\n  is like."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="video" id="attr-video-playsinline" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "playsinline"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="the-video-element:boolean-attribute" {
				- "boolean\n  attribute"
			}
			- ". If present, it serves as a hint to the user agent that the video ought to be\n  displayed \"inline\" in the document by default, constrained to the element's playback area, instead\n  of being displayed fullscreen or in an independent resizable window."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The absence of the "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-video-playsinline-2" {
				a href="#attr-video-playsinline" {
					- "playsinline"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute does not imply that the video will display fullscreen by default. Indeed, most user\n  agents have chosen to play all videos inline by default, and in such user agents the "
			code id="the-video-element:attr-video-playsinline-3" {
				a href="#attr-video-playsinline" {
					- "playsinline"
				}
			}
			- " attribute has no effect."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-7" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element represents what is given for the first matching condition in the\n  list below:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="switch" {
			dt {
				- "When no video data is available (the element's "
				code id="the-video-element:dom-media-readystate" {
					a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
						- "readyState"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is either "
				code id="the-video-element:dom-media-have_nothing" {
					a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" {
						- "HAVE_NOTHING"
					}
				}
				- ", or "
				code id="the-video-element:dom-media-have_metadata" {
					a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
						- "HAVE_METADATA"
					}
				}
				- " but no video data has yet been obtained at\n   all, or the element's "
				code id="the-video-element:dom-media-readystate-2" {
					a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
						- "readyState"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is any\n   subsequent value but the "
				a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-5" {
					- "media resource"
				}
				- " does not have a video channel)"
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-8" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element "
				a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " its "
				a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-7" {
					- "poster frame"
				}
				- ", if any,\n   or else "
				a id="the-video-element:transparent-black" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" data-x-internal="transparent-black" {
					- "transparent black"
				}
				- " with no "
				a id="the-video-element:natural-dimensions" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions" data-x-internal="natural-dimensions" {
					- "natural dimensions"
				}
				- "."
			}
			dt {
				- "When the "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-9" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element is "
				a href="#dom-media-paused" id="the-video-element:dom-media-paused" {
					- "paused"
				}
				- ", the "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position" {
					- "current playback position"
				}
				- " is the first frame of video,\n   and the element's "
				a href="#show-poster-flag" id="the-video-element:show-poster-flag-2" {
					- "show poster flag"
				}
				- " is set"
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-10" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element "
				a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-2" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " its "
				a href="#poster-frame" id="the-video-element:poster-frame-8" {
					- "poster frame"
				}
				- ", if any,\n   or else the first frame of the video."
			}
			dt {
				- "When the "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-11" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element is "
				a href="#dom-media-paused" id="the-video-element:dom-media-paused-2" {
					- "paused"
				}
				- ", and the\n   frame of video corresponding to the "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-2" {
					- "current playback\n   position"
				}
				- " is not available (e.g. because the video is seeking or buffering)"
			}
			dt {
				- "When the "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-12" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element is neither "
				a href="#potentially-playing" id="the-video-element:potentially-playing" {
					- "potentially playing"
				}
				- " nor "
				a href="#dom-media-paused" id="the-video-element:dom-media-paused-3" {
					- "paused"
				}
				- " (e.g. when seeking or stalled)"
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-13" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element "
				a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-3" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " the last frame of the video to have\n   been rendered."
			}
			dt {
				- "When the "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-14" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element is "
				a href="#dom-media-paused" id="the-video-element:dom-media-paused-4" {
					- "paused"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-15" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element "
				a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-4" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " the frame of video corresponding to\n   the "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-3" {
					- "current playback position"
				}
				- "."
			}
			dt {
				- "Otherwise (the "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-16" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element has a video channel and is "
				a href="#potentially-playing" id="the-video-element:potentially-playing-2" {
					- "potentially\n   playing"
				}
				- ")"
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-17" {
					a href="#the-video-element" {
						- "video"
					}
				}
				- " element "
				a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-5" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " the frame of video at the continuously\n   increasing "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-4" {
					- "\"current\" position"
				}
				- ". When the\n   "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-5" {
					- "current playback position"
				}
				- " changes such that the last frame rendered is no longer the\n   frame corresponding to the "
				a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-6" {
					- "current playback position"
				}
				- " in the video, the new frame\n   must be rendered."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Frames of video must be obtained from the video track that was "
			a href="#dom-videotrack-selected" id="the-video-element:dom-videotrack-selected" {
				- "selected"
			}
			- " when the "
			a href="#event-loop" id="the-video-element:event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " last reached\n  "
			a href="#step1" {
				- "step 1"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Which frame in a video stream corresponds to a particular playback position is\n  defined by the video stream's format."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-18" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element also "
			a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-6" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " any "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="the-video-element:text-track-cue" {
				- "text track cues"
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="the-video-element:text-track-cue-active-flag" {
				- "text track cue active flag"
			}
			- " is set and whose\n  "
			a href="#text-track" id="the-video-element:text-track" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " is in the "
			a href="#text-track-showing" id="the-video-element:text-track-showing" {
				- "showing"
			}
			- " mode, and any\n  audio from the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-6" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", at the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-7" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Any audio associated with the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-7" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " must, if played, be played\n  synchronized with the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-8" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- ", at the element's "
			a href="#effective-media-volume" id="the-video-element:effective-media-volume" {
				- "effective\n  media volume"
			}
			- ". The user agent must play the audio from audio tracks that were "
			a href="#dom-audiotrack-enabled" id="the-video-element:dom-audiotrack-enabled" {
				- "enabled"
			}
			- " when the "
			a href="#event-loop" id="the-video-element:event-loop-2" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " last reached step\n  1."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In addition to the above, the user agent may provide messages to the user (such as \"buffering\",\n  \"no video loaded\", \"error\", or more detailed information) by overlaying text or icons on the video\n  or other areas of the element's playback area, or in another appropriate manner."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents that cannot render the video may instead make the element "
			a href="#represents" id="the-video-element:represents-7" {
				- "represent"
			}
			- " a link to an external video playback utility or to the video\n  data itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="the-video-element:the-video-element-19" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-8" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " has a video channel, the\n  element provides a "
			a id="the-video-element:paint-source" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-4/#paint-source" data-x-internal="paint-source" {
				- "paint source"
			}
			- " whose width is the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-9" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "'s\n  "
			a href="#concept-video-intrinsic-width" id="the-video-element:concept-video-intrinsic-width" {
				- "natural width"
			}
			- ", whose height is the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="the-video-element:media-resource-10" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-video-intrinsic-height" id="the-video-element:concept-video-intrinsic-height" {
				- "natural\n  height"
			}
			- ", and whose appearance is the frame of video corresponding to the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="the-video-element:current-playback-position-9" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- ", if that is available, or else\n  (e.g. when the video is seeking or buffering) its previous appearance, if any, or else (e.g.\n  because the video is still loading the first frame) blackness."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
