			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns the "
					a href="#official-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:official-playback-position" {
						- "official playback position"
					}
					- ", in seconds."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Can be set, to seek to the given time."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-3" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="media-timeline" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " that maps times (in seconds) to\n  positions in the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-4" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ". The origin of a timeline is its earliest defined\n  position. The duration of a timeline is its last defined position."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			dfn id="defineTimeline" {
				- "Establishing the media\n  timeline"
			}
			- ": if the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-5" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " somehow specifies an explicit timeline whose\n  origin is not negative (i.e. gives each frame a specific time offset and gives the first frame a\n  zero or positive offset), then the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " should be that timeline. (Whether\n  the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-6" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " can specify a timeline or not depends on the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-7" {
				- "media resource's"
			}
			- " format.) If the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-8" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " specifies an\n  explicit start time "
			em {
				- "and date"
			}
			- ", then that time and date should be considered the zero point\n  in the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-2" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- "; the "
			a href="#timeline-offset" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:timeline-offset" {
				- "timeline offset"
			}
			- " will be the time and date,\n  exposed using the "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-getstartdate" {
				a href="#dom-media-getstartdate" {
					- "getStartDate()"
				}
			}
			- " method."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-9" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " has a discontinuous timeline, the user agent must extend the\n  timeline used at the start of the resource across the entire resource, so that the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-3" {
				- "media\n  timeline"
			}
			- " of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-10" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " increases linearly starting from the\n  "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- " (as defined below), even if the underlying "
			a href="#media-data" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-data" {
				- "media\n  data"
			}
			- " has out-of-order or even overlapping time codes."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, if two clips have been concatenated into one video file, but the\n  video format exposes the original times for the two clips, the video data might expose a timeline\n  that goes, say, 00:15..00:29 and then 00:05..00:38. However, the user agent would not expose those\n  times; it would instead expose the times as 00:15..00:29 and 00:29..01:02, as a single video."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "\n  "
			a id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:tracking-vector" title="There is a tracking vector here." href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tracking-vector" class="tracking-vector" data-x-internal="tracking-vector" {
				img width="46" alt="(This is a tracking vector.)" crossorigin="" src="https://resources.whatwg.org/tracking-vector.svg" height="64"
			}
			- "\n  In the rare case of a "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-11" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " that does not have an explicit timeline, the\n  zero time on the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-4" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " should correspond to the first frame of the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-12" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ". In the even rarer case of a "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-13" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " with no\n  explicit timings of any kind, not even frame durations, the user agent must itself determine the\n  time for each frame in an "
			a id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
				- "implementation-defined"
			}
			- " manner."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "An example of a file format with no explicit timeline but with explicit frame\n  durations is the Animated GIF format. An example of a file format with no explicit timings at all\n  is the JPEG-push format ("
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
				a href="#multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
					- "multipart/x-mixed-replace"
				}
			}
			- " with JPEG frames, often\n  used as the format for MJPEG streams)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If, in the case of a resource with no timing information, the user agent will nonetheless be\n  able to seek to an earlier point than the first frame originally provided by the server, then the\n  zero time should correspond to the earliest seekable time of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-14" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ";\n  otherwise, it should correspond to the first frame received from the server (the point in the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-15" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " at which the user agent began receiving the stream)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "At the time of writing, there is no known format that lacks explicit frame time\n  offsets yet still supports seeking to a frame before the first frame sent by the server."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider a stream from a TV broadcaster, which begins streaming on a sunny Friday afternoon in\n   October, and always sends connecting user agents the media data on the same media timeline, with\n   its zero time set to the start of this stream. Months later, user agents connecting to this\n   stream will find that the first frame they receive has a time with millions of seconds. The "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-getstartdate-2" {
					a href="#dom-media-getstartdate" {
						- "getStartDate()"
					}
				}
				- " method would always return the date that the\n   broadcast started; this would allow controllers to display real times in their scrubber (e.g.\n   \"2:30pm\") rather than a time relative to when the broadcast began (\"8 months, 4 hours, 12\n   minutes, and 23 seconds\")."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider a stream that carries a video with several concatenated fragments, broadcast by a\n   server that does not allow user agents to request specific times but instead just streams the\n   video data in a predetermined order, with the first frame delivered always being identified as\n   the frame with time zero. If a user agent connects to this stream and receives fragments defined\n   as covering timestamps 2010-03-20 23:15:00 UTC to 2010-03-21 00:05:00 UTC and 2010-02-12 14:25:00\n   UTC to 2010-02-12 14:35:00 UTC, it would expose this with a "
				a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-5" {
					- "media timeline"
				}
				- " starting\n   at 0s and extending to 3,600s (one hour). Assuming the streaming server disconnected at the end\n   of the second clip, the "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-duration" {
					a href="#dom-media-duration" {
						- "duration"
					}
				}
				- " attribute would then\n   return 3,600. The "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-getstartdate-3" {
					a href="#dom-media-getstartdate" {
						- "getStartDate()"
					}
				}
				- " method would return a\n   "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:date" {
					a data-x-internal="date" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-date-objects" {
						- "Date"
					}
				}
				- " object with a time corresponding to 2010-03-20 23:15:00 UTC. However, if a\n   different user agent connected five minutes later, "
				em {
					- "it"
				}
				- " would (presumably) receive\n   fragments covering timestamps 2010-03-20 23:20:00 UTC to 2010-03-21 00:05:00 UTC and 2010-02-12\n   14:25:00 UTC to 2010-02-12 14:35:00 UTC, and would expose this with a "
				a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-6" {
					- "media timeline"
				}
				- "\n   starting at 0s and extending to 3,300s (fifty five minutes). In this case, the "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-getstartdate-4" {
					a href="#dom-media-getstartdate" {
						- "getStartDate()"
					}
				}
				- " method would return a "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:date-2" {
					a data-x-internal="date" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-date-objects" {
						- "Date"
					}
				}
				- " object\n   with a time corresponding to 2010-03-20 23:20:00 UTC."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In both of these examples, the "
				code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-seekable" {
					a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
						- "seekable"
					}
				}
				- " attribute\n   would give the ranges that the controller would want to actually display in its UI; typically, if\n   the servers don't support seeking to arbitrary times, this would be the range of time from the\n   moment the user agent connected to the stream up to the latest frame that the user agent has\n   obtained; however, if the user agent starts discarding earlier information, the actual range\n   might be shorter."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In any case, the user agent must ensure that the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-2" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- " (as\n  defined below) using the established "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-7" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- ", is greater than or equal to\n  zero."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-8" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " also has an associated clock. Which clock is used is user-agent\n  defined, and may be "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-16" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "-dependent, but it should approximate the user's\n  wall clock."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element" {
				- "Media elements"
			}
			- " have a "
			dfn id="current-playback-position" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- ",\n  which must initially (i.e. in the absence of "
			a href="#media-data" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-data-2" {
				- "media data"
			}
			- ") be zero seconds. The\n  "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " is a time on the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-9" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-2" {
				- "Media elements"
			}
			- " also have an "
			dfn id="official-playback-position" {
				- "official playback\n  position"
			}
			- ", which must initially be set to zero seconds. The "
			a href="#official-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:official-playback-position-2" {
				- "official playback\n  position"
			}
			- " is an approximation of the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-2" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " that is kept\n  stable while scripts are running."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-3" {
				- "Media elements"
			}
			- " also have a "
			dfn id="default-playback-start-position" {
				- "default playback start\n  position"
			}
			- ", which must initially be set to zero seconds. This time is used to allow the\n  element to be seeked even before the media is loaded."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-4" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="show-poster-flag" {
				- "show poster flag"
			}
			- ". When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-5" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- " is created, this flag must be set to true. This flag is used to control when the\n  user agent is to show a poster frame for a "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:the-video-element" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element instead of showing the video\n  contents."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-currenttime" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "currentTime"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must, on getting, return the\n  "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-6" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#default-playback-start-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:default-playback-start-position" {
				- "default playback start position"
			}
			- ", unless that is zero, in\n  which case it must return the element's "
			a href="#official-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:official-playback-position-3" {
				- "official playback position"
			}
			- ". The returned\n  value must be expressed in seconds. On setting, if the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-7" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-readystate" {
				a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
					- "readyState"
				}
			}
			- " is "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-have_nothing" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" {
					- "HAVE_NOTHING"
				}
			}
			- ", then it must set the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-8" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#default-playback-start-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:default-playback-start-position-2" {
				- "default playback start position"
			}
			- " to the new value; otherwise, it must\n  set the "
			a href="#official-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:official-playback-position-4" {
				- "official playback position"
			}
			- " to the new value and then "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-seek" {
				- "seek"
			}
			- " to the new value. The new value must be interpreted as being\n  in seconds."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-17" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " is a streaming resource, then the user agent might be unable\n  to obtain certain parts of the resource after it has expired from its buffer. Similarly, some\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-18" {
				- "media resources"
			}
			- " might have a "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-10" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " that\n  doesn't start at zero. The "
			dfn id="earliest-possible-position" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- " is the earliest position in the\n  stream or resource that the user agent can ever obtain again. It is also a time on the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-11" {
				- "media\n  timeline"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-3" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- " is not explicitly exposed in the API;\n  it corresponds to the start time of the first range in the "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-seekable-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
					- "seekable"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:timeranges" {
				a href="#timeranges" {
					- "TimeRanges"
				}
			}
			- " object, if any, or\n  the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-3" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " otherwise."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-4" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- " changes, then: if the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-4" {
				- "current playback\n  position"
			}
			- " is before the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-5" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- ", the user agent must "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-seek-2" {
				- "seek"
			}
			- " to the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-6" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- "; otherwise, if\n  the user agent has not fired a "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-timeupdate" {
				a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
					- "timeupdate"
				}
			}
			- " event at\n  the element in the past 15 to 250ms and is not still running event handlers for such an event,\n  then the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task" {
				- "queue a media element task"
			}
			- " given the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-9" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- " to "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-timeupdate-2" {
				a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
					- "timeupdate"
				}
			}
			- " at the element."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Because of the above requirement and the requirement in the "
			a href="#concept-media-load-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:concept-media-load-resource" {
				- "resource fetch algorithm"
			}
			- " that kicks in "
			a href="#getting-media-metadata" {
				- "when the metadata of the clip becomes known"
			}
			- ", the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-5" {
				- "current\n  playback position"
			}
			- " can never be less than the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-7" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If at any time the user agent learns that an audio or video track has ended and all "
			a href="#media-data" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-data-3" {
				- "media\n  data"
			}
			- " relating to that track corresponds to parts of the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-12" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- " that\n  are "
			em {
				- "before"
			}
			- " the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:earliest-possible-position-8" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- ", the user agent may "
			a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-2" {
				- "queue a\n  media element task"
			}
			- " given the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-10" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " to run these steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Remove the track from the "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-audiotracks" {
						a href="#dom-media-audiotracks" {
							- "audioTracks"
						}
					}
					- "\n   attribute's "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:audiotracklist" {
						a href="#audiotracklist" {
							- "AudioTrackList"
						}
					}
					- " object or the "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-videotracks" {
						a href="#dom-media-videotracks" {
							- "videoTracks"
						}
					}
					- " attribute's "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:videotracklist" {
						a href="#videotracklist" {
							- "VideoTrackList"
						}
					}
					- " object\n   as appropriate."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-2" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "Fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-removetrack" {
						a href="#event-media-removetrack" {
							- "removetrack"
						}
					}
					- " at the "
					a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-11" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "'s\n   aforementioned "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:audiotracklist-2" {
						a href="#audiotracklist" {
							- "AudioTrackList"
						}
					}
					- " or "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:videotracklist-2" {
						a href="#videotracklist" {
							- "VideoTrackList"
						}
					}
					- " object, using\n   "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:trackevent" {
						a href="#trackevent" {
							- "TrackEvent"
						}
					}
					- ", with the "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-trackevent-track" {
						a href="#dom-trackevent-track" {
							- "track"
						}
					}
					- " attribute\n   initialized to the "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:audiotrack" {
						a href="#audiotrack" {
							- "AudioTrack"
						}
					}
					- " or "
					code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:videotrack" {
						a href="#videotrack" {
							- "VideoTrack"
						}
					}
					- " object representing the\n   track."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-duration" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "duration"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must return the time of the end of the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-19" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", in seconds, on the "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-13" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- ". If no "
			a href="#media-data" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-data-4" {
				- "media\n  data"
			}
			- " is available, then the attributes must return the Not-a-Number (NaN) value. If the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-20" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " is not known to be bounded (e.g. streaming radio, or a live event with\n  no announced end time), then the attribute must return the positive Infinity value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The user agent must determine the duration of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-21" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " before playing\n  any part of the "
			a href="#media-data" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-data-5" {
				- "media data"
			}
			- " and before setting "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-readystate-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
					- "readyState"
				}
			}
			- " to a value greater than or equal to "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-have_metadata" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
					- "HAVE_METADATA"
				}
			}
			- ", even if doing so requires fetching multiple\n  parts of the resource."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="durationChange" {
			- "When the length of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-22" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " changes to a known value\n  (e.g. from being unknown to known, or from a previously established length to a new length) the\n  user agent must "
			a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-3" {
				- "queue a media element task"
			}
			- " given the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-12" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " to\n  "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-3" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-durationchange" {
				a href="#event-media-durationchange" {
					- "durationchange"
				}
			}
			- " at the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-13" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ". (The\n  event is not fired when the duration is reset as part of loading a new media resource.) If the\n  duration is changed such that the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-6" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " ends up being greater\n  than the time of the end of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-23" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", then the user agent must also "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:dom-media-seek-3" {
				- "seek"
			}
			- " to the time of the end of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-24" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "If an \"infinite\" stream ends for some reason, then the duration would change\n  from positive Infinity to the time of the last frame or sample in the stream, and the "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-durationchange-2" {
				a href="#event-media-durationchange" {
					- "durationchange"
				}
			}
			- " event would be fired. Similarly, if the\n  user agent initially estimated the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-25" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "'s duration instead of determining\n  it precisely, and later revises the estimate based on new information, then the duration would\n  change and the "
			code id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:event-media-durationchange-3" {
				a href="#event-media-durationchange" {
					- "durationchange"
				}
			}
			- " event would be\n  fired."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some video files also have an explicit date and time corresponding to the zero time in the\n  "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-timeline-14" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- ", known as the "
			dfn id="timeline-offset" {
				- "timeline offset"
			}
			- ". Initially, the\n  "
			a href="#timeline-offset" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:timeline-offset-2" {
				- "timeline offset"
			}
			- " must be set to Not-a-Number (NaN)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-getstartdate" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "getStartDate()"
				}
			}
			- " method must return "
			a href="#create-a-date-object" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:create-a-date-object" {
				- "a new "
				code {
					- "Date"
				}
				- " object"
			}
			- " representing the current\n  "
			a href="#timeline-offset" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:timeline-offset-3" {
				- "timeline offset"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="audio,video" id="attr-media-loop" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "loop"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:boolean-attribute" {
				- "boolean attribute"
			}
			- " that, if specified, indicates that the "
			a href="#media-element" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-element-14" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- " is to seek back to the start of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:media-resource-26" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " upon reaching the\n  end."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/loop" title="The HTMLMediaElement.loop property reflects the loop HTML attribute, which controls whether the media element should start over when it reaches the end." {
						- "HTMLMediaElement/loop"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "11+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "37+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-loop" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "loop"
				}
			}
			- " IDL\n  attribute must "
			a href="#reflect" id="offsets-into-the-media-resource:reflect" {
				- "reflect"
			}
			- " the content attribute of the same name."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="ready-states" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.7"
			}
			- " Ready states"
			a href="#ready-states" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "media"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-media-readystate" id="dom-media-readystate-dev" {
						- "readyState"
					}
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/readyState" title="The HTMLMediaElement.readyState property indicates the readiness state of the media." {
								- "HTMLMediaElement/readyState"
							}
						}
						p class="all-engines-text" {
							- "Support in all current engines."
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "3.5+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "3.1+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span {
									- "Chrome"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge"
								}
								span {
									- "79+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge (Legacy)"
								}
								span {
									- "12+"
								}
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span {
									- "Internet Explorer"
								}
								span {
									- "5.5+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Firefox Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="safari_ios yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari iOS"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Chrome Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="webview_android yes" {
								span {
									- "WebView Android"
								}
								span {
									- "37+"
								}
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Samsung Internet"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera Android"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns a value that expresses the current state of the element with respect to rendering the\n    "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ", from the codes in the list below."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element" {
				- "Media elements"
			}
			- " have a "
			i {
				- "ready state"
			}
			- ", which describes to\n  what degree they are ready to be rendered at the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-2" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- ". The\n  possible values are as follows; the ready state of a media element at any particular time is the\n  greatest value describing the state of the element:"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-have_nothing" data-dfn-type="const" {
					code {
						- "HAVE_NOTHING"
					}
				}
				- " (numeric value 0)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "No information regarding the "
					a href="#media-resource" id="ready-states:media-resource" {
						- "media resource"
					}
					- " is available. No data for the\n   "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-3" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " is available. "
					a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-2" {
						- "Media\n   elements"
					}
					- " whose "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-networkstate" {
						a href="#dom-media-networkstate" {
							- "networkState"
						}
					}
					- " attribute are set\n   to "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-network_empty" {
						a href="#dom-media-network_empty" {
							- "NETWORK_EMPTY"
						}
					}
					- " are always in the "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_nothing" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" {
							- "HAVE_NOTHING"
						}
					}
					- " state."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-have_metadata" data-dfn-type="const" {
					code {
						- "HAVE_METADATA"
					}
				}
				- " (numeric value 1)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Enough of the resource has been obtained that the duration of the resource is available.\n   In the case of a "
					code id="ready-states:the-video-element" {
						a href="#the-video-element" {
							- "video"
						}
					}
					- " element, the dimensions of the video are also available. No\n   "
					a href="#media-data" id="ready-states:media-data" {
						- "media data"
					}
					- " is available for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-4" {
						- "current playback\n   position"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-have_current_data" data-dfn-type="const" {
					code {
						- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
					}
				}
				- " (numeric value 2)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Data for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-5" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " is available, but either not\n   enough data is available that the user agent could successfully advance the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-6" {
						- "current\n   playback position"
					}
					- " in the "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id="ready-states:direction-of-playback" {
						- "direction of playback"
					}
					- " at all without immediately\n   reverting to the "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
							- "HAVE_METADATA"
						}
					}
					- " state, or there is no\n   more data to obtain in the "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id="ready-states:direction-of-playback-2" {
						- "direction of playback"
					}
					- ". For example, in video this\n   corresponds to the user agent having data from the current frame, but not the next frame, when\n   the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-7" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " is at the end of the current frame; and to when "
					a href="#ended-playback" id="ready-states:ended-playback" {
						- "playback has ended"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-have_future_data" data-dfn-type="const" {
					code {
						- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
					}
				}
				- " (numeric value 3)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Data for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-8" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " is available, as well as\n   enough data for the user agent to advance the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-9" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " in the\n   "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id="ready-states:direction-of-playback-3" {
						- "direction of playback"
					}
					- " at least a little without immediately reverting to the "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-2" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
							- "HAVE_METADATA"
						}
					}
					- " state, and "
					a href="#the-text-tracks-are-ready" id="ready-states:the-text-tracks-are-ready" {
						- "the text tracks are\n   ready"
					}
					- ". For example, in video this corresponds to the user agent having data for at least\n   the current frame and the next frame when the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-10" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " is at the\n   instant in time between the two frames, or to the user agent having the video data for the\n   current frame and audio data to keep playing at least a little when the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-11" {
						- "current playback\n   position"
					}
					- " is in the middle of a frame. The user agent cannot be in this state if "
					a href="#ended-playback" id="ready-states:ended-playback-2" {
						- "playback has ended"
					}
					- ", as the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-12" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- "\n   can never advance in this case."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-have_enough_data" data-dfn-type="const" {
					code {
						- "HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA"
					}
				}
				- " (numeric value 4)"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n   "
				p {
					- "All the conditions described for the "
					code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
							- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
						}
					}
					- " state are met, and, in addition,\n    either of the following conditions is also true:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ul {
					li {
						- "The user agent estimates that data is being fetched at a rate where the "
						a href="#current-playback-position" id="ready-states:current-playback-position-13" {
							- "current\n     playback position"
						}
						- ", if it were to advance at the element's "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-playbackrate" {
							a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
								- "playbackRate"
							}
						}
						- ", would not overtake the available data\n     before playback reaches the end of the "
						a href="#media-resource" id="ready-states:media-resource-2" {
							- "media resource"
						}
						- "."
					}
					li {
						- "The user agent has entered a state where waiting longer will not result in further data\n     being obtained, and therefore nothing would be gained by delaying playback any further. (For\n     example, the buffer might be full.)"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In practice, the difference between "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-3" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
					- "HAVE_METADATA"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
					- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " is negligible. Really the only time\n  the difference is relevant is when painting a "
			code id="ready-states:the-video-element-2" {
				a href="#the-video-element" {
					- "video"
				}
			}
			- " element onto a\n  "
			code id="ready-states:the-canvas-element" {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" {
					- "canvas"
				}
			}
			- ", where it distinguishes the case where something will be drawn ("
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
					- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " or greater) from the case where\n  nothing is drawn ("
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-4" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
					- "HAVE_METADATA"
				}
			}
			- " or less). Similarly,\n  the difference between "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-3" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
					- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " (only\n  the current frame) and "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
					- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " (at least\n  this frame and the next) can be negligible (in the extreme, only one frame). The only time that\n  distinction really matters is when a page provides an interface for \"frame-by-frame\"\n  navigation."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the ready state of a "
			a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-3" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " whose "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-networkstate-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-networkstate" {
					- "networkState"
				}
			}
			- " is not "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-network_empty-2" {
				a href="#dom-media-network_empty" {
					- "NETWORK_EMPTY"
				}
			}
			- " changes, the user agent must follow the steps\n  given below:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Apply the first applicable set of substeps from the following list:"
				}
				- "\n\n\n    "
				dl class="switch" {
					dt {
						- "If the previous ready state was "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_nothing-2" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" {
								- "HAVE_NOTHING"
							}
						}
						- ",\n     and the new ready state is "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-5" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
								- "HAVE_METADATA"
							}
						}
					}
					dd id="fire-loadedmetadata" {
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task" {
								- "Queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-4" {
								- "media element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-loadedmetadata" {
								a href="#event-media-loadedmetadata" {
									- "loadedmetadata"
								}
							}
							- " at the element."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "Before this task is run, as part of the "
							a href="#event-loop" id="ready-states:event-loop" {
								- "event loop"
							}
							- " mechanism, the\n      rendering will have been updated to resize the "
							code id="ready-states:the-video-element-3" {
								a href="#the-video-element" {
									- "video"
								}
							}
							- " element if appropriate."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					dt id="handling-first-frame-available" {
						- "If the previous ready state was "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-6" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
								- "HAVE_METADATA"
							}
						}
						- " and the new ready state is "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-4" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
								- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
							}
						}
						- " or greater"
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p id="fire-loadeddata" {
							- "If this is the first time this occurs for this "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-5" {
								- "media\n      element"
							}
							- " since the "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-load" {
								a href="#dom-media-load" {
									- "load()"
								}
							}
							- " algorithm was last\n      invoked, the user agent must "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-2" {
								- "queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-6" {
								- "media\n      element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-2" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-loadeddata" {
								a href="#event-media-loadeddata" {
									- "loadeddata"
								}
							}
							- " at the element."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "If the new ready state is "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-3" {
								a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
									- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
								}
							}
							- "\n      or "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_enough_data" {
								a href="#dom-media-have_enough_data" {
									- "HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA"
								}
							}
							- ", then the relevant steps\n      below must then be run also."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					dt {
						- "If the previous ready state was "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-4" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
								- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
							}
						}
						- " or more, and the new ready state is\n     "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-5" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
								- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
							}
						}
						- " or less"
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p id="fire-waiting-when-waiting" {
							- "If the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-7" {
								- "media element"
							}
							- " was "
							a href="#potentially-playing" id="ready-states:potentially-playing" {
								- "potentially\n      playing"
							}
							- " before its "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-readystate" {
								a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
									- "readyState"
								}
							}
							- " attribute\n      changed to a value lower than "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-5" {
								a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
									- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
								}
							}
							- ", and the element has not\n      "
							a href="#ended-playback" id="ready-states:ended-playback-3" {
								- "ended playback"
							}
							- ", and playback has not "
							a href="#stopped-due-to-errors" id="ready-states:stopped-due-to-errors" {
								- "stopped due to errors"
							}
							- ",\n      "
							a href="#paused-for-user-interaction" id="ready-states:paused-for-user-interaction" {
								- "paused for user interaction"
							}
							- ", or "
							a href="#paused-for-in-band-content" id="ready-states:paused-for-in-band-content" {
								- "paused for in-band content"
							}
							- ", the user\n      agent must "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-3" {
								- "queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-8" {
								- "media element"
							}
							- " to\n      "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-3" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-timeupdate" {
								a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
									- "timeupdate"
								}
							}
							- " at the element, and "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-4" {
								- "queue a media\n      element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-9" {
								- "media element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-4" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-waiting" {
								a href="#event-media-waiting" {
									- "waiting"
								}
							}
							- " at the element."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					dt {
						- "If the previous ready state was "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-6" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
								- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
							}
						}
						- " or less, and the new ready state\n     is "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-6" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
								- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
							}
						}
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "The user agent must "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-5" {
								- "queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-10" {
								- "media\n      element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-5" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-canplay" {
								a href="#event-media-canplay" {
									- "canplay"
								}
							}
							- " at the element."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "If the element's "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-paused" {
								a href="#dom-media-paused" {
									- "paused"
								}
							}
							- " attribute is false, the user\n      agent must "
							a href="#notify-about-playing" id="ready-states:notify-about-playing" {
								- "notify about playing"
							}
							- " for the element."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					dt {
						- "If the new ready state is "
						code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_enough_data-2" {
							a href="#dom-media-have_enough_data" {
								- "HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA"
							}
						}
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "If the previous ready state was "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-7" {
								a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
									- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
								}
							}
							- " or less, the user agent must\n      "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-6" {
								- "queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-11" {
								- "media element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-6" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-canplay-2" {
								a href="#event-media-canplay" {
									- "canplay"
								}
							}
							- " at the element, and, if the element's "
							code id="ready-states:dom-media-paused-2" {
								a href="#dom-media-paused" {
									- "paused"
								}
							}
							- " attribute is false, "
							a href="#notify-about-playing" id="ready-states:notify-about-playing-2" {
								- "notify about playing"
							}
							- "\n      for the element."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "The user agent must "
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-7" {
								- "queue a media element task"
							}
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-12" {
								- "media\n      element"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-7" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="ready-states:event-media-canplaythrough" {
								a href="#event-media-canplaythrough" {
									- "canplaythrough"
								}
							}
							- " at the element."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "If the element is not "
							a href="#eligible-for-autoplay" id="ready-states:eligible-for-autoplay" {
								- "eligible for autoplay"
							}
							- ", then the user agent must abort\n      these substeps."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "The user agent may run the following substeps:"
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						ol {
							li {
								- "Set the "
								code id="ready-states:dom-media-paused-3" {
									a href="#dom-media-paused" {
										- "paused"
									}
								}
								- " attribute to false."
							}
							li {
								- "If the element's "
								a href="#show-poster-flag" id="ready-states:show-poster-flag" {
									- "show poster flag"
								}
								- " is true, set it to false and run the\n       "
								i id="ready-states:time-marches-on" {
									a href="#time-marches-on" {
										- "time marches on"
									}
								}
								- " steps."
							}
							li {
								a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-8" {
									- "Queue a media element task"
								}
								- " given the element to "
								a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-8" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
									- "fire an event"
								}
								- " named "
								code id="ready-states:event-media-play" {
									a href="#event-media-play" {
										- "play"
									}
								}
								- " at the element."
							}
							li {
								a href="#notify-about-playing" id="ready-states:notify-about-playing-3" {
									- "Notify about playing"
								}
								- " for the element."
							}
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "Alternatively, if the element is a "
							code id="ready-states:the-video-element-4" {
								a href="#the-video-element" {
									- "video"
								}
							}
							- " element, the user agent may start\n      observing whether the element "
							a href="#intersect-the-viewport" id="ready-states:intersect-the-viewport" {
								- "intersects the\n      viewport"
							}
							- ". When the element starts "
							a href="#intersect-the-viewport" id="ready-states:intersect-the-viewport-2" {
								- "intersecting\n      the viewport"
							}
							- ", if the element is still "
							a href="#eligible-for-autoplay" id="ready-states:eligible-for-autoplay-2" {
								- "eligible for autoplay"
							}
							- ", run the\n      substeps above. Optionally, when the element stops "
							a href="#intersect-the-viewport" id="ready-states:intersect-the-viewport-3" {
								- "intersecting the viewport"
							}
							- ", if the "
							a href="#can-autoplay-flag" id="ready-states:can-autoplay-flag" {
								- "can autoplay flag"
							}
							- " is still\n      true and the "
							code id="ready-states:attr-media-autoplay" {
								a href="#attr-media-autoplay" {
									- "autoplay"
								}
							}
							- " attribute is still specified,\n      run the following substeps:"
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						ol {
							li {
								- "Run the "
								a href="#internal-pause-steps" id="ready-states:internal-pause-steps" {
									- "internal pause steps"
								}
								- " and set the "
								a href="#can-autoplay-flag" id="ready-states:can-autoplay-flag-2" {
									- "can autoplay flag"
								}
								- " to\n       true."
							}
							li {
								a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task-9" {
									- "Queue a media element task"
								}
								- " given the element to "
								a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="ready-states:concept-event-fire-9" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
									- "fire an event"
								}
								- " named "
								code id="ready-states:event-media-pause" {
									a href="#event-media-pause" {
										- "pause"
									}
								}
								- " at the element."
							}
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "The substeps for playing and pausing can run multiple times as the element\n      starts or stops "
							a href="#intersect-the-viewport" id="ready-states:intersect-the-viewport-4" {
								- "intersecting the viewport"
							}
							- ", as\n      long as the "
							a href="#can-autoplay-flag" id="ready-states:can-autoplay-flag-3" {
								- "can autoplay flag"
							}
							- " is true."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "User agents do not need to support autoplay, and it is suggested that user\n      agents honor user preferences on the matter. Authors are urged to use the "
							code id="ready-states:attr-media-autoplay-2" {
								a href="#attr-media-autoplay" {
									- "autoplay"
								}
							}
							- " attribute rather than using script to force the\n      video to play, so as to allow the user to override the behavior if so desired."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "It is possible for the ready state of a media element to jump between these states\n  discontinuously. For example, the state of a media element can jump straight from "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-7" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" {
					- "HAVE_METADATA"
				}
			}
			- " to "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_enough_data-3" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_enough_data" {
					- "HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " without passing through the "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-8" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" {
					- "HAVE_CURRENT_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-7" {
				a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
					- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
				}
			}
			- " states."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-readystate" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "readyState"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute must, on getting, return the\n  value described above that describes the current ready state of the "
			a href="#media-element" id="ready-states:media-element-13" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="audio,video" id="attr-media-autoplay" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "autoplay"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="ready-states:boolean-attribute" {
				- "boolean attribute"
			}
			- ".\n  When present, the user agent (as described in the algorithm described herein)\n  will automatically begin playback of the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="ready-states:media-resource-3" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " as soon as it can do so\n  without stopping."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Authors are urged to use the "
			code id="ready-states:attr-media-autoplay-3" {
				a href="#attr-media-autoplay" {
					- "autoplay"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute rather than using script to trigger automatic playback, as this allows the user to\n  override the automatic playback when it is not desired, e.g. when using a screen reader. Authors\n  are also encouraged to consider not using the automatic playback behavior at all, and instead to\n  let the user agent wait for the user to start playback explicitly."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/autoplay" title="The HTMLMediaElement.autoplay property reflects the autoplay HTML attribute, indicating whether playback should automatically begin as soon as enough media is available to do so without interruption." {
						- "HTMLMediaElement/autoplay"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "3.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "3.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
