				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " is positive or zero,\n  then the "
			dfn id="direction-of-playback" {
				- "direction of playback"
			}
			- " is forwards. Otherwise, it is backwards."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="media-playback" {
			- "When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-58" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#potentially-playing" id="playing-the-media-resource:potentially-playing-4" {
				- "potentially playing"
			}
			- " and\n  its "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " is a "
			a href="#fully-active" id="playing-the-media-resource:fully-active" {
				- "fully active"
			}
			- " "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- ", its "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-9" {
				- "current\n  playback position"
			}
			- " must increase monotonically at the element's "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-playbackrate-6" {
				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " units of media time per unit time of the\n  "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-timeline-2" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- "'s clock. (This specification always refers to this as an\n  "
			i {
				- "increase"
			}
			- ", but that increase could actually be a "
			em {
				- "de"
			}
			- "crease if the element's "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-playbackrate-7" {
				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " is negative.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The element's "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-playbackrate-8" {
				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " can be\n  0.0, in which case the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-10" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " doesn't move, despite playback not\n  being paused ("
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-paused-13" {
				a href="#dom-media-paused" {
					- "paused"
				}
			}
			- " doesn't become true, and the "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-pause-3" {
				a href="#event-media-pause" {
					- "pause"
				}
			}
			- " event doesn't fire)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This specification doesn't define how the user agent achieves the appropriate\n  playback rate — depending on the protocol and media available, it is plausible that the user\n  agent could negotiate with the server to have the server provide the media data at the appropriate\n  rate, so that (except for the period between when the rate is changed and when the server updates\n  the stream's playback rate) the client doesn't actually have to drop or interpolate any\n  frames."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Any time the user agent "
			a href="#await-a-stable-state" id="playing-the-media-resource:await-a-stable-state" {
				- "provides a stable state"
			}
			- ",\n  the "
			a href="#official-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:official-playback-position-2" {
				- "official playback position"
			}
			- " must be set to the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-11" {
				- "current playback\n  position"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- " \n\n  "
		p {
			- "While the "
			a href="#direction-of-playback" id="playing-the-media-resource:direction-of-playback-8" {
				- "direction of playback"
			}
			- " is backwards, any corresponding audio must be\n  "
			a href="#concept-media-muted" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-media-muted-2" {
				- "muted"
			}
			- ". While the element's "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-playbackrate-9" {
				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " is so low or so high that the user agent\n  cannot play audio usefully, the corresponding audio must also be "
			a href="#concept-media-muted" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-media-muted-3" {
				- "muted"
			}
			- ". If the element's "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-playbackrate-10" {
				a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" {
					- "playbackRate"
				}
			}
			- " is not 1.0 and "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-preservespitch" {
				a href="#dom-media-preservespitch" {
					- "preservesPitch"
				}
			}
			- " is true, the user agent must apply pitch\n  adjustment to preserve the original pitch of the audio. Otherwise, the user agent must speed up\n  or slow down the audio without any pitch adjustment."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-59" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#potentially-playing" id="playing-the-media-resource:potentially-playing-5" {
				- "potentially playing"
			}
			- ", its audio data played\n  must be synchronized with the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-12" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- ", at the element's\n  "
			a href="#effective-media-volume" id="playing-the-media-resource:effective-media-volume" {
				- "effective media volume"
			}
			- ". The user agent must play the audio from audio tracks that\n  were enabled when the "
			a href="#event-loop" id="playing-the-media-resource:event-loop-3" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " last reached "
			a href="#step1" {
				- "step 1"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-60" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " is not "
			a href="#potentially-playing" id="playing-the-media-resource:potentially-playing-6" {
				- "potentially playing"
			}
			- ", audio must not play\n  for the element."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-61" {
				- "Media elements"
			}
			- " that are "
			a href="#potentially-playing" id="playing-the-media-resource:potentially-playing-7" {
				- "potentially playing"
			}
			- "\n  while not "
			a id="playing-the-media-resource:in-a-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#in-a-document" data-x-internal="in-a-document" {
				- "in a document"
			}
			- " must not play any video, but should play any audio component.\n  Media elements must not stop playing just because all references to them have been removed; only\n  once a media element is in a state where no further audio could ever be played by that element may\n  the element be garbage collected."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "It is possible for an element to which no explicit references exist to play audio,\n  even if such an element is not still actively playing: for instance, it could be unpaused but\n  stalled waiting for content to buffer, or it could be still buffering, but with a\n  "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-suspend" {
				a href="#event-media-suspend" {
					- "suspend"
				}
			}
			- " event listener that begins playback. Even a\n  media element whose "
			a href="#media-resource" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-resource-19" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " has no audio tracks could eventually play audio\n  again if it had an event listener that changes the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-resource-20" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-62" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="list-of-newly-introduced-cues" {
				- "list of newly introduced cues"
			}
			- ", which must be\n  initially empty. Whenever a "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue" {
				- "text track cue"
			}
			- " is added to the "
			a href="#text-track-list-of-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-list-of-cues" {
				- "list of cues"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " that is in the "
			a href="#list-of-text-tracks" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-text-tracks" {
				- "list of text\n  tracks"
			}
			- " for a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-63" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ", that "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-2" {
				- "cue"
			}
			- " must\n  be added to the "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-64" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#list-of-newly-introduced-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-newly-introduced-cues" {
				- "list of newly introduced cues"
			}
			- ". Whenever\n  a "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-2" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " is added to the "
			a href="#list-of-text-tracks" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-text-tracks-2" {
				- "list of text tracks"
			}
			- " for a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-65" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- ", all of the "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-3" {
				- "cues"
			}
			- " in that "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-3" {
				- "text\n  track"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#text-track-list-of-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-list-of-cues-2" {
				- "list of cues"
			}
			- " must be added to the\n  "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-66" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#list-of-newly-introduced-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-newly-introduced-cues-2" {
				- "list of newly introduced cues"
			}
			- ". When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-67" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#list-of-newly-introduced-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-newly-introduced-cues-3" {
				- "list of newly introduced cues"
			}
			- " has new cues added while the\n  "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-68" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#show-poster-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:show-poster-flag-3" {
				- "show poster flag"
			}
			- " is not set, then the user agent must\n  run the "
			i id="playing-the-media-resource:time-marches-on-2" {
				a href="#time-marches-on" {
					- "time marches on"
				}
			}
			- " steps."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-4" {
				- "text track cue"
			}
			- " is removed from the "
			a href="#text-track-list-of-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-list-of-cues-3" {
				- "list of cues"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-4" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " that is in the "
			a href="#list-of-text-tracks" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-text-tracks-3" {
				- "list of text\n  tracks"
			}
			- " for a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-69" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ", and whenever a "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-5" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " is removed\n  from the "
			a href="#list-of-text-tracks" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-text-tracks-4" {
				- "list of text tracks"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-70" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ", if the "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-71" {
				- "media\n  element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#show-poster-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:show-poster-flag-4" {
				- "show poster flag"
			}
			- " is not set, then the user agent must run the\n  "
			i id="playing-the-media-resource:time-marches-on-3" {
				a href="#time-marches-on" {
					- "time marches on"
				}
			}
			- " steps."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-13" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-72" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " changes (e.g.\n  due to playback or seeking), the user agent must run the "
			i id="playing-the-media-resource:time-marches-on-4" {
				a href="#time-marches-on" {
					- "time marches\n  on"
				}
			}
			- " steps. To support use cases that depend on the timing accuracy of cue event firing, such as\n  synchronizing captions with shot changes in a video, user agents should fire cue events as close\n  as possible to their position on the media timeline, and ideally within 20 milliseconds. If the\n  "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-14" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- " changes while the steps are running, then the user agent\n  must wait for the steps to complete, and then must immediately rerun the steps. These steps are\n  thus run as often as possible or needed."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If one iteration takes a long time, this can cause short duration\n  "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-5" {
				- "cues"
			}
			- " to be skipped over as the user agent rushes ahead to\n  \"catch up\", so these cues will not appear in the "
			code id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-texttrack-activecues" {
				a href="#dom-texttrack-activecues" {
					- "activeCues"
				}
			}
			- " list."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="time-marches-on" {
				i {
					- "time marches on"
				}
			}
			- " steps are as follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "current cues"
					}
					- " be a list of "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-6" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- ", initialized to contain all the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-7" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " of all\n   the "
					a href="#text-track-hidden" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-hidden" {
						- "hidden"
					}
					- " or "
					a href="#text-track-showing" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-showing" {
						- "showing"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-6" {
						- "text tracks"
					}
					- " of the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-73" {
						- "media\n   element"
					}
					- " (not the "
					a href="#text-track-disabled" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-disabled" {
						- "disabled"
					}
					- " ones) whose "
					a href="#text-track-cue-start-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-start-time-2" {
						- "start times"
					}
					- " are less than or equal to the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-15" {
						- "current\n   playback position"
					}
					- " and whose "
					a href="#text-track-cue-end-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-end-time-2" {
						- "end times"
					}
					- " are\n   greater than the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-16" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "other cues"
					}
					- " be a list of "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-8" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- ",\n   initialized to contain all the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-9" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " of "
					a href="#text-track-hidden" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-hidden-2" {
						- "hidden"
					}
					- " and "
					a href="#text-track-showing" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-showing-2" {
						- "showing"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-7" {
						- "text tracks"
					}
					- " of the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-74" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " that are not present in "
					var {
						- "current cues"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "last time"
					}
					- " be the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-17" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " at the\n   time this algorithm was last run for this "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-75" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- ", if this is not the first\n   time it has run."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-18" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " has, since the last time this algorithm was\n   run, only changed through its usual monotonic increase during normal playback, then let\n   "
					var {
						- "missed cues"
					}
					- " be the list of "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-10" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "other\n   cues"
					}
					- " whose "
					a href="#text-track-cue-start-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-start-time-3" {
						- "start times"
					}
					- " are greater than or\n   equal to "
					var {
						- "last time"
					}
					- " and whose "
					a href="#text-track-cue-end-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-end-time-3" {
						- "end times"
					}
					- "\n   are less than or equal to the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-19" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ". Otherwise, let "
					var {
						- "missed\n   cues"
					}
					- " be an empty list."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Remove all the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-11" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "missed cues"
					}
					- "\n   that are also in the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-76" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#list-of-newly-introduced-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-newly-introduced-cues-4" {
						- "list of newly introduced cues"
					}
					- ", and\n   then empty the element's "
					a href="#list-of-newly-introduced-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-newly-introduced-cues-5" {
						- "list of newly introduced cues"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the time was reached through the usual monotonic increase of the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-20" {
						- "current playback\n   position"
					}
					- " during normal playback, and if the user agent has not fired a "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-timeupdate-6" {
						a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
							- "timeupdate"
						}
					}
					- " event at the element in the past 15 to 250ms\n   and is not still running event handlers for such an event, then the user agent must "
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-11" {
						- "queue a\n   media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-77" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " to "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-13" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-timeupdate-7" {
						a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
							- "timeupdate"
						}
					}
					- " at the element. (In the other cases, such as\n   explicit seeks, relevant events get fired as part of the overall process of changing the\n   "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-21" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ".)"
				}
				- "\n\n   "
				p class="note" {
					- "The event thus is not to be fired faster than about 66Hz or slower than 4Hz\n   (assuming the event handlers don't take longer than 250ms to run). User agents are encouraged to\n   vary the frequency of the event based on the system load and the average cost of processing the\n   event each time, so that the UI updates are not any more frequent than the user agent can\n   comfortably handle while decoding the video."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If all of the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-12" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "current cues"
					}
					- "\n   have their "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag" {
						- "text track cue active flag"
					}
					- " set, none of the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-13" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "other cues"
					}
					- " have their "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-2" {
						- "text track cue active\n   flag"
					}
					- " set, and "
					var {
						- "missed cues"
					}
					- " is empty, then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the time was reached through the usual monotonic increase of the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="playing-the-media-resource:current-playback-position-22" {
						- "current playback\n    position"
					}
					- " during normal playback, and there are "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-14" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- "\n    in "
					var {
						- "other cues"
					}
					- " that have their "
					a href="#text-track-cue-pause-on-exit-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-pause-on-exit-flag" {
						- "text track cue pause-on-exit flag"
					}
					- "\n    set and that either have their "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-3" {
						- "text track cue active flag"
					}
					- " set or are also in "
					var {
						- "missed cues"
					}
					- ", then "
					a href="#immediately" id="playing-the-media-resource:immediately" {
						- "immediately"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#dom-media-pause" id="playing-the-media-resource:dom-media-pause" {
						- "pause"
					}
					- " the\n    "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-78" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- ". "
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "In the other cases, such as explicit seeks, playback is not paused by going past\n    the end time of a "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-15" {
						- "cue"
					}
					- ", even if that "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-16" {
						- "cue"
					}
					- " has its "
					a href="#text-track-cue-pause-on-exit-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-pause-on-exit-flag-2" {
						- "text track cue pause-on-exit flag"
					}
					- " set."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "events"
					}
					- " be a list of "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- ",\n    initially empty. Each "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-2" {
						- "task"
					}
					- " in this list will be associated\n    with a "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-8" {
						- "text track"
					}
					- ", a "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-17" {
						- "text track cue"
					}
					- ", and a time, which are used to\n    sort the list before the "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-3" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " are queued."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "affected tracks"
					}
					- " be a list of "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-9" {
						- "text\n    tracks"
					}
					- ", initially empty."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "When the steps below say to "
					dfn id="prepare-an-event" {
						- "prepare an event"
					}
					- " named "
					var {
						- "event"
					}
					- " for a\n    "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-18" {
						- "text track cue"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "target"
					}
					- " with a time "
					var {
						- "time"
					}
					- ", the\n    user agent must run these steps:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "track"
							}
							- " be the "
							a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-10" {
								- "text track"
							}
							- " with which the "
							a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-19" {
								- "text\n     track cue"
							}
							- " "
							var {
								- "target"
							}
							- " is associated."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Create a "
							a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-4" {
								- "task"
							}
							- " to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-14" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							var {
								- "event"
							}
							- " at\n     "
							var {
								- "target"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Add the newly created "
							a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-5" {
								- "task"
							}
							- " to "
							var {
								- "events"
							}
							- ", associated with the time "
							var {
								- "time"
							}
							- ", the "
							a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-11" {
								- "text\n     track"
							}
							- " "
							var {
								- "track"
							}
							- ", and the "
							a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-20" {
								- "text track cue"
							}
							- " "
							var {
								- "target"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Add "
							var {
								- "track"
							}
							- " to "
							var {
								- "affected tracks"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "For each "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-21" {
						- "text track cue"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "missed\n   cues"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="#prepare-an-event" id="playing-the-media-resource:prepare-an-event" {
						- "prepare an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-enter" {
						a href="#event-media-enter" {
							- "enter"
						}
					}
					- " for the\n   "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:texttrackcue" {
						a href="#texttrackcue" {
							- "TextTrackCue"
						}
					}
					- " object with the "
					a href="#text-track-cue-start-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-start-time-4" {
						- "text track cue start time"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "For each "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-22" {
						- "text track cue"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "other\n   cues"
					}
					- " that either has its "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-4" {
						- "text track cue active flag"
					}
					- " set or is in "
					var {
						- "missed cues"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="#prepare-an-event" id="playing-the-media-resource:prepare-an-event-2" {
						- "prepare an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-exit" {
						a href="#event-media-exit" {
							- "exit"
						}
					}
					- " for the "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:texttrackcue-2" {
						a href="#texttrackcue" {
							- "TextTrackCue"
						}
					}
					- " object with the later of the\n   "
					a href="#text-track-cue-end-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-end-time-4" {
						- "text track cue end time"
					}
					- " and the "
					a href="#text-track-cue-start-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-start-time-5" {
						- "text track cue start time"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "For each "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-23" {
						- "text track cue"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "current\n   cues"
					}
					- " that does not have its "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-5" {
						- "text track cue active flag"
					}
					- " set, "
					a href="#prepare-an-event" id="playing-the-media-resource:prepare-an-event-3" {
						- "prepare an\n   event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-enter-2" {
						a href="#event-media-enter" {
							- "enter"
						}
					}
					- " for the "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:texttrackcue-3" {
						a href="#texttrackcue" {
							- "TextTrackCue"
						}
					}
					- "\n   object with the "
					a href="#text-track-cue-start-time" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-start-time-6" {
						- "text track cue start time"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Sort the "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-6" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "events"
					}
					- " in ascending\n    time order ("
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-7" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " with earlier times first)."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Further sort "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-8" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "events"
					}
					- " that have\n    the same time by the relative "
					a href="#text-track-cue-order" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-order" {
						- "text track cue order"
					}
					- " of the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-24" {
						- "text track cues"
					}
					- " associated with these "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-9" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Finally, sort "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-10" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "events"
					}
					- " that have the\n    same time and same "
					a href="#text-track-cue-order" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-order-2" {
						- "text track cue order"
					}
					- " by placing "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-11" {
						- "tasks"
					}
					- " that fire "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-enter-3" {
						a href="#event-media-enter" {
							- "enter"
						}
					}
					- "\n    events before those that fire "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-exit-2" {
						a href="#event-media-exit" {
							- "exit"
						}
					}
					- " events."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-12" {
						- "Queue a media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-79" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " for each\n   "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-12" {
						- "task"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "events"
					}
					- ", in list order."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Sort "
					var {
						- "affected tracks"
					}
					- " in the same order as the "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-12" {
						- "text tracks"
					}
					- " appear in the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-80" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#list-of-text-tracks" id="playing-the-media-resource:list-of-text-tracks-5" {
						- "list of text\n   tracks"
					}
					- ", and remove duplicates."
				}
				- "\n\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "For each "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-13" {
						- "text track"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "affected tracks"
					}
					- ", in the list order,\n   "
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-13" {
						- "queue a media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-81" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " to "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-15" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-cuechange" {
						a href="#event-media-cuechange" {
							- "cuechange"
						}
					}
					- " at the "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:texttrack" {
						a href="#texttrack" {
							- "TextTrack"
						}
					}
					- " object, and, if the\n   "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-14" {
						- "text track"
					}
					- " has a corresponding "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:the-track-element" {
						a href="#the-track-element" {
							- "track"
						}
					}
					- " element, to then "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-event-fire-16" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:event-media-cuechange-2" {
						a href="#event-media-cuechange" {
							- "cuechange"
						}
					}
					- " at the "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:the-track-element-2" {
						a href="#the-track-element" {
							- "track"
						}
					}
					- " element as well."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-6" {
						- "text track cue active flag"
					}
					- " of all the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-25" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in the "
					var {
						- "current cues"
					}
					- ", and unset the "
					a href="#text-track-cue-active-flag" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-active-flag-7" {
						- "text track cue\n   active flag"
					}
					- " of all the "
					a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-26" {
						- "cues"
					}
					- " in the "
					var {
						- "other\n   cues"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Run the "
					a href="#rules-for-updating-the-text-track-rendering" id="playing-the-media-resource:rules-for-updating-the-text-track-rendering" {
						- "rules for updating the text track rendering"
					}
					- " of each of the "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-15" {
						- "text tracks"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "affected tracks"
					}
					- " that are "
					a href="#text-track-showing" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-showing-3" {
						- "showing"
					}
					- ", providing the "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-16" {
						- "text track"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#text-track-language" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-language" {
						- "text track\n   language"
					}
					- " as the fallback language if it is not the empty string. For example, for "
					a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-17" {
						- "text tracks"
					}
					- " based on WebVTT, the "
					a id="playing-the-media-resource:rules-for-updating-the-display-of-webvtt-text-tracks" href="https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#rules-for-updating-the-display-of-webvtt-text-tracks" data-x-internal="rules-for-updating-the-display-of-webvtt-text-tracks" {
						- "rules for updating the display\n   of WebVTT text tracks"
					}
					- ". "
					a href="#refsWEBVTT" {
						- "[WEBVTT]"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purposes of the algorithm above, a "
			a href="#text-track-cue" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-cue-27" {
				- "text track cue"
			}
			- " is considered to be part\n  of a "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-18" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- " only if it is listed in the "
			a href="#text-track-list-of-cues" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-list-of-cues-4" {
				- "text track list of cues"
			}
			- ", not\n  merely if it is associated with the "
			a href="#text-track" id="playing-the-media-resource:text-track-19" {
				- "text track"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If the "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-82" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a id="playing-the-media-resource:node-document-3" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- " stops being a\n  "
			a href="#fully-active" id="playing-the-media-resource:fully-active-2" {
				- "fully active"
			}
			- " document, then the playback will "
			a href="#media-playback" {
				- "stop"
			}
			- "\n  until the document is active again."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-83" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#remove-an-element-from-a-document" id="playing-the-media-resource:remove-an-element-from-a-document" {
				- "removed\n  from a "
				code {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- ", the user agent must run the following steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					a href="#await-a-stable-state" id="playing-the-media-resource:await-a-stable-state-2" {
						- "Await a stable state"
					}
					- ", allowing the "
					a href="#concept-task" id="playing-the-media-resource:concept-task-13" {
						- "task"
					}
					- " that removed the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-84" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " from the\n   "
					code id="playing-the-media-resource:document-3" {
						a href="#document" {
							- "Document"
						}
					}
					- " to continue. The "
					a href="#synchronous-section" id="playing-the-media-resource:synchronous-section" {
						- "synchronous section"
					}
					- " consists of all the\n   remaining steps of this algorithm. (Steps in the "
					a href="#synchronous-section" id="playing-the-media-resource:synchronous-section-2" {
						- "synchronous section"
					}
					- " are marked with\n   ⌛.)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "⌛ If the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-85" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " is "
					a id="playing-the-media-resource:in-a-document-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#in-a-document" data-x-internal="in-a-document" {
						- "in a document"
					}
					- ", return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "⌛ Run the "
					a href="#internal-pause-steps" id="playing-the-media-resource:internal-pause-steps-2" {
						- "internal pause steps"
					}
					- " for the "
					a href="#media-element" id="playing-the-media-resource:media-element-86" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n  "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="seeking" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.9"
			}
			- " Seeking"
			a href="#seeking" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "media"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-media-seeking" id="dom-media-seeking-dev" {
						- "seeking"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns true if the user agent is currently seeking."
				}
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "media"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-media-seekable" id="dom-media-seekable-dev" {
						- "seekable"
					}
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/seekable" title="The seekable read-only property of HTMLMediaElement objects returns a new static normalized TimeRanges object that represents the ranges of the media resource, if any, that the user agent is able to seek to at the time seekable property is accessed." {
								- "HTMLMediaElement/seekable"
							}
						}
						p class="all-engines-text" {
							- "Support in all current engines."
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "8+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "3.1+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span {
									- "Chrome"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge"
								}
								span {
									- "79+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge (Legacy)"
								}
								span {
									- "12+"
								}
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span {
									- "Internet Explorer"
								}
								span {
									- "9+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Firefox Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="safari_ios yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari iOS"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Chrome Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="webview_android yes" {
								span {
									- "WebView Android"
								}
								span {
									- "37+"
								}
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Samsung Internet"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera Android"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns a "
					code id="seeking:timeranges" {
						a href="#timeranges" {
							- "TimeRanges"
						}
					}
					- " object that represents the ranges of the "
					a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource" {
						- "media\n    resource"
					}
					- " to which it is possible for the user agent to seek."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "media"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-media-fastseek" id="dom-media-fastseek-dev" {
						- "fastSeek"
					}
					- "("
					var {
						- "time"
					}
					- ")"
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/fastSeek" title="The HTMLMediaElement.fastSeek() method quickly seeks the media to the new time with precision tradeoff." {
								- "HTMLMediaElement/fastSeek"
							}
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "31+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "8+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome no" {
								span {
									- "Chrome"
								}
								span {
									- "No"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="opera unknown" {
								span {
									- "Opera"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="edge_blink no" {
								span {
									- "Edge"
								}
								span {
									- "No"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="edge unknown" {
								span {
									- "Edge (Legacy)"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="ie no" {
								span {
									- "Internet Explorer"
								}
								span {
									- "No"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Firefox Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="safari_ios unknown" {
								span {
									- "Safari iOS"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Chrome Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="webview_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "WebView Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Samsung Internet"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="opera_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Opera Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Seeks to near the given "
					var {
						- "time"
					}
					- " as fast as possible, trading precision for speed. (To\n    seek to a precise time, use the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-currenttime" {
						a href="#dom-media-currenttime" {
							- "currentTime"
						}
					}
					- "\n    attribute.)"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This does nothing if the media resource has not been loaded."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-seeking" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "seeking"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute must initially have the value false."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-fastseek" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "fastSeek("
					var {
						- "time"
					}
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " method must "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="seeking:dom-media-seek" {
				- "seek"
			}
			- " to the time given by "
			var {
				- "time"
			}
			- ", with the\n  "
			i {
				- "approximate-for-speed"
			}
			- " flag set."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the user agent is required to "
			dfn id="dom-media-seek" {
				- "seek"
			}
			- " to a particular "
			var {
				- "new playback position"
			}
			- " in the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-2" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", optionally with the\n  "
			i {
				- "approximate-for-speed"
			}
			- " flag set, it means that the user agent must run the following steps.\n  This algorithm interacts closely with the "
			a href="#event-loop" id="seeking:event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " mechanism; in particular, it has\n  a "
			a href="#synchronous-section" id="seeking:synchronous-section" {
				- "synchronous section"
			}
			- " (which is triggered as part of the "
			a href="#event-loop" id="seeking:event-loop-2" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- "\n  algorithm). Steps in that section are marked with ⌛."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#show-poster-flag" id="seeking:show-poster-flag" {
						- "show poster flag"
					}
					- " to false."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-2" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- "'s "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-readystate" {
						a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
							- "readyState"
						}
					}
					- "\n   is "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-have_nothing" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" {
							- "HAVE_NOTHING"
						}
					}
					- ", return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element's "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seeking" {
						a href="#dom-media-seeking" {
							- "seeking"
						}
					}
					- " IDL attribute is true,\n   then another instance of this algorithm is already running. Abort that other instance of the\n   algorithm without waiting for the step that it is running to complete."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seeking-2" {
						a href="#dom-media-seeking" {
							- "seeking"
						}
					}
					- " IDL attribute to true."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the seek was in response to a DOM method call or setting of an IDL attribute, then\n   continue the script. The remainder of these steps must be run "
					a href="#in-parallel" id="seeking:in-parallel" {
						- "in parallel"
					}
					- ". With the exception\n   of the steps marked with ⌛, they could be aborted at any time by another instance of this\n   algorithm being invoked."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " is later than the end of the "
					a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-3" {
						- "media\n   resource"
					}
					- ", then let it be the end of the "
					a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-4" {
						- "media resource"
					}
					- " instead."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " is less than the "
					a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="seeking:earliest-possible-position" {
						- "earliest possible\n   position"
					}
					- ", let it be that position instead."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the (possibly now changed) "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " is not in one of\n   the ranges given in the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seekable" {
						a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
							- "seekable"
						}
					}
					- " attribute, then let it\n   be the position in one of the ranges given in the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seekable-2" {
						a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
							- "seekable"
						}
					}
					- " attribute that is the nearest to the "
					var {
						- "new\n   playback position"
					}
					- ". If two positions both satisfy that constraint (i.e. the "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " is exactly in the middle between two ranges in the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seekable-3" {
						a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
							- "seekable"
						}
					}
					- " attribute) then use the position that is closest to\n   the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ". If there are no ranges given in the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seekable-4" {
						a href="#dom-media-seekable" {
							- "seekable"
						}
					}
					- " attribute then set the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seeking-3" {
						a href="#dom-media-seeking" {
							- "seeking"
						}
					}
					- " IDL attribute to false and return."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					i {
						- "approximate-for-speed"
					}
					- " flag is set, adjust the "
					var {
						- "new playback\n    position"
					}
					- " to a value that will allow for playback to resume promptly. If "
					var {
						- "new\n    playback position"
					}
					- " before this step is before "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-2" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ", then\n    the adjusted "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " must also be before the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-3" {
						- "current\n    playback position"
					}
					- ". Similarly, if the "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " before\n    this step is after "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-4" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ", then the adjusted "
					var {
						- "new\n    playback position"
					}
					- " must also be after the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-5" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="example" {
					- "For example, the user agent could snap to a nearby key frame, so that it\n    doesn't have to spend time decoding then discarding intermediate frames before resuming\n    playback."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="seeking:queue-a-media-element-task" {
						- "Queue a media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-3" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " to "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="seeking:concept-event-fire" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="seeking:event-media-seeking" {
						a href="#event-media-seeking" {
							- "seeking"
						}
					}
					- " at the element."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Set the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-6" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- " to the "
					var {
						- "new playback\n    position"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "If the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-4" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " was "
					a href="#potentially-playing" id="seeking:potentially-playing" {
						- "potentially playing"
					}
					- "\n    immediately before it started seeking, but seeking caused its "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-readystate-2" {
						a href="#dom-media-readystate" {
							- "readyState"
						}
					}
					- " attribute to change to a value lower than "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-have_future_data" {
						a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" {
							- "HAVE_FUTURE_DATA"
						}
					}
					- ", then a "
					code id="seeking:event-media-waiting" {
						a href="#event-media-waiting" {
							- "waiting"
						}
					}
					- " event "
					a href="#fire-waiting-when-waiting" {
						- "will be\n    fired"
					}
					- " at the element."
				}
				- " \n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This step sets the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-7" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ", and thus can\n    immediately trigger other conditions, such as the rules regarding when playback \""
					a href="#reaches-the-end" {
						- "reaches the end of the media resource"
					}
					- "\" (part of the logic that\n    handles looping), even before the user agent is actually able to render the media data for that\n    position (as determined in the next step)."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "The "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-currenttime-2" {
						a href="#dom-media-currenttime" {
							- "currentTime"
						}
					}
					- " attribute returns\n    the "
					a href="#official-playback-position" id="seeking:official-playback-position" {
						- "official playback position"
					}
					- ", not the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-8" {
						- "current playback position"
					}
					- ", and\n    therefore gets updated before script execution, separate from this algorithm."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Wait until the user agent has established whether or not the "
					a href="#media-data" id="seeking:media-data" {
						- "media data"
					}
					- " for\n   the "
					var {
						- "new playback position"
					}
					- " is available, and, if it is, until it has decoded\n   enough data to play back that position."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#await-a-stable-state" id="seeking:await-a-stable-state" {
						- "Await a stable state"
					}
					- ". The "
					a href="#synchronous-section" id="seeking:synchronous-section-2" {
						- "synchronous section"
					}
					- " consists of all\n   the remaining steps of this algorithm. (Steps in the "
					a href="#synchronous-section" id="seeking:synchronous-section-3" {
						- "synchronous section"
					}
					- " are marked\n   with ⌛.)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "⌛ Set the "
					code id="seeking:dom-media-seeking-4" {
						a href="#dom-media-seeking" {
							- "seeking"
						}
					}
					- " IDL attribute to\n   false."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "⌛ Run the "
					a href="#time-marches-on" id="seeking:time-marches-on" {
						- "time marches on"
					}
					- " steps."
				}
			}
			li id="seekUpdate" {
				p {
					- "⌛ "
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="seeking:queue-a-media-element-task-2" {
						- "Queue a media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-5" {
						- "media\n   element"
					}
					- " to "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="seeking:concept-event-fire-2" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="seeking:event-media-timeupdate" {
						a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
							- "timeupdate"
						}
					}
					- " at the element."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "⌛ "
					a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id="seeking:queue-a-media-element-task-3" {
						- "Queue a media element task"
					}
					- " given the "
					a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-6" {
						- "media element"
					}
					- " to\n   "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="seeking:concept-event-fire-3" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
						- "fire an event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="seeking:event-media-seeked" {
						a href="#event-media-seeked" {
							- "seeked"
						}
					}
					- " at the element."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-seekable" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "seekable"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must return a new static\n  "
			a href="#normalised-timeranges-object" id="seeking:normalised-timeranges-object" {
				- "normalized "
				code {
					- "TimeRanges"
				}
				- " object"
			}
			- " that represents the ranges of the\n  "
			a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-5" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", if any, that the user agent is able to seek to, at the time the\n  attribute is evaluated."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If the user agent can seek to anywhere in the "
			a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-6" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- ", e.g.\n  because it is a simple movie file and the user agent and the server support HTTP Range requests,\n  then the attribute would return an object with one range, whose start is the time of the first\n  frame (the "
			a href="#earliest-possible-position" id="seeking:earliest-possible-position-2" {
				- "earliest possible position"
			}
			- ", typically zero), and whose end is the same as\n  the time of the first frame plus the "
			code id="seeking:dom-media-duration" {
				a href="#dom-media-duration" {
					- "duration"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's\n  value (which would equal the time of the last frame, and might be positive Infinity)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The range might be continuously changing, e.g. if the user agent is buffering a\n  sliding window on an infinite stream. This is the behavior seen with DVRs viewing live TV, for\n  instance."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="warning" {
			- "Returning a new object each time is a bad pattern for attribute getters and is\n  only enshrined here as it would be costly to change it. It is not to be copied to new APIs."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should adopt a very liberal and optimistic view of what is seekable. User\n  agents should also buffer recent content where possible to enable seeking to be fast."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For instance, consider a large video file served on an HTTP server without\n  support for HTTP Range requests. A browser "
			em {
				- "could"
			}
			- " implement this by only buffering the\n  current frame and data obtained for subsequent frames, never allow seeking, except for seeking to\n  the very start by restarting the playback. However, this would be a poor implementation. A high\n  quality implementation would buffer the last few minutes of content (or more, if sufficient\n  storage space is available), allowing the user to jump back and rewatch something surprising\n  without any latency, and would in addition allow arbitrary seeking by reloading the file from the\n  start if necessary, which would be slower but still more convenient than having to literally\n  restart the video and watch it all the way through just to get to an earlier unbuffered spot."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#media-resource" id="seeking:media-resource-7" {
				- "Media resources"
			}
			- " might be internally scripted or\n  interactive. Thus, a "
			a href="#media-element" id="seeking:media-element-7" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- " could play in a non-linear fashion. If this\n  happens, the user agent must act as if the algorithm for "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="seeking:dom-media-seek-2" {
				- "seeking"
			}
			- " was used whenever the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id="seeking:current-playback-position-9" {
				- "current playback position"
			}
			- "\n  changes in a discontinuous fashion (so that the relevant events fire)."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h5 id="media-resources-with-multiple-media-tracks" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.10"
			}
			- " Media resources with multiple media tracks"
			a href="#media-resources-with-multiple-media-tracks" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#media-resource" id="media-resources-with-multiple-media-tracks:media-resource" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " can have multiple embedded audio and video tracks. For example,\n  in addition to the primary video and audio tracks, a "
			a href="#media-resource" id="media-resources-with-multiple-media-tracks:media-resource-2" {
				- "media resource"
			}
			- " could have\n  foreign-language dubbed dialogues, director's commentaries, audio descriptions, alternative\n  angles, or sign-language overlays."
		}
