		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="best-practices-for-metadata-text-tracks" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.11.7"
			}
			- " Best practices for metadata text tracks"
			a href="#best-practices-for-metadata-text-tracks" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Text tracks can be used for storing data relating to the media data, for interactive or\n  augmented views."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For example, a page showing a sports broadcast could include information about the current\n  score. Suppose a robotics competition was being streamed live. The image could be overlaid with\n  the scores, as follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			iframe src="data:text/html;charset=utf-8,%3C!DOCTYPE%20html%3E%0A%3Cstyle%3E%0A%20body%2C%20html%20%7B%20margin%3A%200%3B%20padding%3A%200%3B%20overflow%3A%20hidden%3B%20%7D%0A%20div%20%7B%20width%3A%20600px%3B%20height%3A%20400px%3B%20position%3A%20relative%3B%20%7D%0A%20p%20%7B%20position%3A%20absolute%3B%20top%3A%200%3B%20margin%3A%200.25em%3B%20font%3A%20small-caps%20900%202em%20sans-serif%3B%20text-shadow%3A%20white%200%200%204px%3B%20%7D%0A%20span%20%7B%20display%3A%20block%3B%20%7D%0A%20.left%20%7B%20color%3A%20red%3B%20left%3A%200%3B%20text-align%3A%20left%3B%20%7D%0A%20.right%20%7B%20color%3A%20blue%3B%20right%3A%200%3B%20text-align%3A%20right%3B%20%7D%0A%20.middle%20%7B%20color%3A%20white%3B%20top%3A%20auto%3B%20bottom%3A%200%3B%20left%3A%200%3B%20right%3A%200%3B%20text-align%3A%20center%3B%20text-shadow%3A%20black%200%200%204px%3B%20%7D%0A%20.middle%20span%20%7B%20display%3A%20inline-block%3B%20margin%3A%200%201em%3B%20font-size%3A%200.75em%3B%20text-transform%3A%20uppercase%3B%20%7D%0A%3C%2Fstyle%3E%0A%3Cdiv%3E%0A%20%3Cimg%20src%3D%22https%3A%2F%2Fhtml.spec.whatwg.org%2Fimages%2Frobots.jpeg%22%3E%0A%20%3Cp%20class%3D%22score%20left%22%3E%3Cspan%3ERed%20Alliance%3C%2Fspan%3E%20%3Cspan%3E78%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%20%3Cp%20class%3D%22score%20right%22%3E%3Cspan%3EBlue%20Alliance%3C%2Fspan%3E%20%3Cspan%3E66%3C%2Fspan%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%20%3Cp%20class%3D%22score%20middle%22%3E%3Cspan%3EQual%20Match%2037%3C%2Fspan%3E%20%3Cspan%3EFriday%2014%3A21%3C%2Fspan%3E%0A%3C%2Fdiv%3E" width="600" height="400"
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		p {
			- "In order to make the score display render correctly whenever the user seeks to an arbitrary\n  point in the video, the metadata text track cues need to be as long as is appropriate for the\n  score. For example, in the frame above, there would be maybe one cue that lasts the length of the\n  match that gives the match number, one cue that lasts until the blue alliance's score changes, and\n  one cue that lasts until the red alliance's score changes. If the video is just a stream of the\n  live event, the time in the bottom right would presumably be automatically derived from the\n  current video time, rather than based on a cue. However, if the video was just the highlights,\n  then that might be given in cues also."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following shows what fragments of this could look like in a WebVTT file:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			- "WEBVTT\n\n...\n\n05:10:00.000 --> 05:12:15.000\nmatchtype:qual\nmatchnumber:37\n\n...\n\n05:11:02.251 --> 05:11:17.198\nred:78\n\n05:11:03.672 --> 05:11:54.198\nblue:66\n\n05:11:17.198 --> 05:11:25.912\nred:80\n\n05:11:25.912 --> 05:11:26.522\nred:83\n\n05:11:26.522 --> 05:11:26.982\nred:86\n\n05:11:26.982 --> 05:11:27.499\nred:89\n\n..."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The key here is to notice that the information is given in cues that span the length of time to\n  which the relevant event applies. If, instead, the scores were given as zero-length (or very\n  brief, nearly zero-length) cues when the score changes, for example saying \"red+2\" at\n  05:11:17.198, \"red+3\" at 05:11:25.912, etc, problems arise: primarily, seeking is much harder to\n  implement, as the script has to walk the entire list of cues to make sure that no notifications\n  have been missed; but also, if the cues are short it's possible the script will never see that\n  they are active unless it listens to them specifically."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When using cues in this manner, authors are encouraged to use the "
			code id="best-practices-for-metadata-text-tracks:event-media-cuechange" {
				a href="#event-media-cuechange" {
					- "cuechange"
				}
			}
			- " event to update the current annotations. (In\n  particular, using the "
			code id="best-practices-for-metadata-text-tracks:event-media-timeupdate" {
				a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
					- "timeupdate"
				}
			}
			- " event would be less\n  appropriate as it would require doing work even when the cues haven't changed, and, more\n  importantly, would introduce a higher latency between when the metadata cues become active and\n  when the display is updated, since "
			code id="best-practices-for-metadata-text-tracks:event-media-timeupdate-2" {
				a href="#event-media-timeupdate" {
					- "timeupdate"
				}
			}
			- " events\n  are rate-limited.)"
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.12"
			}
			- " Identifying a track kind through a URL"
			a href="#identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Other specifications or formats that need a "
			a id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- " to identify the return values of\n  the "
			code id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:audiotrack" {
				a href="#audiotrack" {
					- "AudioTrack"
				}
			}
			- " "
			code id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:dom-audiotrack-kind" {
				a href="#dom-audiotrack-kind" {
					- "kind"
				}
			}
			- " or\n  "
			code id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:videotrack" {
				a href="#videotrack" {
					- "VideoTrack"
				}
			}
			- " "
			code id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:dom-videotrack-kind" {
				a href="#dom-videotrack-kind" {
					- "kind"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attributes, or identify\n  the "
			a href="#text-track-kind" id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:text-track-kind" {
				- "kind of text track"
			}
			- ", must use the\n  "
			code id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:about:html-kind" {
				a href="#about:html-kind" {
					- "about:html-kind"
				}
			}
			- " "
			a id="identifying-a-track-kind-through-a-url:url-2" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="user-interface" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.11.13"
			}
			- " User interface"
			a href="#user-interface" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="audio,video" id="attr-media-controls" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "controls"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="user-interface:boolean-attribute" {
				- "boolean attribute"
			}
			- ".\n  If present, it indicates that the author has not provided a scripted controller and would like the\n  user agent to provide its own set of controls."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the attribute is present, or if "
			a href="#concept-n-noscript" id="user-interface:concept-n-noscript" {
				- "scripting is\n  disabled"
			}
			- " for the "
			a href="#media-element" id="user-interface:media-element" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ", then the user agent should "
			dfn id="expose-a-user-interface-to-the-user" {
				- "expose a user\n  interface to the user"
			}
			- ". This user interface should include features to begin playback, pause\n  playback, seek to an arbitrary position in the content (if the content supports arbitrary\n  seeking), change the volume, change the display of closed captions or embedded sign-language\n  tracks, select different audio tracks or turn on audio descriptions, and show the media content in\n  manners more suitable to the user (e.g. fullscreen video or in an independent resizable window).\n  Other controls may also be made available."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Even when the attribute is absent, however, user agents may provide controls to affect playback\n  of the media resource (e.g. play, pause, seeking, track selection, and volume controls), but such\n  features should not interfere with the page's normal rendering. For example, such features could\n  be exposed in the "
			a href="#media-element" id="user-interface:media-element-2" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s context menu, platform media keys, or a remote\n  control. The user agent may implement this simply by "
			a href="#expose-a-user-interface-to-the-user" id="user-interface:expose-a-user-interface-to-the-user" {
				- "exposing a user interface to the user"
			}
			- " as described above (as if the "
			code id="user-interface:attr-media-controls" {
				a href="#attr-media-controls" {
					- "controls"
				}
			}
			- " attribute was present)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the user agent "
			a href="#expose-a-user-interface-to-the-user" id="user-interface:expose-a-user-interface-to-the-user-2" {
				- "exposes a user interface to\n  the user"
			}
			- " by displaying controls over the "
			a href="#media-element" id="user-interface:media-element-3" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- ", then the user agent\n  should suppress any user interaction events while the user agent is interacting with this\n  interface. (For example, if the user clicks on a video's playback control, "
			code id="user-interface:event-mousedown" {
				a data-x-internal="event-mousedown" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-mousedown" {
					- "mousedown"
				}
			}
			- " events and so forth would not simultaneously be fired at\n  elements on the page.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Where possible (specifically, for starting, stopping, pausing, and unpausing playback, for\n  seeking, for changing the rate of playback, for fast-forwarding or rewinding, for listing,\n  enabling, and disabling text tracks, and for muting or changing the volume of the audio), user\n  interface features exposed by the user agent must be implemented in terms of the DOM API described\n  above, so that, e.g., all the same events fire."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Features such as fast-forward or rewind must be implemented by only changing the "
			code {
				- "playbackRate"
			}
			- " attribute (and not the "
			code {
				- "defaultPlaybackRate"
			}
			- "\n  attribute)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Seeking must be implemented in terms of "
			a href="#dom-media-seek" id="user-interface:dom-media-seek" {
				- "seeking"
			}
			- " to the\n  requested position in the "
			a href="#media-element" id="user-interface:media-element-4" {
				- "media element"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#media-timeline" id="user-interface:media-timeline" {
				- "media timeline"
			}
			- ". For media\n  resources where seeking to an arbitrary position would be slow, user agents are encouraged to use\n  the "
			i {
				- "approximate-for-speed"
			}
			- " flag when seeking in response to the user manipulating an\n  approximate position interface such as a seek bar."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/controls" title="The HTMLMediaElement.controls property reflects the controls HTML attribute, which controls whether user interface controls for playing the media item will be displayed." {
						- "HTMLMediaElement/controls"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "3.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "3.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "3+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "37+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLMediaElement" id="dom-media-controls" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "controls"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute must "
			a href="#reflect" id="user-interface:reflect" {
				- "reflect"
			}
			- " the\n  content attribute of the same name."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "media"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-media-volume" id="dom-media-volume-dev" {
						- "volume"
					}
					- " [ = "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " ]"
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
