			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In other words, the ranges in such an object are ordered, don't overlap, and don't touch\n  (adjacent ranges are folded into one bigger range). A range can be empty (referencing just a\n  single moment in time), e.g. to indicate that only one frame is currently buffered in the case\n  that the user agent has discarded the entire "
