		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="image-map-processing-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.8.14.2"
			}
			- " "
			span id="processing-model"
			- "Processing model"
			a href="#image-map-processing-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If an "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-img-element" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element has a "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-hyperlink-usemap" {
				a href="#attr-hyperlink-usemap" {
					- "usemap"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute specified, user agents must process it as follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Parse the attribute's value using the "
					a href="#rules-for-parsing-a-hash-name-reference" id="image-map-processing-model:rules-for-parsing-a-hash-name-reference" {
						- "rules for parsing a hash-name reference"
					}
					- "\n   to a "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-map-element" {
						a href="#the-map-element" {
							- "map"
						}
					}
					- " element, with the element as the context node. This will return either an\n   element (the "
					var {
						- "map"
					}
					- ") or null."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If that returned null, then return. The image is not associated with an image\n   map after all."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, the user agent must collect all the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " elements that are\n   descendants of the "
					var {
						- "map"
					}
					- ". Let those be the "
					var {
						- "areas"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Having obtained the list of "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-2" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements that form the image map (the "
			var {
				- "areas"
			}
			- "), interactive user agents must process the list in one of two ways."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the user agent intends to show the text that the "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-img-element-2" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element represents, then\n  it must use the following steps."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Remove all the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-3" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " elements in "
					var {
						- "areas"
					}
					- " that have no "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-hyperlink-href" {
						a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
							- "href"
						}
					}
					- " attribute."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Remove all the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-4" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " elements in "
					var {
						- "areas"
					}
					- " that have no "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-alt" {
						a href="#attr-area-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- " attribute, or whose "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-alt-2" {
						a href="#attr-area-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- "\n   attribute's value is the empty string, "
					em {
						- "if"
					}
					- " there is another "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-5" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " element in\n   "
					var {
						- "areas"
					}
					- " with the same value in the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-hyperlink-href-2" {
						a href="#attr-hyperlink-href" {
							- "href"
						}
					}
					- " attribute and with a non-empty "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-alt-3" {
						a href="#attr-area-alt" {
							- "alt"
						}
					}
					- " attribute."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Each remaining "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-6" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " element in "
					var {
						- "areas"
					}
					- " represents a\n   "
					a href="#hyperlink" id="image-map-processing-model:hyperlink" {
						- "hyperlink"
					}
					- ". Those hyperlinks should all be made available to the user in a manner\n   associated with the text of the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-img-element-3" {
						a href="#the-img-element" {
							- "img"
						}
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n   "
				p {
					- "In this context, user agents may represent "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-7" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " and "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-img-element-4" {
						a href="#the-img-element" {
							- "img"
						}
					}
					- " elements\n   with no specified "
					code {
						- "alt"
					}
					- " attributes, or whose "
					code {
						- "alt"
					}
					- "\n   attributes are the empty string or some other non-visible text, in an\n   "
					a id="image-map-processing-model:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
						- "implementation-defined"
					}
					- " fashion intended to indicate the lack of suitable\n   author-provided text."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the user agent intends to show the image and allow interaction with the image to select\n  hyperlinks, then the image must be associated with a set of layered shapes, taken from the\n  "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-8" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " elements in "
			var {
				- "areas"
			}
			- ", in reverse "
			a id="image-map-processing-model:tree-order" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" data-x-internal="tree-order" {
				- "tree order"
			}
			- " (so the last\n  specified "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-9" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " element in the "
			var {
				- "map"
			}
			- " is the bottom-most shape, and\n  the first element in the "
			var {
				- "map"
			}
			- ", in "
			a id="image-map-processing-model:tree-order-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" data-x-internal="tree-order" {
				- "tree order"
			}
			- ", is the top-most shape)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-10" {
				a href="#the-area-element" {
					- "area"
				}
			}
			- " element in "
			var {
				- "areas"
			}
			- " must be processed as follows to\n  obtain a shape to layer onto the image:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Find the state that the element's "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape" {
						a href="#attr-area-shape" {
							- "shape"
						}
					}
					- " attribute\n   represents."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Use the "
					a href="#rules-for-parsing-a-list-of-floating-point-numbers" id="image-map-processing-model:rules-for-parsing-a-list-of-floating-point-numbers" {
						- "rules for parsing a list of floating-point numbers"
					}
					- " to parse the\n   element's "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-coords" {
						a href="#attr-area-coords" {
							- "coords"
						}
					}
					- " attribute, if it is present, and let the\n   result be the "
					var {
						- "coords"
					}
					- " list. If the attribute is absent, let the "
					var {
						- "coords"
					}
					- " list\n   be the empty list."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the number of items in the "
					var {
						- "coords"
					}
					- " list is less than the minimum number\n    given for the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:the-area-element-11" {
						a href="#the-area-element" {
							- "area"
						}
					}
					- " element's current state, as per the following table, then the\n    shape is empty; return."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				table {
					thead {
						tr {
							th {
								- "State\n       "
							}
							th {
								- "Minimum number of items\n     "
							}
						}
					}
					tbody {
						tr {
							td {
								a href="#attr-area-shape-circle" id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-circle" {
									- "Circle state"
								}
								- "\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "3\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								a href="#attr-area-shape-default" id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-default" {
									- "Default state"
								}
								- "\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "0\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								a href="#attr-area-shape-poly" id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-poly" {
									- "Polygon state"
								}
								- "\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "6\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								a href="#attr-area-shape-rect" id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-rect" {
									- "Rectangle state"
								}
								- "\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "4\n    "
							}
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Check for excess items in the "
					var {
						- "coords"
					}
					- " list as per the entry in the\n    following list corresponding to the "
					code id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-2" {
						a href="#attr-area-shape" {
							- "shape"
						}
					}
					- " attribute's\n    state:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				dl class="switch" {
					dt {
						a href="#attr-area-shape-circle" id="image-map-processing-model:attr-area-shape-circle-2" {
							- "Circle state"
						}
					}
