		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-table-element:the-table-element" {
				a href="#the-table-element" {
					- "table"
				}
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="the-table-element:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " data with more than one dimension, in\n  the form of a "
			a href="#concept-table" id="the-table-element:concept-table" {
				- "table"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-table-element:the-table-element-2" {
				a href="#the-table-element" {
					- "table"
				}
			}
			- " element takes part in the "
			a href="#table-model" id="the-table-element:table-model" {
				- "table\n  model"
			}
			- ". Tables have rows, columns, and cells given by their descendants. The rows and\n  columns form a grid; a table's cells must completely cover that grid without overlap."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Precise rules for determining whether this conformance requirement is met are\n  described in the description of the "
			a href="#table-model" id="the-table-element:table-model-2" {
				- "table model"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Authors are encouraged to provide information describing how to interpret complex tables.\n  Guidance on how to "
			a href="#table-descriptions-techniques" {
				- "provide such information"
			}
			- " is given\n  below."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Tables must not be used as layout aids. Historically, some web authors have misused tables in\n  HTML as a way to control their page layout. This usage is non-conforming, because tools attempting\n  to extract tabular data from such documents would obtain very confusing results. In particular,\n  users of accessibility tools like screen readers are likely to find it very difficult to navigate\n  pages with tables used for layout."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "There are a variety of alternatives to using HTML tables for layout, such as CSS\n  grid layout, CSS flexible box layout (\"flexbox\"), CSS multi-column layout, CSS positioning, and\n  the CSS table model. "
			a href="#refsCSS" {
				- "[CSS]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Tables can be complicated to understand and navigate. To help users with this, user agents\n  should clearly delineate cells in a table from each other, unless the user agent has classified\n  the table as a (non-conforming) layout table."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Authors and implementers are encouraged to consider\n  using some of the "
			a href="#table-layout-techniques" {
				- "table design techniques"
			}
			- " described below\n  to make tables easier to navigate for users."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents, especially those that do table analysis on arbitrary content, are encouraged to\n  find heuristics to determine which tables actually contain data and which are merely being used\n  for layout. This specification does not define a precise heuristic, but the following are\n  suggested as possible indicators:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table {
			thead {
				tr {
					th {
						- "Feature\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "Indication\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-aria-role" {
							a href="#attr-aria-role" {
								- "role"
							}
						}
						- " attribute with the value "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-aria-role-presentation" {
							a data-x-internal="attr-aria-role-presentation" href="https://w3c.github.io/aria/#presentation" {
								- "presentation"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a layout table\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the non-conforming "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-table-border" {
							a href="#attr-table-border" {
								- "border"
							}
						}
						- " attribute with the non-conforming value 0\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a layout table\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the non-conforming "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-table-cellspacing" {
							a href="#attr-table-cellspacing" {
								- "cellspacing"
							}
						}
						- " and\n     "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-table-cellpadding" {
							a href="#attr-table-cellpadding" {
								- "cellpadding"
							}
						}
						- " attributes with the value 0\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a layout table\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of "
						code id="the-table-element:the-caption-element-2" {
							a href="#the-caption-element" {
								- "caption"
							}
						}
						- ", "
						code id="the-table-element:the-thead-element-2" {
							a href="#the-thead-element" {
								- "thead"
							}
						}
						- ", or "
						code id="the-table-element:the-th-element" {
							a href="#the-th-element" {
								- "th"
							}
						}
						- " elements\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a non-layout table\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-tdth-headers" {
							a href="#attr-tdth-headers" {
								- "headers"
							}
						}
						- " and "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-th-scope" {
							a href="#attr-th-scope" {
								- "scope"
							}
						}
						- " attributes\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a non-layout table\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the non-conforming "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-table-border-2" {
							a href="#attr-table-border" {
								- "border"
							}
						}
						- " attribute with a value other than 0\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a non-layout table\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "Explicit visible borders set using CSS\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Probably a non-layout table\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						- "The use of the "
						code id="the-table-element:attr-table-summary" {
							a href="#attr-table-summary" {
								- "summary"
							}
						}
						- " attribute\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Not a good indicator (both layout and non-layout tables have historically been given this attribute)\n  "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "It is quite possible that the above suggestions are wrong. Implementers are urged\n  to provide feedback elaborating on their experiences with trying to create a layout table\n  detection heuristic."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If a "
			code id="the-table-element:the-table-element-3" {
				a href="#the-table-element" {
					- "table"
				}
			}
			- " element has a (non-conforming) "
			code id="the-table-element:attr-table-summary-2" {
				a href="#attr-table-summary" {
					- "summary"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, and the user agent has not classified the\n  table as a layout table, the user agent may report the contents of that attribute to the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "table"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-table-caption" id="dom-table-caption-dev" {
						- "caption"
					}
					- " [ = "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " ]"
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLTableElement/caption" title="The HTMLTableElement.caption property represents the table caption. If no caption element is associated with the table, this property is null." {
								- "HTMLTableElement/caption"
							}
						}
						p class="all-engines-text" {
							- "Support in all current engines."
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "1+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
