		- "\n\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="table-descriptions-techniques" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.9.1.1"
			}
			- " Techniques for describing tables"
			a href="#table-descriptions-techniques" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="table-descriptions" {
			- "For tables that consist of more than just a grid of cells with headers\n  in the first row and headers in the first column, and for any table in general where the reader\n  might have difficulty understanding the content, authors should include explanatory information\n  introducing the table. This information is useful for all users, but is especially useful for\n  users who cannot see the table, e.g. users of screen readers."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Such explanatory information should introduce the purpose of the table, outline its basic cell\n  structure, highlight any trends or patterns, and generally teach the user how to use the\n  table."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "For instance, the following table:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table {
			caption {
				- "Characteristics with positive and negative sides"
			}
			thead {
				tr {
					th id="n" {
						- " Negative\n     "
					}
					th {
						- " Characteristic\n     "
					}
					th {
						- " Positive\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td headers="n r1" {
						- " Sad\n     "
					}
					th id="r1" {
						- " Mood\n     "
					}
					td {
						- " Happy\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td headers="n r2" {
						- " Failing\n     "
					}
					th id="r2" {
						- " Grade\n     "
					}
					td {
						- " Passing\n  "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "...might benefit from a description explaining the way the table is laid out, something like\n  \"Characteristics are given in the second column, with the negative side in the left column and the\n  positive side in the right column\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "There are a variety of ways to include this information, such as:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "In prose, surrounding the table"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				div class="example" {
					pre {
						code class="html" {
							strong {
								c- p="" {
									- "<"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "p"
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
								- "In the following table, characteristics are given in the second\ncolumn, with the negative side in the left column and the positive\nside in the right column."
								c- p="" {
									- "</"
								}
								c- f="" {
									- "p"
								}
								c- p="" {
									- ">"
								}
							}
							- "\n"
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "table"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "caption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "Characteristics with positive and negative sides"
							c- p="" {
								- "</"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "caption"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
							- "\n "
							c- p="" {
								- "<"
							}
							c- f="" {
								- "thead"
							}
							c- p="" {
								- ">"
							}
