		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents, especially in non-visual environments or where displaying the table as a 2D grid\n  is impractical, may give the user context for the cell when rendering the contents of a cell; for\n  instance, giving its position in the "
			a href="#table-model" id="the-td-element:table-model-2" {
				- "table model"
			}
			- ", or listing the cell's header cells\n  (as determined by the "
			a href="#algorithm-for-assigning-header-cells" id="the-td-element:algorithm-for-assigning-header-cells" {
				- "algorithm for assigning header cells"
			}
			- "). When a cell's header\n  cells are being listed, user agents may use the value of "
			code id="the-td-element:attr-th-abbr" {
				a href="#attr-th-abbr" {
					- "abbr"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attributes on those header cells, if any, instead of the contents of the header cells\n  themselves."
		}
