		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="introduction-4" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-4" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A form is a component of a web page that has form controls, such as text, buttons, checkboxes,\n  range, or color picker controls. A user can interact with such a form, providing data that can\n  then be sent to the server for further processing (e.g. returning the results of a search or\n  calculation). No client-side scripting is needed in many cases, though an API is available so that\n  scripts can augment the user experience or use forms for purposes other than submitting data to a\n  server."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Writing a form consists of several steps, which can be performed in any order: writing the user\n  interface, implementing the server-side processing, and configuring the user interface to\n  communicate with the server."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="writing-a-form's-user-interface" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.1.1"
			}
			- " Writing a form's user interface"
			a href="#writing-a-form's-user-interface" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purposes of this brief introduction, we will create a pizza ordering form."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Any form starts with a "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-form-element" {
				a href="#the-form-element" {
					- "form"
				}
			}
			- " element, inside which are placed the controls. Most\n  controls are represented by the "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, which by default provides a text\n  control. To label a control, the "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-label-element" {
				a href="#the-label-element" {
					- "label"
				}
			}
			- " element is used; the label text and the\n  control itself go inside the "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-label-element-2" {
				a href="#the-label-element" {
					- "label"
				}
			}
			- " element. Each part of a form is considered a\n  "
			a href="#paragraph" id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:paragraph" {
				- "paragraph"
			}
			- ", and is typically separated from other parts using "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-p-element" {
				a href="#the-p-element" {
					- "p"
				}
			}
			- " elements.\n  Putting this together, here is how one might ask for the customer's name:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="html" {
				strong {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "form"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Customer name: "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
