		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "When a form is submitted, "
			code id="client-side-form-validation:event-invalid" {
				a href="#event-invalid" {
					- "invalid"
				}
			}
			- " events are\n  fired at each form control that is invalid. This can be useful for displaying a summary of the\n  problems with the form, since typically the browser itself will only report one problem at a\n  time."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="enabling-client-side-automatic-filling-of-form-controls" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.1.5"
			}
			- " Enabling client-side automatic filling of form controls"
			a href="#enabling-client-side-automatic-filling-of-form-controls" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some browsers attempt to aid the user by automatically filling form controls rather than having\n  the user reenter their information each time. For example, a field asking for the user's telephone\n  number can be automatically filled with the user's phone number."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To help the user agent with this, the "
			code id="enabling-client-side-automatic-filling-of-form-controls:attr-fe-autocomplete" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" {
					- "autocomplete"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute can be used to describe the field's purpose. In the case of this form, we have three\n  fields that can be usefully annotated in this way: the information about who the pizza is to be\n  delivered to. Adding this information looks like this:"
		}
