		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This requirement is a "
			a href="#willful-violation" id="email-state-(type=email):willful-violation" {
				- "willful violation"
			}
			- " of RFC 5322, which defines a\n  syntax for email addresses that is simultaneously too strict (before the \"@\" character), too\n  vague (after the \"@\" character), and too lax (allowing comments, whitespace characters, and quoted\n  strings in manners unfamiliar to most users) to be of practical use here."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The following JavaScript- and Perl-compatible regular expression is an implementation of the\n   above definition."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				- "/^[a-zA-Z0-9.!#$%&'*+\\/=?^_`{|}~-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?(?:\\.[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*$/"
			}
			- "\n\n   \n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
