		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div id="only-contemporary-times" class="note" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The "
				a href="#date-state-(type=date)" id="date-state-(type=date):date-state-(type=date)-2" {
					- "Date"
				}
				- " state (and other date- and time-related\n   states described in subsequent sections) is not intended for the entry of values for which a\n   precise date and time relative to the contemporary calendar cannot be established. For example,\n   it would be inappropriate for the entry of times like \"one millisecond after the big bang\", \"the\n   early part of the Jurassic period\", or \"a winter around 250 BCE\"."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For the input of dates before the introduction of the Gregorian calendar, authors are\n   encouraged to not use the "
				a href="#date-state-(type=date)" id="date-state-(type=date):date-state-(type=date)-3" {
					- "Date"
				}
				- " state (and the other\n   date- and time-related states described in subsequent sections), as user agents are not required\n   to support converting dates and times from earlier periods to the Gregorian calendar, and asking\n   users to do so manually puts an undue burden on users. (This is complicated by the manner in\n   which the Gregorian calendar was phased in, which occurred at different times in different\n   countries, ranging from partway through the 16th century all the way to early in the 20th.)\n   Instead, authors are encouraged to provide fine-grained input controls using the\n   "
				code id="date-state-(type=date):the-select-element" {
					a href="#the-select-element" {
						- "select"
					}
				}
