		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Here is an example of using a numeric input control:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "How much do you want to charge? $"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "type"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "number"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "min"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "0"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "step"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "0.01"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "name"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "price"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "As described above, a user agent might support numeric input in the user's local format,\n   converting it to the format required for submission as described above. This might include\n   handling grouping separators (as in \"872,000,000,000\") and various decimal separators (such as\n   \"3,99\" vs \"3.99\") or using local digits (such as those in Arabic, Devanagari, Persian, and\n   Thai)."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="when-number-is-not-appropriate" class="note" {
			- "The "
			code {
				- "type=number"
			}
			- " state\n  is not appropriate for input that happens to only consist of numbers but isn't strictly speaking a\n  number. For example, it would be inappropriate for credit card numbers or US postal codes. A\n  simple way of determining whether to use "
			code {
				- "type=number"
			}
			- " is to consider whether\n  it would make sense for the input control to have a spinbox interface (e.g. with \"up\" and \"down\"\n  arrows). Getting a credit card number wrong by 1 in the last digit isn't a minor mistake, it's as\n  wrong as getting every digit incorrect. So it would not make sense for the user to select a credit\n  card number using \"up\" and \"down\" buttons. When a spinbox interface is not appropriate, "
			code {
				- "type=text"
			}
			- " is probably the right choice (possibly with an "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-inputmode" {
				a href="#attr-inputmode" {
					- "inputmode"
				}
			}
			- " or "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-input-pattern-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-pattern" {
					- "pattern"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute)."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="range-state-(type=range)" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.1.13"
			}
			- " "
			dfn data-dfn-for="input" data-dfn-type="element-state" {
				- "Range"
			}
			- " state ("
			code {
				- "type=range"
			}
			- ")"
			a href="#range-state-(type=range)" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/input/range" title="<input> elements of type range let the user specify a numeric value which must be no less than a given value, and no more than another given value. The precise value, however, is not considered important. This is typically represented using a slider or dial control rather than a text entry box like the number input type." {
						- "Element/input/range"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "23+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "3.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "11+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "10+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "52+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "5+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "57+"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "4.4+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "11+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is in\n  the "
			a href="#range-state-(type=range)" id="range-state-(type=range):range-state-(type=range)" {
				- "Range"
			}
			- " state, the rules in this section apply."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="range-state-(type=range):represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " a control for setting the element's\n  "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to a string representing a number, but with the\n  caveat that the exact value is not important, letting UAs provide a simpler interface than they\n  do for the "
			a href="#number-state-(type=number)" id="range-state-(type=range):number-state-(type=number)" {
				- "Number"
			}
			- " state."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the element is "
			i id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-mutable" {
				a href="#concept-fe-mutable" {
					- "mutable"
				}
			}
			- ", the user agent should allow the\n  user to change the number represented by its "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-2" {
				- "value"
			}
			- ", as\n  obtained from applying the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" id="range-state-(type=range):rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" {
				- "rules for parsing floating-point number values"
			}
			- " to it.\n  User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-3" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to a\n  string that is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number" {
				- "valid floating-point number"
			}
			- ". If the user agent provides a user\n  interface for selecting a number, then the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-4" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " must be\n  set to a "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" {
				- "best\n  representation of the number representing the user's selection as a floating-point\n  number"
			}
			- ". User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-5" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to the empty string."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Constraint validation"
			}
			- ": While the user interface describes input that the\n  user agent cannot convert to a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-2" {
				- "valid floating-point number"
			}
			- ", the control is\n  "
			a href="#suffering-from-bad-input" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-bad-input" {
				- "suffering from bad input"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-value" {
				a href="#attr-input-value" {
					- "value"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value\n  that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-3" {
				- "valid floating-point number"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- " \n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#value-sanitization-algorithm" id="range-state-(type=range):value-sanitization-algorithm" {
					- "value sanitization algorithm"
				}
				- " is as follows"
			}
			- ": If the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-6" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " of the element is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-4" {
				- "valid floating-point\n  number"
			}
			- ", then set it to the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number-2" {
				- "best representation, as a floating-point number"
			}
			- ", of the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-default-range" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-default-range" {
				- "default value"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="concept-input-value-default-range" {
				- "default value"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- " plus half the difference between the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-2" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- " and the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- ", unless the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-2" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " is less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-3" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", in which case the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-default-range" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-default-range-2" {
				- "default value"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-4" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-underflow" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-an-underflow" {
				- "suffering from an underflow"
			}
			- ", the user agent must set the\n  element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-7" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number-3" {
				- "best representation, as a floating-point\n  number"
			}
			- ", of the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-5" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-overflow" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-an-overflow" {
				- "suffering from an overflow"
			}
			- ", if the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-3" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " is not less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-6" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", the user agent must set the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-8" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-5" {
				- "valid floating-point number"
			}
			- " that\n  represents the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-4" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" {
				- "suffering from a step mismatch"
			}
			- ", the user agent must round\n  the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-9" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to the nearest number for which the\n  element would not "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch-2" {
				- "suffer from a step\n  mismatch"
			}
			- ", and which is greater than or equal to the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-7" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", and, if the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-5" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " is not less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-8" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", which is less than or equal to the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-6" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- ", if there is a number that matches these constraints.\n  If two numbers match these constraints, then user agents must use the one nearest to positive\n  infinity."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, the markup\n  "
			code {
				- "<input type=\"range\" min=0 max=100 step=20 value=50>"
			}
			- "\n  results in a range control whose initial value is 60."
		}
