			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents may use the value of this attribute to display a more appropriate user interface\n  than a generic file picker. For instance, given the value "
			code {
				- "image/*"
			}
			- ", a user\n  agent could offer the user the option of using a local camera or selecting a photograph from their\n  photo collection; given the value "
			code {
				- "audio/*"
			}
			- ", a user agent could offer the user\n  the option of recording a clip using a headset microphone."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should prevent the user from selecting files that are not accepted by one (or more)\n  of these tokens."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Authors are encouraged to specify both any MIME types and any corresponding\n  extensions when looking for data in a specific format."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, consider an application that converts Microsoft Word documents to Open Document\n   Format files. Since Microsoft Word documents are described with a wide variety of MIME types and\n   extensions, the site can list several, as follows:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
