		- "\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="input-impl-notes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.2"
			}
			- " Implementation notes regarding localization of form controls"
			a href="#input-impl-notes" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The formats shown to the user in date, time, and number controls is independent of the format\n  used for form submission."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browsers are encouraged to use user interfaces that present dates, times, and numbers according\n  to the conventions of either the locale implied by the "
			code id="input-impl-notes:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element's\n  "
			a href="#language" id="input-impl-notes:language" {
				- "language"
			}
			- " or the user's preferred locale. Using the page's locale will ensure\n  consistency with page-provided data.\n\n  "
		}
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, it would be confusing to users if an American English page claimed\n  that a Cirque De Soleil show was going to be showing on 02/03, but their\n  browser, configured to use the British English locale, only showed the date 03/02 in the ticket purchase date picker. Using the page's locale would at least ensure that the\n  date was presented in the same format everywhere. (There's still a risk that the user would end up\n  arriving a month late, of course, but there's only so much that can be done about such cultural\n  differences...)"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="common-input-element-attributes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.3"
			}
			- " Common "
			code id="common-input-element-attributes:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element attributes"
			a href="#common-input-element-attributes" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "These attributes only "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-attributes:concept-input-apply" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- " to an "
			code id="common-input-element-attributes:the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element if its "
			code id="common-input-element-attributes:attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is in a state whose definition\n  declares that the attribute "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-attributes:concept-input-apply-2" {
				- "applies"
			}
			- ". When an attribute\n  "
			a href="#do-not-apply" id="common-input-element-attributes:do-not-apply" {
				- "doesn't apply"
			}
			- " to an "
			code id="common-input-element-attributes:the-input-element-3" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, user agents must\n  "
			a href="#ignore" id="common-input-element-attributes:ignore" {
				- "ignore"
			}
			- " the attribute, regardless of the requirements and definitions below."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h6 id="the-maxlength-and-minlength-attributes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.3.1"
			}
			- " The "
			code id="the-maxlength-and-minlength-attributes:attr-input-maxlength" {
