		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some form controls can have explicit constraints applied limiting the allowed range of values\n  that the user can provide. Normally, such a range would be linear and continuous. A form control\n  can "
			dfn id="has-a-periodic-domain" {
				- "have a periodic domain"
			}
			- ", however, in which case the\n  form control's broadest possible range is finite, and authors can specify explicit ranges within\n  it that span the boundaries."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "Specifically, the broadest range of a "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:time-state-(type=time)" {
				a href="#time-state-(type=time)" {
					- "type=time"
				}
			}
			- " control is midnight to midnight (24 hours), and\n  authors can set both continuous linear ranges (such as 9pm to 11pm) and discontinuous ranges\n  spanning midnight (such as 11pm to 1am)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="input" id="attr-input-min" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for="input" id="attr-input-max" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attributes indicate the\n  allowed range of values for the element."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Their syntax is defined by the section that defines the "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's current state."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the element has a "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, and the result of\n  applying the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-value-string-number" {
				- "algorithm to convert a string to a\n  number"
			}
			- " to the value of the "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-3" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a number,\n  then that number is the element's "
			dfn id="concept-input-min" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "; otherwise, if the\n  "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-type-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's current state defines a "
			dfn id="concept-input-min-default" {
				- "default minimum"
			}
			- ", then that is the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "; otherwise, the element has no "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min-2" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-4" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute also defines the "
			a href="#concept-input-min-zero" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min-zero" {
				- "step base"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the element has a "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-max" {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, and the result of\n  applying the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-value-string-number-2" {
				- "algorithm to convert a string to a\n  number"
			}
			- " to the value of the "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-3" {
				a href="#attr-input-max" {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a number,\n  then that number is the element's "
			dfn id="concept-input-max" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- "; otherwise, if the\n  "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-type-3" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's current state defines a "
			dfn id="concept-input-max-default" {
				- "default maximum"
			}
			- ", then that is the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-max" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- "; otherwise, the element has no "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-max-2" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the element does not "
			a href="#has-a-periodic-domain" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-periodic-domain" {
				- "have a periodic domain"
			}
			- ", the\n  "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-4" {
				a href="#attr-input-max" {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value (the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-max-3" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- ") must not be less than the "
			code id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-5" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's value (its "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min-3" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ")."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If an element that does not "
			a href="#has-a-periodic-domain" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-periodic-domain-2" {
				- "have a periodic\n  domain"
			}
			- " has a "
			a href="#attr-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-5" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " that is less than its "
			a href="#attr-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-6" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", then so long as the element has a "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-fe-value" {
				- "value"
			}
			- ", it will either be "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-underflow" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:suffering-from-an-underflow" {
				- "suffering from an underflow"
			}
			- "\n  or "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-overflow" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:suffering-from-an-overflow" {
				- "suffering from an overflow"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An element "
			dfn id="has-a-reversed-range" {
				- "has a reversed range"
			}
			- " if it "
			a href="#has-a-periodic-domain" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-periodic-domain-3" {
				- "has a periodic domain"
			}
			- " and its\n  "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-max-4" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " is less than its "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min-4" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "An element "
			dfn id="have-range-limitations" {
				- "has range limitations"
			}
			- " if it has a defined\n  "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-min-5" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- " or a defined "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-max-5" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Constraint validation"
			}
			- ": When the element has a "
			a href="#attr-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-7" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- " and does not "
			a href="#has-a-reversed-range" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-reversed-range" {
				- "have a\n  reversed range"
			}
			- ", and the result of applying the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-value-string-number-3" {
				- "algorithm to convert a string to a number"
			}
			- " to\n  the string given by the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-fe-value-2" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " is a number, and\n  the number obtained from that algorithm is less than the "
			a href="#attr-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-8" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-underflow" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:suffering-from-an-underflow-2" {
				- "suffering from an\n  underflow"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Constraint validation"
			}
			- ": When the element has a "
			a href="#attr-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-6" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " and does not "
			a href="#has-a-reversed-range" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-reversed-range-2" {
				- "have a\n  reversed range"
			}
			- ", and the result of applying the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-value-string-number-4" {
				- "algorithm to convert a string to a number"
			}
			- " to\n  the string given by the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-fe-value-3" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " is a number, and\n  the number obtained from that algorithm is more than the "
			a href="#attr-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-7" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- ", the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-overflow" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:suffering-from-an-overflow-2" {
				- "suffering from an\n  overflow"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Constraint validation"
			}
			- ": When an element "
			a href="#has-a-reversed-range" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:has-a-reversed-range-3" {
				- "has a reversed range"
			}
			- ",\n  and the result of applying the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-input-value-string-number-5" {
				- "algorithm to\n  convert a string to a number"
			}
			- " to the string given by the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:concept-fe-value-4" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " is a number, and the number obtained from that algorithm\n  is more than the "
			a href="#attr-input-max" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-max-8" {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " "
			em {
				- "and"
			}
			- " less than the "
			a href="#attr-input-min" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:attr-input-min-9" {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- ", the element is simultaneously "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-underflow" id="the-min-and-max-attributes:suffering-from-an-underflow-3" {
				- "suffering from an\n  underflow"
			}
			- " and "
