			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Normally, time controls are limited to an accuracy of one minute."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h6 id="the-list-attribute" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.3.9"
			}
			- " The "
			code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-list" {
				a href="#attr-input-list" {
					- "list"
				}
			}
			- " attribute"
			a href="#the-list-attribute" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/input#list" title="The <input> HTML element is used to create interactive controls for web-based forms in order to accept data from the user; a wide variety of types of input data and control widgets are available, depending on the device and user agent. The <input> element is one of the most powerful and complex in all of HTML due to the sheer number of combinations of input types and attributes." {
						- "Element/input#list"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "20+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "10+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "4.4.3+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "12.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="input" id="attr-input-list" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "list"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is\n  used to identify an element that lists predefined options suggested to the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If present, its value must be the "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="the-list-attribute:concept-id" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
				- "ID"
			}
			- " of a "
			code id="the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element" {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" {
					- "datalist"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element in the same "
			a id="the-list-attribute:tree" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" data-x-internal="tree" {
				- "tree"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="concept-input-list" {
				- "suggestions source element"
			}
			- " is the first element in\n  the "
			a id="the-list-attribute:tree-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" data-x-internal="tree" {
				- "tree"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="the-list-attribute:tree-order" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" data-x-internal="tree-order" {
				- "tree order"
			}
			- " to have an "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="the-list-attribute:concept-id-2" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
				- "ID"
			}
			- "\n  equal to the value of the "
			code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-list-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-list" {
					- "list"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, if that element\n  is a "
			code id="the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-2" {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" {
					- "datalist"
				}
			}
			- " element. If there is no "
			code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-list-3" {
				a href="#attr-input-list" {
					- "list"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, or if there is no element with that "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="the-list-attribute:concept-id-3" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
				- "ID"
			}
			- ", or if the\n  first element with that "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id="the-list-attribute:concept-id-4" data-x-internal="concept-id" {
				- "ID"
			}
			- " is not a "
			code id="the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-3" {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" {
					- "datalist"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element, then there is no "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id="the-list-attribute:concept-input-list" {
				- "suggestions source\n  element"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If there is a "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id="the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-2" {
				- "suggestions source element"
			}
			- ", then, when\n  the user agent is allowing the user to edit the "
			code id="the-list-attribute:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-fe-value" {
				- "value"
			}
			- ", the user agent should offer the suggestions represented by\n  the "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id="the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-3" {
				- "suggestions source element"
			}
			- " to the user in a manner\n  suitable for the type of control used. If appropriate, the user agent should use the suggestion's\n  "
			a href="#concept-option-label" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-label" {
				- "label"
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to identify the suggestion to the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents are encouraged to filter the suggestions represented by the "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id="the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-4" {
				- "suggestions source element"
			}
			- " when the number of suggestions is\n  large, including only the most relevant ones (e.g. based on the user's input so far). No precise\n  threshold is defined, but capping the list at four to seven values is reasonable. If filtering\n  based on the user's input, user agents should search within both the "
			a href="#concept-option-label" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-label-2" {
				- "label"
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-2" {
				- "value"
			}
			- "\n  of the suggestions for matches. User agents should consider how input variations affect the\n  matching process. Unicode normalization should be applied so that different underlying Unicode\n  code point sequences, caused by different keyboard- or input-specific mechanisms, do not\n  interfere with the matching process. Case variations should be ignored, which may require\n  language-specific case mapping. For examples of these, see "
			cite {
				- "Character Model for the World\n  Wide Web: String Matching"
			}
			- ". User agents may also provide other matching features: for\n  illustration, a few examples include matching different forms of kana to each other (or to kanji),\n  ignoring accents, or applying spelling correction. "
			a href="#refsCHARMODNORM" {
				- "[CHARMODNORM]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "This text field allows you to choose a type of JavaScript function."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "type"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"text\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "list"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"function-types\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
