			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For user agents that follow the above suggestions, both the "
				a href="#concept-option-label" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-label-3" {
					- "label"
				}
				- " and "
				a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-3" {
					- "value"
				}
				- "\n   would be shown:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				img class="darkmode-aware" src="/images/sample-datalist.svg" width="280" alt="A text box with a drop down button on the right hand side; with, below, a drop down box containing a list of the six values the left and the six labels on the right." height="150"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Then, typing \""
				kbd {
					- "arrow"
				}
				- "\" or \""
				kbd {
					- "=>"
				}
				- "\" would filter the list to the entries with\n   labels \"arrow function\" and \"async arrow function\". Typing \""
				kbd {
					- "generator"
				}
				- "\" or\n   \""
				kbd {
					- "*"
				}
				- "\" would filter the list to the entries with labels \"generator function\" and \"async\n   generator function\"."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "As always, user agents are free to make user interface decisions which are\n  appropriate for their particular requirements and for the user's particular circumstances. However,\n  this has historically been an area of confusion for implementers, web developers, and users alike,\n  so we've given some \"should\" suggestions above."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		p {
			- "How user selections of suggestions are handled depends on whether the element is a control\n  accepting a single value only, or whether it accepts multiple values:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="switch" {
			dt {
				- "If the element does not have a "
				code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple" {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" {
						- "multiple"
					}
				}
				- " attribute\n   specified or if the "
				code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple-2" {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" {
						- "multiple"
					}
				}
				- " attribute "
				a href="#do-not-apply" id="the-list-attribute:do-not-apply" {
					- "does not apply"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When the user selects a suggestion, the "
					code id="the-list-attribute:the-input-element-2" {
						a href="#the-input-element" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-fe-value-2" {
						- "value"
					}
					- " must be set to the selected suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-4" {
						- "value"
					}
					- ", as if the user had written that value themself."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "If the element's "
				code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-type" {
					a href="#attr-input-type" {
						- "type"
					}
				}
				- " attribute is in the "
				a href="#email-state-(type=email)" id="the-list-attribute:email-state-(type=email)" {
					- "Email"
				}
				- " state and the element has a "
				code id="the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple-3" {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" {
						- "multiple"
					}
				}
				- " attribute specified"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When the user selects a suggestion, the user agent must either add a new entry to the\n    "
					code id="the-list-attribute:the-input-element-3" {
						a href="#the-input-element" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="the-list-attribute:concept-fe-values" {
						- "values"
					}
					- ", whose value\n    is the selected suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-5" {
						- "value"
					}
					- ", or change an\n    existing entry in the "
					code id="the-list-attribute:the-input-element-4" {
						a href="#the-input-element" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="the-list-attribute:concept-fe-values-2" {
						- "values"
					}
					- " to have the value given by the selected\n    suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id="the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-6" {
						- "value"
					}
					- ", as if the user had themself added\n    an entry with that value, or edited an existing entry to be that value. Which behavior is to be\n    applied depends on the user interface in an "
					a id="the-list-attribute:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
						- "implementation-defined"
					}
					- " manner."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
