		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This example demonstrates how to design a form that uses the autocompletion list feature while\n   still degrading usefully in legacy user agents."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the autocompletion list is merely an aid, and is not important to the content, then simply\n   using a "
				code id="the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-4" {
					a href="#the-datalist-element" {
						- "datalist"
					}
				}
				- " element with children "
				code id="the-list-attribute:the-option-element" {
					a href="#the-option-element" {
						- "option"
					}
				}
				- " elements is enough. To\n   prevent the values from being rendered in legacy user agents, they need to be placed inside the\n   "
				code id="the-list-attribute:attr-option-value" {
					a href="#attr-option-value" {
						- "value"
					}
				}
				- " attribute instead of inline."
			}
