			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " does not "
					a href="#input-support-picker" id="common-input-element-apis:input-support-picker-2" {
						- "support a\n   picker"
					}
					- ", then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " is an "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:the-input-element-12" {
						a href="#the-input-element" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " element and "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "'s "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:attr-input-type-9" {
						a href="#attr-input-type" {
							- "type"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is in the "
					a href="#file-upload-state-(type=file)" id="common-input-element-apis:file-upload-state-(type=file)-4" {
						- "File Upload"
					}
					- " state, then run these steps "
					a href="#in-parallel" id="common-input-element-apis:in-parallel" {
						- "in\n    parallel"
					}
					- ":"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Optionally, wait until any prior execution of this algorithm has terminated."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Display a prompt to the user requesting that the user specify some files. If the "
							code id="common-input-element-apis:attr-input-multiple" {
								a href="#attr-input-multiple" {
									- "multiple"
								}
							}
							- " attribute is not set on "
							var {
								- "element"
							}
							- ", there\n     must be no more than one file selected; otherwise, any number may be selected. Files can be\n     from the filesystem or created on the fly, e.g., a picture taken from a camera connected to the\n     user's device."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Wait for the user to have made their selection."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If the user dismissed the prompt without changing their selection, then "
							a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-apis:queue-an-element-task" {
								- "queue an\n     element task"
							}
							- " on the "
							a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-apis:user-interaction-task-source" {
								- "user interaction task source"
							}
							- " given "
							var {
								- "element"
							}
							- "\n     to "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-apis:concept-event-fire" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
								- "fire an event"
							}
							- " named "
							code id="common-input-element-apis:event-cancel" {
								a href="#event-cancel" {
									- "cancel"
								}
							}
							- " at "
							var {
								- "element"
							}
							- ", with the "
							code id="common-input-element-apis:dom-event-bubbles" {
								a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
									- "bubbles"
								}
							}
							- " attribute initialized to true."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Otherwise, "
							a href="#update-the-file-selection" id="common-input-element-apis:update-the-file-selection" {
								- "update the file selection"
							}
							- " for "
							var {
								- "element"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "As with all user interface specifications, user agents have a good deal of\n    freedom in how they interpret these requirements. The above text implies that a user either\n    dismisses the prompt or changes their selection; exactly one of these will be true. But the\n    mapping of these possibilities to specific user interface elements is not mandated by the\n    standard. For example, a user agent might interpret clicking the \"Cancel\" button when files were\n    previously selected as a change of selection to select zero files, thus firing "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-input" {
						a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " and "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-change" {
						a href="#event-change" {
							- "change"
						}
					}
					- ". Or it might\n    interpret such a click as a dismissal that leaves the selection unchanged, thus firing "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-cancel-2" {
						a href="#event-cancel" {
							- "cancel"
						}
					}
					- ". Similarly, it's up to the user agent whether re-selecting\n    the same files as were previously selected counts as a dismissal, or as a change of\n    selection."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Otherwise, the user agent should show the relevant user interface for selecting a value for\n    "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- ", in the way it normally would when the user interacts with the control."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "When showing such a user interface, it must respect the requirements stated in the relevant\n    parts of the specification for how "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " behaves given its "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:attr-input-type-10" {
						a href="#attr-input-type" {
							- "type"
						}
					}
					- " attribute state. (For example, various sections describe\n    restrictions on the resulting "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-apis:concept-fe-value-21" {
						- "value"
					}
					- " string.)"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This step can have side effects, such as closing other pickers that were previously shown by\n    this algorithm. (If this closes a file selection picker, then per the above that will lead to\n    firing either "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-input-2" {
						a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " and "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-change-2" {
						a href="#event-change" {
							- "change"
						}
					}
					- " events, or a "
					code id="common-input-element-apis:event-cancel-3" {
						a href="#event-cancel" {
							- "cancel"
						}
					}
					- "\n    event.)"
