		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="common-input-element-events" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.5.5"
			}
			- " Common event behaviors"
			a href="#common-input-element-events" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- " events "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-events:concept-input-apply" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- "\n  (which is the case for all "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " controls other than "
			a href="#concept-button" id="common-input-element-events:concept-button" {
				- "buttons"
			}
			- " and those with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute in the "
			a href="#hidden-state-(type=hidden)" id="common-input-element-events:hidden-state-(type=hidden)" {
				- "Hidden"
			}
			- " state), the events are fired to indicate that the\n  user has interacted with the control. The "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-2" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " event fires\n  whenever the user has modified the data of the control. The "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-2" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- " event fires when the value is committed, if that makes sense\n  for the control, or else when the control "
			a href="#unfocus-causes-change-event" {
				- "loses focus"
			}
			- ".\n  In all cases, the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-3" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " event comes before the corresponding\n  "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-3" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- " event (if any)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element has a defined "
			a href="#input-activation-behavior" id="common-input-element-events:input-activation-behavior" {
				- "input activation behavior"
			}
			- ", the\n  rules for dispatching these events, if they "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-events:concept-input-apply-2" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- ", are\n  given in the section above that defines the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:attr-input-type-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's\n  state. (This is the case for all "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-3" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " controls with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:attr-input-type-3" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute in the "
			a href="#checkbox-state-(type=checkbox)" id="common-input-element-events:checkbox-state-(type=checkbox)" {
				- "Checkbox"
			}
			- " state, the "
			a href="#radio-button-state-(type=radio)" id="common-input-element-events:radio-button-state-(type=radio)" {
				- "Radio Button"
			}
			- " state, or the "
			a href="#file-upload-state-(type=file)" id="common-input-element-events:file-upload-state-(type=file)" {
				- "File Upload"
			}
			- " state.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-4" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " elements without a defined "
			a href="#input-activation-behavior" id="common-input-element-events:input-activation-behavior-2" {
				- "input activation behavior"
			}
			- ", but\n  to which these events "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-events:concept-input-apply-3" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- ", and for which the user\n  interface involves both interactive manipulation and an explicit commit action, then when the\n  user changes the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value" {
				- "value"
			}
			- ", the user agent must\n  "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task" {
				- "queue an element task"
			}
			- " on the "
			a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-events:user-interaction-task-source" {
				- "user interaction task source"
			}
			- " given the\n  "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-5" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-4" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-6" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-composed" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-composed" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-composed" {
					- "composed"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attributes initialized to true, and any time the user commits the change, the user agent must\n  "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task-2" {
				- "queue an element task"
			}
			- " on the "
			a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-events:user-interaction-task-source-2" {
				- "user interaction task source"
			}
			- " given the\n  "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-7" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to set its "
			a href="#user-validity" id="common-input-element-events:user-validity" {
				- "user validity"
			}
			- " to true and "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-2" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-4" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- "\n  at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-8" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-2" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute initialized to true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "An example of a user interface involving both interactive manipulation and a\n  commit action would be a "
			a href="#range-state-(type=range)" id="common-input-element-events:range-state-(type=range)" {
				- "Range"
			}
			- " controls that use a\n  slider, when manipulated using a pointing device. While the user is dragging the control's knob,\n  "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-5" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " events would fire whenever the position changed,\n  whereas the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-5" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- " event would only fire when the user\n  let go of the knob, committing to a specific value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-9" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " elements without a defined "
			a href="#input-activation-behavior" id="common-input-element-events:input-activation-behavior-3" {
				- "input activation behavior"
			}
			- ", but\n  to which these events "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-events:concept-input-apply-4" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- ", and for which the user\n  interface involves an explicit commit action but no intermediate manipulation, then any time the\n  user commits a change to the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-2" {
				- "value"
			}
			- ", the user\n  agent must "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task-3" {
				- "queue an element task"
			}
			- " on the "
			a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-events:user-interaction-task-source-3" {
				- "user interaction task source"
			}
			- "\n  given the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-10" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to first "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-3" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an\n  event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-6" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-11" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with\n  the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-3" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-composed-2" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-composed" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-composed" {
					- "composed"
				}
			}
			- " attributes initialized to true, and then "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-4" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-6" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- "\n  at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-12" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-4" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute initialized to true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "An example of a user interface with a commit action would be a "
			a href="#color-state-(type=color)" id="common-input-element-events:color-state-(type=color)" {
				- "Color"
			}
			- " control that consists of a single button that brings\n  up a color wheel: if the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-3" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " only changes when the dialog\n  is closed, then that would be the explicit commit action. On the other hand, if manipulating the\n  control changes the color interactively, then there might be no commit action."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "Another example of a user interface with a commit action would be a "
			a href="#date-state-(type=date)" id="common-input-element-events:date-state-(type=date)" {
				- "Date"
			}
			- " control that allows both text-based user input and user\n  selection from a drop-down calendar: while text input might not have an explicit commit step,\n  selecting a date from the drop down calendar and then dismissing the drop down would be a commit\n  action."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-13" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " elements without a defined "
			a href="#input-activation-behavior" id="common-input-element-events:input-activation-behavior-4" {
				- "input activation behavior"
			}
			- ", but\n  to which these events "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="common-input-element-events:concept-input-apply-5" {
				- "apply"
			}
			- ", any time the user causes\n  the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-4" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " to change without an explicit commit\n  action, the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task-4" {
				- "queue an element task"
			}
			- " on the "
			a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-events:user-interaction-task-source-4" {
				- "user interaction task\n  source"
			}
			- " given the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-14" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-5" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an\n  event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-7" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-15" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with\n  the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-5" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-composed-3" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-composed" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-composed" {
					- "composed"
				}
			}
			- " attributes initialized to true. The corresponding\n  "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-7" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- " event, if any, will be fired when the control "
			a href="#unfocus-causes-change-event" {
				- "loses focus"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "Examples of a user changing the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-5" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " would include the user typing into a text control, pasting\n  a new value into the control, or undoing an edit in that control. Some user interactions do not\n  cause changes to the value, e.g., hitting the \"delete\" key in an empty text control, or replacing\n  some text in the control with text from the clipboard that happens to be exactly the same\n  text."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "A "
			a href="#range-state-(type=range)" id="common-input-element-events:range-state-(type=range)-2" {
				- "Range"
			}
			- " control in the form of a\n  slider that the user has "
			a href="#focused" id="common-input-element-events:focused" {
				- "focused"
			}
			- " and is interacting with using a keyboard would be\n  another example of the user changing the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-6" {
				- "value"
			}
			- "\n  without a commit step."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In the case of "
			a href="#concept-task" id="common-input-element-events:concept-task" {
				- "tasks"
			}
			- " that just fire an "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-8" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " event, user agents may wait for a suitable break in the user's\n  interaction before "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task-5" {
				- "queuing"
			}
			- " the tasks; for example, a\n  user agent could wait for the user to have not hit a key for 100ms, so as to only fire the event\n  when the user pauses, instead of continuously for each keystroke. \n\n  "
		}
		p {
			- "When the user agent is to change an "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-16" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-7" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " on behalf of the user (e.g. as part of a form prefilling\n  feature), the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-an-element-task" id="common-input-element-events:queue-an-element-task-6" {
				- "queue an element task"
			}
			- " on the "
			a href="#user-interaction-task-source" id="common-input-element-events:user-interaction-task-source-5" {
				- "user interaction\n  task source"
			}
			- " given the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-17" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to first update the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="common-input-element-events:concept-fe-value-8" {
				- "value"
			}
			- " accordingly, then "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-6" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an\n  event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-input-9" {
				a data-x-internal="event-input" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-input" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-18" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with\n  the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-6" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-composed-4" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-composed" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-composed" {
					- "composed"
				}
			}
			- " attributes initialized to true, then "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id="common-input-element-events:concept-event-fire-7" data-x-internal="concept-event-fire" {
				- "fire an event"
			}
			- " named "
			code id="common-input-element-events:event-change-8" {
				a href="#event-change" {
					- "change"
				}
			}
			- "\n  at the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:the-input-element-19" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element, with the "
			code id="common-input-element-events:dom-event-bubbles-7" {
				a data-x-internal="dom-event-bubbles" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-bubbles" {
					- "bubbles"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute initialized to true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "These events are not fired in response to changes made to the values of form\n  controls by scripts. (This is to make it easier to update the values of form controls in response\n  to the user manipulating the controls, without having to then filter out the script's own changes\n  to avoid an infinite loop.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "These events are also not fired when the browser changes the values of form\n  controls as part of "
			a href="#restore-persisted-state" id="common-input-element-events:restore-persisted-state" {
				- "state restoration during\n  navigation"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-button-element" {
