		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-meter-element:the-meter-element-2" {
				a href="#the-meter-element" {
					- "meter"
				}
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="the-meter-element:represents" {
				- "represents"
			}
			- " a scalar measurement within a known\n  range, or a fractional value; for example disk usage, the relevance of a query result, or the\n  fraction of a voting population to have selected a particular candidate."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This is also known as a gauge."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-meter-element:the-meter-element-3" {
				a href="#the-meter-element" {
					- "meter"
				}
			}
			- " element should not be used to indicate progress (as in a progress bar).\n  For that role, HTML provides a separate "
			code id="the-meter-element:the-progress-element" {
				a href="#the-progress-element" {
					- "progress"
				}
			}
			- " element."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="the-meter-element:the-meter-element-4" {
				a href="#the-meter-element" {
					- "meter"
				}
			}
			- " element also does not represent a scalar value of arbitrary\n  range — for example, it would be wrong to use this to report a weight, or height, unless\n  there is a known maximum value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "There are six attributes that determine the semantics of the gauge represented by the\n  element."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
