		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-min" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  specifies the lower bound of the range, and the "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-max" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attribute specifies the upper bound. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-value" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "value"
				}
			}
			- " attribute specifies\n  the value to have the gauge indicate as the \"measured\" value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The other three attributes can be used to segment the gauge's range into \"low\", \"medium\", and\n  \"high\" parts, and to indicate which part of the gauge is the \"optimum\" part. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-low" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "low"
				}
			}
			- " attribute specifies the range that is\n  considered to be the \"low\" part, and the "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-high" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "high"
				}
			}
			- " attribute specifies the range that is considered to be\n  the \"high\" part. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="meter" id="attr-meter-optimum" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "optimum"
				}
			}
			- " attribute gives the position that is \"optimum\";\n  if that is higher than the \"high\" value then this indicates that the higher the value, the better;\n  if it's lower than the \"low\" mark then it indicates that lower values are better, and naturally if\n  it is in between then it indicates that neither high nor low values are good."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Authoring requirements"
			}
			- ": The "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" {
					- "value"
				}
			}
			- " attribute must be specified. The "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-3" {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" {
					- "value"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-low" {
					- "low"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-high" {
					- "high"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-max" {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-2" {
				a href="#attr-meter-optimum" {
					- "optimum"
				}
			}
			- " attributes,\n  when present, must have values that are "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="the-meter-element:valid-floating-point-number" {
				- "valid\n  floating-point numbers"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In addition, the attributes' values are further constrained:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Let "
			var {
				- "value"
			}
			- " be the "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-4" {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" {
					- "value"
				}
			}
			- " attribute's\n  number."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-3" {
				a href="#attr-meter-min" {
					- "min"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is specified, then let "
			var {
				- "minimum"
			}
			- " be that attribute's value; otherwise, let it be zero."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-3" {
				a href="#attr-meter-max" {
					- "max"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is specified, then let "
			var {
				- "maximum"
			}
			- " be that attribute's value; otherwise, let it be 1.0."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following inequalities must hold, as applicable:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					var {
						- "minimum"
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var {
						- "maximum"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					var {
						- "minimum"
					}
					- " ≤ "
					code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-3" {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" {
							- "low"
						}
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var {
						- "maximum"
					}
					- "\n   (if "
					code id="the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-4" {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" {
							- "low"
						}
					}
					- " is specified)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					var {
						- "minimum"
					}
					- " ≤ "
