				- " of \"e\" would be the outer form \"a\"."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This happens as follows: First, the \"e\" node gets associated with \"c\" in the "
				a href="#html-parser" id="association-of-controls-and-forms:html-parser" {
					- "HTML\n   parser"
				}
				- ". Then, the "
				code id="association-of-controls-and-forms:dom-element-innerhtml" {
					a href="#dom-element-innerhtml" {
						- "innerHTML"
					}
				}
				- " algorithm moves the nodes\n   from the temporary document to the \"b\" element. At this point, the nodes see their ancestor chain\n   change, and thus all the \"magic\" associations done by the parser are reset to normal ancestor\n   associations."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This example is a non-conforming document, though, as it is a violation of the content models\n   to nest "
				code id="association-of-controls-and-forms:the-form-element-13" {
