				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Optionally, a token that is an "
					a id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:ascii-case-insensitive-8" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
						- "ASCII case-insensitive"
					}
					- " match for the string\n   \""
					dfn id="attr-fe-autocomplete-webauthn" {
						code {
							- "webauthn"
						}
					}
					- "\", meaning the user agent\n   should show "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#public-key-credential" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:public-key-credential" data-x-internal="public-key-credential" {
						- "public key credentials"
					}
					- " available via\n   "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:conditional-mediation" {
						a data-x-internal="conditional-mediation" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialmediationrequirement-conditional" {
							- "conditional"
						}
					}
					- " mediation when the user interacts with the\n   form control. "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-webauthn" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-webauthn" {
							- "webauthn"
						}
					}
					- " is only valid for\n   "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:the-input-element-2" {
						a href="#the-input-element" {
							- "input"
						}
					}
					- " and "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:the-textarea-element" {
						a href="#the-textarea-element" {
							- "textarea"
						}
					}
					- " elements."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "As noted earlier, the meaning of the attribute and its keywords depends on the mantle that the\n  attribute is wearing."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="switch" {
			dt {
				- "When wearing the "
				a href="#autofill-expectation-mantle" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:autofill-expectation-mantle-3" {
					- "autofill expectation mantle"
				}
				- "...\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The \""
					dfn data-dfn-for="button/autocomplete,fieldset/autocomplete,input/autocomplete,object/autocomplete,output/autocomplete,select/autocomplete,textarea/autocomplete" id="attr-fe-autocomplete-off" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
						code {
							- "off"
						}
					}
					- "\" keyword indicates either that the control's\n    input data is particularly sensitive (for example the activation code for a nuclear weapon); or\n    that it is a value that will never be reused (for example a one-time-key for a bank login) and\n    the user will therefore have to explicitly enter the data each time, instead of being able to\n    rely on the UA to prefill the value for them; or that the document provides its own autocomplete\n    mechanism and does not want the user agent to provide autocompletion values."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The \""
					dfn data-dfn-for="button/autocomplete,fieldset/autocomplete,input/autocomplete,object/autocomplete,output/autocomplete,select/autocomplete,textarea/autocomplete" id="attr-fe-autocomplete-on" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
						code {
							- "on"
						}
					}
					- "\" keyword indicates that the user agent is\n    allowed to provide the user with autocompletion values, but does not provide any further\n    information about what kind of data the user might be expected to enter. User agents would have\n    to use heuristics to decide what autocompletion values to suggest."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The "
					a href="#autofill-field" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:autofill-field-3" {
						- "autofill field"
					}
					- " listed above indicate that the user agent is allowed to\n    provide the user with autocompletion values, and specifies what kind of value is expected. The\n    meaning of each such keyword is described in the table below."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-7" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" {
							- "autocomplete"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is omitted, the default\n    value corresponding to the state of the element's "
					a href="#form-owner" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:form-owner" {
						- "form owner"
					}
					- "'s "
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-form-autocomplete" {
						a href="#attr-form-autocomplete" {
							- "autocomplete"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is used instead (either \""
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-on-3" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-on" {
							- "on"
						}
					}
					- "\" or \""
					code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-off-3" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-off" {
							- "off"
						}
					}
					- "\"). If there is no "
					a href="#form-owner" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:form-owner-2" {
						- "form owner"
					}
					- ", then the\n    value \""
