		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="autofill-field" {
				- "autofill field"
			}
			- " keywords relate to each other as described in the table below. Each field name\n  listed on a row of this table corresponds to the meaning given in the cell for that row in the\n  column labeled \"Meaning\". Some fields correspond to subparts of other fields; for example, a\n  credit card expiry date can be expressed as one field giving both the month and year of expiry\n  (\""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp" {
					- "cc-exp"
				}
			}
			- "\"), or as two fields, one giving the\n  month (\""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp-month-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp-month" {
					- "cc-exp-month"
				}
			}
			- "\") and one the year\n  (\""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp-year-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp-year" {
					- "cc-exp-year"
				}
			}
			- "\"). In such cases, the names of\n  the broader fields cover multiple rows, in which the narrower fields are defined."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Generally, authors are encouraged to use the broader fields rather than the\n  narrower fields, as the narrower fields tend to expose Western biases. For example, while it is\n  common in some Western cultures to have a given name and a family name, in that order (and thus\n  often referred to as a "
			i {
				- "first name"
			}
			- " and a "
			i {
				- "surname"
			}
			- "), many cultures put the family name\n  first and the given name second, and many others simply have one name (a "
			i {
				- "mononym"
			}
			- "). Having a\n  single field is therefore more flexible."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Some fields are only appropriate for certain form controls. An "
			a href="#autofill-field" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:autofill-field-5" {
				- "autofill field"
			}
			- " name\n  is "
			dfn id="inappropriate-for-the-control" {
				- "inappropriate for a control"
			}
			- " if the control\n  does not belong to the group listed for that "
			a href="#autofill-field" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:autofill-field-6" {
				- "autofill field"
			}
			- " in the fifth column of\n  the first row describing that "
			a href="#autofill-field" id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:autofill-field-7" {
				- "autofill field"
			}
			- " in the table below. What controls fall\n  into each group is described below the table."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
