		- "\n\n  "
		p id="more-on-address-levels" {
			strong {
				- "Address levels"
			}
			- ": The \""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1" {
					- "address-level1"
				}
			}
			- "\" – \""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level4-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level4" {
					- "address-level4"
				}
			}
			- "\" fields are used to describe\n  the locality of the street address. Different locales have different numbers of levels. For\n  example, the US uses two levels (state and town), the UK uses one or two depending on the address\n  (the post town, and in some cases the locality), and China can use three (province, city,\n  district). The \""
			code id="autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1-3" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1" {
					- "address-level1"
				}
			}
			- "\" field\n  represents the widest administrative division. Different locales order the fields in different\n  ways; for example, in the US the town (level 2) precedes the state (level 1); while in Japan the\n  prefecture (level 1) precedes the city (level 2) which precedes the district (level 3). Authors\n  are encouraged to provide forms that are presented in a way that matches the country's conventions\n  (hiding, showing, and rearranging fields accordingly as the user changes the country)."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h6 id="autofill-processing-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.10.18.7.2"
			}
			- " "
			span id="processing-model-3"
			- "Processing model"
			a href="#autofill-processing-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element to which the "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" {
					- "autocomplete"
				}
			}
			- " attribute "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id="autofill-processing-model:concept-input-apply" {
				- "applies"
			}
			- ", each "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:the-select-element" {
				a href="#the-select-element" {
					- "select"
				}
			}
			- " element, and each "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:the-textarea-element" {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" {
					- "textarea"
				}
			}
			- " element, has an\n  "
			dfn id="autofill-hint-set" {
				- "autofill hint set"
			}
			- ", an "
			dfn id="autofill-scope" {
				- "autofill scope"
			}
			- ", an "
			dfn id="autofill-field-name" {
				- "autofill field name"
			}
			- ", a\n  "
			dfn id="non-autofill-credential-type" {
				- "non-autofill credential type"
			}
			- ", and an "
			dfn id="idl-exposed-autofill-value" {
				- "IDL-exposed autofill value"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-field-name" id="autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name" {
				- "autofill field name"
			}
			- " specifies the specific kind of data expected in the field,\n  e.g. \""
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-street-address" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-street-address" {
					- "street-address"
				}
			}
			- "\" or \""
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp" {
					- "cc-exp"
				}
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-hint-set" id="autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set" {
				- "autofill hint set"
			}
			- " identifies what address or contact information type the user\n  agent is to look at, e.g. \""
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-shipping" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-shipping" {
					- "shipping"
				}
			}
			- " "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-fax" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-fax" {
					- "fax"
				}
			}
			- "\" or \""
			code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-billing" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-billing" {
					- "billing"
				}
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#non-autofill-credential-type" id="autofill-processing-model:non-autofill-credential-type" {
				- "non-autofill credential type"
			}
			- " identifies a type of\n  "
			a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#credential" id="autofill-processing-model:credman-credential" data-x-internal="credman-credential" {
				- "credential"
			}
			- " that may be offered by the user agent when the\n  user interacts with the field alongside other "
			a href="#autofill-field" id="autofill-processing-model:autofill-field" {
				- "autofill field"
			}
			- " values. If this value is\n  \""
			code {
				- "webauthn"
			}
			- "\" instead of null, selecting a credential of that type will resolve\n  a pending "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:conditional-mediation" {
				a data-x-internal="conditional-mediation" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialmediationrequirement-conditional" {
					- "conditional"
				}
			}
			- " mediation\n  "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:navigator.credentials.get()" {
				a data-x-internal="navigator.credentials.get()" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialscontainer-get" {
					- "navigator.credentials.get()"
				}
			}
			- " request, instead of autofilling the field."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, a sign-in page could instruct the user agent to either autofill a saved password,\n   or show a "
				a id="autofill-processing-model:public-key-credential" href="https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#public-key-credential" data-x-internal="public-key-credential" {
					- "public key credential"
				}
				- " that will resolve a pending\n   "
				code id="autofill-processing-model:navigator.credentials.get()-2" {
					a data-x-internal="navigator.credentials.get()" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialscontainer-get" {
						- "navigator.credentials.get()"
					}
				}
				- " request. A user can select either to sign-in."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "name"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "password"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "type"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "password"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "autocomplete"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"current-password webauthn\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-scope" id="autofill-processing-model:autofill-scope" {
				- "autofill scope"
			}
			- " identifies the group of fields whose information concerns the\n  same subject, and consists of the "
			a href="#autofill-hint-set" id="autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set-2" {
				- "autofill hint set"
			}
			- " with, if\n  applicable, the \""
			code {
				- "section-*"
			}
			- "\" prefix, e.g. \""
			code {
				- "billing"
			}
			- "\",\n  \""
			code {
				- "section-parent shipping"
			}
			- "\", or \""
			code {
				- "section-child shipping\n  home"
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "These values are defined as the result of running the following algorithm:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element has no "
					code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-2" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" {
							- "autocomplete"
						}
					}
					- " attribute,\n   then jump to the step labeled "
					i {
						- "default"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "tokens"
					}
					- " be the result of "
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id="autofill-processing-model:split-a-string-on-spaces" data-x-internal="split-a-string-on-spaces" {
						- "splitting the attribute's value on ASCII whitespace"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "tokens"
					}
					- " is empty, then jump to the step labeled "
					i {
						- "default"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "index"
					}
					- " be the index of the last token in "
					var {
						- "tokens"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "field"
					}
					- " be the "
					var {
						- "index"
					}
					- "th token in "
					var {
						- "tokens"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					var {
						- "category"
					}
					- ", "
					var {
						- "maximum tokens"
					}
					- " pair to the result of "
					a href="#determine-a-field's-category" id="autofill-processing-model:determine-a-field's-category" {
						- "determining a field's category"
					}
					- " given\n   "
					var {
						- "field"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "category"
					}
					- " is null, then jump to the step labeled "
					i {
						- "default"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the number of tokens in "
					var {
						- "tokens"
					}
					- " is greater than "
					var {
						- "maximum tokens"
					}
					- ",\n   then jump to the step labeled "
					i {
						- "default"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "category"
					}
					- " is Off or Automatic but the element's "
					code id="autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-3" {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" {
							- "autocomplete"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is wearing the "
