				a href="#dom-elementinternals-setvalidity" {
					- "setValidity()"
				}
			}
			- " method. The user agent should use the\n  "
			a href="#custom-validity-error-message" id="definitions:custom-validity-error-message-3" {
				- "custom validity error message"
			}
			- " when alerting the user to the problem with the\n  control."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An element can be constrained in various ways. The following is the list of "
			dfn id="validity-states" {
				- "validity\n  states"
			}
			- " that a form control can be in, making the control invalid for the purposes of\n  constraint validation. (The definitions below are non-normative; other parts of this specification\n  define more precisely when each state applies or does not.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- " "
