							- "returnValue"
						}
						- ");\n};"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-dialog-element:the-dialog-element" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element represents a transitory part of an application, in the form of\n  a small window (\"dialog box\"), which the user interacts with to perform a task or gather\n  information. Once the user is done, the dialog can be automatically closed by the application, or\n  manually closed by the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Especially for modal dialogs, which are a familiar pattern across all types of applications,\n  authors should work to ensure that dialogs in their web applications behave in a way that is\n  familiar to users of non-web applications."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "As with all HTML elements, it is not conforming to use the "
			code id="the-dialog-element:the-dialog-element-2" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element when attempting to represent another type of control. For example, context menus,\n  tooltips, and popup listboxes are not dialog boxes, so abusing the "
			code id="the-dialog-element:the-dialog-element-3" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element to\n  implement these patterns is incorrect."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An important part of user-facing dialog behavior is the placement of initial focus. The\n  "
			a href="#dialog-focusing-steps" id="the-dialog-element:dialog-focusing-steps" {
				- "dialog focusing steps"
			}
			- " attempt to pick a good candidate for initial focus when a\n  dialog is shown, but might not be a substitute for authors carefully thinking through the correct\n  choice to match user expectations for a specific dialog. As such, authors should use the "
			code id="the-dialog-element:attr-fe-autofocus" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autofocus" {
					- "autofocus"
				}
			}
			- " attribute on the descendant element of the dialog that\n  the user is expected to immediately interact with after the dialog opens. If there is no such\n  element, then authors should use the "
			code id="the-dialog-element:attr-fe-autofocus-2" {
				a href="#attr-fe-autofocus" {
					- "autofocus"
				}
			}
			- " attribute\n  on the "
			code id="the-dialog-element:the-dialog-element-4" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "In the following example, a dialog is used for editing the details of a product in an\n   inventory management web application."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dialog"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Product Number "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "type"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"text\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "readonly"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Product Name "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "input"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "type"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"text\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "autofocus"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "label"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dialog"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the "
				code id="the-dialog-element:attr-fe-autofocus-3" {
					a href="#attr-fe-autofocus" {
						- "autofocus"
					}
				}
				- " attribute was not present, the\n   Product Number field would have been focused by the dialog focusing steps. Although that is\n   reasonable behavior, the author determined that the more relevant field to focus was the Product\n   Name field, as the Product Number field is readonly and expects no user input. So, the author\n   used autofocus to override the default."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Even if the author wants to focus the Product Number field by default, they are best off\n   explicitly specifying that by using autofocus on that "
				code id="the-dialog-element:the-input-element" {
					a href="#the-input-element" {
						- "input"
					}
				}
				- " element. This makes the\n   intent obvious to future readers of the code, and ensures the code stays robust in the face of\n   future updates. (For example, if another developer added a close button, and positioned it in the\n   node tree before the Product Number field)."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Another important aspect of user behavior is whether dialogs are scrollable or not. In some\n  cases, overflow (and thus scrollability) cannot be avoided, e.g., when it is caused by the user's\n  high text zoom settings. But in general, scrollable dialogs are not expected by users. Adding\n  large text nodes directly to dialog elements is particularly bad as this is likely to cause the\n  dialog element itself to overflow. Authors are best off avoiding them."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "The following terms of service dialog respects the above suggestions."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dialog"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "style"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"height: 80vh;\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "div"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "style"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"overflow: auto; height: 60vh;\""
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "autofocus"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
