		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements:the-script-element-3" {
				a href="#the-script-element" {
					- "script"
				}
			}
			- " element contains "
			a href="#inline-documentation-for-external-scripts" id="restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements:inline-documentation-for-external-scripts" {
				- "script documentation"
			}
			- ", there are\n  further restrictions on the contents of the element, as described in the section below."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The following script illustrates this issue. Suppose you have a script that contains a string,\n   as in:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="js" {
					c- a="" {
						- "const"
					}
					- " example "
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					- " "
					c- t="" {
						- "'Consider this string: <!-- <script>'"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ";"
					}
					- "\nconsole"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "log"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					- "example"
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If one were to put this string directly in a "
				code id="restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements:the-script-element-4" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " block, it would violate the\n   restrictions above:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- a="" {
						- "const"
					}
					- " example "
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					- " "
					c- t="" {
						- "'Consider this string: <!-- <script>'"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ";"
					}
					- "\n  console"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "log"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					- "example"
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The bigger problem, though, and the reason why it would violate those restrictions, is that\n   actually the script would get parsed weirdly: "
				em {
					- "the script block above is not terminated"
				}
				- ".\n   That is, what looks like a \""
				code {
					- "</script>"
				}
				- "\" end tag in this snippet is\n   actually still part of the "
				code id="restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements:the-script-element-5" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " block. The script doesn't execute (since it's not\n   terminated); if it somehow were to execute, as it might if the markup looked as follows, it would\n   fail because the script (highlighted here) is not valid JavaScript:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					mark {
						- "\n  "
						c- a="" {
							- "const"
						}
						- " example "
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						- " "
						c- t="" {
							- "'Consider this string: <!-- <script>'"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ";"
						}
						- "\n  console"
						c- p="" {
							- "."
						}
						- "log"
						c- p="" {
							- "("
						}
						- "example"
						c- p="" {
							- ");"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- p="" {
							- "</"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "script"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- c="" {
							- "<!-- despite appearances, this is actually part of the script still! -->"
						}
						- "\n"
						c- p="" {
							- "<"
						}
						c- f="" {
							- "script"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ">"
						}
						- "\n "
						c- p="" {
							- "..."
						}
						- " "
						c- c1="" {
							- "// this is the same script block still..."
						}
						- "\n"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "What is going on here is that for legacy reasons, \""
				code {
					- "<!--"
				}
				- "\" and \""
				code {
					- "<script"
				}
				- "\" strings in "
				code id="restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements:the-script-element-6" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " elements in HTML need to be balanced\n   in order for the parser to consider closing the block."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "By escaping the problematic strings as mentioned at the top of this section, the problem is\n   avoided entirely:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					mark {
						- "\n  "
						c- c1="" {
							- "// Note: `\\x3C` is an escape sequence for `<`."
						}
						- "\n  "
						c- a="" {
							- "const"
						}
						- " example "
						c- o="" {
							- "="
						}
						- " "
						c- t="" {
							- "'Consider this string: \\x3C!-- \\x3Cscript>'"
						}
						c- p="" {
							- ";"
						}
						- "\n  console"
						c- p="" {
							- "."
						}
						- "log"
						c- p="" {
							- "("
						}
						- "example"
						c- p="" {
							- ");"
						}
						- "\n"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- c="" {
						- "<!-- this is just a comment between script blocks -->"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					mark {
						- "\n "
						c- p="" {
							- "..."
						}
						- " "
						c- c1="" {
							- "// this is a new script block"
						}
						- "\n"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "It is possible for these sequences to naturally occur in script expressions, as in the\n   following examples:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
