		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This corresponds to putting the contents of the element in JavaScript\n  comments."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This requirement is in addition to the earlier restrictions on the syntax of\n  contents of "
			code id="inline-documentation-for-external-scripts:the-script-element-3" {
				a href="#the-script-element" {
					- "script"
				}
			}
			- " elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This allows authors to include documentation, such as license information or API information,\n   inside their documents while still referring to external script files. The syntax is constrained\n   so that authors don't accidentally include what looks like valid script while also providing a\n   "
				code id="inline-documentation-for-external-scripts:attr-script-src-2" {
					a href="#attr-script-src" {
						- "src"
					}
				}
				- " attribute."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "src"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"cool-effects.js\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- c1="" {
						- "// create new instances using:"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- c1="" {
						- "//    var e = new Effect();"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- c1="" {
						- "// start the effect using .play, stop using .stop:"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- c1="" {
						- "//    e.play();"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- c1="" {
						- "//    e.stop();"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="scriptTagXSLT" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.12.1.5"
			}
			- " Interaction of "
			code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element" {
				a href="#the-script-element" {
					- "script"
				}
			}
			- " elements and XSLT"
			a href="#scriptTagXSLT" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification does not define how XSLT interacts with the "
			code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element-2" {
				a href="#the-script-element" {
					- "script"
				}
			}
			- " element.\n  However, in the absence of another specification actually defining this, here are some guidelines\n  for implementers, based on existing implementations:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "When an XSLT transformation program is triggered by an "
					code {
						- "<?xml-stylesheet?>"
					}
					- " processing instruction and the browser implements a\n   direct-to-DOM transformation, "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element-3" {
						a href="#the-script-element" {
							- "script"
						}
					}
					- " elements created by the XSLT processor need to\n   have its "
					a href="#parser-document" id="scriptTagXSLT:parser-document" {
						- "parser document"
					}
					- " set correctly, and run in document order (modulo scripts\n   marked "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:attr-script-defer" {
						a href="#attr-script-defer" {
							- "defer"
						}
					}
					- " or "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:attr-script-async" {
						a href="#attr-script-async" {
							- "async"
						}
					}
					- "), "
					a href="#immediately" id="scriptTagXSLT:immediately" {
						- "immediately"
					}
					- ", as the transformation is\n   occurring."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:xsltprocessor" {
						a href="#xsltprocessor" {
							- "XSLTProcessor"
						}
					}
					- " "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:dom-xsltprocessor-transformtodocument" {
						a href="#dom-xsltprocessor-transformtodocument" {
							- "transformToDocument()"
						}
					}
					- " method adds elements\n   to a "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:document" {
						a href="#document" {
							- "Document"
						}
					}
					- " object with a null "
					a href="#concept-document-bc" id="scriptTagXSLT:concept-document-bc" {
						- "browsing\n   context"
					}
					- ", and, accordingly, any "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element-4" {
						a href="#the-script-element" {
							- "script"
						}
					}
					- " elements they create need to have\n   their "
					a href="#already-started" id="scriptTagXSLT:already-started" {
						- "already started"
					}
					- " set to true in the "
					a href="#prepare-the-script-element" id="scriptTagXSLT:prepare-the-script-element" {
						- "prepare the script element"
					}
					- "\n   algorithm and never get executed ("
					a href="#concept-environment-noscript" id="scriptTagXSLT:concept-environment-noscript" {
						- "scripting is\n   disabled"
					}
					- "). Such "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element-5" {
						a href="#the-script-element" {
							- "script"
						}
					}
					- " elements still need to have their "
					a href="#parser-document" id="scriptTagXSLT:parser-document-2" {
						- "parser\n   document"
					}
					- " set, though, such that their "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:dom-script-async" {
						a href="#dom-script-async" {
							- "async"
						}
					}
					- " IDL\n   attribute will return false in the absence of an "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:attr-script-async-2" {
						a href="#attr-script-async" {
							- "async"
						}
					}
					- "\n   content attribute."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:xsltprocessor-2" {
						a href="#xsltprocessor" {
							- "XSLTProcessor"
						}
					}
					- " "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:dom-xsltprocessor-transformtofragment" {
						a href="#dom-xsltprocessor-transformtofragment" {
							- "transformToFragment()"
						}
					}
					- " method needs to\n   create a fragment that is equivalent to one built manually by creating the elements using "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:dom-document-createelementns" {
						a data-x-internal="dom-document-createelementns" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createelementns" {
							- "document.createElementNS()"
						}
					}
					- ". For instance, it needs\n   to create "
					code id="scriptTagXSLT:the-script-element-6" {
						a href="#the-script-element" {
							- "script"
						}
					}
					- " elements with null "
					a href="#parser-document" id="scriptTagXSLT:parser-document-3" {
						- "parser document"
					}
					- " and with their\n   "
					a href="#already-started" id="scriptTagXSLT:already-started-2" {
						- "already started"
					}
					- " set to false, so that they will execute when the fragment is\n   inserted into a document."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The main distinction between the first two cases and the last case is that the first two\n  operate on "
			code id="scriptTagXSLT:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "s and the last operates on a fragment."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-noscript-element" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.12.2"
			}
			- " The "
			dfn data-dfn-type="element" {
				code {
					- "noscript"
				}
			}
			- " element"
			a href="#the-noscript-element" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
