		h5 id="template-XSLT-XPath" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.12.3.1"
			}
			- " Interaction of "
			code id="template-XSLT-XPath:the-template-element" {
				a href="#the-template-element" {
					- "template"
				}
			}
			- " elements with XSLT and XPath"
			a href="#template-XSLT-XPath" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification does not define how XSLT and XPath interact with the "
			code id="template-XSLT-XPath:the-template-element-2" {
				a href="#the-template-element" {
					- "template"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element. However, in the absence of another specification actually defining this, here are some\n  guidelines for implementers, which are intended to be consistent with other processing described\n  in this specification:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "An XSLT processor based on an XML parser that acts "
					a href="#xml-parser" id="template-XSLT-XPath:xml-parser" {
						- "as described\n   in this specification"
					}
					- " needs to act as if "
					code id="template-XSLT-XPath:the-template-element-3" {
						a href="#the-template-element" {
							- "template"
						}
					}
					- " elements contain as\n   descendants their "
					a href="#template-contents" id="template-XSLT-XPath:template-contents" {
						- "template contents"
					}
					- " for the purposes of the transform."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "An XSLT processor that outputs a DOM needs to ensure that nodes that would go into a\n   "
					code id="template-XSLT-XPath:the-template-element-4" {
						a href="#the-template-element" {
							- "template"
						}
					}
					- " element are instead placed into the element's "
					a href="#template-contents" id="template-XSLT-XPath:template-contents-2" {
						- "template\n   contents"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "XPath evaluation using the XPath DOM API when applied to a "
					code id="template-XSLT-XPath:document" {
						a href="#document" {
							- "Document"
						}
					}
					- " parsed\n   using the "
					a href="#html-parser" id="template-XSLT-XPath:html-parser" {
						- "HTML parser"
					}
					- " or the "
					a href="#xml-parser" id="template-XSLT-XPath:xml-parser-2" {
						- "XML parser"
					}
					- " described in this specification\n   needs to ignore "
					a href="#template-contents" id="template-XSLT-XPath:template-contents-3" {
						- "template contents"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n  "
			}
		}
