		- "\n\n \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "To maintain compatibility with existing web content, user agents need to\n  enumerate methods defined in "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasuserinterface-2" {
				a href="#canvasuserinterface" {
					- "CanvasUserInterface"
				}
			}
			- " immediately after the "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-stroke-2" {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-stroke" {
					- "stroke()"
				}
			}
			- " method on "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-17" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- "\n  objects."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " = "
					var {
						- "canvas"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-canvas-getcontext" id="2dcontext:dom-canvas-getcontext" {
						- "getContext"
					}
					- "('2d' [, { [ "
					a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha" id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha-2" {
						- "alpha"
					}
					- ": true ] [, "
					a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized-2" {
						- "desynchronized"
					}
					- ": false ] [, "
					a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace" id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace-2" {
						- "colorSpace"
					}
					- ": 'srgb'] [, "
					a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently" id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently-2" {
						- "willReadFrequently"
					}
					- ": false ]} ])"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns a "
					code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-18" {
						a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
							- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
						}
					}
					- " object that is permanently bound to a\n    particular "
					code id="2dcontext:the-canvas-element" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " element."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha-3" {
						a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha" {
							- "alpha"
						}
					}
					- " member is\n    false, then the context is forced to always be opaque."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized-3" {
						a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized" {
							- "desynchronized"
						}
					}
					- " member is\n    true, then the context might be "
					a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized" {
						- "desynchronized"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The "
					code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace-3" {
						a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace" {
							- "colorSpace"
						}
					}
					- " member\n    specifies the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-color-space" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-color-space" {
						- "color space"
					}
					- " of the rendering\n    context."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently-3" {
						a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently" {
							- "willReadFrequently"
						}
					}
					- "\n    member is true, then the context is marked for "
					a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" {
						- "readback optimization"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-context-2d-canvas" id="dom-context-2d-canvas-dev" {
						- "canvas"
					}
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CanvasRenderingContext2D/canvas" title="The CanvasRenderingContext2D.canvas property, part of the Canvas API, is a read-only reference to the HTMLCanvasElement object that is associated with a given context. It might be null if there is no associated <canvas> element." {
								- "CanvasRenderingContext2D/canvas"
							}
						}
						p class="all-engines-text" {
							- "Support in all current engines."
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "1.5+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span {
									- "Chrome"
								}
								span {
									- "1+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge"
								}
								span {
									- "79+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge (Legacy)"
								}
								span {
									- "12+"
								}
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span {
									- "Internet Explorer"
								}
								span {
									- "9+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Firefox Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="safari_ios yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari iOS"
								}
								span {
									- "1+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Chrome Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="webview_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "WebView Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Samsung Internet"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera Android"
								}
								span {
									- "12.1+"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns the "
					code id="2dcontext:the-canvas-element-2" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " element."
				}
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "attributes"
					}
					- " = "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-context-2d-canvas-getcontextattributes" id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-canvas-getcontextattributes-2" {
						- "getContextAttributes"
					}
					- "()"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns an object whose:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ul {
					li {
						code id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-alpha" {
							a href="#concept-canvas-alpha" {
								- "alpha"
							}
						}
						- " member is true if the context has an alpha\n     channel, or false if it was forced to be opaque."
					}
					li {
						code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized-4" {
							a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized" {
								- "desynchronized"
							}
						}
						- "\n     member is true if the context can be "
						a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized-2" {
							- "desynchronized"
						}
						- "."
					}
					li {
						code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace-4" {
							a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace" {
								- "colorSpace"
							}
						}
						- " member is\n     a string indicating the context's "
						a href="#concept-canvas-color-space" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-color-space-2" {
							- "color\n     space"
						}
						- "."
					}
					li {
						code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently-4" {
							a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently" {
								- "willReadFrequently"
							}
						}
						- "\n     member is true if the context is marked for "
						a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently-2" {
							- "readback\n     optimization"
						}
						- "."
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-19" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object has an "
			dfn id="output-bitmap" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " that\n  is initialized when the object is created."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " has an "
			a href="#concept-canvas-origin-clean" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-origin-clean" {
				- "origin-clean"
			}
			- " flag, which can be set to true or false.\n  Initially, when one of these bitmaps is created, its "
			a href="#concept-canvas-origin-clean" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-origin-clean-2" {
				- "origin-clean"
			}
			- " flag must be set to true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-20" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object also has an "
			dfn id="concept-canvas-alpha" {
				- "alpha"
			}
			- " boolean. When a\n  "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-21" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#concept-canvas-alpha" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-alpha-2" {
				- "alpha"
			}
			- " is false, then its alpha channel must be fixed to 1.0\n  (fully opaque) for all pixels, and attempts to change the alpha component of any pixel must be\n  silently ignored."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Thus, the bitmap of such a context starts off as "
			a id="2dcontext:opaque-black" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#opaque-black" data-x-internal="opaque-black" {
				- "opaque black"
			}
			- " instead\n  of "
			a id="2dcontext:transparent-black-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" data-x-internal="transparent-black" {
				- "transparent black"
			}
			- "; "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-clearrect-2" {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-clearrect" {
					- "clearRect()"
				}
			}
			- "\n  always results in "
			a id="2dcontext:opaque-black-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#opaque-black" data-x-internal="opaque-black" {
				- "opaque black"
			}
			- " pixels, every fourth byte from "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-getimagedata-2" {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-getimagedata" {
					- "getImageData()"
				}
			}
			- " is always 255, the "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-putimagedata-3" {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-putimagedata" {
					- "putImageData()"
				}
			}
			- " method effectively ignores every\n  fourth byte in its input, and so on. However, the alpha component of styles and images drawn\n  onto the canvas are still honoured up to the point where they would impact the "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-2" {
				- "output\n  bitmap"
			}
			- "'s alpha channel; for instance, drawing a 50% transparent white square on a freshly\n  created "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-3" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " with its "
			a href="#concept-canvas-alpha" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-alpha-3" {
				- "alpha"
			}
			- " set\n  to false will result in a fully-opaque gray square."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-22" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object also has a "
			dfn id="concept-canvas-desynchronized" {
				- "desynchronized"
			}
			- " boolean. When a\n  "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-23" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized-3" {
				- "desynchronized"
			}
			- " is true, then the user agent may\n  optimize the rendering of the canvas to reduce the latency, as measured from input events to\n  rasterization, by desynchronizing the canvas paint cycle from the event loop, bypassing the\n  ordinary user agent rendering algorithm, or both. Insofar as this mode involves bypassing the\n  usual paint mechanisms, rasterization, or both, it might introduce visible tearing artifacts."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The user agent usually renders on a buffer which is not being displayed, quickly\n  swapping it and the one being scanned out for presentation; the former buffer is called\n  back buffer and the latter "
			i {
				- "front buffer"
			}
			- ". A popular technique for reducing latency is called\n  front buffer rendering, also known as "
			i {
				- "single buffer"
			}
			- " rendering, where rendering happens in\n  parallel and racily with the scanning out process. This technique reduces the latency at the price\n  of potentially introducing tearing artifacts and can be used to implement in total or part of the\n  "
			a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized-4" {
				- "desynchronized"
			}
			- " boolean.\n  "
			a href="#refsMULTIPLEBUFFERING" {
				- "[MULTIPLEBUFFERING]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized-5" {
				- "desynchronized"
			}
			- " boolean\n  can be useful when implementing certain kinds of applications, such as drawing applications,\n  where the latency between input and rasterization is critical."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-24" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object also has a "
			dfn id="concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" {
				- "will read frequently"
			}
			- " boolean. When a\n  "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-25" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently-3" {
				- "will read frequently"
			}
			- " is true, the user agent\n  may optimize the canvas for readback operations."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "On most devices the user agent needs to decide whether to store the canvas's\n  "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-4" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " on the GPU (this is also called \"hardware accelerated\"), or on the CPU\n  (also called \"software\"). Most rendering operations are more performant for accelerated canvases,\n  with the major exception being readback with "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-context-2d-getimagedata-3" {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-getimagedata" {
					- "getImageData()"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvas-todataurl" {
				a href="#dom-canvas-todataurl" {
					- "toDataURL()"
				}
			}
			- ", or "
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvas-toblob" {
				a href="#dom-canvas-toblob" {
					- "toBlob()"
				}
			}
			- ". "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-26" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " objects with\n  "
			a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently-4" {
				- "will read frequently"
			}
			- " equal to true tell\n  the user agent that the webpage is likely to perform many readback operations and that it is\n  advantageous to use a software canvas."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-27" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object also has a "
			dfn id="concept-canvas-color-space" {
				- "color space"
			}
			- " setting of type\n  "
			code id="2dcontext:predefinedcolorspace-4" {
				a href="#predefinedcolorspace" {
					- "PredefinedColorSpace"
				}
			}
			- ". The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-28" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#concept-canvas-color-space" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-color-space-3" {
				- "color space"
			}
			- " indicates the color space for the\n  "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-5" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="CanvasRenderingContext2D" id="dom-context-2d-canvas-getcontextattributes" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "getContextAttributes()"
				}
			}
			- " method\n  steps are to return «[ \""
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha-4" {
				a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-alpha" {
					- "alpha"
				}
			}
			- "\" →\n  "
			a id="2dcontext:this" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-canvas-alpha" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-alpha-4" {
				- "alpha"
			}
			- ", \""
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized-5" {
				a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-desynchronized" {
					- "desynchronized"
				}
			}
			- "\" →\n  "
			a id="2dcontext:this-2" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-canvas-desynchronized" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-desynchronized-6" {
				- "desynchronized"
			}
			- ", \""
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace-5" {
				a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-colorspace" {
					- "colorSpace"
				}
			}
			- "\" → "
			a id="2dcontext:this-3" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s\n  "
			a href="#concept-canvas-color-space" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-color-space-4" {
				- "color space"
			}
			- ", \""
			code id="2dcontext:dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently-5" {
				a href="#dom-canvasrenderingcontext2dsettings-willreadfrequently" {
					- "willReadFrequently"
				}
			}
			- "\" →\n  "
			a id="2dcontext:this-4" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently-5" {
				- "will read frequently"
			}
			- "\n  ]»."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-29" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
					- "CanvasRenderingContext2D"
				}
			}
			- " 2D rendering context represents a flat linear\n  Cartesian surface whose origin (0,0) is at the top left corner, with the coordinate space having\n  "
			var {
				- "x"
			}
			- " values increasing when going right, and "
			var {
				- "y"
			}
			- " values increasing when going\n  down. The "
			var {
				- "x"
			}
			- "-coordinate of the right-most edge is equal to the width of the rendering\n  context's "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-6" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " in "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'" data-x-internal="'px'" {
				- "CSS pixels"
			}
			- "; similarly, the\n  "
			var {
				- "y"
			}
			- "-coordinate of the bottom-most edge is equal to the height of the rendering context's\n  "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-7" {
				- "output bitmap"
			}
			- " in "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-2" data-x-internal="'px'" {
				- "CSS pixels"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The size of the coordinate space does not necessarily represent the size of the actual bitmaps\n  that the user agent will use internally or during rendering. On high-definition displays, for\n  instance, the user agent may internally use bitmaps with four device pixels per unit in the\n  coordinate space, so that the rendering remains at high quality throughout. Anti-aliasing can\n  similarly be implemented using oversampling with bitmaps of a higher resolution than the final\n  image on the display."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Using "
				a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-3" data-x-internal="'px'" {
					- "CSS pixels"
				}
				- " to describe the size of a rendering context's\n   "
				a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-8" {
					- "output bitmap"
				}
				- " does not mean that when rendered the canvas will cover an equivalent\n   area in "
				a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-4" data-x-internal="'px'" {
					- "CSS pixels"
				}
				- ". "
				a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-5" data-x-internal="'px'" {
					- "CSS pixels"
				}
				- " are reused\n   for ease of integration with CSS features, such as text layout."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In other words, the "
				code id="2dcontext:the-canvas-element-3" {
					a href="#the-canvas-element" {
						- "canvas"
					}
				}
				- " element below's rendering context has a 200x200\n   "
				a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-9" {
					- "output bitmap"
				}
				- " (which internally uses "
				a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-6" data-x-internal="'px'" {
					- "CSS pixels"
				}
				- " as a\n   unit for ease of integration with CSS) and is rendered as 100x100 "
				a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-7" data-x-internal="'px'" {
					- "CSS\n   pixels"
				}
				- ":\n\n   "
			}
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "canvas"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "width"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
