		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			img src="/images/baselines.png" width="738" alt="The em-over baseline is roughly at the top of the glyphs in a font, the hanging baseline is where some glyphs like आ are anchored, the middle is half-way between the em-over and em-under baselines, the alphabetic baseline is where characters like Á, ÿ, f, and Ω are anchored, the ideographic-under baseline is where glyphs like 私 and 達 are anchored, and the em-under baseline is roughly at the bottom of the glyphs in a font. The top and bottom of the bounding box can be far from these baselines, due to glyphs extending far outside em-over and em-under baselines." height="300"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
