					- "closePath()"
				}
			}
			- " method, when invoked, must do nothing\n  if the object's path has no subpaths. Otherwise, it must mark the last subpath as closed, create a\n  new subpath whose first point is the same as the previous subpath's first point, and finally add\n  this new subpath to the path."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If the last subpath had more than one point in its list of points, then this is\n  equivalent to adding a straight line connecting the last point back to the first point of the last\n  subpath, thus \"closing\" the subpath."
