		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a pattern is to be rendered within an area, the user agent must run the following steps to\n  determine what is rendered:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Create an infinite "
					a id="fill-and-stroke-styles:transparent-black-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" data-x-internal="transparent-black" {
						- "transparent black"
					}
					- " bitmap."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Place a copy of the image on the bitmap, anchored such that its top left corner is at the\n    origin of the coordinate space, with one coordinate space unit per "
					a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="fill-and-stroke-styles:'px'-2" data-x-internal="'px'" {
						- "CSS\n    pixel"
					}
					- " of the image, then place repeated copies of this image horizontally to the left and\n    right, if the repetition behavior is \""
					code {
						- "repeat-x"
					}
					- "\", or vertically up and\n    down, if the repetition behavior is \""
					code {
						- "repeat-y"
					}
					- "\", or in all four\n    directions all over the bitmap, if the repetition behavior is \""
					code {
						- "repeat"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the original image data is a bitmap image, then the value painted at a point in the area\n    of the repetitions is computed by filtering the original image data. When scaling up, if the\n    "
					code id="fill-and-stroke-styles:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
							- "imageSmoothingEnabled"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is\n    set to false, then the image must be rendered using nearest-neighbor interpolation. Otherwise,\n    the user agent may use any filtering algorithm (for example bilinear interpolation or\n    nearest-neighbor). User agents which support multiple filtering algorithms may use the value of\n    the "
					code id="fill-and-stroke-styles:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingquality" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingquality" {
							- "imageSmoothingQuality"
						}
					}
					- " attribute\n    to guide the choice of filtering algorithm. When such a filtering algorithm requires a pixel\n    value from outside the original image data, it must instead use the value from wrapping the\n    pixel's coordinates to the original image's dimensions. (That is, the filter uses 'repeat'\n    behavior, regardless of the value of the pattern's repetition behavior.)"
				}
				- " \n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Transform the resulting bitmap according to the pattern's transformation matrix."
