				- "context"
			}
			- ", an element "
			var {
				- "element"
			}
			- ", and a "
			a href="#concept-path" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:concept-path" {
				- "path"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "path"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " is not "
					a href="#focused" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:focused-3" {
						- "focused"
					}
					- " or is not a descendant of\n   "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "'s "
					code id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:the-canvas-element" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " element, then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Draw a focus ring of the appropriate style along "
					var {
						- "path"
					}
					- ", following platform\n    conventions."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Some platforms only draw focus rings around elements that have been focused from\n    the keyboard, and not those focused from the mouse. Other platforms simply don't draw focus\n    rings around some elements at all unless relevant accessibility features are enabled. This API\n    is intended to follow these conventions. User agents that implement distinctions based on the\n    manner in which the element was focused are encouraged to classify focus driven by the "
					code id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:dom-focus" {
						a href="#dom-focus" {
							- "focus()"
						}
					}
					- " method based on the kind of user interaction event from which\n    the call was triggered (if any)."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The focus ring should not be subject to the "
					a href="#shadows" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:shadows" {
						- "shadow effects"
					}
					- ",\n    the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-global-alpha" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:concept-canvas-global-alpha" {
						- "global alpha"
					}
					- ", the "
					a href="#current-compositing-and-blending-operator" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:current-compositing-and-blending-operator" {
						- "current\n    compositing and blending operator"
					}
					- ", the "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style" {
						- "fill style"
					}
					- ", the "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style" {
						- "stroke style"
					}
					- ", or any of the members\n    in the "
					code id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:canvaspathdrawingstyles" {
						a href="#canvaspathdrawingstyles" {
							- "CanvasPathDrawingStyles"
						}
					}
					- ", "
					code id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:canvastextdrawingstyles" {
						a href="#canvastextdrawingstyles" {
							- "CanvasTextDrawingStyles"
						}
					}
					- " interfaces,\n    but "
					em {
						- "should"
					}
					- " be subject to the "
					a href="#clipping-region" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:clipping-region" {
						- "clipping region"
					}
					- ". (The effect of\n    transformations is described above and varies based on which path is being used.)"
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#inform" {
						- "Inform the user"
					}
					- " that the focus is at the location given by the\n   intended path. User agents may wait until the next time the "
					a href="#event-loop" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:event-loop" {
						- "event loop"
					}
					- " reaches its\n   "
					a href="#update-the-rendering" id="drawing-focus-rings-and-scrolling-paths-into-view:update-the-rendering" {
						- "update the rendering"
					}
					- " step to optionally inform the user."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should not implicitly close open subpaths in the intended path when drawing the\n  focus ring."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This might be a moot point, however. For example, if the focus ring is drawn as an\n  axis-aligned bounding rectangle around the points in the intended path, then whether the subpaths\n  are closed or not has no effect. This specification intentionally does not specify precisely how\n  focus rings are to be drawn: user agents are expected to honor their platform's native\n  conventions."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="inform" {
			- "\"Inform the user\", as used in this section, does not imply any persistent state\n  change. It could mean, for instance, calling a system accessibility API to notify assistive\n  technologies such as magnification tools so that the user's magnifier moves to the given area of\n  the canvas. However, it does not associate the path with the element, or provide a region for\n  tactile feedback, etc."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
