			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Paint the region of the "
					var {
						- "image"
					}
					- " argument specified by the source rectangle\n    on the region of the rendering context's "
					a href="#output-bitmap" id="drawing-images:output-bitmap-6" {
						- "output bitmap"
					}
					- " specified by the\n    destination rectangle, after applying the "
					a href="#transformations" id="drawing-images:transformations" {
						- "current\n    transformation matrix"
					}
					- " to the destination rectangle."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The image data must be processed in the original direction, even if the dimensions given are\n    negative. "
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "When scaling up, if the "
					code id="drawing-images:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
							- "imageSmoothingEnabled"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is set to\n    true, the user agent should attempt to apply a smoothing algorithm to the image data when it is\n    scaled. User agents which support multiple filtering algorithms may use the value of the "
					code id="drawing-images:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingquality" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingquality" {
							- "imageSmoothingQuality"
						}
					}
					- " attribute to guide\n    the choice of filtering algorithm when the "
					code id="drawing-images:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled-2" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
							- "imageSmoothingEnabled"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is set to\n    true. Otherwise, the image must be rendered using nearest-neighbor interpolation."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This specification does not define the precise algorithm to use when scaling an\n    image down, or when scaling an image up when the "
					code id="drawing-images:dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled-3" {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-imagesmoothingenabled" {
							- "imageSmoothingEnabled"
						}
					}
					- " attribute is set to\n    true."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "When a "
					code id="drawing-images:the-canvas-element" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " element is drawn onto itself, the "
					a href="#drawing-model" id="drawing-images:drawing-model" {
						- "drawing\n    model"
					}
					- " requires the source to be copied before the image is drawn, so it is possible to\n    copy parts of a "
					code id="drawing-images:the-canvas-element-2" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " element onto overlapping parts of itself."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the original image data is a bitmap image, then the value painted at a point in the\n    destination rectangle is computed by filtering the original image data. The user agent may use\n    any filtering algorithm (for example bilinear interpolation or nearest-neighbor). When the\n    filtering algorithm requires a pixel value from outside the original image data, it must instead\n    use the value from the nearest edge pixel. (That is, the filter uses 'clamp-to-edge' behavior.)\n    When the filtering algorithm requires a pixel value from outside the source rectangle but inside\n    the original image data, then the value from the original image data must be used."
				}
				- "\n    \n    \n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Thus, scaling an image in parts or in whole will have the same effect. This does\n    mean that when sprites coming from a single sprite sheet are to be scaled, adjacent images in\n    the sprite sheet can interfere. This can be avoided by ensuring each sprite in the sheet is\n    surrounded by a border of "
					a id="drawing-images:transparent-black" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" data-x-internal="transparent-black" {
						- "transparent black"
					}
					- ", or by copying sprites to be scaled\n    into temporary "
					code id="drawing-images:the-canvas-element-3" {
						a href="#the-canvas-element" {
							- "canvas"
						}
					}
					- " elements and drawing the scaled sprites from there."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Images are painted without affecting the current path, and are subject to "
					a href="#shadows" id="drawing-images:shadows" {
						- "shadow effects"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="#concept-canvas-global-alpha" id="drawing-images:concept-canvas-global-alpha" {
						- "global\n    alpha"
					}
					- ", the "
					a href="#clipping-region" id="drawing-images:clipping-region" {
						- "clipping region"
					}
					- ", and the "
					a href="#current-compositing-and-blending-operator" id="drawing-images:current-compositing-and-blending-operator" {
						- "current compositing and blending\n    operator"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "image"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#the-image-argument-is-not-origin-clean" id="drawing-images:the-image-argument-is-not-origin-clean" {
						- "is not origin-clean"
					}
					- ", then set the\n   "
					code id="drawing-images:canvasrenderingcontext2d" {
