		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="custom-elements-intro" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.13.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#custom-elements-intro" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#custom-element" id="custom-elements-intro:custom-element" {
				- "Custom elements"
			}
			- " provide a way for authors to build their\n  own fully-featured DOM elements. Although authors could always use non-standard elements in their\n  documents, with application-specific behavior added after the fact by scripting or similar, such\n  elements have historically been non-conforming and not very functional. By "
			a href="#element-definition" id="custom-elements-intro:element-definition" {
				- "defining"
			}
			- " a custom element, authors can inform the parser how to\n  properly construct an element and how elements of that class should react to changes."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Custom elements are part of a larger effort to \"rationalise the platform\", by explaining\n  existing platform features (like the elements of HTML) in terms of lower-level author-exposed\n  extensibility points (like custom element definition). Although today there are many limitations\n  on the capabilities of custom elements—both functionally and semantically—that prevent them from\n  fully explaining the behaviors of HTML's existing elements, we hope to shrink this gap over\n  time."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h5 id="custom-elements-autonomous-example" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.13.1.1"
			}
			- " Creating an autonomous custom element"
			a href="#custom-elements-autonomous-example" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purposes of illustrating how to create an "
			a href="#autonomous-custom-element" id="custom-elements-autonomous-example:autonomous-custom-element" {
				- "autonomous custom element"
			}
			- ", let's\n  define a custom element that encapsulates rendering a small icon for a country flag. Our goal is\n  to be able to use it like so:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="html" {
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "flag-icon"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "country"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"nl\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "></"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "flag-icon"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To do this, we first declare a class for the custom element, extending\n  "
			code id="custom-elements-autonomous-example:htmlelement" {
				a href="#htmlelement" {
					- "HTMLElement"
				}
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="js" {
