		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Even with this rather-complicated element definition, the element is not a pleasure to use for\n  consumers: it will be continually \"sprouting\" "
			code id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:attr-tabindex-3" {
				a href="#attr-tabindex" {
					- "tabindex"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attributes of its own volition, and its choice of "
			code {
				- "tabindex=\"0\""
			}
			- " focusability\n  behavior may not match the "
			code id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:the-button-element" {
				a href="#the-button-element" {
					- "button"
				}
			}
			- " behavior on the current platform. This is because\n  as of now there is no way to specify default focus behavior for custom elements, forcing the use\n  of the "
			code id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:attr-tabindex-4" {
				a href="#attr-tabindex" {
					- "tabindex"
				}
			}
			- " attribute to do so (even though it is usually\n  reserved for allowing the consumer to override default behavior)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In contrast, a simple "
			a href="#customized-built-in-element" id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:customized-built-in-element" {
				- "customized built-in element"
			}
			- ", as shown in the previous\n  section, would automatically inherit the semantics and behavior of the "
			code id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:the-button-element-2" {
				a href="#the-button-element" {
					- "button"
				}
			}
			- "\n  element, with no need to implement these behaviors manually. In general, for any elements with\n  nontrivial behavior and semantics that build on top of existing elements of HTML, "
			a href="#customized-built-in-element" id="custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:customized-built-in-element-2" {
				- "customized built-in elements"
			}
			- " will be easier to\n  develop, maintain, and consume."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h5 id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.13.1.6"
			}
			- " Upgrading elements after their creation"
			a href="#custom-elements-upgrades-examples" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Because "
			a href="#element-definition" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:element-definition" {
				- "element definition"
			}
			- " can occur at any time, a non-custom element could be\n  "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-create-element" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:create-an-element" data-x-internal="create-an-element" {
				- "created"
			}
			- ", and then later become a "
			a href="#custom-element" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element" {
				- "custom\n  element"
			}
			- " after an appropriate "
			a href="#custom-element-definition" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element-definition" {
				- "definition"
			}
			- " is\n  registered. We call this process \"upgrading\" the element, from a normal element into a custom\n  element."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="#upgrades" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:upgrades" {
				- "Upgrades"
			}
			- " enable scenarios where it may be\n  preferable for "
			a href="#custom-element-definition" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element-definition-2" {
				- "custom element definitions"
			}
			- " to be\n  registered after relevant elements have been initially created, such as by the parser. They allow\n  progressive enhancement of the content in the custom element. For example, in the following HTML\n  document the element definition for "
			code {
				- "img-viewer"
			}
			- " is loaded\n  asynchronously:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="html" {
				c- cp="" {
					- "<!DOCTYPE html>"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "html"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "lang"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"en\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "title"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "Image viewer example"
				c- p="" {
					- "</"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "title"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "img-viewer"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "filter"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"Kelvin\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n  "
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "img"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "src"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"images/tree.jpg\""
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "alt"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"A beautiful tree towering over an empty savannah\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "</"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "img-viewer"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "script"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "src"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"js/elements/img-viewer.js\""
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "async"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "></"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "script"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The definition for the "
			code {
				- "img-viewer"
			}
			- " element here is loaded using a\n  "
			code id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:the-script-element" {
				a href="#the-script-element" {
					- "script"
				}
			}
			- " element marked with the "
			code id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:attr-script-async" {
				a href="#attr-script-async" {
					- "async"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, placed after the "
			code {
				- "<img-viewer>"
			}
			- " tag in the markup. While the\n  script is loading, the "
			code {
				- "img-viewer"
			}
			- " element will be treated as an undefined\n  element, similar to a "
			code id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:the-span-element" {
				a href="#the-span-element" {
					- "span"
				}
			}
			- ". Once the script loads, it will define the "
			code {
				- "img-viewer"
			}
			- " element, and the existing "
			code {
				- "img-viewer"
			}
			- " element on\n  the page will be upgraded, applying the custom element's definition (which presumably includes\n  applying an image filter identified by the string \"Kelvin\", enhancing the image's visual\n  appearance)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Note that "
			a href="#upgrades" id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:upgrades-2" {
				- "upgrades"
			}
			- " only apply to elements in the\n  document tree. (Formally, elements that are "
			a id="custom-elements-upgrades-examples:connected" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#connected" data-x-internal="connected" {
				- "connected"
			}
			- ".) An element that is not\n  inserted into a document will stay un-upgraded. An example illustrates this point:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="html" {
				c- cp="" {
					- "<!DOCTYPE html>"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "<"
				}
				c- f="" {
					- "html"
				}
				- " "
				c- e="" {
					- "lang"
				}
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				c- s="" {
					- "\"en\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ">"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
