		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="custom-element-conformance" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.13.2"
			}
			- " Requirements for custom element constructors and\n  reactions"
			a href="#custom-element-conformance" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When authoring "
			a href="#custom-element-constructor" id="custom-element-conformance:custom-element-constructor" {
				- "custom element constructors"
			}
			- ",\n  authors are bound by the following conformance requirements:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A parameter-less call to "
					code {
						- "super()"
					}
					- " must be the first statement in the\n   constructor body, to establish the correct prototype chain and "
					b {
						- "this"
					}
					- " value before any\n   further code is run."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					code {
						- "return"
					}
					- " statement must not appear anywhere inside the constructor\n   body, unless it is a simple early-return ("
					code {
						- "return"
					}
					- " or "
					code {
						- "return\n   this"
					}
					- ")."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The constructor must not use the "
					code id="custom-element-conformance:dom-document-write" {
						a href="#dom-document-write" {
							- "document.write()"
						}
					}
					- "\n   or "
					code id="custom-element-conformance:dom-document-open" {
						a href="#dom-document-open" {
							- "document.open()"
						}
					}
					- " methods."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's attributes and children must not be inspected, as in the non-"
					a href="#upgrades" id="custom-element-conformance:upgrades" {
						- "upgrade"
					}
					- " case none will be present, and relying on\n   upgrades makes the element less usable."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element must not gain any attributes or children, as this violates the expectations of\n   consumers who use the "
					code id="custom-element-conformance:dom-document-createelement" {
						a data-x-internal="dom-document-createelement" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createelement" {
							- "createElement"
						}
					}
					- " or "
					code id="custom-element-conformance:dom-document-createelementns" {
						a data-x-internal="dom-document-createelementns" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createelementns" {
							- "createElementNS"
						}
					}
					- " methods."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "In general, work should be deferred to "
					code {
						- "connectedCallback"
					}
					- " as much as\n   possible—especially work involving fetching resources or rendering. However, note that "
					code {
						- "connectedCallback"
					}
					- " can be called more than once, so any initialization work that\n   is truly one-time will need a guard to prevent it from running twice."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "In general, the constructor should be used to set up initial state and default values, and\n   to set up event listeners and possibly a "
					a id="custom-element-conformance:shadow-root" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-root" data-x-internal="shadow-root" {
						- "shadow root"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Several of these requirements are checked during "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-create-element" id="custom-element-conformance:create-an-element" data-x-internal="create-an-element" {
				- "element\n  creation"
			}
			- ", either directly or indirectly, and failing to follow them will result in a custom\n  element that cannot be instantiated by the parser or DOM APIs. This is true even if the work is\n  done inside a constructor-initiated "
			a href="#microtask" id="custom-element-conformance:microtask" {
				- "microtask"
			}
			- ", as a "
			a href="#perform-a-microtask-checkpoint" id="custom-element-conformance:perform-a-microtask-checkpoint" {
				- "microtask checkpoint"
			}
			- " can occur immediately after construction."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When authoring "
			a href="#concept-custom-element-reaction" id="custom-element-conformance:concept-custom-element-reaction" {
				- "custom element reactions"
			}
			- ",\n  authors should avoid manipulating the node tree as this can lead to unexpected results."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "An element's "
				code {
					- "connectedCallback"
				}
				- " can be queued before the element is\n   disconnected, but as the callback queue is still processed, it results in a "
				code {
					- "connectedCallback"
				}
				- " for an element that is no longer connected:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="js" {
					c- a="" {
						- "class"
					}
					- " CParent "
					c- k="" {
						- "extends"
					}
					- " HTMLElement "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n  connectedCallback"
					c- p="" {
						- "()"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n    "
					c- k="" {
						- "this"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "firstChild"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "remove"
					c- p="" {
						- "();"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "}"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "}"
					}
					- "\ncustomElements"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "define"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					c- u="" {
						- "\"c-parent\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ","
					}
					- " CParent"
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
					- "\n\n"
					c- a="" {
						- "class"
					}
					- " CChild "
					c- k="" {
						- "extends"
					}
					- " HTMLElement "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n  connectedCallback"
					c- p="" {
						- "()"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n    console"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "log"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					c- u="" {
