		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "The intent behind this extended attribute is somewhat subtle. One way of accomplishing its\n   goals would be to say that every operation, attribute, setter, and deleter on the platform\n   must have these steps inserted, and to allow implementers to optimize away\n   unnecessary cases (where no DOM mutation is possible that could cause "
				a href="#concept-custom-element-reaction" id="custom-element-reactions:concept-custom-element-reaction-6" {
					- "custom element reactions"
				}
				- " to occur)."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, in practice this imprecision could lead to non-interoperable implementations of "
				a href="#concept-custom-element-reaction" id="custom-element-reactions:concept-custom-element-reaction-7" {
					- "custom element reactions"
				}
				- ", as some implementations\n   might forget to invoke these steps in some cases. Instead, we settled on the approach of\n   explicitly annotating all relevant IDL constructs, as a way of ensuring interoperable behavior\n   and helping implementations easily pinpoint all cases where these steps are necessary."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Any nonstandard APIs introduced by the user agent that could modify the DOM in such a way as to\n  cause "
			a href="#enqueue-a-custom-element-callback-reaction" id="custom-element-reactions:enqueue-a-custom-element-callback-reaction" {
				- "enqueuing a custom element\n  callback reaction"
			}
			- " or "
			a href="#enqueue-a-custom-element-upgrade-reaction" id="custom-element-reactions:enqueue-a-custom-element-upgrade-reaction" {
				- "enqueuing a\n  custom element upgrade reaction"
			}
			- ", for example by modifying any attributes or child elements,\n  must also be decorated with the "
			code id="custom-element-reactions:cereactions-4" {
				a href="#cereactions" {
					- "[CEReactions]"
				}
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "As of the time of this writing, the following nonstandard or not-yet-standardized APIs are\n   known to fall into this category:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			ul {
				li {
					p {
						code id="custom-element-reactions:htmlinputelement" {
							a href="#htmlinputelement" {
								- "HTMLInputElement"
							}
						}
						- "'s "
						code {
							- "webkitdirectory"
						}
						- " and "
						code {
							- "incremental"
						}
						- " IDL attributes"
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						code id="custom-element-reactions:htmllinkelement" {
							a href="#htmllinkelement" {
								- "HTMLLinkElement"
							}
						}
						- "'s "
						code {
							- "scope"
						}
						- " IDL attribute"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="element-internals" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.13.7"
			}
			- " Element internals"
			a href="#element-internals" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Certain capabilities are meant to be available to a custom element author, but not to a custom\n  element consumer. These are provided by the "
			code id="element-internals:dom-attachinternals" {
				a href="#dom-attachinternals" {
					- "element.attachInternals()"
				}
			}
			- " method, which returns an instance of\n  "
			code id="element-internals:elementinternals" {
				a href="#elementinternals" {
					- "ElementInternals"
				}
			}
			- ". The properties and methods of "
			code id="element-internals:elementinternals-2" {
				a href="#elementinternals" {
					- "ElementInternals"
				}
			}
			- " allow\n  control over internal features which the user agent provides to all elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-attachinternals" id="dom-attachinternals-dev" {
						- "attachInternals()"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns an "
					code id="element-internals:elementinternals-3" {
						a href="#elementinternals" {
							- "ElementInternals"
						}
					}
					- " object targeting the "
					a href="#custom-element" id="element-internals:custom-element" {
						- "custom element"
					}
					- "\n   "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- ". Throws an exception if "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " is not a "
					a href="#custom-element" id="element-internals:custom-element-2" {
						- "custom\n   element"
					}
					- ", if the \""
					code {
						- "internals"
					}
					- "\" feature was disabled as part of the\n   element definition, or if it is called twice on the same element."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="element-internals:htmlelement" {
				a href="#htmlelement" {
					- "HTMLElement"
				}
			}
			- " has an "
			dfn id="attached-internals" {
				- "attached internals"
			}
			- " (null or an\n  "
			code id="element-internals:elementinternals-4" {
				a href="#elementinternals" {
					- "ElementInternals"
				}
			}
			- " object), initially null."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
