		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The following extract shows how an IM conversation log could be marked up, using the\n   "
				code id="conversations:the-data-element" {
					a href="#the-data-element" {
						- "data"
					}
				}
				- " element to provide Unix timestamps for each line. Note that the timestamps are\n   provided in a format that the "
				code id="conversations:the-time-element" {
					a href="#the-time-element" {
						- "time"
					}
				}
				- " element does not support, so the\n   "
				code id="conversations:the-data-element-2" {
					a href="#the-data-element" {
						- "data"
					}
				}
				- " element is used instead (namely, Unix "
				code {
					- "time_t"
				}
				- " timestamps).\n   Had the author wished to mark up the data using one of the date and time formats supported by the\n   "
				code id="conversations:the-time-element-2" {
					a href="#the-time-element" {
						- "time"
					}
				}
				- " element, that element could have been used instead of "
				code id="conversations:the-data-element-3" {
					a href="#the-data-element" {
						- "data"
					}
				}
				- ". This\n   could be advantageous as it would allow data analysis tools to detect the timestamps\n   unambiguously, without coordination with the page author."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
