		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "HTML does not have a good way to mark up graphs, so descriptions of interactive conversations\n   from games are more difficult to mark up. This example shows one possible convention using\n   "
				code id="conversations:the-dl-element" {
					a href="#the-dl-element" {
						- "dl"
					}
				}
				- " elements to list the possible responses at each point in the conversation.\n   Another option to consider is describing the conversation in the form of a DOT file, and\n   outputting the result as an SVG image to place in the document. "
				a href="#refsDOT" {
					- "[DOT]"
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " Next, you meet a fisher. You can say one of several greetings:\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Hello there!\"\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She responds with \"Hello, how may I help you?\"; you can respond with:\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"I would like to buy a fish.\"\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She sells you a fish and the conversation finishes.\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Can I borrow your boat?\"\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She is surprised and asks \"What are you offering in return?\".\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Five gold.\" (if you have enough)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Ten gold.\" (if you have enough)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Fifteen gold.\" (if you have enough)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She lends you her boat. The conversation ends.\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"A fish.\" (if you have one)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"A newspaper.\" (if you have one)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"A pebble.\" (if you have one)\n     "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"No thanks\", she replies. Your conversation options\n     at this point are the same as they were after asking to borrow\n     her boat, minus any options you've suggested before.\n    "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Vote for me in the next election!\"\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She turns away. The conversation finishes.\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Madam, are you aware that your fish are running away?\"\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She looks at you skeptically and says \"Fish cannot run, miss\".\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"You got me!\"\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " The fisher sighs and the conversation ends.\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Only kidding.\"\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Good one!\" she retorts. Your conversation options at this\n   point are the same as those following \"Hello there!\" above.\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dt"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " \"Oh, then what are they doing?\"\n   "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- " She looks at her fish, giving you an opportunity to steal\n   her boat, which you do. The conversation ends.\n  "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dd"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "dl"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In some games, conversations are simpler: each character merely has a fixed set of lines that\n   they say. In this example, a game FAQ/walkthrough lists some of the known possible responses for\n   each character:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "section"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Dialogue"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "h1"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n "
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "p"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "small"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "Some characters repeat their lines in order each time you interact\n with them, others randomly pick from amongst their lines. Those who respond in\n order have numbered entries in the lists below."
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "small"
					}
					c- p="" {
