		h3 id="disabled-elements" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.15"
			}
			- " Disabled elements"
			a href="#disabled-elements" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An element is said to be "
			dfn id="concept-element-disabled" {
				- "actually disabled"
			}
			- " if it\n  is one of the following:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "a "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-button-element" {
					a href="#the-button-element" {
						- "button"
					}
				}
				- " element that is "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fe-disabled" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "an "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-input-element" {
					a href="#the-input-element" {
						- "input"
					}
				}
				- " element that is "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fe-disabled-2" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "a "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-select-element" {
					a href="#the-select-element" {
						- "select"
					}
				}
				- " element that is "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fe-disabled-3" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "a "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-textarea-element" {
					a href="#the-textarea-element" {
						- "textarea"
					}
				}
				- " element that is "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fe-disabled-4" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "an "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-optgroup-element" {
					a href="#the-optgroup-element" {
						- "optgroup"
					}
				}
				- " element that has a "
				code id="disabled-elements:attr-optgroup-disabled" {
					a href="#attr-optgroup-disabled" {
						- "disabled"
					}
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			li {
				- "an "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-option-element" {
					a href="#the-option-element" {
						- "option"
					}
				}
				- " element that is "
				a href="#concept-option-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-option-disabled" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "a "
				code id="disabled-elements:the-fieldset-element" {
					a href="#the-fieldset-element" {
						- "fieldset"
					}
				}
				- " element that is a "
				a href="#concept-fieldset-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fieldset-disabled" {
					- "disabled fieldset"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "a "
				a href="#form-associated-custom-element" id="disabled-elements:form-associated-custom-element" {
					- "form-associated custom element"
				}
				- " that is\n   "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="disabled-elements:concept-fe-disabled-5" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This definition is used to determine what elements are "
			a href="#focusable" id="disabled-elements:focusable" {
				- "focusable"
			}
			- " and\n  which elements match the "
			code id="disabled-elements:selector-enabled" {
				a href="#selector-enabled" {
					- ":enabled"
				}
			}
			- " and\n  "
			code id="disabled-elements:selector-disabled" {
				a href="#selector-disabled" {
					- ":disabled"
				}
			}
			- " "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#pseudo-class" id="disabled-elements:pseudo-class" data-x-internal="pseudo-class" {
				- "pseudo\n  classes"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h3 id="selectors" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.16"
			}
			- " Matching HTML elements using selectors and CSS"
			a href="#selectors" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.16.1"
			}
			- " Case-sensitivity of the CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:'attr()'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#funcdef-attr" data-x-internal="'attr()'" {
				- "'attr()'"
			}
			- " function"
			a href="#case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			cite {
				- "CSS Values and Units"
			}
			- " leaves the case-sensitivity of attribute names for the\n  purpose of the "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:'attr()'-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#funcdef-attr" data-x-internal="'attr()'" {
				- "'attr()'"
			}
			- " function to be defined by the host language.\n  "
			a href="#refsCSSVALUES" {
				- "[CSSVALUES]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When comparing the attribute name part of a CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:'attr()'-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#funcdef-attr" data-x-internal="'attr()'" {
				- "'attr()'"
			}
			- " function to the names of\n  namespace-less attributes on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:html-elements" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:html-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML documents"
			}
			- ", the name\n  part of the CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:'attr()'-4" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#funcdef-attr" data-x-internal="'attr()'" {
				- "'attr()'"
			}
			- " function must first be "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:converted-to-ascii-lowercase" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" data-x-internal="converted-to-ascii-lowercase" {
				- "converted to ASCII\n  lowercase"
			}
			- ". The same function when compared to other attributes must be compared according\n  to its original case. In both cases, to match the values must be "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:identical-to" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-is" data-x-internal="identical-to" {
				- "identical to"
			}
			- " each\n  other (and therefore the comparison is case sensitive)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This is the same as comparing the name part of a CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-the-css-'attr()'-function:attribute-selector" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#attribute-selector" data-x-internal="attribute-selector" {
				- "attribute\n  selector"
			}
			- ", specified in the next section."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "4.16.2"
			}
			- " Case-sensitivity of selectors"
			a href="#case-sensitivity-of-selectors" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			cite {
				- "Selectors"
			}
			- " leaves the case-sensitivity of element names, attribute names, and\n  attribute values to be defined by the host language. "
			a href="#refsSELECTORS" {
				- "[SELECTORS]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When comparing a CSS element "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:type-selector" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#type-selector" data-x-internal="type-selector" {
				- "type selector"
			}
			- " to the names of "
			a href="#html-elements" id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:html-elements" {
				- "HTML\n  elements"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:html-documents" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML documents"
			}
			- ", the CSS element "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:type-selector-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#type-selector" data-x-internal="type-selector" {
				- "type selector"
			}
			- " must\n  first be "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:converted-to-ascii-lowercase" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" data-x-internal="converted-to-ascii-lowercase" {
				- "converted to ASCII lowercase"
			}
			- ". The same selector when compared to other\n  elements must be compared according to its original case. In both cases, to match the values must\n  be "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:identical-to" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-is" data-x-internal="identical-to" {
				- "identical to"
			}
			- " each other (and therefore the comparison is case sensitive)."
		}
		- "\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When comparing the name part of a CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:attribute-selector" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#attribute-selector" data-x-internal="attribute-selector" {
				- "attribute selector"
			}
			- " to the names of\n  attributes on "
			a href="#html-elements" id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:html-elements-2" {
				- "HTML elements"
			}
			- " in "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:html-documents-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
				- "HTML documents"
			}
			- ", the name\n  part of the CSS "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:attribute-selector-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/selectors/#attribute-selector" data-x-internal="attribute-selector" {
				- "attribute selector"
			}
			- " must first be "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:converted-to-ascii-lowercase-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" data-x-internal="converted-to-ascii-lowercase" {
				- "converted to ASCII\n  lowercase"
			}
			- ". The same selector when compared to other attributes must be compared according\n  to its original case. In both cases, the comparison is case-sensitive."
		}
		- "\n  \n\n  "
		p {
