		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, the selector "
				code {
					- "[bgcolor=\"#ffffff\"]"
				}
				- " will match any HTML\n   element with a "
				code {
					- "bgcolor"
				}
				- " attribute with values including "
				code {
					- "#ffffff"
				}
				- ", "
				code {
					- "#FFFFFF"
				}
				- " and "
				code {
					- "#fffFFF"
				}
				- ". This\n   happens even if "
				code {
					- "bgcolor"
				}
				- " has no effect for a given element (e.g.,\n   "
				code id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:the-div-element" {
					a href="#the-div-element" {
						- "div"
					}
				}
				- ")."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The selector "
				code {
					- "[type=a s]"
				}
				- " will match any\n   HTML element with a "
				code {
					- "type"
				}
				- " attribute whose value is "
				code {
					- "a"
				}
				- ", but not whose value is "
				code {
					- "A"
				}
				- ", due to the "
				code {
					- "s"
				}
				- " flag."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All other attribute values and everything else must be treated as entirely "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:identical-to-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-is" data-x-internal="identical-to" {
				- "identical\n  to"
			}
			- " each other for the purposes of selector matching. This includes:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
