		p class="note" {
			cite {
				- "Selectors"
			}
			- " defines that ID and class selectors (such as "
			code {
				- "#foo"
			}
			- " and "
			code {
				- ".bar"
			}
			- "), when matched against elements in documents\n  that are in "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:quirks-mode" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" data-x-internal="quirks-mode" {
				- "quirks mode"
			}
			- ", will be matched in an "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:ascii-case-insensitive-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
				- "ASCII case-insensitive"
			}
			- "\n  manner. However, this does not apply for attribute selectors with \""
			code {
				- "id"
			}
			- "\" or\n  \""
			code {
				- "class"
			}
			- "\" as the name part. The selector "
			code {
				- "[class=\"foobar\"]"
			}
			- " will treat its value as case-sensitive even in\n  "
			a id="case-sensitivity-of-selectors:quirks-mode-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" data-x-internal="quirks-mode" {
