		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h2 id="microdata" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "5"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				- "Microdata"
			}
			a href="#microdata" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="introduction-7" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "5.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-7" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="overview" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "5.1.1"
			}
			- " Overview"
			a href="#overview" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Sometimes, it is desirable to annotate content with specific machine-readable labels, e.g. to\n  allow generic scripts to provide services that are customized to the page, or to enable content\n  from a variety of cooperating authors to be processed by a single script in a consistent\n  manner."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For this purpose, authors can use the microdata features described in this section. Microdata\n  allows nested groups of name-value pairs to be added to documents, in parallel with the existing\n  content."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-basic-syntax" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "5.1.2"
			}
			- " The basic syntax"
			a href="#the-basic-syntax" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "At a high level, microdata consists of a group of name-value pairs. The groups are called "
			a href="#concept-item" id="the-basic-syntax:concept-item" {
				- "items"
			}
			- ", and each name-value pair is a property. Items and properties\n  are represented by regular elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To create an item, the "
			code id="the-basic-syntax:attr-itemscope" {
				a href="#attr-itemscope" {
					- "itemscope"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is used."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To add a property to an item, the "
			code id="the-basic-syntax:names:-the-itemprop-attribute" {
				a href="#names:-the-itemprop-attribute" {
					- "itemprop"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is used\n  on one of the "
