		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="items:attr-itemref-3" {
				a href="#attr-itemref" {
					- "itemref"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is not part of the\n  microdata data model. It is merely a syntactic construct to aid authors in adding annotations to\n  pages where the data to be annotated does not follow a convenient tree structure. For example, it\n  allows authors to mark up data in a table so that each column defines a separate "
			a href="#concept-item" id="items:concept-item-12" {
				- "item"
			}
			- ", while keeping the properties in the cells."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This example shows a simple vocabulary used to describe the products of a model railway\n   manufacturer. The vocabulary has just five property names:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			dl {
				dt {
					- "product-code"
				}
				dd {
					- "An integer that names the product in the manufacturer's catalog."
				}
				dt {
					- "name"
				}
				dd {
					- "A brief description of the product."
				}
				dt {
					- "scale"
				}
				dd {
					- "One of \"HO\", \"1\", or \"Z\" (potentially with leading or trailing\n    whitespace), indicating the scale of the product."
				}
				dt {
					- "digital"
				}
				dd {
					- "If present, one of \"Digital\", \"Delta\", or \"Systems\"\n    (potentially with leading or trailing whitespace) indicating that\n    the product has a digital decoder of the given type."
				}
				dt {
					- "track-type"
				}
				dd {
					- "For track-specific products, one of \"K\", \"M\", \"C\" (potentially\n    with leading or trailing whitespace) indicating the type of track\n    for which the product is intended."
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This vocabulary has four defined "
				a href="#item-types" id="items:item-types-10" {
