		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="inert-subtrees" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.3"
			}
			- " Inert subtrees"
			a href="#inert-subtrees" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "See also "
			code id="inert-subtrees:the-inert-attribute" {
				a href="#the-inert-attribute" {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " for an explanation of the\n  attribute of the same name."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A node (in particular elements and text nodes) can be "
			dfn id="inert" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- ". When a node is\n  "
			a href="#inert" id="inert-subtrees:inert" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "Hit-testing must act as if the "
					a id="inert-subtrees:'pointer-events'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui-4/#pointer-events-control" data-x-internal="'pointer-events'" {
						- "'pointer-events'"
					}
					- " CSS property were set to\n   'none'."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Text selection functionality must act as if the "
					a id="inert-subtrees:'user-select'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui-4/#content-selection" data-x-internal="'user-select'" {
						- "'user-select'"
					}
					- " CSS property\n   were set to 'none'."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If it is "
					a id="inert-subtrees:editable" href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" data-x-internal="editable" {
						- "editable"
					}
					- ", the node behaves as if it were non-editable."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The user agent should ignore the node for the purposes of "
					a href="#find-in-page-2" id="inert-subtrees:find-in-page-2" {
						- "find-in-page"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Inert nodes generally cannot be focused, and user agents do not expose the inert\n  nodes to accessibility APIs or assistive technologies. Inert nodes that are "
			a href="#concept-command" id="inert-subtrees:concept-command" {
				- "commands"
			}
			- " will become inoperable to users, in the manner described\n  above."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents may allow the user to override the restrictions on "
			a href="#find-in-page-2" id="inert-subtrees:find-in-page-2-2" {
				- "find-in-page"
			}
			- " and\n  text selection, however."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "By default, a node is not "
			a href="#inert" id="inert-subtrees:inert-2" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.3.1"
			}
			- " Modal dialogs and inert subtrees"
			a href="#modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "document"
			}
			- " is "
			dfn id="blocked-by-a-modal-dialog" {
				- "blocked by a modal dialog"
			}
			- "\n  "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " if "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " is the topmost "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:the-dialog-element" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element in\n  "
			var {
				- "document"
			}
			- "'s "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:top-layer" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#document-top-layer" data-x-internal="top-layer" {
				- "top layer"
			}
			- ". While "
			var {
				- "document"
			}
			- " is so blocked, every node\n  that is "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:connected" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#connected" data-x-internal="connected" {
				- "connected"
			}
			- " to "
			var {
				- "document"
			}
			- ", with the exception of the\n  "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " element and its "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:flat-tree" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree" data-x-internal="flat-tree" {
				- "flat tree"
			}
			- " descendants, must become\n  "
			a href="#inert" id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:inert" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " can additionally become "
			a href="#inert" id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:inert-2" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- " via the "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:the-inert-attribute" {
				a href="#the-inert-attribute" {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " attribute, but only if specified on "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " itself\n  (i.e., "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- " escapes inertness of ancestors); "
			var {
				- "subject"
			}
			- "'s "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:flat-tree-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree" data-x-internal="flat-tree" {
				- "flat\n  tree"
			}
			- " descendants can become "
			a href="#inert" id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:inert-3" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- " in a similar fashion."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:the-dialog-element-2" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:dom-dialog-showmodal" {
				a href="#dom-dialog-showmodal" {
					- "showModal()"
				}
			}
			- " method causes this mechanism to trigger, by "
			a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#add-an-element-to-the-top-layer" id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:add-an-element-to-the-top-layer" data-x-internal="add-an-element-to-the-top-layer" {
				- "adding"
			}
			- " the "
			code id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:the-dialog-element-3" {
				a href="#the-dialog-element" {
					- "dialog"
				}
			}
			- " element to its\n  "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- "'s "
			a id="modal-dialogs-and-inert-subtrees:top-layer-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-position-4/#document-top-layer" data-x-internal="top-layer" {
				- "top layer"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-inert-attribute" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.3.2"
			}
			- " The "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " attribute"
			a href="#the-inert-attribute" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/inert" title="The inert global attribute is a Boolean attribute indicating that the browser will ignore the element. With the inert attribute, all of the element's flat tree descendants (such as modal <dialog>s) that don't otherwise escape inertness are ignored. The inert attribute also makes the browser ignore input events sent by the user, including focus-related events and events from assistive technologies." {
						- "Global_attributes/inert"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "112+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "15.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "102+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "102+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge unknown" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "No"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="the-inert-attribute:the-inert-attribute" {
				a href="#the-inert-attribute" {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="the-inert-attribute:boolean-attribute" {
				- "boolean attribute"
			}
			- " that\n  indicates, by its presence, that the element and all its "
			a id="the-inert-attribute:flat-tree" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scoping/#flat-tree" data-x-internal="flat-tree" {
				- "flat tree"
			}
			- " descendants which\n  don't otherwise escape inertness (such as modal dialogs) are to be made "
			a href="#inert" id="the-inert-attribute:inert" {
				- "inert"
			}
			- " by the\n  user agent."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An inert subtree should not contain any content or controls which are critical to\n  understanding or using aspects of the page which are not in the inert state. Content in an inert\n  subtree will not be perceivable by all users, or interactive. Authors should not specify elements\n  as inert unless the content they represent are also visually obscured in some way. In most cases,\n  authors should not specify the "
			code id="the-inert-attribute:inert-2" {
				a href="#inert" {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " attribute on individual form controls. In these\n  instances, the "
			code id="the-inert-attribute:attr-fe-disabled" {
				a href="#attr-fe-disabled" {
					- "disabled"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is probably more\n  appropriate."
		}
