						- "div"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "section"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			img src="/images/inert-example-loading-section.png" width="947" alt="Screenshot of Population by City content with an overlaid loading message which visually obscures the form controls and data table which have not fully rendered, and thus are in the inert state." height="243"
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The \"loading\" overlay obscures the inert content, making it visually apparent that the inert\n   content is not presently accessible. Notice that the heading and \"loading\" text are not\n   descendants of the element with the "
				code id="the-inert-attribute:inert-3" {
					a href="#inert" {
						- "inert"
					}
				}
				- " attribute. This will ensure this text is\n   accessible to all users, while the inert content cannot be interacted with by anyone."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "By default, there is no persistent visual indication of an element or its subtree being\n   inert. Appropriate visual styles for such content is often context-dependent. For instance, an\n   inert off-screen navigation panel would not require a default style, as its off-screen position\n   visually obscures the content. Similarly, a modal "
				code id="the-inert-attribute:the-dialog-element" {
					a href="#the-dialog-element" {
						- "dialog"
					}
				}
				- " element's backdrop will\n   serve as the means to visually obscure the inert content of the web page, rather than styling\n   the inert content specifically."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "However, for many other situations authors are strongly encouraged to clearly mark what parts\n   of their document are active and which are inert, to avoid user confusion. In particular, it is\n   worth remembering that not all users can see all parts of a page at once; for example, users of\n   screen readers, users on small devices or with magnifiers, and even users using particularly\n   small windows might not be able to see the active part of a page and might get frustrated if\n   inert sections are not obviously inert."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLElement/inert" title="The HTMLElement property inert reflects the value of the element's inert attribute. It is a boolean value that, when present, makes the browser \"ignore\" user input events for the element, including focus events and events from assistive technologies. The browser may also ignore page search and text selection in the element. This can be useful when building UIs such as modals where you would want to \"trap\" the focus inside the modal when it's visible." {
						- "HTMLElement/inert"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "112+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "15.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "102+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "102+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge unknown" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "No"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLElement" id="dom-inert" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "inert"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute\n  must "
			a href="#reflect" id="the-inert-attribute:reflect" {
				- "reflect"
			}
			- " the content attribute of the same name."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h3 id="tracking-user-activation" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.4"
			}
			- " Tracking "
			dfn data-export="" {
				- "user activation"
			}
			a href="#tracking-user-activation" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To prevent abuse of certain APIs that could be annoying to users (e.g., opening popups or\n  vibrating phones), user agents allow these APIs only when the user is actively interacting with\n  the web page or has interacted with the page at least once. This \"active interaction\" state is\n  maintained through the mechanisms defined in this section."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="user-activation-data-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.4.1"
			}
			- " Data model"
			a href="#user-activation-data-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purpose of tracking user activation, each "
			code id="user-activation-data-model:window" {
				a href="#window" {
					- "Window"
				}
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "W"
			}
			- " has two\n  relevant values:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="last-activation-timestamp" {
						- "last activation timestamp"
					}
					- ", which is either a\n   "
					code id="user-activation-data-model:domhighrestimestamp" {
						a data-x-internal="domhighrestimestamp" href="https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dom-domhighrestimestamp" {
							- "DOMHighResTimeStamp"
						}
					}
					- ", positive infinity (indicating that "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " has never been\n   activated), or negative infinity (indicating that the activation has been "
					a href="#consume-user-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:consume-user-activation" {
						- "consumed"
					}
					- "). Initially positive infinity."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="last-history-action-activation-timestamp" {
						- "last history-action activation timestamp"
					}
					- ", which is either a\n   "
					code id="user-activation-data-model:domhighrestimestamp-2" {
						a data-x-internal="domhighrestimestamp" href="https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dom-domhighrestimestamp" {
							- "DOMHighResTimeStamp"
						}
					}
					- " or positive infinity, initially positive infinity."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A user agent also defines a "
			dfn id="transient-activation-duration" {
				- "transient activation duration"
			}
			- ", which is a constant\n  number indicating how long a user activation is available for certain "
			a href="#user-activation-gated-apis" {
				- "user activation-gated APIs"
			}
			- " (e.g., for opening popups)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			a href="#transient-activation-duration" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-duration" {
				- "transient activation duration"
			}
			- " is expected be at most a few\n  seconds, so that the user can possibly perceive the link between an interaction with the page and\n  the page calling the activation-gated API."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "We then have the following boolean user activation states for "
			var {
				- "W"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="sticky-activation" data-export="" {
					- "Sticky activation"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When the "
					a id="user-activation-data-model:current-high-resolution-time" href="https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-current-high-resolution-time" data-x-internal="current-high-resolution-time" {
						- "current high resolution time"
					}
					- " given "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is greater than or\n    equal to the "
					a href="#last-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-activation-timestamp" {
						- "last activation timestamp"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- ", "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is said to\n    have "
					a href="#sticky-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:sticky-activation" {
						- "sticky activation"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This is "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- "'s historical activation state, indicating whether the user has ever\n    interacted in "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- ". It starts false, then changes to true (and never changes back to\n    false) when "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " gets the very first "
					a href="#activation-notification" id="user-activation-data-model:activation-notification" {
						- "activation notification"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="transient-activation" data-export="" {
					- "Transient activation"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When the "
					a id="user-activation-data-model:current-high-resolution-time-2" href="https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-current-high-resolution-time" data-x-internal="current-high-resolution-time" {
						- "current high resolution time"
					}
					- " given "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is greater than or\n    equal to the "
					a href="#last-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-activation-timestamp-2" {
						- "last activation timestamp"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- ", and less than the\n    "
					a href="#last-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-activation-timestamp-3" {
						- "last activation timestamp"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " plus the "
					a href="#transient-activation-duration" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-duration-2" {
						- "transient activation\n    duration"
					}
					- ", then "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is said to have "
					a href="#transient-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation" {
						- "transient activation"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This is "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- "'s current activation state, indicating whether the user has interacted\n    in "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " recently. This starts with a false value, and remains true for a limited time\n    after every "
					a href="#activation-notification" id="user-activation-data-model:activation-notification-2" {
						- "activation notification"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " gets."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The "
					a href="#transient-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-2" {
						- "transient activation"
					}
					- " state is considered "
					dfn id="activation-expiry" {
						- "expired"
					}
					- " if it becomes false because the "
					a href="#transient-activation-duration" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-duration-3" {
						- "transient\n    activation duration"
					}
					- " time has elapsed since the last user activation. Note that it can\n    become false even before the expiry time through an "
					a href="#consume-user-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:consume-user-activation-2" {
						- "activation consumption"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="history-action-activation" {
					- "History-action activation"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "When the "
					a href="#last-history-action-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-history-action-activation-timestamp" {
						- "last history-action activation timestamp"
					}
					- " of "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is not equal\n    to the "
					a href="#last-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-activation-timestamp-4" {
						- "last activation timestamp"
					}
					- " of "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- ", then "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- " is said to have\n    "
					a href="#history-action-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:history-action-activation" {
						- "history-action activation"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This is a special variant of user activation, used to allow access to certain session history\n    APIs which, if used too frequently, would make it harder for the user to traverse back using "
					a href="#nav-traversal-ui" {
						- "browser UI"
					}
					- ". It starts with a false value, and becomes true whenever\n    the user interacts with "
					var {
						- "W"
					}
					- ", but is reset to false through "
					a href="#consume-history-action-user-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:consume-history-action-user-activation" {
						- "history-action activation consumption"
					}
					- ". This ensures such\n    APIs cannot be used multiple times in a row without an intervening user activation. But unlike\n    "
					a href="#transient-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-3" {
						- "transient activation"
					}
					- ", there is no time limit within which such APIs must be\n    used."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			a href="#last-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-activation-timestamp-5" {
				- "last activation timestamp"
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#last-history-action-activation-timestamp" id="user-activation-data-model:last-history-action-activation-timestamp-2" {
				- "last history-action\n  activation timestamp"
			}
			- " are retained even after the "
			code id="user-activation-data-model:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " changes its\n  "
			a href="#fully-active" id="user-activation-data-model:fully-active" {
				- "fully active"
			}
			- " status (e.g., after navigating away from a "
			code id="user-activation-data-model:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- ", or\n  navigating to a cached "
			code id="user-activation-data-model:document-3" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "). This means "
			a href="#sticky-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:sticky-activation-2" {
				- "sticky activation"
			}
			- " state\n  spans multiple navigations as long as the same "
			code id="user-activation-data-model:document-4" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " gets reused. For the\n  transient activation state, the original "
			a href="#activation-expiry" id="user-activation-data-model:activation-expiry" {
				- "expiry"
			}
			- " time\n  remains unchanged (i.e., the state still expires within the "
			a href="#transient-activation-duration" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-duration-4" {
				- "transient activation\n  duration"
			}
			- " limit from the original "
			a href="#activation-triggering-input-event" id="user-activation-data-model:activation-triggering-input-event" {
				- "activation triggering input event"
			}
			- "). It is\n  important to consider this when deciding whether to base certain things off "
			a href="#sticky-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:sticky-activation-3" {
				- "sticky\n  activation"
			}
			- " or "
			a href="#transient-activation" id="user-activation-data-model:transient-activation-4" {
				- "transient activation"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="user-activation-processing-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.4.2"
			}
			- " Processing model"
			a href="#user-activation-processing-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a user interaction causes firing of an "
			a href="#activation-triggering-input-event" id="user-activation-processing-model:activation-triggering-input-event" {
				- "activation triggering input\n  event"
			}
			- " in a "
			code id="user-activation-processing-model:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "document"
			}
			- ", the user agent must perform the\n  following "
			dfn id="activation-notification" {
				- "activation notification"
			}
			- " steps "
			em {
				- "before"
			}
			- " "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch" id="user-activation-processing-model:concept-event-dispatch" data-x-internal="concept-event-dispatch" {
				- "dispatching"
			}
			- " the event:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					a id="user-activation-processing-model:assert" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#assert" data-x-internal="assert" {
						- "Assert"
					}
					- ": "
					var {
						- "document"
					}
					- " is "
					a href="#fully-active" id="user-activation-processing-model:fully-active" {
						- "fully active"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "windows"
					}
					- " be « "
					var {
						- "document"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-relevant-global" id="user-activation-processing-model:concept-relevant-global" {
						- "relevant global object"
					}
					- "\n   »."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-extend" id="user-activation-processing-model:list-extend" data-x-internal="list-extend" {
						- "Extend"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "windows"
					}
					- " with the "
					a href="#nav-window" id="user-activation-processing-model:nav-window" {
						- "active window"
					}
					- " of each of "
					var {
						- "document"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#ancestor-navigables" id="user-activation-processing-model:ancestor-navigables" {
						- "ancestor\n   navigables"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-extend" id="user-activation-processing-model:list-extend-2" data-x-internal="list-extend" {
						- "Extend"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "windows"
					}
					- " with the "
					a href="#nav-window" id="user-activation-processing-model:nav-window-2" {
						- "active window"
					}
					- " of each of "
					var {
						- "document"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#descendant-navigables" id="user-activation-processing-model:descendant-navigables" {
						- "descendant\n   navigables"
					}
					- ", filtered to include only those "
					a href="#navigable" id="user-activation-processing-model:navigable" {
						- "navigables"
					}
					- "\n   whose "
					a href="#nav-document" id="user-activation-processing-model:nav-document" {
						- "active document"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="user-activation-processing-model:concept-document-origin" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
						- "origin"
					}
					- " is "
					a href="#same-origin" id="user-activation-processing-model:same-origin" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- " with\n   "
					var {
						- "document"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="user-activation-processing-model:concept-document-origin-2" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
						- "origin"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id="user-activation-processing-model:list-iterate" data-x-internal="list-iterate" {
						- "For each"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "window"
					}
					- " in "
					var {
						- "windows"
					}
					- ":"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Set "
							var {
								- "window"
							}
