		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="user-activation-user-agent-automation" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.4.5"
			}
			- " User agent automation"
			a href="#user-activation-user-agent-automation" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purposes of user-agent automation and application testing, this specification defines\n  the following "
			a id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:extension-command" href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#dfn-extension-commands" data-x-internal="extension-command" {
				- "extension command"
			}
			- " for the "
			cite {
				- "Web Driver"
			}
			- " specification. It is\n  optional for a user agent to support the following "
			a id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:extension-command-2" href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#dfn-extension-commands" data-x-internal="extension-command" {
				- "extension command"
			}
			- ".\n  "
			a href="#refsWEBDRIVER" {
				- "[WEBDRIVER]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table class="data" {
			thead {
				tr {
					th {
						- "HTTP Method"
					}
					th {
						- "URI Template"
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						- "`"
						code {
							- "POST"
						}
						- "`"
					}
					td {
						code {
							- "/session/{"
							var {
								- "session id"
							}
							- "}/window/consume-user-activation"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:remote-end-steps" href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#dfn-remote-end-steps" data-x-internal="remote-end-steps" {
				- "remote end steps"
			}
			- " are:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "window"
					}
					- " be "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#dfn-current-browsing-context" id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:webdriver-current-browsing-context" data-x-internal="webdriver-current-browsing-context" {
						- "current\n   browsing context"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-window" id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:active-window" {
						- "active window"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "consume"
					}
					- " be true if "
					var {
						- "window"
					}
					- " has "
					a href="#transient-activation" id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:transient-activation" {
						- "transient activation"
					}
					- ";\n   otherwise false."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "consume"
					}
					- " is true, then "
					a href="#consume-user-activation" id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:consume-user-activation" {
						- "consume user activation"
					}
					- " of\n   "
					var {
						- "window"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return "
					a href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#dfn-success" id="user-activation-user-agent-automation:success-value" data-x-internal="success-value" {
						- "success"
					}
					- " with data "
					var {
						- "consume"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h3 id="activation" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.5"
			}
			- " Activation behavior of elements"
			a href="#activation" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Certain elements in HTML have an "
			a id="activation:activation-behaviour" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#eventtarget-activation-behavior" data-x-internal="activation-behaviour" {
				- "activation behavior"
			}
			- ", which means that the user\n  can activate them. This is always caused by a "
			code id="activation:event-click" {
				a data-x-internal="event-click" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-click" {
					- "click"
				}
			}
			- " event."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The user agent should allow the user to manually trigger elements that have an "
			a id="activation:activation-behaviour-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#eventtarget-activation-behavior" data-x-internal="activation-behaviour" {
				- "activation\n  behavior"
			}
			- ", for instance using keyboard or voice input, or through mouse clicks. When the\n  user triggers an element with a defined "
			a id="activation:activation-behaviour-3" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#eventtarget-activation-behavior" data-x-internal="activation-behaviour" {
				- "activation behavior"
			}
			- " in a manner other than\n  clicking it, the default action of the interaction event must be to "
			a href="#fire-a-click-event" id="activation:fire-a-click-event" {
				- "fire a "
				code {
					- "click"
				}
				- " event"
			}
			- " at the element."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-click" id="dom-click-dev" {
						- "click"
					}
					- "()"
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
						b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
							- "✔"
						}
						span {
							- "MDN"
						}
					}
					div class="feature" {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLElement/click" title="The HTMLElement.click() method simulates a mouse click on an element." {
								- "HTMLElement/click"
							}
						}
						p class="all-engines-text" {
							- "Support in all current engines."
						}
						div class="support" {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox"
								}
								span {
									- "3+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span {
									- "Safari"
								}
								span {
									- "6+"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span {
									- "Chrome"
								}
								span {
									- "9+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera"
								}
								span {
									- "10.5+"
								}
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge"
								}
								span {
									- "79+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span {
									- "Edge (Legacy)"
								}
								span {
									- "12+"
								}
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span {
									- "Internet Explorer"
								}
								span {
									- "5.5+"
								}
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Firefox Android"
								}
								span {
									- "4+"
								}
							}
							span class="safari_ios unknown" {
								span {
									- "Safari iOS"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span {
									- "Chrome Android"
								}
								span {
									- "?"
								}
							}
							span class="webview_android yes" {
								span {
									- "WebView Android"
								}
								span {
									- "4.4+"
								}
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Samsung Internet"
								}
								span {
									- "1.0+"
								}
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span {
									- "Opera Android"
								}
								span {
									- "11+"
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Acts as if the element was clicked."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each element has an associated "
			dfn id="click-in-progress-flag" {
				- "click in progress flag"
			}
			- ", which is initially unset."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLElement" id="dom-click" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "click()"
				}
			}
			- " method must run\n  the following steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If this element is a form control that is "
					a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="activation:concept-fe-disabled" {
						- "disabled"
					}
					- ", then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If this element's "
					a href="#click-in-progress-flag" id="activation:click-in-progress-flag" {
						- "click in progress flag"
					}
					- " is set, then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set this element's "
					a href="#click-in-progress-flag" id="activation:click-in-progress-flag-2" {
						- "click in progress flag"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#fire-a-synthetic-pointer-event" id="activation:fire-a-synthetic-pointer-event" {
						- "Fire a synthetic pointer event"
					}
					- " named "
					code id="activation:event-click-2" {
						a data-x-internal="event-click" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-click" {
							- "click"
						}
					}
					- "\n   at this element, with the "
					var {
						- "not trusted flag"
					}
					- " set."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Unset this element's "
