		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="focus" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.6"
			}
			- " Focus"
			a href="#focus" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="introduction-8" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.6.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-8" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An HTML user interface typically consists of multiple interactive widgets, such as form\n  controls, scrollable regions, links, dialog boxes, browser tabs, and so forth. These widgets form\n  a hierarchy, with some (e.g. browser tabs, dialog boxes) containing others (e.g. links, form\n  controls)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When interacting with an interface using a keyboard, key input is channeled from the system,\n  through the hierarchy of interactive widgets, to an active widget, which is said to be\n  "
			a href="#focused" id="introduction-8:focused" {
				- "focused"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider an HTML application running in a browser tab running in a graphical environment.\n   Suppose this application had a page with some text controls and links, and was currently showing\n   a modal dialog, which itself had a text control and a button."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The hierarchy of focusable widgets, in this scenario, would include the browser window, which\n   would have, amongst its children, the browser tab containing the HTML application. The tab itself\n   would have as its children the various links and text controls, as well as the dialog. The dialog\n   itself would have as its children the text control and the button."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				img width="800" src="/images/focus-tree.png" height="450" alt=""
				- " \n\n   "
			}
			p {
				- "If the widget with "
				a href="#focused" id="introduction-8:focused-2" {
					- "focus"
				}
				- " in this example was the text control in\n   the dialog box, then key input would be channeled from the graphical system to ① the web\n   browser, then to ② the tab, then to ③ the dialog, and finally to ④ the text\n   control."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Keyboard "
			em {
				- "events"
			}
			- " are always targeted at this "
			a href="#focused" id="introduction-8:focused-3" {
				- "focused"
			}
			- " element."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="data-model" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.6.2"
			}
			- " Data model"
			a href="#data-model" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="tlbc-system-focus" {
			- "A "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="data-model:top-level-traversable" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- " has "
			dfn data-dfn-for="top-level\n  traversable" id="system-focus" data-export="" {
				- "system focus"
			}
			- " when it can receive keyboard input channeled from the operating\n  system, possibly targeted at one of its "
			a href="#nav-document" id="data-model:nav-document" {
				- "active document"
			}
			- "'s\n  "
			a href="#descendant-navigables" id="data-model:descendant-navigables" {
				- "descendant navigables"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="data-model:top-level-traversable-2" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- " has "
			dfn data-dfn-for="top-level traversable" id="user-attention" {
				- "user attention"
			}
			- "\n  when its "
			a href="#system-visibility-state" id="data-model:system-visibility-state" {
				- "system visibility state"
			}
			- " is \""
			code {
				- "visible"
			}
			- "\", and it either\n  has "
			a href="#system-focus" id="data-model:system-focus" {
				- "system focus"
			}
			- " or user agent widgets directly related to it can receive keyboard\n  input channeled from the operating system."
		}
		- "\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "User attention is lost when a browser window loses focus, whereas system focus\n  might also be lost to other system widgets in the browser window such as a location bar."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="data-model:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "d"
			}
			- " is a "
			dfn data-dfn-for="Document" id="fully-active-descendant-of-a-top-level-traversable-with-user-attention" data-export="" {
				- "fully active descendant of\n  a top-level traversable with user attention"
			}
			- " when "
			var {
				- "d"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#fully-active" id="data-model:fully-active" {
				- "fully active"
			}
			- "\n  and "
			var {
				- "d"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#node-navigable" id="data-model:node-navigable" {
				- "node navigable"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#nav-top" id="data-model:nav-top" {
				- "top-level\n  traversable"
			}
			- " has "
			a href="#user-attention" id="data-model:user-attention" {
				- "user attention"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The term "
			dfn id="focusable-area" {
				- "focusable area"
			}
			- " is used to refer to regions of the interface that can further become\n  the target of such keyboard input. Focusable areas can be elements, parts of elements, or other regions\n  managed by the user agent."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area" {
				- "focusable area"
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="dom-anchor" {
				- "DOM anchor"
			}
			- ", which is a "
			code id="data-model:node" {
				a data-x-internal="node" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-node" {
					- "Node"
				}
			}
			- " object\n  that represents the position of the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-2" {
				- "focusable area"
			}
			- " in the DOM. (When the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-3" {
				- "focusable\n  area"
			}
			- " is itself a "
			code id="data-model:node-2" {
				a data-x-internal="node" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-node" {
					- "Node"
				}
			}
			- ", it is its own "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id="data-model:dom-anchor" {
				- "DOM anchor"
			}
			- ".) The "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id="data-model:dom-anchor-2" {
				- "DOM anchor"
			}
			- " is\n  used in some APIs as a substitute for the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-4" {
				- "focusable area"
			}
			- " when there is no other DOM object\n  to represent the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-5" {
				- "focusable area"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following table describes what objects can be "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-6" {
				- "focusable\n  areas"
			}
			- ". The cells in the left column describe objects that can be "
			a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-7" {
				- "focusable areas"
			}
			- "; the cells in the right column describe the "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id="data-model:dom-anchor-3" {
				- "DOM\n  anchors"
			}
			- " for those elements. (The cells that span both columns are non-normative examples.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table id="table-fa" {
			thead {
				tr {
					th id="th-fa-area" {
						a href="#focusable-area" id="data-model:focusable-area-8" {
							- "Focusable area"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					th id="th-fa-dom-rep" {
						a href="#dom-anchor" id="data-model:dom-anchor-4" {
							- "DOM anchor"
						}
						- "\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					th colspan="2" id="th-fa-examples" {
						- "Examples\n\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					th headers="th-fa-area" id="td-fa-1" class="data-header" {
						- "\n     Elements that meet all the following criteria:\n\n     "
						ul class="brief" {
							li {
								- "the element's "
								a href="#tabindex-value" id="data-model:tabindex-value" {
									- "tabindex value"
								}
								- " is non-null, or the element is determined by the\n      user agent to be focusable;"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is either not a "
								a id="data-model:shadow-host" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-shadow-host" data-x-internal="shadow-host" {
									- "shadow host"
								}
								- ", or has a "
								a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-shadow-root" id="data-model:concept-element-shadow-root" data-x-internal="concept-element-shadow-root" {
									- "shadow root"
								}
								- " whose "
								a id="data-model:delegates-focus" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#shadowroot-delegates-focus" data-x-internal="delegates-focus" {
									- "delegates focus"
								}
								- " is\n      false;"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is not "
								a href="#concept-element-disabled" id="data-model:concept-element-disabled" {
									- "actually disabled"
								}
								- ";"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is not "
								a href="#inert" id="data-model:inert" {
									- "inert"
								}
								- ";"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is either "
								a href="#being-rendered" id="data-model:being-rendered" {
									- "being rendered"
								}
								- ", "
								a href="#delegating-its-rendering-to-its-children" id="data-model:delegating-its-rendering-to-its-children" {
									- "delegating its rendering to its\n      children"
								}
								- ", or "
								a href="#being-used-as-relevant-canvas-fallback-content" id="data-model:being-used-as-relevant-canvas-fallback-content" {
									- "being used as relevant canvas fallback content"
								}
								- "."
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td headers="td-fa-1 th-fa-dom-rep" {
						- "\n     The element itself.\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td colspan="2" headers="td-fa-1 th-fa-examples" {
						- "\n     "
						p class="example" {
							code id="data-model:the-iframe-element" {
								a href="#the-iframe-element" {
									- "iframe"
								}
							}
							- ", "
							code id="data-model:the-dialog-element" {
								a href="#the-dialog-element" {
									- "dialog"
								}
							}
							- ", "
							code id="data-model:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" {
								a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" {
									- "<input type=text>"
								}
							}
							- ", sometimes "
							code id="data-model:the-a-element" {
								a href="#the-a-element" {
									- "<a\n     href=\"\">"
								}
							}
							- " (depending on platform conventions).\n\n   "
						}
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					th headers="th-fa-area" id="td-fa-2" class="data-header" {
						- "\n     The shapes of "
						code id="data-model:the-area-element" {
							a href="#the-area-element" {
								- "area"
							}
						}
						- " elements in an "
						a href="#image-map" id="data-model:image-map" {
							- "image map"
						}
						- " associated with an\n     "
						code id="data-model:the-img-element" {
							a href="#the-img-element" {
								- "img"
							}
						}
						- " element that is "
						a href="#being-rendered" id="data-model:being-rendered-2" {
							- "being rendered"
						}
						- " and is not "
						a href="#inert" id="data-model:inert-2" {
							- "inert"
						}
						- ".\n     "
					}
					td headers="td-fa-2 th-fa-dom-rep" {
						- "\n     The "
						code id="data-model:the-img-element-2" {
							a href="#the-img-element" {
								- "img"
							}
						}
						- " element.\n    "
					}
