		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:designMode-2" {
				a href="#designMode" {
					- "designMode"
				}
			}
			- " setter steps are:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " be the given value, "
					a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:converted-to-ascii-lowercase" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" data-x-internal="converted-to-ascii-lowercase" {
						- "converted to ASCII\n   lowercase"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " is \""
					code {
						- "on"
					}
					- "\" and "
					a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-2" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
						- "this"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#design-mode-enabled" id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-2" {
						- "design mode\n    enabled"
					}
					- " is false, then:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Set "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-3" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
								- "this"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="#design-mode-enabled" id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-3" {
								- "design mode enabled"
							}
							- " to true."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Reset "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-4" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
								- "this"
							}
							- "'s "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:active-range" href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#active-range" data-x-internal="active-range" {
								- "active range"
							}
							- "'s start and end boundary points to\n     be at the start of "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-5" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
								- "this"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Run the "
							a href="#focusing-steps" id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:focusing-steps" {
								- "focusing steps"
							}
							- " for "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-6" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
								- "this"
							}
							- "'s "
							a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:document-element" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" data-x-internal="document-element" {
								- "document\n     element"
							}
							- ", if non-null."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " is \""
					code {
						- "off"
					}
					- "\", then set "
					a id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-7" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
						- "this"
					}
					- "'s\n   "
					a href="#design-mode-enabled" id="making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-4" {
						- "design mode enabled"
					}
					- " to false."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h4 id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.8.3"
			}
			- " Best practices for in-page editors"
			a href="#best-practices-for-in-page-editors" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Authors are encouraged to set the "
			a id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" data-x-internal="'white-space'" {
				- "'white-space'"
			}
			- " property on "
			a href="#editing-host" id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:editing-host" {
				- "editing hosts"
			}
			- " and on markup that was originally created through these editing\n  mechanisms to the value 'pre-wrap'. Default HTML whitespace handling is not well suited to WYSIWYG\n  editing, and line wrapping will not work correctly in some corner cases if\n  "
			a id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" data-x-internal="'white-space'" {
				- "'white-space'"
			}
			- " is left at its default value."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "As an example of problems that occur if the default 'normal' value is used instead, consider\n   the case of the user typing \""
				kbd {
					- "yellow␣␣ball"
				}
				- "\", with two spaces (here\n   represented by \"␣\") between the words. With the editing rules in place for the default\n   value of "
				a id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" data-x-internal="'white-space'" {
					- "'white-space'"
				}
				- " ('normal'), the resulting markup will either consist of\n   \""
				samp {
					- "yellow&nbsp; ball"
				}
				- "\" or \""
				samp {
					- "yellow &nbsp;ball"
				}
				- "\"; i.e.,\n   there will be a non-breaking space between the two words in addition to the regular space. This\n   is necessary because the 'normal' value for "
				a id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-4" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" data-x-internal="'white-space'" {
					- "'white-space'"
				}
				- " requires adjacent regular\n   spaces to be collapsed together."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In the former case, \""
				samp {
					- "yellow⍽"
				}
				- "\" might wrap to the next line (\"⍽\"\n   being used here to represent a non-breaking space) even though \""
				samp {
					- "yellow"
				}
				- "\" alone might\n   fit at the end of the line; in the latter case, \""
				samp {
					- "⍽ball"
				}
				- "\", if wrapped to the\n   start of the line, would have visible indentation from the non-breaking space."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When "
				a id="best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-5" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" data-x-internal="'white-space'" {
					- "'white-space'"
				}
				- " is set to 'pre-wrap', however, the editing rules will instead\n   simply put two regular spaces between the words, and should the two words be split at the end of\n   a line, the spaces would be neatly removed from the rendering."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="editing-apis" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.8.4"
			}
			- " Editing APIs"
			a href="#editing-apis" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id="editing-host" data-export="" {
				- "editing host"
			}
			- " is either an "
			a href="#html-elements" id="editing-apis:html-elements" {
				- "HTML element"
			}
			- "\n  with its "
			code id="editing-apis:attr-contenteditable" {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable" {
					- "contenteditable"
				}
			}
			- " attribute in the "
			i {
				- "true"
			}
			- "\n  state or "
			i {
				- "plaintext-only"
			}
			- " state, or a "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-child" id="editing-apis:concept-tree-child" data-x-internal="concept-tree-child" {
				- "child"
			}
			- " "
			a href="#html-elements" id="editing-apis:html-elements-2" {
				- "HTML element"
			}
			- " of a "
			code id="editing-apis:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#design-mode-enabled" id="editing-apis:design-mode-enabled" {
				- "design mode\n  enabled"
			}
			- " is true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The definition of the terms "
			dfn id="active-range" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#active-range" {
					- "active range"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id="editing-host-of" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editing-host-of" {
					- "editing host\n  of"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			dfn id="editable" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" {
					- "editable"
				}
			}
			- ", the user\n  interface requirements of elements that are "
			a href="#editing-host" id="editing-apis:editing-host" {
				- "editing hosts"
			}
			- " or\n  "
			a id="editing-apis:editable" href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" data-x-internal="editable" {
				- "editable"
			}
			- ", the\n\n  "
			dfn id="execCommand" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#execcommand%28%29" {
					code {
						- "execCommand()"
					}
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			dfn id="dom-document-querycommandenabled" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandenabled%28%29" {
					code {
						- "queryCommandEnabled()"
					}
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			dfn id="dom-document-querycommandindeterm" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandindeterm%28%29" {
					code {
						- "queryCommandIndeterm()"
					}
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			dfn id="dom-document-querycommandstate" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandstate%28%29" {
					code {
						- "queryCommandState()"
					}
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			dfn id="dom-document-querycommandsupported" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandsupported%28%29" {
					code {
						- "queryCommandSupported()"
					}
				}
			}
			- ", and\n  "
			dfn id="dom-document-querycommandvalue" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandvalue%28%29" {
					code {
						- "queryCommandValue()"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n  methods, text selections, and the "
			dfn id="delete-the-selection" {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#delete-the-selection" {
					- "delete the\n  selection"
				}
			}
			- " algorithm are defined in "
			cite {
				- "execCommand"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsEXECCOMMAND" {
				- "[EXECCOMMAND]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="spelling-and-grammar-checking" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.8.5"
			}
			- " Spelling and grammar checking"
			a href="#spelling-and-grammar-checking" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents can support the checking of spelling and grammar of editable text, either in form\n  controls (such as the value of "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-textarea-element" {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" {
					- "textarea"
				}
			}
			- " elements), or in elements in an "
			a href="#editing-host" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:editing-host" {
				- "editing\n  host"
			}
			- " (e.g. using "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-contenteditable" {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable" {
					- "contenteditable"
				}
			}
			- ")."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For each element, user agents must establish a "
			dfn id="concept-spellcheck-default" {
				- "default\n  behavior"
			}
			- ", either through defaults or through preferences expressed by the user. There are\n  three possible default behaviors for each element:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-spellcheck-default-true" {
					- "true-by-default"
				}
				- "\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "The element will be checked for spelling and grammar if its contents are editable and\n   spellchecking is not explicitly disabled through the "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck" {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
				}
				- " attribute.\n\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-spellcheck-default-false" {
					- "false-by-default"
				}
				- "\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "The element will never be checked for spelling and grammar unless spellchecking is\n   explicitly enabled through the "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-2" {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
				}
				- " attribute.\n\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="concept-spellcheck-default-inherit" {
					- "inherit-by-default"
				}
				- "\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "The element's default behavior is the same as its parent element's. Elements that have no\n   parent element cannot have this as their default behavior.\n  "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/spellcheck" title="The spellcheck global attribute is an enumerated attribute that defines whether the element may be checked for spelling errors." {
						- "Global_attributes/spellcheck"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "11"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "57+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "9.3+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "47+"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "37+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="html-global" id="attr-spellcheck" data-dfn-type="element-attr" {
				code {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute is an "
			a href="#enumerated-attribute" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:enumerated-attribute" {
				- "enumerated attribute"
			}
			- " with the following keywords and states:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		table {
			thead {
				tr {
					th {
						- "Keyword\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "State\n     "
					}
					th {
						- "Brief description\n   "
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="html-global/spellcheck" id="attr-spellcheck-true" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "true"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td rowspan="2" {
						dfn id="attr-spellcheck-true-state" {
							- "true"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td rowspan="2" {
						- "Spelling and grammar will be checked.\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						- "(the empty string)\n    "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="html-global/spellcheck" id="attr-spellcheck-false" data-dfn-type="attr-value" {
							code {
								- "false"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						dfn id="attr-spellcheck-false-state" {
							- "false"
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					td {
						- "Spelling and grammar will not be checked.\n  "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The attribute's "
			i id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:missing-value-default" {
				a href="#missing-value-default" {
					- "missing value default"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			i id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:invalid-value-default" {
				a href="#invalid-value-default" {
					- "invalid value default"
				}
			}
			- " are both the "
			dfn id="attr-spellcheck-default-state" {
				- "default"
			}
			- " state. The default state indicates that the\n  element is to act according to a default behavior, possibly based on the parent element's own\n  "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-3" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " state, as defined below."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
					a href="#dom-spellcheck" id="dom-spellcheck-dev" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
					- " [ = "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " ]"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns true if the element is to have its spelling and grammar checked; otherwise, returns\n    false."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Can be set, to override the default and set the "
					code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-4" {
						a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
							- "spellcheck"
						}
					}
					- " content attribute."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="HTMLElement" id="dom-spellcheck" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " IDL\n  attribute, on getting, must return true if the element's "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-5" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " content attribute is in the "
			a href="#attr-spellcheck-true-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-true-state" {
				- "true"
			}
			- " state, or if the element's "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-6" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " content attribute is in the "
			a href="#attr-spellcheck-default-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-default-state" {
				- "default"
			}
			- " state and the element's "
			a href="#concept-spellcheck-default" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default" {
				- "default behavior"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#concept-spellcheck-default-true" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-true" {
				- "true-by-default"
			}
			- ", or if the element's "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-7" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " content attribute is in the "
			a href="#attr-spellcheck-default-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-default-state-2" {
				- "default"
			}
			- " state and the element's "
			a href="#concept-spellcheck-default" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-2" {
				- "default behavior"
			}
			- " is "
			a href="#concept-spellcheck-default-inherit" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-inherit" {
				- "inherit-by-default"
			}
			- " and the element's parent\n  element's "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:dom-spellcheck" {
				a href="#dom-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute would return true;\n  otherwise, if none of those conditions applies, then the attribute must instead return false."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:dom-spellcheck-2" {
				a href="#dom-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " IDL attribute is not affected\n  by user preferences that override the "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-8" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " content\n  attribute, and therefore might not reflect the actual spellchecking state."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "On setting, if the new value is true, then the element's "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-9" {
				a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
					- "spellcheck"
				}
			}
			- " content attribute must be set to\n  \""
			code {
				- "true"
			}
			- "\", otherwise it must be set to \""
			code {
				- "false"
			}
			- "\".\n\n  "
		}
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents should only consider the following pieces of text as checkable for the purposes of\n  this feature:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "The "
				a href="#concept-fe-value" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-fe-value" {
					- "value"
				}
				- " of "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-input-element" {
					a href="#the-input-element" {
						- "input"
					}
				}
				- " elements whose "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-input-type" {
					a href="#attr-input-type" {
						- "type"
					}
				}
				- " attributes are in the "
				a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" {
					- "Text"
				}
				- ", "
				a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)-2" {
					- "Search"
				}
				- ",\n   "
				a href="#url-state-(type=url)" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:url-state-(type=url)" {
					- "URL"
				}
				- ", or "
				a href="#email-state-(type=email)" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:email-state-(type=email)" {
					- "Email"
				}
				- " states and that are "
				i id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-fe-mutable" {
					a href="#concept-fe-mutable" {
						- "mutable"
					}
				}
				- " (i.e. that do not have the "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-input-readonly" {
					a href="#attr-input-readonly" {
						- "readonly"
					}
				}
				- " attribute specified and that are not "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-fe-disabled" {
					- "disabled"
				}
				- ")."
			}
			li {
				- "The "
				a href="#concept-fe-value" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-fe-value-2" {
					- "value"
				}
				- " of "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-textarea-element-2" {
					a href="#the-textarea-element" {
						- "textarea"
					}
				}
				- " elements that do not\n   have a "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-textarea-readonly" {
					a href="#attr-textarea-readonly" {
						- "readonly"
					}
				}
				- " attribute and that are not "
				a href="#concept-fe-disabled" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-fe-disabled-2" {
					- "disabled"
				}
				- "."
			}
			li {
				- "Text in "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:text" {
					a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
						- "Text"
					}
				}
				- " nodes that are children of "
				a href="#editing-host" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:editing-host-2" {
					- "editing\n   hosts"
				}
				- " or "
				a id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:editable" href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" data-x-internal="editable" {
					- "editable"
				}
				- " elements."
			}
			li {
				- "Text in attributes of "
				a id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:editable-2" href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" data-x-internal="editable" {
					- "editable"
				}
				- " elements."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For text that is part of a "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:text-2" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- " node, the element with which the text is\n  associated is the element that is the immediate parent of the first character of the word,\n  sentence, or other piece of text. For text in attributes, it is the attribute's element. For the\n  values of "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-textarea-element-3" {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" {
					- "textarea"
				}
			}
			- " elements, it is the element itself."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To determine if a word, sentence, or other piece of text in an applicable element (as defined\n  above) is to have spelling- and grammar-checking enabled, the UA must use the following\n  algorithm:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "If the user has disabled the checking for this text, then the checking is disabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if the user has forced the checking for this text to always be enabled, then the\n   checking is enabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if the element with which the text is associated has a "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-10" {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
				}
				- " content attribute, then: if that attribute is in the\n   "
				a href="#attr-spellcheck-true-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-true-state-2" {
					- "true"
				}
				- " state, then checking is enabled; otherwise, if that attribute is in the "
				a href="#attr-spellcheck-false-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-false-state" {
					- "false"
				}
				- "\n   state, then checking is disabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if there is an ancestor element with a "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-11" {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
				}
				- " content attribute that is not in the "
				a href="#attr-spellcheck-default-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-default-state-3" {
					- "default"
				}
				- "\n   state, then: if the nearest such ancestor's "
				code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-12" {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" {
						- "spellcheck"
					}
				}
				- "\n   content attribute is in the "
				a href="#attr-spellcheck-true-state" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck-true-state-3" {
					- "true"
				}
				- " state, then\n   checking is enabled; otherwise, checking is disabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if the element's "
				a href="#concept-spellcheck-default" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-3" {
					- "default behavior"
				}
				- "\n   is "
				a href="#concept-spellcheck-default-true" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-true-2" {
					- "true-by-default"
				}
				- ", then checking is\n   enabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if the element's "
				a href="#concept-spellcheck-default" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-4" {
					- "default behavior"
				}
				- "\n   is "
				a href="#concept-spellcheck-default-false" id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:concept-spellcheck-default-false" {
					- "false-by-default"
				}
				- ", then checking is\n   disabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, if the element's parent element has "
				em {
					- "its"
				}
				- " checking enabled, then checking\n   is enabled."
			}
			li {
				- "Otherwise, checking is disabled."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the checking is enabled for a word/sentence/text, the user agent should indicate spelling\n  and grammar errors in that text. User agents should take into account the other semantics given in\n  the document when suggesting spelling and grammar corrections. User agents may use the language of\n  the element to determine what spelling and grammar rules to use, or may use the user's preferred\n  language settings. UAs should use "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-input-element-3" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element attributes such as "
			code id="spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-input-pattern" {
				a href="#attr-input-pattern" {
					- "pattern"
				}
			}
			- " to ensure that the resulting value is valid, where\n  possible."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If checking is disabled, the user agent should not indicate spelling or grammar errors for that\n  text."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The element with ID \"a\" in the following example would be the one used to determine if the\n   word \"Hello\" is checked for spelling errors. In this example, it would not be."
