		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This section defines an event-based drag-and-drop mechanism."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification does not define exactly what a "
			em {
				- "drag-and-drop operation"
			}
			- " actually\n  is."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "On a visual medium with a pointing device, a drag operation could be the default action of a\n  "
			code id="dnd:event-mousedown" {
				a data-x-internal="event-mousedown" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-mousedown" {
					- "mousedown"
				}
			}
			- " event that is followed by a series of "
			code id="dnd:event-mousemove" {
				a data-x-internal="event-mousemove" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-mousemove" {
					- "mousemove"
				}
			}
			- " events, and the drop could be triggered by the mouse\n  being released."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When using an input modality other than a pointing device, users would probably have to\n  explicitly indicate their intention to perform a drag-and-drop operation, stating what they wish\n  to drag and where they wish to drop it, respectively."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "However it is implemented, drag-and-drop operations must have a starting point (e.g. where the\n  mouse was clicked, or the start of the selection or element that was selected for the drag), may\n  have any number of intermediate steps (elements that the mouse moves over during a drag, or\n  elements that the user picks as possible drop points as they cycle through possibilities), and must\n  either have an end point (the element above which the mouse button was released, or the element\n  that was finally selected), or be canceled. The end point must be the last element selected as a\n  possible drop point before the drop occurs (so if the operation is not canceled, there must be at\n  least one element in the middle step)."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h4 id="event-drag" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "6.11.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#event-drag" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To make an element draggable, give the element a "
			code id="event-drag:attr-draggable" {
				a href="#attr-draggable" {
					- "draggable"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute, and set an event listener for "
			code id="event-drag:event-dnd-dragstart" {
				a href="#event-dnd-dragstart" {
					- "dragstart"
				}
			}
			- " that\n  stores the data being dragged."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The event handler typically needs to check that it's not a text selection that is being\n  dragged, and then needs to store data into the "
			code id="event-drag:datatransfer" {
				a href="#datatransfer" {
					- "DataTransfer"
				}
			}
			- " object and set the\n  allowed effects (copy, move, link, or some combination)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For example:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
