		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To accept a drop, the drop target has to listen to the following events:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "The "
				code id="event-drag:event-dnd-dragenter" {
					a href="#event-dnd-dragenter" {
						- "dragenter"
					}
				}
				- " event handler reports\n    whether or not the drop target is potentially willing to accept the drop, by canceling the\n    event."
			}
			li {
				- "The "
				code id="event-drag:event-dnd-dragover" {
					a href="#event-dnd-dragover" {
						- "dragover"
					}
				}
				- " event handler specifies what feedback\n    will be shown to the user, by setting the "
				code id="event-drag:dom-datatransfer-dropeffect" {
					a href="#dom-datatransfer-dropeffect" {
						- "dropEffect"
					}
				}
				- " attribute of the\n    "
				code id="event-drag:datatransfer-2" {
					a href="#datatransfer" {
						- "DataTransfer"
					}
				}
				- " associated with the event. This event also needs to be canceled."
			}
			li {
				- "The "
				code id="event-drag:event-dnd-drop" {
					a href="#event-dnd-drop" {
						- "drop"
					}
				}
				- " event handler has a final chance to accept or\n    reject the drop. If the drop is accepted, the event handler must perform the drop operation on\n    the target. This event needs to be canceled, so that the "
				code id="event-drag:dom-datatransfer-dropeffect-2" {
					a href="#dom-datatransfer-dropeffect" {
						- "dropEffect"
					}
				}
				- " attribute's value can be used by the\n    source. Otherwise, the drop operation is rejected."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For example:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
