				- "HTML element"
			}
			- " or null."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "The "
				a href="#topmost-popover-ancestor" id="the-popover-attribute:topmost-popover-ancestor-5" {
					- "topmost popover ancestor"
				}
				- " algorithm will return the topmost (latest in the\n   "
				a href="#auto-popover-list" id="the-popover-attribute:auto-popover-list-9" {
					- "showing auto popover list"
				}
				- ") ancestor popover for the provided popover or top layer\n   element. Popovers can be related to each other in several ways, creating a tree of popovers.\n   There are two paths through which one popover (call it the \"child\" popover) can have a topmost\n   ancestor popover (call it the \"parent\" popover):"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			ol {
				li {
					p {
						- "The popovers are nested within each other in the node tree. In this case, the descendant\n    popover is the \"child\" and its topmost ancestor popover is the \"parent\"."
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "An invoking element (e.g., a "
						code id="the-popover-attribute:the-button-element" {
							a href="#the-button-element" {
								- "button"
							}
						}
						- ") has a "
						code id="the-popover-attribute:attr-popovertarget" {
							a href="#attr-popovertarget" {
								- "popovertarget"
							}
						}
						- " attribute pointing to a popover. In this case,\n    the popover is the \"child\", and the popover subtree the invoking element is in is the\n    \"parent\". The invoker has to be in a popover and reference an open popover."
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In each of the relationships formed above, the parent popover has to be strictly earlier in\n   the "
				a href="#auto-popover-list" id="the-popover-attribute:auto-popover-list-10" {
					- "showing auto popover list"
				}
				- " than the child popover, or it does not form a valid\n   ancestral relationship. This eliminates non-showing popovers and self-pointers (e.g., a popover\n   containing an invoking element that points back to the containing popover), and it allows for the\n   construction of a well-formed tree from the (possibly cyclic) graph of connections. Only "
				a href="#attr-popover-auto-state" id="the-popover-attribute:attr-popover-auto-state-7" {
					- "auto"
				}
				- " popovers are considered."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the provided element is a top layer element such as a "
				code id="the-popover-attribute:the-dialog-element" {
					a href="#the-dialog-element" {
						- "dialog"
					}
				}
				- " which is not\n   showing as a popover, then "
				a href="#topmost-popover-ancestor" id="the-popover-attribute:topmost-popover-ancestor-6" {
					- "topmost popover ancestor"
				}
				- " will only look in the node tree\n   to find the first popover."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
