		- "\n\n\n  "
		h2 id="browsers" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7"
			}
			- " Loading web pages"
			a href="#browsers" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "This section describes features that apply most directly to web browsers. Having said that,\n  except where specified otherwise, the requirements defined in this section "
			em {
				- "do"
			}
			- " apply to\n  all user agents, whether they are web browsers or not."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h3 id="loading-web-pages-supporting-concepts" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.1"
			}
			- " Supporting concepts"
			a href="#loading-web-pages-supporting-concepts" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="origin" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.1.1"
			}
			- " Origins"
			a href="#origin" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Origins are the fundamental currency of the web's security model. Two actors in the web\n  platform that share an origin are assumed to trust each other and to have the same authority.\n  Actors with differing origins are considered potentially hostile versus each other, and are\n  isolated from each other to varying degrees."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, if Example Bank's web site, hosted at "
			code {
				- "bank.example.com"
			}
			- ", tries to examine the DOM of Example Charity's web site, hosted\n  at "
			code {
				- "charity.example.org"
			}
			- ", a "
			a id="origin:securityerror" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#securityerror" data-x-internal="securityerror" {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "SecurityError"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			- "\n  "
			code id="origin:domexception" {
				a data-x-internal="domexception" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" {
					- "DOMException"
				}
			}
			- " will be raised."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="origin-2" {
			- "An "
			dfn id="concept-origin" data-export="" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " is one of the following:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "An "
				dfn id="concept-origin-opaque" data-export="" {
					- "opaque origin"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "An internal value, with no serialization it can be recreated from (it is serialized as\n   \""
					code {
						- "null"
					}
					- "\" per "
					a href="#ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin" id="origin:ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin" {
						- "serialization of an origin"
					}
					- "), for which the only\n   meaningful operation is testing for equality."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn id="concept-origin-tuple" data-export="" {
					- "tuple origin"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "A "
					a href="#concept-origin-tuple" id="origin:concept-origin-tuple" {
						- "tuple"
					}
					- " consists of:\n\n    "
				}
				ul class="brief" {
					li {
						- "A "
						dfn data-dfn-for="origin" id="concept-origin-scheme" data-export="" {
							- "scheme"
						}
						- " (an "
						a id="origin:ascii-string" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-string" data-x-internal="ascii-string" {
							- "ASCII\n     string"
						}
						- ")."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						dfn data-dfn-for="origin" id="concept-origin-host" data-export="" {
							- "host"
						}
						- " (a "
						a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-host" id="origin:concept-host" data-x-internal="concept-host" {
							- "host"
						}
						- ")."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						dfn data-dfn-for="origin" id="concept-origin-port" data-export="" {
							- "port"
						}
						- " (null or a 16-bit\n     unsigned integer)."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						dfn data-dfn-for="origin" id="concept-origin-domain" data-export="" {
							- "domain"
						}
						- " (null or a "
						a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-domain" id="origin:concept-domain" data-x-internal="concept-domain" {
							- "domain"
						}
						- "). Null unless stated otherwise."
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			a href="#concept-origin" id="origin:concept-origin" {
				- "Origins"
			}
			- " can be shared, e.g., among multiple\n  "
			code id="origin:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " objects. Furthermore, "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="origin:concept-origin-2" {
				- "origins"
			}
			- " are generally\n  immutable. Only the "
			a href="#concept-origin-domain" id="origin:concept-origin-domain" {
				- "domain"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#concept-origin-tuple" id="origin:concept-origin-tuple-2" {
				- "tuple origin"
			}
			- " can be changed, and only through the "
			code id="origin:dom-document-domain" {
				a href="#dom-document-domain" {
					- "document.domain"
				}
			}
			- " API."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="concept-origin-effective-domain" data-export="" {
				- "effective domain"
			}
			- " of an\n  "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="origin:concept-origin-3" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " is computed as follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "origin"
					}
					- " is an "
					a href="#concept-origin-opaque" id="origin:concept-origin-opaque" {
						- "opaque origin"
					}
