		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h4 id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.1.2"
			}
			- " "
			span id="origin-isolation"
			- "Origin-keyed agent clusters"
			a href="#origin-keyed-agent-clusters" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="domintro" {
			dt {
				code {
					- "window."
					a href="#dom-originagentcluster" id="dom-originagentcluster-dev" {
						- "originAgentCluster"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Returns true if this "
					code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:window" {
						a href="#window" {
							- "Window"
						}
					}
					- " belongs to an "
					a id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
						- "agent cluster"
					}
					- " which is\n    "
					a href="#concept-origin" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin" {
						- "origin"
					}
					- "-"
					a href="#agent-cluster-key" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key" {
						- "keyed"
					}
					- ", in the manner described in\n    this section."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " delivered over a "
			a href="#secure-context" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:secure-context" {
				- "secure context"
			}
			- " can request that it be\n  placed in an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin-2" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- "-"
			a href="#agent-cluster-key" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key-2" {
				- "keyed"
			}
			- " "
			a id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
				- "agent\n  cluster"
			}
			- ", by using the `"
			dfn id="origin-agent-cluster" data-dfn-type="http-header" {
				code {
					- "Origin-Agent-Cluster"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP\n  response header. This header is a "
			a href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header" data-x-internal="http-structured-header" {
				- "structured header"
			}
			- "\n  whose value must be a "
			a href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html#boolean" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header-boolean" data-x-internal="http-structured-header-boolean" {
				- "boolean"
			}
			- ".\n  "
			a href="#refsSTRUCTURED-FIELDS" {
				- "[STRUCTURED-FIELDS]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Per the processing model in the "
			a href="#initialise-the-document-object" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:initialise-the-document-object" {
				- "create\n  and initialize a new "
				code {
					- "Document"
				}
				- " object"
			}
			- ", values\n  that are not the "
			a href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html#boolean" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header-boolean-2" data-x-internal="http-structured-header-boolean" {
				- "structured header boolean"
			}
			- "\n  true value (i.e., `"
			code {
				- "?1"
			}
			- "`) will be ignored."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The consequences of using this header are that the resulting\n  "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#agent-cluster-key" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key-3" {
				- "agent cluster key"
			}
			- " is its "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-document-origin" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- ", instead of the "
			a href="#obtain-a-site" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:obtain-a-site" {
				- "corresponding site"
			}
			- ". In terms of observable effects, this means that\n  attempting to "
			a href="#relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction" {
				- "relax the same-origin\n  restriction"
			}
			- " using "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-document-domain" {
				a href="#dom-document-domain" {
					- "document.domain"
				}
			}
			- " will instead do\n  nothing, and it will not be possible to send "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:webassembly.module" {
				a data-x-internal="webassembly.module" href="https://webassembly.github.io/spec/js-api/#module" {
					- "WebAssembly.Module"
				}
			}
			- " objects to\n  cross-origin "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-3" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "s (even if they are "
			a href="#same-site" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:same-site" {
				- "same site"
			}
			- "). Behind the scenes,\n  this isolation can allow user agents to allocate implementation-specific resources corresponding\n  to "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-3" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
				- "agent clusters"
			}
			- ", such as processes or threads, more\n  efficiently."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Note that within a "
			a href="#browsing-context-group" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:browsing-context-group" {
				- "browsing context group"
			}
			- ", the\n  `"
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:origin-agent-cluster" {
				a href="#origin-agent-cluster" {
					- "Origin-Agent-Cluster"
				}
			}
			- "` header can never cause same-origin "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-4" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "\n  objects to end up in different "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-4" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
				- "agent clusters"
			}
			- ", even if one\n  sends the header and the other doesn't. This is prevented by means of the\n  "
			a href="#historical-agent-cluster-key-map" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:historical-agent-cluster-key-map" {
				- "historical agent cluster key map"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This means that the "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-originagentcluster" {
				a href="#dom-originagentcluster" {
					- "originAgentCluster"
				}
			}
			- " getter can return false, even if the\n  header is set, if the header was omitted on a previously-loaded same-origin page in the same\n  "
			a href="#browsing-context-group" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:browsing-context-group-2" {
				- "browsing context group"
			}
			- ". Similarly, it can return true even when the header is not\n  set."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="Window" id="dom-originagentcluster" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "originAgentCluster"
				}
			}
			- " getter steps are to return the\n  "
			a id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:surrounding-agent" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#surrounding-agent" data-x-internal="surrounding-agent" {
				- "surrounding agent"
			}
			- "'s "
			a id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-5" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
				- "agent cluster"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#is-origin-keyed" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:is-origin-keyed" {
				- "is origin-keyed"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-5" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "s with an "
			a href="#concept-origin-opaque" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin-opaque" {
				- "opaque\n  origin"
			}
			- " can be considered unconditionally origin-keyed; for them the header has no effect,\n  and the "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-originagentcluster-2" {
				a href="#dom-originagentcluster" {
					- "originAgentCluster"
				}
			}
			- " getter will always return\n  true."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Similarly, "
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-6" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "s whose "
			a id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-6" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
				- "agent cluster"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#agent-cluster-cross-origin-isolation" id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-cross-origin-isolation" {
				- "cross-origin isolation mode"
			}
			- " is not \""
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-isolation-none" {
				a href="#cross-origin-isolation-none" {
					- "none"
				}
			}
			- "\" are automatically origin-keyed. The\n  `"
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:origin-agent-cluster-2" {
				a href="#origin-agent-cluster" {
					- "Origin-Agent-Cluster"
				}
			}
			- "` header might be useful as an additional hint to\n  implementations about resource allocation, since the `"
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-opener-policy-2" {
				a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" {
					- "Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy"
				}
			}
			- "`\n  and `"
			code id="origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-embedder-policy" {
				a href="#cross-origin-embedder-policy" {
					- "Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy"
				}
			}
			- "` headers used to achieve cross-origin isolation\n  are more about ensuring that everything in the same address space opts in to being there. But\n  adding it would have no additional observable effects on author code."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="cross-origin-opener-policies" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.1.3"
			}
			- " Cross-origin opener policies"
			a href="#cross-origin-opener-policies" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id="cross-origin-opener-policy-value" {
				- "opener policy value"
			}
			- " allows a document which\n  is navigated to in a "
			a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context" {
				- "top-level browsing context"
			}
			- " to force the creation of a new\n  "
			a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-2" {
				- "top-level browsing context"
			}
			- ", and a corresponding "
			a href="#tlbc-group" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:tlbc-group" {
				- "group"
			}
			- ". The possible values are:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id="coop-unsafe-none" {
					code {
						- "unsafe-none"
					}
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This is the (current) default and means that the document will occupy the same\n   "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-3" {
						- "top-level browsing context"
					}
					- " as its predecessor, unless that document specified a\n   different "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy" {
						- "opener policy"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id="coop-same-origin-allow-popups" {
					code {
						- "same-origin-allow-popups"
					}
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This forces the creation of a new "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-4" {
						- "top-level browsing context"
					}
					- " for the\n   document, unless its predecessor specified the same "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2" {
						- "opener policy"
					}
					- " and they are\n   "
					a href="#same-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:same-origin" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id="coop-same-origin" {
					code {
						- "same-origin"
					}
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This behaves the same as \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-allow-popups" {
						a href="#coop-same-origin-allow-popups" {
							- "same-origin-allow-popups"
						}
					}
					- "\", with the addition that\n   any "
					a href="#auxiliary-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:auxiliary-browsing-context" {
						- "auxiliary browsing context"
					}
					- " created needs to contain "
					a href="#same-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:same-origin-2" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- "\n   documents that also have the same "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-3" {
						- "opener policy"
					}
					- " or it will appear closed to the\n   opener."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id="coop-same-origin-plus-coep" {
					code {
						- "same-origin-plus-COEP"
					}
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "This behaves the same as \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin" {
						a href="#coop-same-origin" {
							- "same-origin"
						}
					}
					- "\", with the\n    addition that it sets the (new) "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-5" {
						- "top-level browsing context"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#tlbc-group" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:tlbc-group-2" {
						- "group"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#bcg-cross-origin-isolation" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:bcg-cross-origin-isolation" {
						- "cross-origin isolation\n    mode"
					}
					- " to one of \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-isolation-logical" {
						a href="#cross-origin-isolation-logical" {
							- "logical"
						}
					}
					- "\" or \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-isolation-concrete" {
						a href="#cross-origin-isolation-concrete" {
							- "concrete"
						}
					}
					- "\"."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "\""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-plus-coep" {
						a href="#coop-same-origin-plus-coep" {
							- "same-origin-plus-COEP"
						}
					}
					- "\" cannot\n    be directly set via the `"
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2-2" {
						a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" {
							- "Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy"
						}
					}
					- "` header, but results from a\n    combination of setting both `"
					code {
						a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2-3" {
							- "Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy"
						}
						- ": "
						a href="#coop-same-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-2" {
							- "same-origin"
						}
					}
					- "` and a\n    `"
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-embedder-policy" {
						a href="#cross-origin-embedder-policy" {
							- "Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy"
						}
					}
					- "` header whose value is "
					a href="#compatible-with-cross-origin-isolation" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:compatible-with-cross-origin-isolation" {
						- "compatible with\n    cross-origin isolation"
					}
					- " together."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id="coop-noopener-allow-popups" {
					code {
						- "noopener-allow-popups"
					}
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "This forces the creation of a new "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-6" {
						- "top-level browsing context"
					}
					- " for the document,\n    regardless of its predecessor."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				div class="note" {
					- "\n     "
					p {
						- "While including a "
						code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-noopener-allow-popups" {
							a href="#coop-noopener-allow-popups" {
								- "noopener-allow-popups"
							}
						}
						- " value severs the opener\n     relationship between the document on which it is applied and its opener, it does not create a\n     robust security boundary between those same-origin documents."
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Other risks from same-origin applications include:"
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					ul {
						li {
							p {
								- "Same-origin requests fetching the document's content — could be mitigated through\n      Fetch Metadata filtering. "
								a href="#refsFETCHMETADATA" {
									- "[FETCHMETADATA]"
								}
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Same-origin framing - could be mitigated through "
								code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:x-frame-options" {
									a href="#x-frame-options" {
										- "X-Frame-Options"
									}
								}
								- " or CSP\n      "
								code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:frame-ancestors-directive" {
									a data-x-internal="frame-ancestors-directive" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#frame-ancestors" {
										- "frame-ancestors"
									}
								}
								- "."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "JavaScript accessible cookies - can be mitigated by ensuring all cookies are "
								code {
									- "httponly"
								}
								- "."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:dom-localstorage" {
									a href="#dom-localstorage" {
										- "localStorage"
									}
								}
								- " access to sensitive data."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Service worker installation."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								a href="https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#cache" {
									- "Cache API"
								}
								- " manipulation or\n      access to sensitive data. "
								a href="#refsSW" {
									- "[SW]"
								}
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								code {
									- "postMessage"
								}
								- " or "
								code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:broadcastchannel" {
									a href="#broadcastchannel" {
										- "BroadcastChannel"
									}
								}
								- " messaging that\n      exposes sensitive information."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Autofill which may not require user interaction for same-origin documents."
							}
						}
					}
					- "\n\n     "
					p {
						- "Developers using "
						code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-noopener-allow-popups-2" {
							a href="#coop-noopener-allow-popups" {
								- "noopener-allow-popups"
							}
						}
						- "\n     need to make sure that their sensitive applications don't rely on client-side features\n     accessible to other same-origin documents, e.g., "
						code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:dom-localstorage-2" {
							a href="#dom-localstorage" {
								- "localStorage"
							}
						}
						- " and other client-side storage APIs,\n     "
						code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:broadcastchannel-2" {
							a href="#broadcastchannel" {
								- "BroadcastChannel"
							}
						}
						- " and related same-origin communication mechanisms. They also need\n     to make sure that their server-side endpoints don't return sensitive data to non-navigation\n     requests, whose response content is accessible to same-origin\n     documents."
					}
					- "\n    "
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id="cross-origin-opener-policy" {
				- "opener policy"
			}
			- " consists of:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="coop-struct-value" {
						- "value"
					}
					- ", which is an "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-value" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-value" {
						- "opener policy value"
					}
					- ", initially \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="coop-struct-report-endpoint" {
						- "reporting endpoint"
					}
					- ", which is string or\n   null, initially null."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="coop-struct-report-only-value" {
						- "report-only value"
					}
					- ", which is an "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-value" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-value-2" {
						- "opener policy value"
					}
					- ", initially \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none-2" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id="coop-struct-report-only-endpoint" {
						- "report-only reporting endpoint"
					}
					- ",\n   which is a string or null, initially null."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="matching-coop" {
				- "match opener policy values"
			}
			- ", given an "
			a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-value" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-value-3" {
				- "opener policy\n  value"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "documentCOOP"
			}
			- ", an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:concept-origin" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "documentOrigin"
			}
			- ", an\n  "
			a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-value" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-value-4" {
				- "opener policy value"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "responseCOOP"
			}
			- ", and an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:concept-origin-2" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- "\n  "
			var {
				- "responseOrigin"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "documentCOOP"
					}
					- " is \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none-3" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\" and\n   "
					var {
						- "responseCOOP"
					}
					- " is \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none-4" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\", then return\n   true."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "documentCOOP"
					}
					- " is \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none-5" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\" or\n   "
					var {
						- "responseCOOP"
					}
					- " is \""
					code id="cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-unsafe-none-6" {
						a href="#coop-unsafe-none" {
							- "unsafe-none"
						}
					}
					- "\", then return\n   false."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "documentCOOP"
					}
					- " is "
					var {
						- "responseCOOP"
					}
					- " and "
					var {
						- "documentOrigin"
					}
					- " is\n   "
					a href="#same-origin" id="cross-origin-opener-policies:same-origin-3" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- " with "
					var {
						- "responseOrigin"
					}
					- ", then return true."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return false."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h5 id="the-coop-headers" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.1.3.1"
			}
			- " The headers"
			a href="#the-coop-headers" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy" title="The HTTP Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy (COOP) response header allows you to ensure a top-level document does not share a browsing context group with cross-origin documents." {
						- "Headers/Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
