			p {
				- "In systems without script, this still works like the previous example. However, users that\n   "
				em {
					- "do"
				}
				- " have script support can now navigate much faster, since there is no network access\n   for the same experience. Furthermore, contrary to the experience the user would have with just a\n   naïve script-based approach, bookmarking and navigating the session history still work."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "In the example above, the "
				var {
					- "data"
				}
				- " argument to the "
				code id="the-history-interface:dom-history-pushstate-3" {
					a href="#dom-history-pushstate" {
						- "pushState()"
					}
				}
				- " method is the same information as would be sent\n   to the server, but in a more convenient form, so that the script doesn't have to parse the URL\n   each time the user navigates."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
