		p {
			- "Note that the "
			code id="navigation-api-intro:dom-navigationinterceptoptions-handler" {
				a href="#dom-navigationinterceptoptions-handler" {
					- "handler"
				}
			}
			- " function can return a promise to represent the asynchronous progress, and success or failure, of the navigation. While the promise is still pending, browser UI can treat the navigation as ongoing (e.g., by presenting a loading spinner). Other parts of the navigation API are also sensitive to these promises, such as the return value of "
			code id="navigation-api-intro:dom-navigation-navigate" {
				a href="#dom-navigation-navigate" {
					- "navigation.navigate()"
				}
			}
			- ":\n\n  "
