			}
			- " is a "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="the-notrestoredreasons-interface:top-level-traversable" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- ";\n  otherwise null."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h3 id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.3"
			}
			- " Infrastructure for sequences of documents"
			a href="#infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This standard contains several related concepts for grouping sequences of documents. As a\n  brief, non-normative summary:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					a href="#navigable" id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:navigable" {
						- "Navigables"
					}
					- " are a user-facing representation of a sequence\n   of documents, i.e., they represent something that can be navigated between documents. Typical\n   examples are tabs or windows in a web browser, or "
					code id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:the-iframe-element" {
						a href="#the-iframe-element" {
							- "iframe"
						}
					}
					- "s, or\n   "
					code id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:frame" {
						a href="#frame" {
							- "frame"
						}
					}
					- "s in a "
					code id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:frameset" {
						a href="#frameset" {
							- "frameset"
						}
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#traversable-navigable" id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:traversable-navigable" {
						- "Traversable navigables"
					}
					- " are a special type of\n   navigable which control the session history of themselves and of their descendant navigables.\n   That is, in addition to their own series of documents, they represent a tree of further series\n   of documents, plus the ability to linearly traverse back and forward through a flattened view of\n   this tree."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#browsing-context" id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:browsing-context" {
						- "Browsing contexts"
					}
					- " are a developer-facing\n   representation of a series of documents. They correspond 1:1 with "
					code id="infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:windowproxy" {
						a href="#windowproxy" {
							- "WindowProxy"
						}
					}
					- "\n   objects. Each navigable can present a series of browsing contexts, with "
					a href="#browsing-context-group-switches-due-to-cross-origin-opener-policy" {
						- "switches"
					}
					- " between\n   those browsing contexts occuring under certain well-defined circumstances."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Most of this standard works in the language of navigables, but certain APIs expose the\n  existence of browsing context switches, and so some parts of the standard need to work in terms\n  of browsing contexts."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="navigables" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.3.1"
			}
			- " Navigables"
			a href="#navigables" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id="navigable" data-export="" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- " presents a "
			code id="navigables:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " to the user via its "
			a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id="navigables:nav-active-history-entry" {
				- "active session history entry"
			}
			- ". Each navigable has:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "An "
					dfn id="nav-id" {
						- "id"
					}
					- ", a "
					a href="#new-unique-internal-value" id="navigables:new-unique-internal-value" {
						- "new unique internal value"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p id="parent-browsing-context" {
					- "A "
					dfn data-dfn-for="navigable" id="nav-parent" data-export="" {
						- "parent"
					}
					- ",\n   a "
					a href="#navigable" id="navigables:navigable" {
						- "navigable"
					}
					- " or null."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p id="current-entry" {
					- "A "
					dfn id="nav-current-history-entry" {
						- "current session history\n    entry"
					}
					- ", a "
					a href="#session-history-entry" id="navigables:session-history-entry" {
						- "session history entry"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This can only be modified within the "
					a href="#tn-session-history-traversal-queue" id="navigables:tn-session-history-traversal-queue" {
						- "session history traversal queue"
					}
					- " of the\n    parent "
					a href="#traversable-navigable" id="navigables:traversable-navigable" {
						- "traversable navigable"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "An "
					dfn id="nav-active-history-entry" {
						- "active session history entry"
					}
					- ", a\n    "
					a href="#session-history-entry" id="navigables:session-history-entry-2" {
						- "session history entry"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "This can only be modified from the event loop of the "
					a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id="navigables:nav-active-history-entry-2" {
						- "active session history entry"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#she-document" id="navigables:she-document" {
						- "document"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "An "
					dfn id="is-closing" {
						- "is closing"
					}
					- " boolean, initially false."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This is only ever set to true for "
					a href="#top-level-traversable" id="navigables:top-level-traversable" {
						- "top-level traversable navigables"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "An "
					dfn id="delaying-load-events-mode" {
						- "is delaying "
						code {
							- "load"
						}
						- "\n    events"
					}
					- " boolean, initially false."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
