			- ", user agents also\n  allow stopping traversals, i.e. cases where the "
			a href="#ongoing-navigation" id="aborting-a-document-load:ongoing-navigation-3" {
				- "ongoing navigation"
			}
			- " is \""
			code {
				- "traversal"
			}
			- "\". The above algorithm does not account for this. (On the other hand,\n  user agents do not allow "
			code id="aborting-a-document-load:dom-window-stop" {
				a href="#dom-window-stop" {
					- "window.stop()"
				}
			}
			- " to stop traversals,\n  so the above algorithm is correct for that caller.) See "
			a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6905" {
				- "issue #6905"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="the-x-frame-options-header" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.6"
			}
			- " The `"
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options" {
				a href="#x-frame-options" {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
			}
			- "` header"
			a href="#the-x-frame-options-header" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/X-Frame-Options" title="The X-Frame-Options HTTP response header can be used to indicate whether or not a browser should be allowed to render a page in a <frame>, <iframe>, <embed> or <object>. Sites can use this to avoid click-jacking attacks, by ensuring that their content is not embedded into other sites." {
						- "Headers/X-Frame-Options"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "10.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "8+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "Yes"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "?"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The `"
			dfn id="x-frame-options" data-dfn-type="http-header" {
				code {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP response header is a legacy way\n  of controlling whether and how a "
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " may be loaded inside of a "
			a href="#child-navigable" id="the-x-frame-options-header:child-navigable" {
				- "child\n  navigable"
			}
			- ". It is obsoleted by the "
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:frame-ancestors-directive" {
				a data-x-internal="frame-ancestors-directive" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#frame-ancestors" {
					- "frame-ancestors"
				}
			}
			- " CSP directive, which provides more granular control over the\n  same situations. It was originally defined in "
			cite {
				- "HTTP Header Field X-Frame-Options"
			}
			- ", but\n  the definition and processing model here supersedes that document.\n  "
			a href="#refsCSP" {
				- "[CSP]"
			}
			- " "
			a href="#refsRFC7034" {
				- "[RFC7034]"
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		p class="note" {
			- "In particular, "
			cite {
				- "HTTP Header Field X-Frame-Options"
			}
			- " specified an `"
			code {
				- "ALLOW-FROM"
			}
			- "` variant of the header, but that is not to be implemented."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Per the below processing model, if both\n  a CSP "
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:frame-ancestors-directive-2" {
				a data-x-internal="frame-ancestors-directive" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#frame-ancestors" {
					- "frame-ancestors"
				}
			}
			- " directive and an\n  `"
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-2" {
				a href="#x-frame-options" {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
			}
			- "` header are used in the same "
			a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-response" data-x-internal="concept-response" {
				- "response"
			}
			- ", then `"
			code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-3" {
				a href="#x-frame-options" {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
			}
			- "` is ignored."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For web developers and conformance checkers, its value "
			a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#abnf" id="the-x-frame-options-header:header-abnf" data-x-internal="header-abnf" {
				- "ABNF"
			}
			- "\n  is:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="abnf" {
				c- nc="" {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
				- " "
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				- " "
				c- l="" {
					- "\"DENY\""
				}
				- " "
				c- o="" {
					- "/"
				}
				- " "
				c- l="" {
					- "\"SAMEORIGIN\""
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="check-a-navigation-response's-adherence-to-x-frame-options" {
				- "check a navigation response's adherence to `"
				code {
					- "X-Frame-Options"
				}
				- "`"
			}
			- ", given\n  a "
			a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-response-2" data-x-internal="concept-response" {
				- "response"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "response"
			}
			- ", a "
			a href="#navigable" id="the-x-frame-options-header:navigable" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- "\n  "
			var {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- ", a "
			a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#csp-list" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-csp-list" data-x-internal="concept-csp-list" {
				- "CSP list"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "cspList"
			}
			- ", and\n  an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-origin" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "destinationOrigin"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "navigable"
					}
					- " is not a "
					a href="#child-navigable" id="the-x-frame-options-header:child-navigable-2" {
						- "child navigable"
					}
					- ", then return true."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-iterate" data-x-internal="list-iterate" {
						- "For each"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "policy"
					}
					- " of "
					var {
						- "cspList"
					}
					- ":"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var {
								- "policy"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#policy-disposition" id="the-x-frame-options-header:csp-disposition" data-x-internal="csp-disposition" {
								- "disposition"
							}
							- " is not \""
							code {
								- "enforce"
							}
							- "\", then "
							a id="the-x-frame-options-header:continue" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#iteration-continue" data-x-internal="continue" {
								- "continue"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var {
								- "policy"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#policy-directive-set" id="the-x-frame-options-header:csp-directive-set" data-x-internal="csp-directive-set" {
								- "directive set"
							}
							- " "
							a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-contains" data-x-internal="list-contains" {
								- "contains"
							}
							- " a "
							code id="the-x-frame-options-header:frame-ancestors-directive-3" {
								a data-x-internal="frame-ancestors-directive" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#frame-ancestors" {
									- "frame-ancestors"
								}
							}
							- " directive, then return true."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "rawXFrameOptions"
					}
					- " be the result of "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-header-list-get-decode-split" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-header-list-get-decode-split" data-x-internal="concept-header-list-get-decode-split" {
						- "getting, decoding, and splitting"
					}
					- "\n   `"
					code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-4" {
						a href="#x-frame-options" {
							- "X-Frame-Options"
						}
					}
					- "` from "
					var {
						- "response"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response-header-list" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-response-header-list" data-x-internal="concept-response-header-list" {
						- "header list"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- " be a new "
					a id="the-x-frame-options-header:set" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" data-x-internal="set" {
						- "set"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-iterate" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-iterate-2" data-x-internal="list-iterate" {
						- "For each"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " of\n   "
					var {
						- "rawXFrameOptions"
					}
					- ", "
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#set-append" id="the-x-frame-options-header:set-append" data-x-internal="set-append" {
						- "append"
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- ",\n   "
					a id="the-x-frame-options-header:converted-to-ascii-lowercase" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" data-x-internal="converted-to-ascii-lowercase" {
						- "converted to ASCII lowercase"
					}
					- ", to "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-size" data-x-internal="list-size" {
						- "size"
					}
					- " is greater than 1, and\n    "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- " "
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-contain" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-contains-2" data-x-internal="list-contains" {
						- "contains"
					}
					- " any of \""
					code {
						- "deny"
					}
					- "\", \""
					code {
						- "allowall"
					}
					- "\", or \""
					code {
						- "sameorigin"
					}
					- "\", then return false."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "The intention here is to block any attempts at applying\n    `"
					code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-5" {
						a href="#x-frame-options" {
							- "X-Frame-Options"
						}
					}
					- "` which were trying to do something valid, but appear confused."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This is the only impact of the legacy `"
					code {
						- "ALLOWALL"
					}
					- "` value\n    on the processing model."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list-size" id="the-x-frame-options-header:list-size-2" data-x-internal="list-size" {
						- "size"
					}
					- " is greater than 1, then\n    return true."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This means it contains multiple invalid values, which we treat the same way as\n    if the header was omitted entirely."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- "[0] is \""
					code {
						- "deny"
					}
					- "\", then return\n   false."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "xFrameOptions"
					}
					- "[0] is \""
					code {
						- "sameorigin"
					}
					- "\", then:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "containerDocument"
							}
							- " be "
							var {
								- "navigable"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="#nav-container-document" id="the-x-frame-options-header:nav-container-document" {
								- "container document"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							a id="the-x-frame-options-header:while" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#iteration-while" data-x-internal="while" {
								- "While"
							}
							- " "
							var {
								- "containerDocument"
							}
							- " is not null:"
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									- "If "
									var {
										- "containerDocument"
									}
									- "'s "
									a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="the-x-frame-options-header:concept-document-origin" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
										- "origin"
									}
									- "\n       is not "
									a href="#same-origin" id="the-x-frame-options-header:same-origin" {
										- "same origin"
									}
									- " with "
									var {
										- "destinationOrigin"
									}
									- ", then return\n       false."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Set "
									var {
										- "containerDocument"
									}
									- " to "
									var {
										- "containerDocument"
									}
									- "'s "
									a href="#doc-container-document" id="the-x-frame-options-header:doc-container-document" {
										- "container document"
									}
									- "."
								}
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Return true."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "If we've reached this point then we have a lone invalid value (which could\n    potentially be one the legacy `"
					code {
						- "ALLOWALL"
					}
					- "` or `"
					code {
						- "ALLOW-FROM"
					}
					- "` forms). These are treated as if the header were omitted\n    entirely."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "The following table illustrates the processing of various values for the header, including\n   non-conformant ones:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			table class="data" {
				thead {
					tr {
						th {
							- "`"
							code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-6" {
								a href="#x-frame-options" {
									- "X-Frame-Options"
								}
							}
							- "`"
						}
						th {
							- "Valid"
						}
						th {
							- "Result"
						}
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "DENY"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "✅"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "✅"
						}
						td {
							- "same-origin embedding allowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "INVALID"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "❌"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding allowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "ALLOWALL"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "❌"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding allowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "ALLOW-FROM=https://example.com/"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "❌"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding allowed (from anywhere)"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "The following table illustrates how various non-conformant cases involving multiple values are\n   processed:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			table class="data" {
				thead {
					tr {
						th {
							- "`"
							code id="the-x-frame-options-header:x-frame-options-7" {
								a href="#x-frame-options" {
									- "X-Frame-Options"
								}
							}
							- "`"
						}
						th {
							- "Result"
						}
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN, SAMEORIGIN"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "same-origin embedding allowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN, DENY"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN,"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN, ALLOWALL"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "SAMEORIGIN, INVALID"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "ALLOWALL, INVALID"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "ALLOWALL,"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding disallowed"
						}
					}
					tr {
						td {
							- "`"
							code {
								- "INVALID, INVALID"
							}
							- "`"
						}
						td {
							- "embedding allowed"
						}
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The same results are obtained whether the values are delivered in a single header whose value is comma-delimited,\n   or in multiple headers."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="the-refresh-header" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.7"
			}
			- " The `"
			code id="the-refresh-header:refresh" {
				a href="#refresh" {
					- "Refresh"
				}
			}
			- "` header"
			a href="#the-refresh-header" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The `"
			dfn id="refresh" data-dfn-type="http-header" {
				code {
					- "Refresh"
				}
			}
			- "` HTTP response header is the HTTP-equivalent\n  to a "
			code id="the-refresh-header:the-meta-element" {
				a href="#the-meta-element" {
					- "meta"
				}
			}
			- " element with an "
			code id="the-refresh-header:attr-meta-http-equiv" {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
					- "http-equiv"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute in the "
			a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" id="the-refresh-header:attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" {
				- "Refresh state"
			}
			- ". It takes "
			a href="#conformance-attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" {
				- "the same value"
			}
			- " and works largely the\n  same. Its processing model is detailed in "
			a href="#initialise-the-document-object" id="the-refresh-header:initialise-the-document-object" {
				- "create and initialize a "
				code {
					- "Document"
				}
				- "\n  object"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n  \n\n\n  "
		h3 id="nav-traversal-ui" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "7.8"
			}
			- " "
			span id="history-notes"
			- "Browser user interface\n  considerations"
			a href="#nav-traversal-ui" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents should provide the ability to "
			a href="#navigate" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigate" {
				- "navigate"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#reload" id="nav-traversal-ui:reload" {
				- "reload"
			}
			- ", and "
			a href="#nav-stop" id="nav-traversal-ui:nav-stop" {
				- "stop loading"
			}
			- "\n  any "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- " in their "
			a href="#top-level-traversable-set" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-set" {
				- "top-level traversable set"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, via a location bar and reload/stop button UI."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents should provide the ability to "
			a href="#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta" id="nav-traversal-ui:traverse-the-history-by-a-delta" {
				- "traverse by a delta"
			}
			- " any "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-2" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- " in their "
			a href="#top-level-traversable-set" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-set-2" {
				- "top-level\n  traversable set"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, via back and forward buttons, possibly including long-press\n  abilities to change the delta."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "It is suggested that such user agents allow traversal by deltas greater than one, to avoid\n  letting a page \"trap\" the user by stuffing the session history with spurious entries. (For\n  example, via repeated calls to "
			code id="nav-traversal-ui:dom-history-pushstate" {
				a href="#dom-history-pushstate" {
					- "history.pushState()"
				}
			}
			- " or\n  "
			a href="#navigate-fragid" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigate-fragid" {
				- "fragment navigations"
			}
			- ".)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Some user agents have heuristics for translating a single \"back\" or \"forward\"\n  button press into a larger delta, specifically to overcome such abuses. We are contemplating\n  specifying these heuristics in "
			a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7832" {
				- "issue\n  #7832"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents should offer users the ability to "
			a href="#create-a-fresh-top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:create-a-fresh-top-level-traversable" {
				- "create a fresh top-level\n  traversable"
			}
			- ", given a user-provided or user agent-determined initial "
			a id="nav-traversal-ui:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, via a \"new tab\" or \"new window\" button."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents should offer users the ability to arbitrarily "
			a href="#close-a-top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:close-a-top-level-traversable" {
				- "close"
			}
			- " any "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-3" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- " in their\n  "
			a href="#top-level-traversable-set" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-set-3" {
				- "top-level traversable set"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, by clicking a \"close tab\" button."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents may provide ways for the user to explicitly cause any\n  "
			a href="#navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigable" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- " (not just a "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-4" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- ") to "
			a href="#navigate" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigate-2" {
				- "navigate"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#reload" id="nav-traversal-ui:reload-2" {
				- "reload"
			}
			- ", or "
			a href="#nav-stop" id="nav-traversal-ui:nav-stop-2" {
				- "stop\n  loading"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, via a context menu."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents may provide the ability for users to "
			a href="#destroy-a-top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:destroy-a-top-level-traversable" {
				- "destroy a top-level\n  traversable"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, by force-closing a window containing one or more such "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-5" {
				- "top-level traversables"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a user requests a "
			a href="#reload" id="nav-traversal-ui:reload-3" {
				- "reload"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigable-2" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id="nav-traversal-ui:nav-active-history-entry" {
				- "active session history entry"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#she-document-state" id="nav-traversal-ui:she-document-state" {
				- "document state"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#document-state-resource" id="nav-traversal-ui:document-state-resource" {
				- "resource"
			}
			- " is a "
			a href="#post-resource" id="nav-traversal-ui:post-resource" {
				- "POST resource"
			}
			- ", the user agent\n  should prompt the user to confirm the operation first, since otherwise transactions (e.g.,\n  purchases or database modifications) could be repeated."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a user requests a "
			a href="#reload" id="nav-traversal-ui:reload-4" {
				- "reload"
			}
			- " of a "
			a href="#navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigable-3" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- ", user agents may provide\n  a mechanism for ignoring any caches when reloading."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All calls to "
			a href="#navigate" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigate-3" {
				- "navigate"
			}
			- " initiated by the mechanisms mentioned above must have the "
			i id="nav-traversal-ui:navigation-user-involvement" {
				a href="#navigation-user-involvement" {
					- "userInvolvement"
				}
			}
			- " argument set to \""
			code id="nav-traversal-ui:uni-browser-ui" {
				a href="#uni-browser-ui" {
					- "browser UI"
				}
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All calls to "
			a href="#reload" id="nav-traversal-ui:reload-5" {
				- "reload"
			}
			- " initiated by the mechanisms mentioned above must have the "
			i id="nav-traversal-ui:reload-user-involvement" {
				a href="#reload-user-involvement" {
					- "userInvolvement"
				}
			}
			- " argument set to \""
			code id="nav-traversal-ui:uni-browser-ui-2" {
				a href="#uni-browser-ui" {
					- "browser UI"
				}
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All calls to "
			a href="#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta" id="nav-traversal-ui:traverse-the-history-by-a-delta-2" {
				- "traverse the history by a delta"
			}
			- " initiated by the mechanisms mentioned\n  above must not pass a value for the "
			i id="nav-traversal-ui:traverse-sourcedocument" {
				a href="#traverse-sourcedocument" {
					- "sourceDocument"
				}
			}
			- "\n  argument."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The above recommendations, and the data structures in this specification, are not meant to\n  place restrictions on how user agents represent the session history to the user."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For example, although a "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-6" {
				- "top-level traversable"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#tn-session-history-entries" id="nav-traversal-ui:tn-session-history-entries" {
				- "session history entries"
			}
			- " are stored and maintained as a\n  list, and the user agent is recommended to give an interface for "
			a href="#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta" id="nav-traversal-ui:traverse-the-history-by-a-delta-3" {
				- "traversing that list by a delta"
			}
			- ", a novel user agent could instead or\n  in addition present a tree-like view, with each page having multiple \"forward\" pages that the user\n  can choose between."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, although session history for all descendant "
			a href="#navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigable-4" {
				- "navigables"
			}
			- " is stored in their "
			a href="#traversable-navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:traversable-navigable" {
				- "traversable navigable"
			}
			- ", user\n  agents could present the user with a more nuanced per-"
			a href="#navigable" id="nav-traversal-ui:navigable-5" {
				- "navigable"
			}
			- " view of the session\n  history."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Browser user agents may use a "
			a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-browsing-context" {
				- "top-level browsing context"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#is-popup" id="nav-traversal-ui:is-popup" {
				- "is\n  popup"
			}
			- " boolean for the following purposes:\n\n  "
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "Deciding whether or not to provide a minimal web browser user interface for the\n   corresponding "
					a href="#top-level-traversable" id="nav-traversal-ui:top-level-traversable-7" {
						- "top-level traversable"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Performing the optional steps in "
					a id="nav-traversal-ui:set-up-browsing-context-features" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#set-up-browsing-context-features" data-x-internal="set-up-browsing-context-features" {
						- "set up browsing context features"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In both cases user agents might additionally incorporate user preferences, or present a choice\n  as to whether to go down the popup route."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents that provides a minimal user interface for such popups are encouraged to not hide\n  the browser's location bar."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h2 id="webappapis" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8"
			}
			- " Web application APIs"
			a href="#webappapis" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h3 id="scripting" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1"
			}
			- " Scripting"
			a href="#scripting" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="introduction-11" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-11" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Various mechanisms can cause author-provided executable code to run in the context of a\n  document. These mechanisms include, but are probably not limited to:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "Processing of "
				code id="introduction-11:the-script-element" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " elements."
			}
			li {
				- "Navigating to "
				a href="#the-javascript:-url-special-case" id="introduction-11:the-javascript:-url-special-case" {
					code {
						- "javascript:"
					}
					- " URLs"
				}
				- "."
			}
			li {
				- "Event handlers, whether registered through the DOM using "
				code {
					- "addEventListener()"
				}
				- ", by explicit "
				a href="#event-handler-content-attributes" id="introduction-11:event-handler-content-attributes" {
					- "event handler content attributes"
				}
				- ", by\n   "
				a href="#event-handler-idl-attributes" id="introduction-11:event-handler-idl-attributes" {
					- "event handler IDL attributes"
				}
				- ", or otherwise."
			}
			li {
				- "Processing of technologies like SVG that have their own scripting features."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="agents-and-agent-clusters" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.2"
			}
			- " Agents and agent clusters"
			a href="#agents-and-agent-clusters" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h5 id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.2.1"
			}
			- " Integration with the JavaScript agent formalism"
			a href="#integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "JavaScript defines the concept of an "
			a id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:agent" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" data-x-internal="agent" {
				- "agent"
			}
			- ". This section gives the mapping of that\n  language-level concept on to the web platform."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="note" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Conceptually, the "
				a id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:agent-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" data-x-internal="agent" {
					- "agent"
				}
				- " concept is an architecture-independent, idealized\n   \"thread\" in which JavaScript code runs. Such code can involve multiple globals/"
				a href="#concept-global-object-realm" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:concept-global-object-realm" {
					- "realms"
				}
				- " that can synchronously access each other, and\n   thus needs to run in a single execution thread."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Two "
				code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:window" {
					a href="#window" {
						- "Window"
					}
				}
				- " objects having the same "
				a id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:agent-3" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" data-x-internal="agent" {
					- "agent"
				}
				- " does not indicate\n   they can directly access all objects created in each other's realms. They would have to be\n   "
				a href="#same-origin-domain" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:same-origin-domain" {
					- "same origin-domain"
				}
				- "; see "
				a href="#isplatformobjectsameorigin-(-o-)" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:isplatformobjectsameorigin-(-o-)" {
					- "IsPlatformObjectSameOrigin"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following types of agents exist on the web platform:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id="similar-origin-window-agent" data-export="" {
					- "Similar-origin window agent"
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Contains various "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:window-2" {
						a href="#window" {
							- "Window"
						}
					}
					- " objects which can potentially reach each other, either\n    directly or by using "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:dom-document-domain" {
						a href="#dom-document-domain" {
							- "document.domain"
						}
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "If the encompassing "
					a id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:agent-cluster" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" data-x-internal="agent-cluster" {
						- "agent cluster"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#is-origin-keyed" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:is-origin-keyed" {
						- "is origin-keyed"
					}
					- " is true, then\n    all the "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:window-3" {
						a href="#window" {
							- "Window"
						}
					}
					- " objects will be "
					a href="#same-origin" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:same-origin" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- ", can reach each other\n    directly, and "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:dom-document-domain-2" {
						a href="#dom-document-domain" {
							- "document.domain"
						}
					}
					- " will no-op."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Two "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:window-4" {
						a href="#window" {
							- "Window"
						}
					}
					- " objects that are "
					a href="#same-origin" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:same-origin-2" {
						- "same origin"
					}
					- " can be in\n    different "
					a href="#similar-origin-window-agent" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:similar-origin-window-agent" {
						- "similar-origin window agents"
					}
					- ", for\n    instance if they are each in their own "
					a href="#browsing-context-group" id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:browsing-context-group" {
						- "browsing context group"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="dedicated-worker-agent" data-export="" {
					- "Dedicated worker agent"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Contains a single "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-agent-formalism:dedicatedworkerglobalscope" {
						a href="#dedicatedworkerglobalscope" {
							- "DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope"
						}
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id="shared-worker-agent" data-export="" {
					- "Shared worker agent"
				}
			}
			dd {
