			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "If the algorithm for the "
				code id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:dom-navigator-getbattery-2" {
					a data-x-internal="dom-navigator-getbattery" href="https://w3c.github.io/battery/#widl-Navigator-getBattery-Promise-BatteryManager" {
						- "getBattery()"
					}
				}
				- " method\n   had instead used the "
				a id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:current-realm-3" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#current-realm" data-x-internal="current-realm" {
					- "current realm"
				}
				- ", all the results would be reversed. That is,\n   after the first call to "
				code id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:dom-navigator-getbattery-3" {
					a data-x-internal="dom-navigator-getbattery" href="https://w3c.github.io/battery/#widl-Navigator-getBattery-Promise-BatteryManager" {
						- "getBattery()"
					}
				}
				- " in "
				code {
					- "outer.html"
				}
				- ", the "
				code id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:navigator-2" {
					a href="#navigator" {
						- "Navigator"
					}
				}
				- " object in "
				code {
					- "inner.html"
				}
				- " would be permanently storing a "
				code {
					- "Promise"
				}
				- " object\n   created in "
				code {
					- "outer.html"
				}
				- "'s "
				a id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:realm-11" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" data-x-internal="realm" {
					- "realm"
				}
				- ", and calls like that inside the\n   "
				code {
					- "hello()"
				}
				- " function would thus return a promise from the \"wrong\" realm. Since\n   this is undesirable, the algorithm instead uses the "
				a href="#concept-relevant-realm" id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:concept-relevant-realm-6" {
					- "relevant realm"
				}
				- ", giving the sensible results indicated in\n   the comments above."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The rest of this section deals with formally defining the "
			a href="#concept-entry-everything" id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:concept-entry-everything-4" {
				- "entry"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#concept-incumbent-everything" id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:concept-incumbent-everything-4" {
				- "incumbent"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#concept-current-everything" id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:concept-current-everything-4" {
				- "current"
			}
			- ", and "
			a href="#concept-relevant-everything" id="realms-settings-objects-global-objects:concept-relevant-everything-4" {
				- "relevant"
			}
			- " concepts."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h6 id="entry" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.3.3.1"
			}
			- " Entry"
			a href="#entry" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The process of "
			a href="#calling-scripts" {
				- "calling scripts"
			}
			- " will push or pop "
			a href="#realm-execution-context" id="entry:realm-execution-context" {
				- "realm execution contexts"
			}
			- " onto the "
			a id="entry:javascript-execution-context-stack" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript\n  execution context stack"
			}
			- ", interspersed with other "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-execution-contexts" id="entry:javascript-execution-context" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context" {
				- "execution contexts"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "With this in hand, we define the "
			dfn id="entry-execution-context" {
				- "entry execution context"
			}
			- " to be the most recently\n  pushed item in the "
			a id="entry:javascript-execution-context-stack-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript execution context stack"
			}
			- " that is a "
			a href="#realm-execution-context" id="entry:realm-execution-context-2" {
				- "realm execution context"
			}
			- ". The "
			dfn id="concept-entry-realm" {
				- "entry\n  realm"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#entry-execution-context" id="entry:entry-execution-context" {
				- "entry execution context"
			}
			- "'s Realm component."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Then, the "
			dfn id="entry-settings-object" {
				- "entry settings object"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-realm-settings-object" id="entry:concept-realm-settings-object" {
				- "environment settings object"
			}
			- " of the "
			a href="#concept-entry-realm" id="entry:concept-entry-realm" {
				- "entry realm"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, the "
			dfn id="entry-global-object" {
				- "entry global object"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-realm-global" id="entry:concept-realm-global" {
				- "global object"
			}
			- " of the "
			a href="#concept-entry-realm" id="entry:concept-entry-realm-2" {
				- "entry\n  realm"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h6 id="incumbent" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.3.3.2"
			}
			- " Incumbent"
			a href="#incumbent" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-execution-contexts" id="incumbent:javascript-execution-context" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context" {
				- "JavaScript execution contexts"
			}
			- " must\n  contain, as part of their code evaluation state, a "
			dfn id="skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" {
				- "skip-when-determining-incumbent\n  counter"
			}
			- " value, which is initially zero. In the process of "
			a href="#prepare-to-run-a-callback" id="incumbent:prepare-to-run-a-callback" {
				- "preparing to run a callback"
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#clean-up-after-running-a-callback" id="incumbent:clean-up-after-running-a-callback" {
				- "cleaning up after running a callback"
			}
			- ", this value will be incremented and\n  decremented."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Every "
			a href="#event-loop" id="incumbent:event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " has an associated "
			dfn id="backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" {
				- "backup incumbent settings object\n  stack"
			}
			- ", initially empty. Roughly speaking, it is used to determine the "
			a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object" {
				- "incumbent\n  settings object"
			}
			- " when no author code is on the stack, but author code is responsible for the\n  current algorithm having been run in some way. The process of "
			a href="#prepare-to-run-a-callback" id="incumbent:prepare-to-run-a-callback-2" {
				- "preparing to run a callback"
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#clean-up-after-running-a-callback" id="incumbent:clean-up-after-running-a-callback-2" {
				- "cleaning up after running a callback"
			}
			- " manipulate this stack. "
			a href="#refsWEBIDL" {
				- "[WEBIDL]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When Web IDL is used to "
			a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invoke-a-callback-function" id="incumbent:es-invoking-callback-functions" data-x-internal="es-invoking-callback-functions" {
				- "invoke"
			}
			- " author\n  code, or when "
			a href="#hostenqueuepromisejob" id="incumbent:hostenqueuepromisejob" {
				- "HostEnqueuePromiseJob"
			}
			- " invokes a promise job, they use the following\n  algorithms to track relevant data for determining the "
			a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-2" {
				- "incumbent settings object"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="prepare-to-run-a-callback" data-export="" {
				- "prepare to run a callback"
			}
			- " with an "
			a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object" {
				- "environment settings object"
			}
			- "\n  "
			var {
				- "settings"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Push "
					var {
						- "settings"
					}
					- " onto the "
					a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" {
						- "backup incumbent settings object\n   stack"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " be the "
					a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context" {
						- "topmost script-having execution\n   context"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " is not null, increment "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "'s\n   "
					a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" {
						- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="clean-up-after-running-a-callback" data-export="" {
				- "clean up after running a callback"
			}
			- " with an "
			a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-2" {
				- "environment settings\n  object"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "settings"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " be the "
					a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-2" {
						- "topmost script-having execution context"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This will be the same as the "
					a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-3" {
						- "topmost script-having execution\n    context"
					}
					- " inside the corresponding invocation of "
					a href="#prepare-to-run-a-callback" id="incumbent:prepare-to-run-a-callback-3" {
						- "prepare to run a\n    callback"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " is not null, decrement "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "'s\n   "
					a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-2" {
						- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a id="incumbent:assert" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#assert" data-x-internal="assert" {
						- "Assert"
					}
					- ": the topmost entry of the "
					a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-2" {
						- "backup incumbent settings object\n   stack"
					}
					- " is "
					var {
						- "settings"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Remove "
					var {
						- "settings"
					}
					- " from the "
					a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-3" {
						- "backup incumbent settings object\n   stack"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Here, the "
			dfn id="topmost-script-having-execution-context" {
				- "topmost script-having execution context"
			}
			- " is the topmost entry of the\n  "
			a id="incumbent:javascript-execution-context-stack" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript execution context stack"
			}
			- " that has a non-null ScriptOrModule component, or\n  null if there is no such entry in the "
			a id="incumbent:javascript-execution-context-stack-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript execution context stack"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "With all this in place, the "
			dfn id="incumbent-settings-object" data-export="" {
				- "incumbent settings object"
			}
			- " is determined as\n  follows:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " be the "
					a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-4" {
						- "topmost script-having execution\n   context"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- " is null, or if "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "'s\n    "
					a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-3" {
						- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
					}
					- " is greater than zero, then:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							a id="incumbent:assert-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#assert" data-x-internal="assert" {
								- "Assert"
							}
							- ": the "
							a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-4" {
								- "backup incumbent settings object stack"
							}
							- " is not\n      empty."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "This assert would fail if you try to obtain the "
							a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-3" {
								- "incumbent settings\n      object"
							}
							- " from inside an algorithm that was triggered neither by "
							a href="#calling-scripts" {
								- "calling scripts"
							}
							- " nor by Web IDL "
							a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invoke-a-callback-function" id="incumbent:es-invoking-callback-functions-2" data-x-internal="es-invoking-callback-functions" {
								- "invoking"
							}
							- " a callback. For example, it would\n      trigger if you tried to obtain the "
							a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-4" {
								- "incumbent settings object"
							}
							- " inside an algorithm\n      that ran periodically as part of the "
							a href="#event-loop" id="incumbent:event-loop-2" {
								- "event loop"
							}
							- ", with no involvement of author\n      code. In such cases the "
							a href="#concept-incumbent-everything" id="incumbent:concept-incumbent-everything" {
								- "incumbent"
							}
							- " concept\n      cannot be used."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Return the topmost entry of the "
							a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-5" {
								- "backup incumbent settings object\n     stack"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return "
					var {
						- "context"
					}
					- "'s Realm component's "
					a href="#concept-realm-settings-object" id="incumbent:concept-realm-settings-object" {
						- "settings object"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Then, the "
			dfn id="concept-incumbent-realm" data-export="" {
				- "incumbent realm"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#environment-settings-object's-realm" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object's-realm" {
				- "realm"
			}
			- " of the "
			a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-5" {
				- "incumbent settings\n  object"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, the "
			dfn id="concept-incumbent-global" data-export="" {
				- "incumbent global object"
			}
			- " is\n  the "
			a href="#concept-settings-object-global" id="incumbent:concept-settings-object-global" {
				- "global object"
			}
			- " of the "
			a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-6" {
				- "incumbent\n  settings object"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following series of examples is intended to make it clear how all of the different\n  mechanisms contribute to the definition of the "
			a href="#incumbent" {
				- "incumbent"
			}
			- " concept:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div id="example-incumbent-1" class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider the following starter example:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- cp="" {
						- "<!DOCTYPE html>"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "iframe"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "iframe"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  frames"
					c- p="" {
						- "["
					}
					c- mf="" {
						- "0"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "]."
					}
					- "postMessage"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					c- u="" {
						- "\"some data\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ","
					}
					- " "
					c- u="" {
						- "\"*\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "There are two interesting "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-3" {
					- "environment settings\n   objects"
				}
				- " here: that of "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- ", and that of "
				code {
					- "frames[0]"
				}
				- ". Our concern is: what is the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-7" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- " at\n   the time that the algorithm for "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- "\n   executes?"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "It should be that of "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- ", to capture the intuitive notion that the\n   author script responsible for causing the algorithm to happen is executing in "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- ", not "
				code {
					- "frames[0]"
				}
				- ". This makes sense: the "
				a href="#window-post-message-steps" id="incumbent:window-post-message-steps" {
					- "window\n   post message steps"
				}
				- " use the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-8" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- " to determine the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-messageevent-source" {
					a href="#dom-messageevent-source" {
						- "source"
					}
				}
				- " property of the resulting\n   "
				code id="incumbent:messageevent" {
					a href="#messageevent" {
						- "MessageEvent"
					}
				}
				- ", and in this case "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- " is definitely the\n   source of the message."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Let us now explain how the steps given above give us our intuitively-desired result of "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- "'s "
				a href="#relevant-settings-object" id="incumbent:relevant-settings-object" {
					- "relevant settings object"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When the "
				a href="#window-post-message-steps" id="incumbent:window-post-message-steps-2" {
					- "window post message steps"
				}
				- " look up the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-9" {
					- "incumbent settings\n   object"
				}
				- ", the "
				a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-5" {
					- "topmost script-having execution context"
				}
				- " will be that\n   corresponding to the "
				code id="incumbent:the-script-element" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " element: it was pushed onto the "
				a id="incumbent:javascript-execution-context-stack-3" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
					- "JavaScript\n   execution context stack"
				}
				- " as part of "
				a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-runtime-semantics-scriptevaluation" id="incumbent:js-scriptevaluation" data-x-internal="js-scriptevaluation" {
					- "ScriptEvaluation"
				}
				- " during the "
				a href="#run-a-classic-script" id="incumbent:run-a-classic-script" {
					- "run a classic script"
				}
				- "\n   algorithm. Since there are no Web IDL callback invocations involved, the context's\n   "
				a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-4" {
					- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
				}
				- " is zero, so it is used to determine the\n   "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-10" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- "; the result is the "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-4" {
					- "environment settings\n   object"
				}
				- " of "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "(Note how the "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-5" {
					- "environment settings object"
				}
				- " of "
				code {
					- "frames[0]"
				}
				- " is\n   the "
				a href="#relevant-settings-object" id="incumbent:relevant-settings-object-2" {
					- "relevant settings object"
				}
				- " of "
				a id="incumbent:this" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
					- "this"
				}
				- " at the time the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage-2" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- " method is called, and thus is involved in\n   determining the "
				em {
					- "target"
				}
				- " of the message. Whereas the incumbent is used to determine the\n   "
				em {
					- "source"
				}
				- ".)\n  "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div id="example-incumbent-2" class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "Consider the following more complicated example:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- cp="" {
						- "<!DOCTYPE html>"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "iframe"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "iframe"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- a="" {
						- "const"
					}
					- " bound "
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					- " frames"
					c- p="" {
						- "["
					}
					c- mf="" {
						- "0"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "]."
					}
					- "postMessage"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "bind"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					- "frames"
					c- p="" {
						- "["
					}
					c- mf="" {
						- "0"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "],"
					}
					- " "
					c- u="" {
						- "\"some data\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ","
					}
					- " "
					c- u="" {
						- "\"*\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
					- "\n  window"
					c- p="" {
						- "."
					}
					- "setTimeout"
					c- p="" {
						- "("
					}
					- "bound"
					c- p="" {
						- ");"
					}
					- "\n"
					c- p="" {
						- "</"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "script"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ">"
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This example is very similar to the previous one, but with an extra indirection through "
				code {
					- "Function.prototype.bind"
				}
				- " as well as "
				code id="incumbent:dom-settimeout" {
					a href="#dom-settimeout" {
						- "setTimeout()"
					}
				}
				- ". But, the answer should be the same: invoking\n   algorithms asynchronously should not change the "
				a href="#concept-incumbent-everything" id="incumbent:concept-incumbent-everything-2" {
					- "incumbent"
				}
				- " concept."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This time, the result involves more complicated mechanisms:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When "
				code {
					- "bound"
				}
				- " is "
				a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#es-type-mapping" id="incumbent:concept-idl-convert" data-x-internal="concept-idl-convert" {
					- "converted"
				}
				- " to a\n   Web IDL callback type, the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-11" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- " is that corresponding to "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- " (in the same manner as in our starter example above). Web IDL stores this\n   as the resulting callback value's "
				a id="incumbent:callback-context" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-callback-context" data-x-internal="callback-context" {
					- "callback context"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When the "
				a href="#concept-task" id="incumbent:concept-task" {
					- "task"
				}
				- " posted by "
				code id="incumbent:dom-settimeout-2" {
					a href="#dom-settimeout" {
						- "setTimeout()"
					}
				}
				- " executes, the algorithm for that task uses Web IDL to\n   "
				a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invoke-a-callback-function" id="incumbent:es-invoking-callback-functions-3" data-x-internal="es-invoking-callback-functions" {
					- "invoke"
				}
				- " the stored callback value. Web IDL in\n   turn calls the above "
				a href="#prepare-to-run-a-callback" id="incumbent:prepare-to-run-a-callback-4" {
					- "prepare to run a callback"
				}
				- " algorithm. This pushes the stored\n   "
				a id="incumbent:callback-context-2" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-callback-context" data-x-internal="callback-context" {
					- "callback context"
				}
				- " onto the "
				a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-6" {
					- "backup incumbent settings object stack"
				}
				- ". At\n   this time (inside the timer task) there is no author code on the stack, so the "
				a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-6" {
					- "topmost\n   script-having execution context"
				}
				- " is null, and nothing gets its\n   "
				a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-5" {
					- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
				}
				- " incremented."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Invoking the callback then calls "
				code {
					- "bound"
				}
				- ", which in turn calls\n   the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage-3" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- " method of "
				code {
					- "frames[0]"
				}
				- ". When the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage-4" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- "\n   algorithm looks up the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-12" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- ", there is still no author code on\n   the stack, since the bound function just directly calls the built-in method. So the\n   "
				a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-7" {
					- "topmost script-having execution context"
				}
				- " will be null: the "
				a id="incumbent:javascript-execution-context-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-execution-contexts" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context" {
					- "JavaScript execution\n   context"
				}
				- " stack only contains an execution context corresponding to "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage-5" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- ", with no "
				a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-runtime-semantics-scriptevaluation" id="incumbent:js-scriptevaluation-2" data-x-internal="js-scriptevaluation" {
					- "ScriptEvaluation"
				}
				- " context or similar below it."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This is where we fall back to the "
				a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-7" {
					- "backup incumbent settings object stack"
				}
				- ". As\n   noted above, it will contain as its topmost entry the "
				a href="#relevant-settings-object" id="incumbent:relevant-settings-object-3" {
					- "relevant settings object"
				}
				- " of\n   "
				code {
					- "window"
				}
				- ". So that is what is used as the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-13" {
					- "incumbent settings\n   object"
				}
				- " while executing the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-window-postmessage-6" {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
						- "postMessage()"
					}
				}
				- "\n   algorithm."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div id="example-incumbent-3" class="example" {
