			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Again there are two interesting "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-6" {
					- "environment\n   settings objects"
				}
				- " in play: that of "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ", and that of "
				code {
					- "b.html"
				}
				- ". When the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-location-assign" {
					a href="#dom-location-assign" {
						- "location.assign()"
					}
				}
				- "\n   method triggers the "
				a href="#location-object-navigate" id="incumbent:location-object-navigate" {
					code {
						- "Location"
					}
					- "-object navigate"
				}
				- " algorithm, what will be\n   the "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-14" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- "? As before, it should intuitively be that of "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ": the "
				code id="incumbent:event-click" {
					a data-x-internal="event-click" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-click" {
						- "click"
					}
				}
				- " listener was originally\n   scheduled by "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ", so even if something involving "
				code {
					- "b.html"
				}
				- " causes the listener to fire, the "
				a href="#concept-incumbent-everything" id="incumbent:concept-incumbent-everything-3" {
					- "incumbent"
				}
				- " responsible is that of "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "The callback setup is similar to the previous example: when "
				code {
					- "bound"
				}
				- " is\n   "
				a href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#es-type-mapping" id="incumbent:concept-idl-convert-2" data-x-internal="concept-idl-convert" {
					- "converted"
				}
				- " to a Web IDL callback type, the\n   "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-15" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- " is that corresponding to "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ",\n   which is stored as the callback's "
				a id="incumbent:callback-context-3" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-callback-context" data-x-internal="callback-context" {
					- "callback context"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When the "
				code id="incumbent:dom-click" {
					a href="#dom-click" {
						- "click()"
					}
				}
				- " method is called inside "
				code {
					- "b.html"
				}
				- ", it "
				a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch" id="incumbent:concept-event-dispatch" data-x-internal="concept-event-dispatch" {
					- "dispatches"
				}
				- " a "
				code id="incumbent:event-click-2" {
					a data-x-internal="event-click" href="https://w3c.github.io/uievents/#event-type-click" {
						- "click"
					}
				}
				- " event on the button that is inside "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ". This time, when the "
				a href="#prepare-to-run-a-callback" id="incumbent:prepare-to-run-a-callback-5" {
					- "prepare to run a callback"
				}
				- " algorithm\n   executes as part of event dispatch, there "
				em {
					- "is"
				}
				- " author code on the stack; the "
				a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-8" {
					- "topmost\n   script-having execution context"
				}
				- " is that of the "
				code {
					- "onLoad"
				}
				- " function,\n   whose "
				a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-6" {
					- "skip-when-determining-incumbent counter"
				}
				- " gets incremented. Additionally, "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- "'s "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-7" {
					- "environment settings object"
				}
				- " (stored as the\n   "
				code id="incumbent:eventhandler" {
					a href="#eventhandler" {
						- "EventHandler"
					}
				}
				- "'s "
				a id="incumbent:callback-context-4" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-callback-context" data-x-internal="callback-context" {
					- "callback context"
				}
				- ") is pushed onto the\n   "
				a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-8" {
					- "backup incumbent settings object stack"
				}
				- "."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Now, when the "
				a href="#location-object-navigate" id="incumbent:location-object-navigate-2" {
					code {
						- "Location"
					}
					- "-object navigate"
				}
				- " algorithm looks up the\n   "
				a href="#incumbent-settings-object" id="incumbent:incumbent-settings-object-16" {
					- "incumbent settings object"
				}
				- ", the "
				a href="#topmost-script-having-execution-context" id="incumbent:topmost-script-having-execution-context-9" {
					- "topmost script-having execution\n   context"
				}
				- " is still that of the "
				code {
					- "onLoad"
				}
				- " function (due to the fact we\n   are using a bound function as the callback). Its "
				a href="#skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter" id="incumbent:skip-when-determining-incumbent-counter-7" {
					- "skip-when-determining-incumbent\n   counter"
				}
				- " value is one, however, so we fall back to the "
				a href="#backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack" id="incumbent:backup-incumbent-settings-object-stack-9" {
					- "backup incumbent settings\n   object stack"
				}
				- ". This gives us the "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id="incumbent:environment-settings-object-8" {
					- "environment settings object"
				}
				- " of "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- ", as expected."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "Note that this means that even though it is the "
				code id="incumbent:the-iframe-element" {
					a href="#the-iframe-element" {
						- "iframe"
					}
				}
				- " inside "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- " that navigates, it is "
				code {
					- "a.html"
				}
				- " itself that is used\n   as the source "
				code id="incumbent:document" {
					a href="#document" {
						- "Document"
					}
				}
				- ", which determines among other things the "
				a href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-client" id="incumbent:concept-request-client" data-x-internal="concept-request-client" {
					- "request client"
				}
				- ". This is "
				a href="https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=26603#c36" {
					- "perhaps the only justifiable use\n   of the incumbent concept on the web platform"
				}
				- "; in all other cases the consequences of using it\n   are simply confusing and we hope to one day switch them to use "
				a href="#concept-current-everything" id="incumbent:concept-current-everything" {
					- "current"
				}
				- " or "
				a href="#concept-relevant-everything" id="incumbent:concept-relevant-everything" {
					- "relevant"
				}
				- " as appropriate."
			}
			- "\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h6 id="current" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.3.3.3"
			}
			- " Current"
			a href="#current" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The JavaScript specification defines the "
			a id="current:current-realm" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#current-realm" data-x-internal="current-realm" {
				- "current realm"
			}
			- ", also known as the \"current\n  Realm Record\". "
			a href="#refsJAVASCRIPT" {
				- "[JAVASCRIPT]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Then, the "
			dfn id="current-settings-object" data-export="" {
				- "current settings object"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-realm-settings-object" id="current:concept-realm-settings-object" {
				- "environment settings object"
			}
			- " of the "
			a id="current:current-realm-2" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#current-realm" data-x-internal="current-realm" {
				- "current\n  realm"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Similarly, the "
			dfn id="current-global-object" data-export="" {
				- "current global object"
			}
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-realm-global" id="current:concept-realm-global" {
				- "global object"
			}
			- " of the "
			a id="current:current-realm-3" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#current-realm" data-x-internal="current-realm" {
				- "current realm"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h6 id="relevant" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.3.3.4"
			}
			- " Relevant"
			a href="#relevant" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="concept-relevant-realm" data-export="" {
				- "relevant realm"
			}
			- " for a "
