		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="killing-scripts" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "8.1.4.5"
			}
			- " Killing scripts"
			a href="#killing-scripts" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Although the JavaScript specification does not account for this possibility, it's sometimes\n  necessary to "
			dfn id="abort-a-running-script" data-lt="abort a running script|abort the running script" data-export="" {
				- "abort a\n  running script"
			}
			- ". This causes any "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-runtime-semantics-scriptevaluation" id="killing-scripts:js-scriptevaluation" data-x-internal="js-scriptevaluation" {
				- "ScriptEvaluation"
			}
			- "\n  or "
			a id="killing-scripts:source-text-module-record" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-source-text-module-records" data-x-internal="source-text-module-record" {
				- "Source Text Module Record"
			}
			- " "
			a href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-moduleevaluation" id="killing-scripts:js-evaluate" data-x-internal="js-evaluate" {
				- "Evaluate"
			}
			- " invocations\n  to cease immediately, emptying the "
			a id="killing-scripts:javascript-execution-context-stack" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript execution context stack"
			}
			- " without\n  triggering any of the normal mechanisms like "
			code {
				- "finally"
			}
			- " blocks.\n  "
			a href="#refsJAVASCRIPT" {
				- "[JAVASCRIPT]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents may impose resource limitations on scripts, for example CPU quotas, memory limits,\n  total execution time limits, or bandwidth limitations. When a script exceeds a limit, the user\n  agent may either throw a "
			a id="killing-scripts:quotaexceedederror" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#quotaexceedederror" data-x-internal="quotaexceedederror" {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "QuotaExceededError"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			- " "
			code id="killing-scripts:domexception" {
				a data-x-internal="domexception" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" {
					- "DOMException"
				}
			}
			- ",\n  "
			a href="#abort-a-running-script" id="killing-scripts:abort-a-running-script" {
				- "abort the script"
			}
			- " without an exception, prompt the\n  user, or throttle script execution."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, the following script never terminates. A user agent could, after waiting for a\n   few seconds, prompt the user to either terminate the script or let it continue."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
