		- "\n\n  "
		div id="example-import-map-merge-unrelated" class="example" {
			- "\n   "
			p {
				- "There are two cases when rules of the new import map don't get merged into the existing\n   one."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			ol {
				li {
					p {
						- "The new import map rule has the exact same scope and specifier as a rule in the existing\n    import map. We'll call that \"conflicting rule\"."
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "The new import map rule may impact the resolution of an already resolved module. We'll\n    call that \"impacted already resolved module\"."
					}
				}
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "When the new import map has no conflicting rules, and there are no impacted resolved modules,\n   the resulting map would be a combination of the new and existing maps. Rules that would have\n   individually impacted similar modules (e.g. \"/app/\" and \"/app/helper\") but are not an exact\n   match are not conflicting, and all make it to the merged map."
