		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "It is possible for a "
			a href="#microtask" id="queuing-tasks:microtask" {
				- "microtask"
			}
			- " to be moved to a regular "
			a href="#task-queue" id="queuing-tasks:task-queue-2" {
				- "task\n  queue"
			}
			- ", if, during its initial execution, it "
			a href="#spin-the-event-loop" id="queuing-tasks:spin-the-event-loop" {
				- "spins the\n  event loop"
			}
			- ". This is the only case in which the "
			a href="#concept-task-source" id="queuing-tasks:concept-task-source-3" {
				- "source"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#concept-task-document" id="queuing-tasks:concept-task-document-3" {
				- "document"
			}
			- ",\n  and "
			a href="#script-evaluation-environment-settings-object-set" id="queuing-tasks:script-evaluation-environment-settings-object-set-3" {
				- "script evaluation environment settings object set"
			}
			- " of the microtask are consulted;\n  they are ignored by the "
			a href="#perform-a-microtask-checkpoint" id="queuing-tasks:perform-a-microtask-checkpoint" {
				- "perform a microtask checkpoint"
			}
			- " algorithm."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="implied-event-loop" {
				- "implied event loop"
			}
			- " when queuing a task is the one that can deduced from the\n  context of the calling algorithm. This is generally unambiguous, as most specification algorithms\n  only ever involve a single "
			a id="queuing-tasks:agent" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" data-x-internal="agent" {
				- "agent"
			}
			- " (and thus a single "
			a href="#event-loop" id="queuing-tasks:event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- "). The\n  exception is algorithms involving or specifying cross-agent communication (e.g., between a window\n  and a worker); for those cases, the "
			a href="#implied-event-loop" id="queuing-tasks:implied-event-loop-3" {
				- "implied event loop"
			}
			- " concept must not be relied\n  upon and specifications must explicitly provide an "
			a href="#event-loop" id="queuing-tasks:event-loop-2" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " when "
			a href="#queue-a-task" id="queuing-tasks:queue-a-task-3" {
				- "queuing a task"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="implied-document" {
				- "implied document"
			}
			- " when queuing a task on an "
			a href="#event-loop" id="queuing-tasks:event-loop-3" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "event\n  loop"
			}
			- " is determined as follows:"
