		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="microtask-queuing:dom-queuemicrotask" {
				a href="#dom-queuemicrotask" {
					- "queueMicrotask()"
				}
			}
			- " method allows authors to schedule\n  a callback on the "
			a href="#microtask-queue" id="microtask-queuing:microtask-queue" {
				- "microtask queue"
			}
			- ". This allows their code to run once the\n  "
			a id="microtask-queuing:javascript-execution-context-stack" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" data-x-internal="javascript-execution-context-stack" {
				- "JavaScript execution context stack"
			}
			- " is next empty, which happens once all currently\n  executing synchronous JavaScript has run to completion. This doesn't yield control back to the\n  "
			a href="#event-loop" id="microtask-queuing:event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- ", as would be the case when using, for example, "
			code id="microtask-queuing:dom-settimeout" {
				a href="#dom-settimeout" {
					- "setTimeout("
					var {
						- "f"
					}
					- ", 0)"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Authors ought to be aware that scheduling a lot of microtasks has the same performance\n  downsides as running a lot of synchronous code. Both will prevent the browser from doing its own\n  work, such as rendering. In many cases, "
			code id="microtask-queuing:dom-animationframeprovider-requestanimationframe" {
				a href="#dom-animationframeprovider-requestanimationframe" {
					- "requestAnimationFrame()"
				}
			}
			- " or\n  "
			code id="microtask-queuing:requestidlecallback()" {
				a data-x-internal="requestidlecallback()" href="https://w3c.github.io/requestidlecallback/#the-requestidlecallback-method" {
					- "requestIdleCallback()"
				}
			}
			- " is a better choice. In particular, if the goal is to run code\n  before the next rendering cycle, that is the purpose of "
			code id="microtask-queuing:dom-animationframeprovider-requestanimationframe-2" {
				a href="#dom-animationframeprovider-requestanimationframe" {
					- "requestAnimationFrame()"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "As can be seen from the following examples, the best way of thinking about "
			code id="microtask-queuing:dom-queuemicrotask-2" {
				a href="#dom-queuemicrotask" {
					- "queueMicrotask()"
				}
			}
			- " is as a mechanism for rearranging synchronous\n  code, effectively placing the queued code immediately after the currently executing synchronous\n  JavaScript has run to completion."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
