		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Although these days detecting PDF viewer support can be done via "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:dom-navigator-pdfviewerenabled-2" {
				a href="#dom-navigator-pdfviewerenabled" {
					- "navigator.pdfViewerEnabled"
				}
			}
			- ", for historical reasons,\n  there are a number of complex and intertwined interfaces that provide the same capability, which\n  legacy code relies on. This section specifies both the simple modern variant and the complicated\n  historical one."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n  "
		p {
			- "Each user agent has a "
			dfn id="pdf-viewer-supported" {
				- "PDF viewer supported"
			}
			- " boolean, whose value is\n  "
			a id="pdf-viewing-support:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
				- "implementation-defined"
			}
			- " (and might vary according to user preferences)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This value also impacts the "
			a href="#navigate" id="pdf-viewing-support:navigate-2" {
				- "navigation"
			}
			- " processing\n  model."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:window" {
				a href="#window" {
					- "Window"
				}
			}
			- " object has a "
			dfn id="pdf-viewer-plugin-objects" {
				- "PDF viewer plugin objects"
			}
			- " list. If the user\n  agent's "
			a href="#pdf-viewer-supported" id="pdf-viewing-support:pdf-viewer-supported" {
				- "PDF viewer supported"
			}
			- " is false, then it is the empty list. Otherwise, it is a\n  list containing five "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:dom-plugin" {
				a href="#dom-plugin" {
					- "Plugin"
				}
			}
			- " objects, whose "
			a href="#concept-plugin-name" id="pdf-viewing-support:concept-plugin-name" {
				- "names"
			}
			- " are, respectively:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol start="0" class="brief" {
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "PDF Viewer"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "Chrome PDF Viewer"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "Chromium PDF Viewer"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "Microsoft Edge PDF Viewer"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "WebKit built-in PDF"
				}
				- "\""
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The values of the above list form the "
			dfn id="pdf-viewer-plugin-names" {
				- "PDF viewer plugin names"
			}
			- " list."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "These names were chosen based on evidence of what websites historically search\n  for, and thus what is necessary for user agents to expose in order to maintain compatibility with\n  existing content. They are ordered alphabetically. The \""
			code {
				- "PDF Viewer"
			}
			- "\" name\n  was then inserted in the 0th position so that the "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:dom-mimetype-enabledplugin-2" {
				a href="#dom-mimetype-enabledplugin" {
					- "enabledPlugin"
				}
			}
			- " getter could point to a generic plugin\n  name."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:window-2" {
				a href="#window" {
					- "Window"
				}
			}
			- " object has a "
			dfn id="pdf-viewer-mime-type-objects" {
				- "PDF viewer mime type objects"
			}
			- " list. If the user\n  agent's "
			a href="#pdf-viewer-supported" id="pdf-viewing-support:pdf-viewer-supported-2" {
				- "PDF viewer supported"
			}
			- " is false, then it is the empty list. Otherwise, it is a\n  list containing two "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:mimetype-5" {
				a href="#mimetype" {
					- "MimeType"
				}
			}
			- " objects, whose "
			a href="#concept-mimetype-type" id="pdf-viewing-support:concept-mimetype-type" {
				- "types"
			}
			- " are, respectively:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol start="0" class="brief" {
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "application/pdf"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "\""
				code {
					- "text/pdf"
				}
				- "\""
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The values of the above list form the "
			dfn id="pdf-viewer-mime-types" {
				- "PDF viewer mime types"
			}
			- " list."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:navigatorplugins" {
				a href="#navigatorplugins" {
					- "NavigatorPlugins"
				}
			}
			- " object has a "
			dfn id="plugins-array" {
				- "plugins array"
			}
			- ", which is a new\n  "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:pluginarray-2" {
				a href="#pluginarray" {
					- "PluginArray"
				}
			}
			- ", and a "
			dfn id="mime-types-array" {
				- "mime types array"
			}
			- ", which is a new\n  "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:mimetypearray-2" {
				a href="#mimetypearray" {
					- "MimeTypeArray"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:navigatorplugins-2" {
				a href="#navigatorplugins" {
					- "NavigatorPlugins"
				}
			}
			- " mixin's "
			dfn data-dfn-for="NavigatorPlugins" id="dom-navigator-plugins" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "plugins"
				}
			}
			- " getter steps are to return "
			a id="pdf-viewing-support:this" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s\n  "
			a href="#plugins-array" id="pdf-viewing-support:plugins-array" {
				- "plugins array"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:navigatorplugins-3" {
				a href="#navigatorplugins" {
					- "NavigatorPlugins"
				}
			}
			- " mixin's "
			dfn data-dfn-for="NavigatorPlugins" id="dom-navigator-mimetypes" data-dfn-type="attribute" {
				code {
					- "mimeTypes"
				}
			}
			- " getter steps are to return\n  "
			a id="pdf-viewing-support:this-2" href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" data-x-internal="this" {
				- "this"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#mime-types-array" id="pdf-viewing-support:mime-types-array" {
				- "mime types array"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="pdf-viewing-support:navigatorplugins-4" {
				a href="#navigatorplugins" {
					- "NavigatorPlugins"
				}
			}
			- " mixin's "
			dfn data-dfn-for="NavigatorPlugins" id="dom-navigator-javaenabled" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "javaEnabled()"
				}
			}
			- " method steps are to return false."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
