		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Event stream requests can be redirected using HTTP 301 and 307 redirects as with normal HTTP\n  requests. Clients will reconnect if the connection is closed; a client can be told to stop\n  reconnecting using the HTTP 204 No Content response code."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Using this API rather than emulating it using "
			code id="server-sent-events-intro:xmlhttprequest" {
				a data-x-internal="xmlhttprequest" href="https://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#xmlhttprequest" {
					- "XMLHttpRequest"
				}
			}
			- " or an\n  "
			code id="server-sent-events-intro:the-iframe-element" {
				a href="#the-iframe-element" {
					- "iframe"
				}
			}
			- " allows the user agent to make better use of network resources in cases where\n  the user agent implementer and the network operator are able to coordinate in advance. Amongst\n  other benefits, this can result in significant savings in battery life on portable devices. This\n  is discussed further in the section below on "
			a href="#eventsource-push" {
				- "connectionless\n  push"
			}
			- "."
		}
