		- "\n\n  "
		h4 id="introduction-13" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "9.4.1"
			}
			- " Introduction"
			a href="#introduction-13" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To enable independent pieces of code (e.g. running in different "
			a href="#browsing-context" id="introduction-13:browsing-context" {
				- "browsing contexts"
			}
			- ") to communicate directly, authors can use "
			a href="#channel-messaging" id="introduction-13:channel-messaging" {
				- "channel\n  messaging"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Communication channels in this mechanism are implemented as two-ways pipes, with a port at each\n  end. Messages sent in one port are delivered at the other port, and vice-versa. Messages are\n  delivered as DOM events, without interrupting or blocking running "
			a href="#concept-task" id="introduction-13:concept-task" {
				- "tasks"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To create a connection (two \"entangled\" ports), the "
			code {
				- "MessageChannel()"
			}
			- "\n  constructor is called:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="js" {
				c- a="" {
					- "var"
				}
				- " channel "
				c- o="" {
					- "="
				}
				- " "
				c- k="" {
					- "new"
				}
				- " MessageChannel"
				c- p="" {
					- "();"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "One of the ports is kept as the local port, and the other port is sent to the remote code, e.g.\n  using "
			code id="introduction-13:dom-window-postmessage" {
				a href="#dom-window-postmessage" {
					- "postMessage()"
				}
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="js" {
				- "otherWindow"
				c- p="" {
					- "."
				}
