		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The bulk of this code is simply an unoptimized search for a prime number. The "
			code id="a-background-number-crunching-worker:dom-dedicatedworkerglobalscope-postmessage" {
				a href="#dom-dedicatedworkerglobalscope-postmessage" {
					- "postMessage()"
				}
			}
			- " method is used to send a\n  message back to the page when a prime is found."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="/demos/workers/primes/page.html" {
				- "View this example online"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="module-worker-example" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.1.2.2"
			}
			- " Using a JavaScript module as a worker"
			a href="#module-worker-example" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All of our examples so far show workers that run "
			a href="#classic-script" id="module-worker-example:classic-script" {
				- "classic\n  scripts"
			}
			- ". Workers can instead be instantiated using "
			a href="#module-script" id="module-worker-example:module-script" {
				- "module\n  scripts"
			}
			- ", which have the usual benefits: the ability to use the JavaScript\n  "
			code {
				- "import"
			}
			- " statement to import other modules; strict mode by default; and\n  top-level declarations not polluting the worker's global scope."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "As the "
			code {
				- "import"
			}
			- " statement is available, the "
			code id="module-worker-example:dom-workerglobalscope-importscripts" {
				a href="#dom-workerglobalscope-importscripts" {
					- "importScripts()"
				}
			}
			- " method will automatically fail\n  inside module workers."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In this example, the main document uses a worker to do off-main-thread image manipulation.\n  It imports the filters used from another module."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The main page is as follows:"
		}
