		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "There are several key things worth noting about the way the viewer is written."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Multiple listeners"
			}
			- ". Instead of a single message processing function, the code\n  here attaches multiple event listeners, each one performing a quick check to see if it is relevant\n  for the message. In this example it doesn't make much difference, but if multiple authors wanted\n  to collaborate using a single port to communicate with a worker, it would allow for independent\n  code instead of changes having to all be made to a single event handling function."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Registering event listeners in this way also allows you to unregister specific listeners when\n  you are done with them, as is done with the "
			code {
				- "configure()"
			}
			- " method in this\n  example."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Finally, the worker:"
		}
