		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Connecting to multiple pages"
			}
			- ". The script uses the "
			code id="shared-state-using-a-shared-worker:handler-sharedworkerglobalscope-onconnect" {
				a href="#handler-sharedworkerglobalscope-onconnect" {
					- "onconnect"
				}
			}
			- " event listener to listen for\n  multiple connections."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			strong {
				- "Direct channels"
			}
			- ". When the worker receives a \"msg\" message from one viewer\n  naming another viewer, it sets up a direct connection between the two, so that the two viewers can\n  communicate directly without the worker having to proxy all the messages."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="/demos/workers/multiviewer/page.html" {
				- "View this example online"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="delegation" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.1.2.5"
			}
			- " Delegation"
			a href="#delegation" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "With multicore CPUs becoming prevalent, one way to obtain better performance is to split\n  computationally expensive tasks amongst multiple workers. In this example, a computationally\n  expensive task that is to be performed for every number from 1 to 10,000,000 is farmed out to ten\n  subworkers."
		}
