		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "They receive two numbers in two events, perform the computation for the range of numbers thus\n  specified, and then report the result back to the parent."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="/demos/workers/multicore/page.html" {
				- "View this example online"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="providing-libraries" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.1.2.6"
			}
			- " Providing libraries"
			a href="#providing-libraries" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Suppose that a cryptography library is made available that provides three tasks:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Generate a public/private key pair"
			}
			dd {
				- "Takes a port, on which it will send two messages, first the public key and then the private\n   key."
			}
			dt {
				- "Given a plaintext and a public key, return the corresponding ciphertext"
			}
			dd {
				- "Takes a port, to which any number of messages can be sent, the first giving the public key,\n   and the remainder giving the plaintext, each of which is encrypted and then sent on that same\n   channel as the ciphertext. The user can close the port when it is done encrypting content."
			}
			dt {
				- "Given a ciphertext and a private key, return the corresponding plaintext"
			}
			dd {
				- "Takes a port, to which any number of messages can be sent, the first giving the private key,\n   and the remainder giving the ciphertext, each of which is decrypted and then sent on that same\n   channel as the plaintext. The user can close the port when it is done decrypting content."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The library itself is as follows:"
		}
