		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Shared workers are identified by the URL of the script used to create it, optionally with an\n  explicit name. The name allows multiple instances of a particular shared worker to be started."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Shared workers are scoped by "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="shared-workers:concept-origin" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- ". Two different sites using the same names will\n  not collide. However, if a page tries to use the same shared worker name as another page on the\n  same site, but with a different script URL, it will fail."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Creating shared workers is done using the "
			code id="shared-workers:dom-sharedworker" {
				a href="#dom-sharedworker" {
					- "SharedWorker()"
				}
			}
			- "\n  constructor. This constructor takes the URL to the script to use for its first argument, and the\n  name of the worker, if any, as the second argument."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="js" {
				c- a="" {
