		- "\n\n\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="infrastructure-2" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.2"
			}
			- " Infrastructure"
			a href="#infrastructure-2" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This standard defines two kinds of workers: dedicated workers, and shared workers. Dedicated\n  workers, once created, are linked to their creator, but message ports can be used to communicate\n  from a dedicated worker to multiple other browsing contexts or workers. Shared workers, on the\n  other hand, are named, and once created any script running in the same "
			a href="#concept-origin" id="infrastructure-2:concept-origin" {
				- "origin"
			}
			- " can\n  obtain a reference to that worker and communicate with it. "
			cite {
				- "Service Workers"
			}
			- " defines a\n  third kind. "
			a href="#refsSW" {
				- "[SW]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="the-global-scope" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.2.1"
			}
			- " The global scope"
			a href="#the-global-scope" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The global scope is the \"inside\" of a worker."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h5 id="the-workerglobalscope-common-interface" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "10.2.1.1"
			}
			- " The "
			code id="workerglobalscope-dev" {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" {
					- "WorkerGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " common interface"
			a href="#the-workerglobalscope-common-interface" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WorkerGlobalScope" title="The WorkerGlobalScope interface of the Web Workers API is an interface representing the scope of any worker. Workers have no browsing context; this scope contains the information usually conveyed by Window objects — in this case event handlers, the console or the associated WorkerNavigator object. Each WorkerGlobalScope has its own event loop." {
						- "WorkerGlobalScope"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "3.5+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "10.6+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
