		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h5 id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "11.3.1.1"
			}
			- " Agents and event loops"
			a href="#worklet-agents-and-event-loops" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			i {
				- "This section is non-normative."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:workletglobalscope" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " is contained in its own "
			a href="#worklet-agent" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:worklet-agent" {
				- "worklet agent"
			}
			- ", which\n  has its corresponding "
			a href="#concept-agent-event-loop" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:concept-agent-event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- ". However, in\n  practice, implementation of these agents and event loops is expected to be different from most\n  others."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#worklet-agent" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:worklet-agent-2" {
				- "worklet agent"
			}
			- " exists for each "
			code id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:workletglobalscope-2" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " since, in theory,\n  an implementation could use a separate thread for each "
			code id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:workletglobalscope-3" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " instance,\n  and allowing this level of parallelism is best done using agents. However, because their\n  [[CanBlock]] value is false, there is no requirement that agents and threads are one-to-one. This\n  allows implementations the freedom to execute scripts loaded into a worklet on any thread,\n  including one running code from other agents with [[CanBlock]] of false, such as the thread of a\n  "
			a href="#similar-origin-window-agent" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:similar-origin-window-agent" {
				- "similar-origin window agent"
			}
			- " (\"the main thread\"). Contrast this with "
			a href="#dedicated-worker-agent" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:dedicated-worker-agent" {
				- "dedicated worker agents"
			}
			- ", whose true value for [[CanBlock]]\n  effectively requires them to get a dedicated operating system thread."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Worklet "
			a href="#event-loop" id="worklet-agents-and-event-loops:event-loop" {
