		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="worklets-lifetime" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "11.3.3"
			}
			- " The worklet's lifetime"
			a href="#worklets-lifetime" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The lifetime of a "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:worklet" {
				a href="#worklet" {
					- "Worklet"
				}
			}
			- " has no special considerations; it is tied to the object\n  it belongs to, such as the "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:window" {
				a href="#window" {
					- "Window"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="concept-document-worklet-global-scopes" {
				- "worklet\n  global scopes"
			}
			- ", which is a "
			a id="worklets-lifetime:set" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-set" data-x-internal="set" {
				- "set"
			}
			- " of "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:workletglobalscope" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- "s, initially\n  empty."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The lifetime of a "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:workletglobalscope-2" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " is, at a minimum, tied to the\n  "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#concept-document-worklet-global-scopes" id="worklets-lifetime:concept-document-worklet-global-scopes" {
				- "worklet global\n  scopes"
			}
			- " contain it. In particular, "
			a href="#destroy-a-document" id="worklets-lifetime:destroy-a-document" {
				- "destroying"
			}
			- " the\n  "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:document-3" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " will "
			a href="#terminate-a-worklet-global-scope" id="worklets-lifetime:terminate-a-worklet-global-scope" {
				- "terminate"
			}
			- " the\n  corresponding "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:workletglobalscope-3" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- " and allow it to be garbage-collected."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Additionally, user agents may, at any time, "
			a href="#terminate-a-worklet-global-scope" id="worklets-lifetime:terminate-a-worklet-global-scope-2" {
				- "terminate"
			}
			- " a given "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:workletglobalscope-4" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- ", unless the specification defining\n  the corresponding worklet type says otherwise. For example, they might terminate them if the\n  "
			a href="#worklet-agent" id="worklets-lifetime:worklet-agent" {
				- "worklet agent"
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-agent-event-loop" id="worklets-lifetime:concept-agent-event-loop" {
				- "event loop"
			}
			- " has no\n  "
			a href="#concept-task" id="worklets-lifetime:concept-task" {
				- "tasks"
			}
			- " queued, or if the user agent has no pending operations\n  planning to make use of the worklet, or if the user agent detects abnormal operations such as\n  infinite loops or callbacks exceeding imposed time limits."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Finally, specifications for specific worklet types can give more specific details on when to\n  "
			a href="#create-a-worklet-global-scope" id="worklets-lifetime:create-a-worklet-global-scope" {
				- "create"
			}
			- " "
			code id="worklets-lifetime:workletglobalscope-5" {
				a href="#workletglobalscope" {
					- "WorkletGlobalScope"
				}
			}
			- "s for a\n  given worklet type. For example, they might create them during specific processes that call upon\n  worklet code, as in the "
			a href="#worklets-example-registering" {
				- "example"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		h2 id="webstorage" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "12"
			}
			- " Web storage"
			a href="#webstorage" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
