		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="the-input-byte-stream" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.3"
			}
			- " The "
			dfn {
				- "input byte stream"
			}
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The stream of code points that comprises the input to the tokenization stage will be initially\n  seen by the user agent as a stream of bytes (typically coming over the network or from the local\n  file system). The bytes encode the actual characters according to a particular "
			i {
				- "character\n  encoding"
			}
			- ", which the user agent uses to decode the bytes into characters."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "For XML documents, the algorithm user agents are required to use to determine the\n  character encoding is given by "
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- ". This section does not apply to XML documents.\n  "
			a href="#refsXML" {
				- "[XML]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Usually, the "
			a href="#encoding-sniffing-algorithm" id="the-input-byte-stream:encoding-sniffing-algorithm" {
				- "encoding sniffing algorithm"
			}
			- " defined below is used to determine the\n  character encoding."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Given a character encoding, the bytes in the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id="the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream" {
				- "input byte stream"
			}
			- " must be converted\n  to characters for the tokenizer's "
			a href="#input-stream" id="the-input-byte-stream:input-stream" {
				- "input stream"
			}
			- ", by passing the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id="the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream-2" {
				- "input byte\n  stream"
			}
			- " and character encoding to "
			a id="the-input-byte-stream:decode" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode" data-x-internal="decode" {
				- "decode"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "A leading Byte Order Mark (BOM) causes the character encoding argument to be\n  ignored and will itself be skipped."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Bytes or sequences of bytes in the original byte stream that did not conform to\n  the Encoding standard (e.g. invalid UTF-8 byte sequences in a UTF-8 input byte stream) are errors\n  that conformance checkers are expected to report. "
			a href="#refsENCODING" {
				- "[ENCODING]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="warning" {
			- "The decoder algorithms describe how to handle invalid input; for security\n  reasons, it is imperative that those rules be followed precisely. Differences in how invalid byte\n  sequences are handled can result in, amongst other problems, script injection vulnerabilities\n  (\"XSS\")."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the HTML parser is decoding an input byte stream, it uses a character encoding and a "
			dfn id="concept-encoding-confidence" {
				- "confidence"
			}
			- ". The confidence is either "
			i {
				- "tentative"
			}
			- ",\n  "
			i {
				- "certain"
			}
			- ", or "
			i {
				- "irrelevant"
			}
			- ". The encoding used, and whether the confidence in that\n  encoding is "
			i {
				- "tentative"
			}
			- " or "
			i {
				- "certain"
			}
			- ", is "
			a href="#meta-charset-during-parse" {
				- "used\n  during the parsing"
			}
			- " to determine whether to "
			a href="#change-the-encoding" id="the-input-byte-stream:change-the-encoding" {
				- "change the encoding"
			}
			- ". If no encoding is\n  necessary, e.g. because the parser is operating on a Unicode stream and doesn't have to use a\n  character encoding at all, then the "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="the-input-byte-stream:concept-encoding-confidence" {
				- "confidence"
			}
			- " is\n  "
			i {
				- "irrelevant"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Some algorithms feed the parser by directly adding characters to the "
			a href="#input-stream" id="the-input-byte-stream:input-stream-2" {
				- "input\n  stream"
			}
			- " rather than adding bytes to the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id="the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream-3" {
				- "input byte stream"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.3.1"
			}
			- " Parsing with a known character encoding"
			a href="#parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the HTML parser is to operate on an input byte stream that has "
			dfn id="a-known-definite-encoding" data-export="" {
				- "a known\n  definite encoding"
			}
			- ", then the character encoding is that encoding and the "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence" {
				- "confidence"
			}
			- " is "
			i {
				- "certain"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="determining-the-character-encoding" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.3.2"
			}
			- " Determining the character encoding"
			a href="#determining-the-character-encoding" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "In some cases, it might be impractical to unambiguously determine the encoding before parsing\n  the document. Because of this, this specification provides for a two-pass mechanism with an\n  optional pre-scan. Implementations are allowed, as described below, to apply a simplified parsing\n  algorithm to whatever bytes they have available before beginning to parse the document. Then, the\n  real parser is started, using a tentative encoding derived from this pre-parse and other\n  out-of-band metadata. If, while the document is being loaded, the user agent discovers a character\n  encoding declaration that conflicts with this information, then the parser can get reinvoked to\n  perform a parse of the document with the real encoding."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="documentEncoding" {
			- "User agents must use the following algorithm, called the "
			dfn id="encoding-sniffing-algorithm" {
				- "encoding\n  sniffing algorithm"
			}
			- ", to determine the character encoding to use when decoding a document in\n  the first pass. This algorithm takes as input any out-of-band metadata available to the user agent\n  (e.g. the "
			a href="#content-type" id="determining-the-character-encoding:content-type" {
				- "Content-Type metadata"
			}
			- " of the document) and all the\n  bytes available so far, and returns a character encoding and a "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence" {
				- "confidence"
			}
			- " that is either "
			i {
				- "tentative"
			}
			- " or\n  "
			i {
				- "certain"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the result of "
					a href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#bom-sniff" id="determining-the-character-encoding:bom-sniff" data-x-internal="bom-sniff" {
						- "BOM sniffing"
					}
					- " is an encoding, return that\n    encoding with "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-2" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "certain"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Although the "
					a id="determining-the-character-encoding:decode" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode" data-x-internal="decode" {
						- "decode"
					}
					- " algorithm will itself change the encoding to\n    use based on the presence of a byte order mark, this algorithm sniffs the BOM as well in order\n    to set the correct "
					a id="determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
						- "document's character encoding"
					}
					- " and "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-3" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the user has explicitly instructed the user agent to override the document's character\n    encoding with a specific encoding, optionally return that encoding with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-4" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "certain"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "Typically, user agents remember such user requests across sessions, and in some\n    cases apply them to documents in "
					code id="determining-the-character-encoding:the-iframe-element" {
						a href="#the-iframe-element" {
							- "iframe"
						}
					}
					- "s as well."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The user agent may wait for more bytes of the resource to be available, either in this step\n    or at any later step in this algorithm. For instance, a user agent might wait 500ms or 1024\n    bytes, whichever came first. In general preparsing the source to find the encoding improves\n    performance, as it reduces the need to throw away the data structures used when parsing upon\n    finding the encoding information. However, if the user agent delays too long to obtain data to\n    determine the encoding, then the cost of the delay could outweigh any performance improvements\n    from the preparse."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "The authoring conformance requirements for character encoding declarations limit\n    them to only appearing "
					a href="#charset1024" {
						- "in the first 1024 bytes"
					}
					- ". User agents are\n    therefore encouraged to use the prescan algorithm below (as invoked by these steps) on the first\n    1024 bytes, but not to stall beyond that."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the transport layer specifies a character encoding, and it is supported, return that\n   encoding with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-5" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "certain"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Optionally "
					a href="#prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding" id="determining-the-character-encoding:prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding" {
						- "prescan the byte\n    stream to determine its encoding"
					}
					- ", with the "
					i {
						a href="#prescan-end-condition" id="determining-the-character-encoding:prescan-end-condition" {
							- "end\n    condition"
						}
					}
					- " being when the user agent decides that scanning further bytes would not be\n    efficient. User agents are encouraged to only prescan the first 1024 bytes. User agents may\n    decide that scanning "
					em {
						- "any"
					}
					- " bytes is not efficient, in which case these substeps are\n    entirely skipped."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "The aforementioned algorithm returns either a character encoding or failure. If it returns a\n    character encoding, then return the same encoding, with "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-6" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "tentative"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#html-parser" id="determining-the-character-encoding:html-parser" {
						- "HTML parser"
					}
					- " for which this algorithm is being run is associated with a\n    "
					code id="determining-the-character-encoding:document" {
						a href="#document" {
							- "Document"
						}
					}
					- " "
					var {
						- "d"
					}
					- " whose "
					a href="#doc-container-document" id="determining-the-character-encoding:doc-container-document" {
						- "container\n    document"
					}
					- " is non-null, then:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "parentDocument"
							}
							- " be "
							var {
								- "d"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="#doc-container-document" id="determining-the-character-encoding:doc-container-document-2" {
								- "container document"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var {
								- "parentDocument"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-document-origin" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
								- "origin"
							}
							- " is\n     "
							a href="#same-origin" id="determining-the-character-encoding:same-origin" {
								- "same origin"
							}
							- " with "
							var {
								- "d"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-document-origin-2" data-x-internal="concept-document-origin" {
								- "origin"
							}
							- " and "
							var {
								- "parentDocument"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id="determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding-2" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
								- "character encoding"
							}
							- " is not\n     "
							a id="determining-the-character-encoding:utf-16-encoding" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-16be-le" data-x-internal="utf-16-encoding" {
								- "UTF-16BE/LE"
							}
							- ", then return "
							var {
								- "parentDocument"
							}
							- "'s "
							a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id="determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding-3" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
								- "character encoding"
							}
							- ", with the "
							a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-7" {
								- "confidence"
							}
							- " "
							i {
								- "tentative"
							}
							- "."
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, if the user agent has information on the likely encoding for this page, e.g.\n   based on the encoding of the page when it was last visited, then return that encoding, with the\n   "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-8" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "tentative"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The user agent may attempt to autodetect the character encoding from applying frequency\n    analysis or other algorithms to the data stream. Such algorithms may use information about the\n    resource other than the resource's contents, including the address of the resource. If\n    autodetection succeeds in determining a character encoding, and that encoding is a supported\n    encoding, then return that encoding, with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-9" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- " "
					i {
						- "tentative"
					}
					- ".\n    "
					a href="#refsUNIVCHARDET" {
						- "[UNIVCHARDET]"
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "User agents are generally discouraged from attempting to autodetect encodings\n    for resources obtained over the network, since doing so involves inherently non-interoperable\n    heuristics. Attempting to detect encodings based on an HTML document's preamble is especially\n    tricky since HTML markup typically uses only ASCII characters, and HTML documents tend to begin\n    with a lot of markup rather than with text content."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "The UTF-8 encoding has a highly detectable bit pattern. Files from the local\n    file system that contain bytes with values greater than 0x7F which match the UTF-8 pattern are\n    very likely to be UTF-8, while documents with byte sequences that do not match it are very\n    likely not. When a user agent can examine the whole file, rather than just the preamble,\n    detecting for UTF-8 specifically can be especially effective. "
					a href="#refsPPUTF8" {
						- "[PPUTF8]"
					}
					- "\n    "
					a href="#refsUTF8DET" {
						- "[UTF8DET]"
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Otherwise, return an "
					a id="determining-the-character-encoding:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
						- "implementation-defined"
					}
					- " or user-specified default character\n    encoding, with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id="determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-10" {
						- "confidence"
					}
					- "\n    "
					i {
						- "tentative"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "In controlled environments or in environments where the encoding of documents can be\n    prescribed (for example, for user agents intended for dedicated use in new networks), the\n    comprehensive "
					code {
						- "UTF-8"
					}
					- " encoding is suggested."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "In other environments, the default encoding is typically dependent on the user's locale (an\n    approximation of the languages, and thus often encodings, of the pages that the user is likely\n    to frequent). The following table gives suggested defaults based on the user's locale, for\n    compatibility with legacy content. Locales are identified by BCP 47 language tags.\n    "
					a href="#refsBCP47" {
						- "[BCP47]"
					}
					- " "
					a href="#refsENCODING" {
						- "[ENCODING]"
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    \n\n    "
				table {
					thead {
						tr {
							th colspan="2" {
								- "Locale language\n       "
							}
							th {
								- "Suggested default encoding\n     "
							}
						}
					}
					tbody {
						tr {
							td {
								- "ar\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Arabic\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1256" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1256" data-x-internal="windows-1256" {
									- "windows-1256"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      \n      \n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "az\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Azeri\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1254" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1254" data-x-internal="windows-1254" {
									- "windows-1254"
								}
								- "\n\n      \n\n      \n      \n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "ba\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Bashkir\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1251" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1251" data-x-internal="windows-1251" {
									- "windows-1251"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n      \n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "be\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Belarusian\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1251-2" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1251" data-x-internal="windows-1251" {
									- "windows-1251"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "bg\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Bulgarian\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1251-3" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1251" data-x-internal="windows-1251" {
									- "windows-1251"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "cs\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Czech\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1250" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1250" data-x-internal="windows-1250" {
									- "windows-1250"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n      \n      \n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "el\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Greek\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:iso-8859-7" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#iso-8859-7" data-x-internal="iso-8859-7" {
									- "ISO-8859-7"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "et\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Estonian\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1257" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1257" data-x-internal="windows-1257" {
									- "windows-1257"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "fa\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Persian\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1256-2" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1256" data-x-internal="windows-1256" {
									- "windows-1256"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "he\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Hebrew\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1255" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1255" data-x-internal="windows-1255" {
									- "windows-1255"
								}
								- " \n\n      \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "hr\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Croatian\n       "
							}
							td {
								a id="determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1250-2" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1250" data-x-internal="windows-1250" {
									- "windows-1250"
								}
								- " \n\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "hu\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "Hungarian\n       "
							}
							td {
