		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Typically, the "
			a href="#special" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:special" {
				- "special"
			}
			- " elements have the start and end tag tokens\n  handled specifically, while "
			a href="#ordinary" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:ordinary" {
				- "ordinary"
			}
			- " elements' tokens fall into \"any other start tag\"\n  and \"any other end tag\" clauses, and some parts of the tree builder check if a particular element\n  in the "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:stack-of-open-elements-6" {
				- "stack of open elements"
			}
			- " is in the "
			a href="#special" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:special-2" {
				- "special"
			}
			- " category. However, some\n  elements (e.g., the "
			code id="the-stack-of-open-elements:the-option-element" {
				a href="#the-option-element" {
					- "option"
				}
			}
			- " element) have their start or end tag tokens handled\n  specifically, but are still not in the "
			a href="#special" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:special-3" {
				- "special"
			}
			- " category, so that they get the\n  "
			a href="#ordinary" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:ordinary-2" {
				- "ordinary"
			}
			- " handling elsewhere."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:stack-of-open-elements-7" {
				- "stack of open elements"
			}
			- " is said to "
			dfn id="has-an-element-in-the-specific-scope" {
				- "have an element "
				var {
					- "target node"
				}
				- " in a specific scope"
			}
			- " consisting of a\n  list of element types "
			var {
				- "list"
			}
			- " when the following algorithm terminates in a match\n  state:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Initialize "
					var {
						- "node"
					}
					- " to be the "
					a href="#current-node" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:current-node-4" {
						- "current node"
					}
					- " (the bottommost\n   node of the stack)."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "node"
					}
					- " is the target node, terminate in a match state."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, if "
					var {
						- "node"
					}
					- " is one of the element types in "
					var {
						- "list"
					}
					- ", terminate in a failure state."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, set "
					var {
						- "node"
					}
					- " to the previous entry in the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:stack-of-open-elements-8" {
						- "stack of open\n   elements"
					}
					- " and return to step 2. (This will never fail, since the loop will always terminate\n   in the previous step if the top of the stack — an "
					code id="the-stack-of-open-elements:the-html-element-5" {
						a href="#the-html-element" {
							- "html"
						}
					}
					- " element — is\n   reached.)"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:stack-of-open-elements-9" {
				- "stack of open elements"
			}
			- " is said to "
			dfn id="has-an-element-in-scope" {
				- "have a\n  particular element in scope"
			}
			- " when it "
			a href="#has-an-element-in-the-specific-scope" id="the-stack-of-open-elements:has-an-element-in-the-specific-scope" {
				- "has\n  that element in the specific scope"
			}
			- " consisting of the following element types:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul class="brief" {
			li {
