				a href="#character-reference-code" {
					- "character reference code"
				}
			}
			- " to\n  the "
			var id="numeric-character-reference-end-state:temporary-buffer-2" {
				a href="#temporary-buffer" {
					- "temporary buffer"
				}
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#flush-code-points-consumed-as-a-character-reference" id="numeric-character-reference-end-state:flush-code-points-consumed-as-a-character-reference" {
				- "Flush code points consumed as a\n  character reference"
			}
			- ". Switch to the "
			var id="numeric-character-reference-end-state:return-state" {
				a href="#return-state" {
					- "return state"
				}
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="tree-construction" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.6"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				- "Tree construction"
			}
			a href="#tree-construction" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The input to the tree construction stage is a sequence of tokens from the\n  "
			a href="#tokenization" id="tree-construction:tokenization" {
				- "tokenization"
			}
			- " stage. The tree construction stage is associated with a DOM\n  "
			code id="tree-construction:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " object when a parser is created. The \"output\" of this stage consists of\n  dynamically modifying or extending that document's DOM tree."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification does not define when an interactive user agent has to render the\n  "
			code id="tree-construction:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " so that it is available to the user, or when it has to begin accepting user\n  input."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "As each token is emitted from the tokenizer, the user agent must follow the appropriate steps\n  from the following list, known as the "
			dfn id="tree-construction-dispatcher" {
				- "tree construction dispatcher"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="switch" {
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="tree-construction:stack-of-open-elements" {
					- "stack of open elements"
				}
				- " is empty"
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is an element in the "
				a id="tree-construction:html-namespace-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace" data-x-internal="html-namespace-2" {
					- "HTML namespace"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node-2" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is a "
				a href="#mathml-text-integration-point" id="tree-construction:mathml-text-integration-point" {
					- "MathML text integration point"
				}
				- " and the token is a start tag whose tag name is neither \"mglyph\" nor \"malignmark\""
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node-3" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is a "
				a href="#mathml-text-integration-point" id="tree-construction:mathml-text-integration-point-2" {
					- "MathML text integration point"
				}
				- " and the token is a character token"
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node-4" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is a "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-annotation-xml" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#dfn-annotation-xml" data-x-internal="mathml-annotation-xml" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "annotation-xml"
					}
				}
				- " element and the token is a start tag whose tag name is \"svg\""
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node-5" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is an "
				a href="#html-integration-point" id="tree-construction:html-integration-point" {
					- "HTML integration point"
				}
				- " and the token is a start tag"
			}
			dt {
				- "If the "
				a href="#adjusted-current-node" id="tree-construction:adjusted-current-node-6" {
					- "adjusted current node"
				}
				- " is an "
				a href="#html-integration-point" id="tree-construction:html-integration-point-2" {
					- "HTML integration point"
				}
				- " and the token is a character token"
			}
			dt {
				- "If the token is an end-of-file token"
			}
			dd {
				- "Process the token according to the rules given in the section corresponding to the current\n   "
				a href="#insertion-mode" id="tree-construction:insertion-mode" {
					- "insertion mode"
				}
				- " in HTML content."
			}
			dt {
				- "Otherwise"
			}
			dd {
				- "Process the token according to the rules given in the section for parsing tokens "
				a href="#parsing-main-inforeign" id="tree-construction:parsing-main-inforeign" {
					- "in foreign content"
				}
				- "."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="next-token" {
				- "next token"
			}
			- " is the token that is about to be processed by the "
			a href="#tree-construction-dispatcher" id="tree-construction:tree-construction-dispatcher" {
				- "tree\n  construction dispatcher"
			}
			- " (even if the token is subsequently just ignored)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A node is a "
			dfn id="mathml-text-integration-point" {
				- "MathML text integration point"
			}
			- " if it is one of the following\n  elements:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul class="brief" {
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-mi" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#the-mi-element" data-x-internal="mathml-mi" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "mi"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-mo" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#operator-fence-separator-or-accent-mo" data-x-internal="mathml-mo" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "mo"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-mn" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#number-mn" data-x-internal="mathml-mn" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "mn"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-ms" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#string-literal-ms" data-x-internal="mathml-ms" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "ms"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-mtext" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#text-mtext" data-x-internal="mathml-mtext" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "mtext"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A node is an "
			dfn id="html-integration-point" {
				- "HTML integration point"
			}
			- " if it is one of the following elements:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul class="brief" {
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-annotation-xml-2" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#dfn-annotation-xml" data-x-internal="mathml-annotation-xml" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "annotation-xml"
					}
				}
				- " element whose start tag token had an\n   attribute with the name \"encoding\" whose value was an "
				a id="tree-construction:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
					- "ASCII case-insensitive"
				}
				- " match\n   for the string \""
				code {
					- "text/html"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a id="tree-construction:mathml-annotation-xml-3" href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#dfn-annotation-xml" data-x-internal="mathml-annotation-xml" {
					- "MathML "
					code {
						- "annotation-xml"
					}
				}
				- " element whose start tag token had an\n   attribute with the name \"encoding\" whose value was an "
				a id="tree-construction:ascii-case-insensitive-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
					- "ASCII case-insensitive"
				}
				- " match\n   for the string \""
				code {
					- "application/xhtml+xml"
				}
				- "\""
			}
			li {
				- "An "
				a id="tree-construction:svg-foreignobject" href="https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/embedded.html#ForeignObjectElement" data-x-internal="svg-foreignobject" {
					- "SVG "
					code {
						- "foreignObject"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "An "
				a id="tree-construction:svg-desc" href="https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/struct.html#DescElement" data-x-internal="svg-desc" {
					- "SVG "
					code {
						- "desc"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
			li {
				- "An "
				a id="tree-construction:svg-title" href="https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/struct.html#TitleElement" data-x-internal="svg-title" {
					- "SVG "
					code {
						- "title"
					}
				}
				- " element"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "If the node in question is the "
			var id="tree-construction:concept-frag-parse-context" {
				a href="#concept-frag-parse-context" {
					- "context"
				}
			}
			- " element passed to the "
			a href="#html-fragment-parsing-algorithm" id="tree-construction:html-fragment-parsing-algorithm" {
				- "HTML fragment\n  parsing algorithm"
			}
			- ", then the start tag token for that element is the \"fake\" token created\n  during by that "
			a href="#html-fragment-parsing-algorithm" id="tree-construction:html-fragment-parsing-algorithm-2" {
				- "HTML fragment parsing algorithm"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "Not all of the tag names mentioned below are conformant tag names in this\n  specification; many are included to handle legacy content. They still form part of the algorithm\n  that implementations are required to implement to claim conformance."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The algorithm described below places no limit on the depth of the DOM tree\n  generated, or on the length of tag names, attribute names, attribute values, "
			code id="tree-construction:text" {
				a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
					- "Text"
				}
			}
			- "\n  nodes, etc. While implementers are encouraged to "
			a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-limits" {
				- "avoid arbitrary limits"
			}
			- ", it is\n  recognized that practical concerns will likely force user agents to impose nesting depth\n  constraints."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h5 id="creating-and-inserting-nodes" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.6.1"
			}
			- " Creating and inserting nodes"
			a href="#creating-and-inserting-nodes" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "While the parser is processing a token, it can enable or disable "
			dfn id="foster-parent" {
				- "foster parenting"
			}
			- ". This affects the following algorithm."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="appropriate-place-for-inserting-a-node" {
				- "appropriate place for inserting a node"
			}
			- ", optionally using a particular\n  "
			i {
				- "override target"
			}
			- ", is the position in an element returned by running the following steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If there was an "
					i {
						- "override target"
					}
					- " specified, then let "
					var {
						- "target"
					}
					- " be the\n    "
					i {
						- "override target"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Otherwise, let "
					var {
						- "target"
					}
					- " be the "
					a href="#current-node" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:current-node" {
						- "current node"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Determine the "
					var {
						- "adjusted insertion location"
					}
					- " using the first matching steps\n    from the following list:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				dl class="switch" {
					dt {
						- "If "
						a href="#foster-parent" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:foster-parent" {
							- "foster parenting"
						}
						- " is enabled and "
						var {
							- "target"
						}
						- " is a "
						code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-table-element" {
							a href="#the-table-element" {
								- "table"
							}
						}
						- ", "
						code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-tbody-element" {
							a href="#the-tbody-element" {
								- "tbody"
							}
						}
						- ", "
						code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-tfoot-element" {
							a href="#the-tfoot-element" {
								- "tfoot"
							}
						}
						- ",\n     "
						code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-thead-element" {
							a href="#the-thead-element" {
								- "thead"
							}
						}
						- ", or "
						code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-tr-element" {
							a href="#the-tr-element" {
								- "tr"
							}
						}
						- " element"
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "Foster parenting happens when content is misnested in tables."
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p {
							- "Run these substeps:"
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									var {
										- "last template"
									}
									- " be the last "
									code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-template-element" {
										a href="#the-template-element" {
											- "template"
										}
									}
									- " element in the\n       "
									a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:stack-of-open-elements" {
										- "stack of open elements"
									}
									- ", if any."
								}
								- "\n\n       "
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- " be the last "
									code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-table-element-2" {
										a href="#the-table-element" {
											- "table"
										}
									}
									- " element in the\n       "
									a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:stack-of-open-elements-2" {
										- "stack of open elements"
									}
									- ", if any."
								}
								- "\n\n       "
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "If there is a "
									var {
										- "last template"
									}
									- " and either there is no "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- ", or there is one, but "
									var {
										- "last template"
									}
									- " is lower\n       (more recently added) than "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- " in the "
									a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:stack-of-open-elements-3" {
										- "stack of open\n       elements"
									}
									- ", then: let "
									var {
										- "adjusted insertion location"
									}
									- " be inside "
									var {
										- "last template"
									}
									- "'s "
									a href="#template-contents" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:template-contents" {
										- "template contents"
									}
									- ", after its last child (if any),\n       and abort these steps."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "If there is no "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- ",  then let "
									var {
										- "adjusted insertion\n       location"
									}
									- " be inside the first element in the "
									a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:stack-of-open-elements-4" {
										- "stack of open elements"
									}
									- " (the\n       "
									code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-html-element" {
										a href="#the-html-element" {
											- "html"
										}
									}
									- " element), after its last child (if any), and abort these steps.\n       ("
									a href="#fragment-case" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:fragment-case" {
										- "fragment case"
									}
									- ")"
								}
								- "\n\n       \n\n       "
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "If "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- " has a parent node, then let "
									var {
										- "adjusted insertion location"
									}
									- " be inside "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- "'s parent\n       node, immediately before "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- ", and abort these steps."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									var {
										- "previous element"
									}
									- " be the element immediately above "
									var {
										- "last table"
									}
									- " in the "
									a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:stack-of-open-elements-5" {
										- "stack of open elements"
									}
									- "."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									var {
										- "adjusted insertion location"
									}
									- " be inside "
									var {
										- "previous\n       element"
									}
									- ", after its last child (if any)."
								}
							}
						}
						- "\n\n      "
						p class="note" {
							- "These steps are involved in part because it's possible for elements, the\n      "
							code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-table-element-3" {
								a href="#the-table-element" {
									- "table"
								}
							}
							- " element in this case in particular, to have been moved by a script around\n      in the DOM, or indeed removed from the DOM entirely, after the element was inserted by the\n      parser."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
					dt {
						- "Otherwise"
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "Let "
							var {
								- "adjusted insertion location"
							}
							- " be inside "
							var {
								- "target"
							}
							- ",\n      after its last child (if any)."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					var {
						- "adjusted insertion location"
					}
					- " is inside a "
					code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-template-element-2" {
						a href="#the-template-element" {
							- "template"
						}
					}
					- "\n    element, let it instead be inside the "
					code id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:the-template-element-3" {
						a href="#the-template-element" {
							- "template"
						}
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#template-contents" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:template-contents-2" {
						- "template\n    contents"
					}
					- ", after its last child (if any)."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Return the "
					var {
						- "adjusted insertion location"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the steps below require the UA to "
			dfn id="create-an-element-for-the-token" {
				- "create an\n  element for a token"
			}
			- " in a particular "
			var {
				- "given namespace"
			}
			- " and with a\n  particular "
			var {
				- "intended parent"
			}
			- ", the UA must run the following steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:active-speculative-html-parser" {
						- "active speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " is not null, then return the result of\n   "
					a href="#create-a-speculative-mock-element" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:create-a-speculative-mock-element" {
						- "creating a speculative mock element"
					}
					- "\n   given "
					var {
						- "given namespace"
					}
					- ", the tag name of the given token, and the attributes of the\n   given token."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Otherwise, optionally "
					a href="#create-a-speculative-mock-element" id="creating-and-inserting-nodes:create-a-speculative-mock-element-2" {
						- "create a speculative mock element"
					}
					- " given "
