		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the user agent is to "
			dfn id="abort-a-parser" {
				- "abort a parser"
			}
			- ", it must run the following steps:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Throw away any pending content in the "
					a href="#input-stream" id="the-end:input-stream" {
						- "input stream"
					}
					- ", and discard any future\n   content that would have been added to it."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#stop-the-speculative-html-parser" id="the-end:stop-the-speculative-html-parser-2" {
						- "Stop the speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " for this HTML parser."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#update-the-current-document-readiness" id="the-end:update-the-current-document-readiness-3" {
						- "Update the current document readiness"
					}
					- " to \""
					code {
						- "interactive"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Pop "
					em {
						- "all"
					}
					- " the nodes off the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="the-end:stack-of-open-elements-2" {
						- "stack of open elements"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#update-the-current-document-readiness" id="the-end:update-the-current-document-readiness-4" {
						- "Update the current document readiness"
					}
					- " to \""
					code {
						- "complete"
					}
					- "\"."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="speculative-html-parsing" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.8"
			}
			- " Speculative HTML parsing"
			a href="#speculative-html-parsing" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents may implement an optimization, as described in this section, to speculatively fetch\n  resources that are declared in the HTML markup while the HTML parser is waiting for a\n  "
			a href="#pending-parsing-blocking-script" id="speculative-html-parsing:pending-parsing-blocking-script" {
				- "pending parsing-blocking script"
			}
			- " to be fetched and executed, or during normal parsing,\n  at the time "
			a href="#create-an-element-for-the-token" id="speculative-html-parsing:create-an-element-for-the-token" {
				- "an element is created for a token"
			}
			- ".\n  While this optimization is not defined in precise detail, there are some rules to consider for\n  interoperability."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:html-parser" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- " can have an "
			dfn id="active-speculative-html-parser" data-export="" {
				- "active speculative HTML parser"
			}
			- ". It\n  is initially null."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id="speculative-html-parser" data-export="" {
				- "speculative HTML parser"
			}
			- " must act like the normal HTML parser (e.g., the\n  tree builder rules apply), with some exceptions:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The state of the normal HTML parser and the document itself must not be affected."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="example" {
					- "For example, the "
					a href="#next-input-character" id="speculative-html-parsing:next-input-character" {
						- "next input character"
					}
					- " or the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="speculative-html-parsing:stack-of-open-elements" {
						- "stack of open\n    elements"
					}
					- " for the normal HTML parser is not affected by the "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser" {
						- "speculative HTML\n    parser"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Bytes pushed into the HTML parser's "
					a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id="speculative-html-parsing:the-input-byte-stream" {
						- "input byte stream"
					}
					- " must also be pushed into\n    the speculative HTML parser's "
					a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id="speculative-html-parsing:the-input-byte-stream-2" {
						- "input byte stream"
					}
					- ". Bytes read from the streams must\n    be independent."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "The result of the speculative parsing is primarily a series of "
					a href="#speculative-fetch" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-fetch" {
						- "speculative fetches"
					}
					- ". Which kinds of resources to speculatively fetch is\n    "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:implementation-defined" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" data-x-internal="implementation-defined" {
						- "implementation-defined"
					}
					- ", but user agents must not speculatively fetch resources that\n    would not be fetched with the normal HTML parser, under the assumption that the script that is\n    blocking the HTML parser does nothing."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "It is possible that the same markup is seen multiple times from the\n    "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-2" {
						- "speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " and then the normal HTML parser. It is expected that\n    duplicated fetches will be prevented by caching rules, which are not yet fully specified."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id="speculative-fetch" {
				- "speculative fetch"
			}
			- " for a "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element" {
				- "speculative mock element"
			}
			- " "
			var {
				- "element"
			}
			- "\n  must follow these rules:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="XXX" {
			- "Should some of these things be applied to the document \"for real\", even\n  though they are found speculatively?"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-3" {
						- "speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " encounters one of the following elements, then\n    act as if that element is processed for the purpose of its effect of subsequent speculative\n    fetches."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				ul class="brief" {
					li {
						- "A "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-base-element" {
							a href="#the-base-element" {
								- "base"
							}
						}
						- " element."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element" {
							a href="#the-meta-element" {
								- "meta"
							}
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-http-equiv" {
							a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" {
								- "http-equiv"
							}
						}
						- "\n     attribute is in the "
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" id="speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" {
							- "Content\n     security policy"
						}
						- " state."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element-2" {
							a href="#the-meta-element" {
								- "meta"
							}
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-name" {
							a href="#attr-meta-name" {
								- "name"
							}
						}
						- " attribute is an\n     "
						a id="speculative-html-parsing:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
							- "ASCII case-insensitive"
						}
						- " match for \""
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:meta-referrer" {
							a href="#meta-referrer" {
								- "referrer"
							}
						}
						- "\"."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element-3" {
							a href="#the-meta-element" {
								- "meta"
							}
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id="speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-name-2" {
							a href="#attr-meta-name" {
								- "name"
							}
						}
						- " attribute is an\n     "
						a id="speculative-html-parsing:ascii-case-insensitive-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
							- "ASCII case-insensitive"
						}
						- " match for \""
						code {
							- "viewport"
						}
						- "\". (This can\n     affect whether a media query list "
						a href="#matches-the-environment" id="speculative-html-parsing:matches-the-environment" {
							- "matches the environment"
						}
						- ".) "
						a href="#refsCSSDEVICEADAPT" {
							- "[CSSDEVICEADAPT]"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "url"
					}
					- " be the "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "URL"
					}
					- " that "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " would fetch if it was\n   processed normally. If there is no such "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:url-2" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "URL"
					}
					- " or if it is the empty string, then do\n   nothing. Otherwise, if "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:url-3" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "url"
					}
					- " is already in the "
					a href="#list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" id="speculative-html-parsing:list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" {
						- "list of speculative fetch\n   URLs"
					}
					- ", then do nothing. Otherwise, fetch "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:url-4" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" data-x-internal="url" {
						- "url"
					}
					- " as if the element was processed\n   normally, and add "
					var {
						- "url"
					}
					- " to the "
					a href="#list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" id="speculative-html-parsing:list-of-speculative-fetch-urls-2" {
						- "list of speculative fetch URLs"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id="speculative-html-parsing:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id="list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" {
				- "list of speculative fetch URLs"
			}
			- ", which is a\n  "
			a id="speculative-html-parsing:list" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" data-x-internal="list" {
				- "list"
			}
			- " of "
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id="speculative-html-parsing:url-5" data-x-internal="url" {
				- "URLs"
			}
			- ", initially empty."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="start-the-speculative-html-parser" {
				- "start the speculative HTML parser"
			}
			- " for an instance of an HTML parser\n  "
			var {
				- "parser"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Optionally, return."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This step allows user agents to opt out of speculative HTML parsing."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser" {
						- "active speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " is not null, then\n    "
					a href="#stop-the-speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:stop-the-speculative-html-parser" {
						- "stop the speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " for "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p class="note" {
					- "This can happen when "
					code id="speculative-html-parsing:dom-document-write" {
						a href="#dom-document-write" {
							- "document.write()"
						}
					}
					- "\n    writes another parser-blocking script. For simplicity, this specification always restarts\n    speculative parsing, but user agents can implement a more efficient strategy, so long as the end\n    result is equivalent."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- " be a new "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-4" {
						- "speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- ", with the\n   same state as "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "speculativeDoc"
					}
					- " be a new isomorphic representation of "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "'s\n   "
					code id="speculative-html-parsing:document-2" {
						a href="#document" {
							- "Document"
						}
					}
					- ", where all elements are instead "
					a href="#speculative-mock-element" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-2" {
						- "speculative mock elements"
					}
					- ". Let "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- " parse into\n   "
					var {
						- "speculativeDoc"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-2" {
						- "active speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " to\n   "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#in-parallel" id="speculative-html-parsing:in-parallel" {
						- "In parallel"
					}
					- ", run "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- " until it is stopped or until it\n   reaches the end of its "
					a href="#input-stream" id="speculative-html-parsing:input-stream" {
						- "input stream"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="stop-the-speculative-html-parser" {
				- "stop the speculative HTML parser"
			}
			- " for an instance of an HTML parser\n  "
			var {
				- "parser"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- " be "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-3" {
						- "active speculative HTML\n   parser"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- " is null, then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Throw away any pending content in "
					var {
						- "speculativeParser"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#input-stream" id="speculative-html-parsing:input-stream-2" {
						- "input\n   stream"
					}
					- ", and discard any future content that would have been added to it."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "parser"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-4" {
						- "active speculative HTML parser"
					}
					- " to null."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#speculative-html-parser" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-5" {
				- "speculative HTML parser"
			}
			- " will create "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-3" {
				- "speculative mock elements"
			}
			- " instead of normal elements. DOM\n  operations that the tree builder normally does on elements are expected to work appropriately on\n  speculative mock elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id="speculative-mock-element" {
				- "speculative mock element"
			}
			- " is a "
			a id="speculative-html-parsing:struct" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" data-x-internal="struct" {
				- "struct"
			}
			- " with the following "
			a href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id="speculative-html-parsing:struct-item" data-x-internal="struct-item" {
				- "items"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:string" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" data-x-internal="string" {
						- "string"
					}
					- " "
					dfn id="concept-mock-namespace" {
						- "namespace"
					}
					- ", corresponding\n   to an element's "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-namespace" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-element-namespace" data-x-internal="concept-element-namespace" {
						- "namespace"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:string-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" data-x-internal="string" {
						- "string"
					}
					- " "
					dfn id="concept-mock-local-name" {
						- "local name"
					}
					- ",\n   corresponding to an element's "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-local-name" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-element-local-name" data-x-internal="concept-element-local-name" {
						- "local\n   name"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:list-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" data-x-internal="list" {
						- "list"
					}
					- " "
					dfn id="concept-mock-attribute-list" {
						- "attribute list"
					}
					- ",\n   corresponding to an element's "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:attribute-list" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-attribute" data-x-internal="attribute-list" {
						- "attribute list"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:list-3" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" data-x-internal="list" {
						- "list"
					}
					- " "
					dfn id="concept-mock-children" {
						- "children"
					}
					- ", corresponding to\n   an element's "
					a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-child" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-tree-child" data-x-internal="concept-tree-child" {
						- "children"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id="create-a-speculative-mock-element" {
				- "create a speculative mock element"
			}
			- " given a "
			var {
				- "namespace"
			}
			- ",\n  "
			var {
				- "tagName"
			}
			- ", and "
			var {
				- "attributes"
			}
			- ":"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- " be a new "
					a href="#speculative-mock-element" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-4" {
						- "speculative mock element"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-namespace" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-namespace" {
						- "namespace"
					}
					- " to\n   "
					var {
						- "namespace"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-local-name" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-local-name" {
						- "local name"
					}
					- " to\n   "
					var {
						- "tagName"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-attribute-list" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-attribute-list" {
						- "attribute list"
					}
					- "\n   to "
					var {
						- "attributes"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-children" id="speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-children" {
						- "children"
					}
					- " to a new\n   empty "
					a id="speculative-html-parsing:list-4" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" data-x-internal="list" {
						- "list"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Optionally, perform a "
					a href="#speculative-fetch" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-fetch-2" {
						- "speculative fetch"
					}
					- " for "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return "
					var {
						- "element"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the tree builder says to insert an element into a "
			code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element" {
				a href="#the-template-element" {
					- "template"
				}
			}
			- " element's\n  "
			a href="#template-contents" id="speculative-html-parsing:template-contents" {
				- "template contents"
			}
			- ", if that is a "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id="speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-5" {
				- "speculative mock element"
			}
			- ", and the\n  "
			code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element-2" {
				a href="#the-template-element" {
					- "template"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#template-contents" id="speculative-html-parsing:template-contents-2" {
				- "template contents"
			}
			- " is not a\n  "
			code id="speculative-html-parsing:shadowroot" {
				a data-x-internal="shadowroot" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-shadowroot" {
					- "ShadowRoot"
				}
			}
			- " node, instead do nothing. URLs found speculatively inside\n  non-declarative-shadow-root "
			code id="speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element-3" {
				a href="#the-template-element" {
					- "template"
				}
			}
			- " elements might themselves be templates, and must\n  not be speculatively fetched."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h4 id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "13.2.9"
			}
			- " Coercing an HTML DOM into an infoset"
			a href="#coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an application uses an "
			a href="#html-parser" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- " in conjunction with an XML pipeline, it is\n  possible that the constructed DOM is not compatible with the XML tool chain in certain subtle\n  ways. For example, an XML toolchain might not be able to represent attributes with the name "
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- ", since they conflict with the Namespaces in XML syntax. There is also some\n  data that the "
			a href="#html-parser" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-2" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- " generates that isn't included in the DOM itself. This\n  section specifies some rules for handling these issues."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API being used doesn't support DOCTYPEs, the tool may drop DOCTYPEs altogether."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API doesn't support attributes in no namespace that are named \""
			code {
				- "xmlns"
			}
			- "\", attributes whose names start with \""
			code {
				- "xmlns:"
			}
			- "\", or\n  attributes in the "
			a id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:xmlns-namespace" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#xmlns-namespace" data-x-internal="xmlns-namespace" {
				- "XMLNS namespace"
			}
			- ", then the tool may drop such attributes."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The tool may annotate the output with any namespace declarations required for proper\n  operation."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API being used restricts the allowable characters in the local names of elements and\n  attributes, then the tool may map all element and attribute local names that the API wouldn't\n  support to a set of names that "
			em {
				- "are"
			}
			- " allowed, by replacing any character that isn't\n  supported with the uppercase letter U and the six digits of the character's code point when\n  expressed in hexadecimal, using digits 0-9 and capital letters A-F as the symbols, in increasing\n  numeric order."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "For example, the element name "
			code {
				- "foo<bar"
			}
			- ", which can be\n  output by the "
			a href="#html-parser" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-3" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- ", though it is neither a legal HTML element name nor a\n  well-formed XML element name, would be converted into "
			code {
				- "fooU00003Cbar"
			}
			- ", which\n  "
			em {
				- "is"
			}
			- " a well-formed XML element name (though it's still not legal in HTML by any means)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="example" {
			- "As another example, consider the attribute "
			code {
				- "xlink:href"
			}
			- ".\n  Used on a MathML element, it becomes, after being "
			a href="#adjust-foreign-attributes" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:adjust-foreign-attributes" {
				- "adjusted"
			}
			- ", an attribute with a prefix \""
			code {
				- "xlink"
			}
			- "\" and a local\n  name \""
			code {
				- "href"
			}
			- "\". However, used on an HTML element, it becomes an attribute with\n  no prefix and the local name \""
			code {
				- "xlink:href"
			}
			- "\", which is not a valid NCName, and\n  thus might not be accepted by an XML API. It could thus get converted, becoming \""
			code {
				- "xlinkU00003Ahref"
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The resulting names from this conversion conveniently can't clash with any\n  attribute generated by the "
			a href="#html-parser" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-4" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- ", since those are all either lowercase or those\n  listed in the "
			a href="#adjust-foreign-attributes" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:adjust-foreign-attributes-2" {
				- "adjust foreign attributes"
			}
			- " algorithm's table."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API restricts comments from having two consecutive U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS characters\n  (--), the tool may insert a single U+0020 SPACE character between any such offending\n  characters."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API restricts comments from ending in a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-), the tool\n  may insert a single U+0020 SPACE character at the end of such comments."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the XML API restricts allowed characters in character data, attribute values, or comments,\n  the tool may replace any U+000C FORM FEED (FF) character with a U+0020 SPACE character, and any\n  other literal non-XML character with a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "If the tool has no way to convey out-of-band information, then the tool may drop the following\n  information:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ul {
			li {
				- "Whether the document is set to "
				i id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:no-quirks-mode" {
					a data-x-internal="no-quirks-mode" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-no-quirks" {
						- "no-quirks mode"
					}
				}
				- ", "
				i id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:limited-quirks-mode" {
					a data-x-internal="limited-quirks-mode" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-limited-quirks" {
						- "limited-quirks mode"
					}
				}
				- ", or\n   "
				i id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:quirks-mode" {
					a data-x-internal="quirks-mode" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" {
						- "quirks mode"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				- "The association between form controls and forms that aren't their nearest "
				code id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:the-form-element" {
					a href="#the-form-element" {
						- "form"
					}
				}
				- "\n   element ancestor (use of the "
				a href="#form-element-pointer" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:form-element-pointer" {
					code {
						- "form"
					}
					- " element pointer"
				}
				- " in the parser)"
			}
			li {
				- "The "
				a href="#template-contents" id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:template-contents" {
					- "template contents"
				}
				- " of any "
				code id="coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:the-template-element" {
