			li {
				p {
					- "Return "
					var {
						- "s"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="warning" {
			- "It is possible that the output of this algorithm, if parsed with an "
			a href="#html-parser" id="serialising-html-fragments:html-parser-3" {
				- "HTML\n  parser"
			}
			- ", will not return the original tree structure. Tree structures that do not roundtrip\n  a serialize and reparse step can also be produced by the "
			a href="#html-parser" id="serialising-html-fragments:html-parser-4" {
				- "HTML parser"
			}
			- " itself, although\n  such cases are typically non-conforming."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For instance, if a "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-textarea-element" {
					a href="#the-textarea-element" {
						- "textarea"
					}
				}
				- " element to which a "
				code {
					- "Comment"
				}
				- "\n   node has been appended is serialized and the output is then reparsed, the comment will end up\n   being displayed in the text control. Similarly, if, as a result of DOM manipulation, an element\n   contains a comment that contains \""
				code {
					- "-->"
				}
				- "\", then when\n   the result of serializing the element is parsed, the comment will be truncated at that point and\n   the rest of the comment will be interpreted as markup. More examples would be making a\n   "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-script-element-2" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " element contain a "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:text-2" {
					a data-x-internal="text" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" {
						- "Text"
					}
				}
				- " node with the text string \""
				code {
					- "</script>"
				}
				- "\", or having a "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-p-element" {
					a href="#the-p-element" {
						- "p"
					}
				}
				- " element that contains a\n   "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-ul-element" {
					a href="#the-ul-element" {
						- "ul"
					}
				}
				- " element (as the "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-ul-element-2" {
					a href="#the-ul-element" {
						- "ul"
					}
				}
				- " element's "
				a href="#syntax-start-tag" id="serialising-html-fragments:syntax-start-tag" {
					- "start\n   tag"
				}
				- " would imply the end tag for the "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-p-element-2" {
					a href="#the-p-element" {
						- "p"
					}
				}
				- ")."
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "This can enable cross-site scripting attacks. An example of this would be a page that lets the\n   user enter some font family names that are then inserted into a CSS "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-style-element-2" {
					a href="#the-style-element" {
						- "style"
					}
				}
				- " block via\n   the DOM and which then uses the "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:dom-element-innerhtml" {
					a href="#dom-element-innerhtml" {
						- "innerHTML"
					}
				}
				- " IDL attribute to get\n   the HTML serialization of that "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-style-element-3" {
					a href="#the-style-element" {
						- "style"
					}
				}
				- " element: if the user enters\n   \""
				code {
					- "</style><script>attack</script>"
				}
				- "\" as a font family name, "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:dom-element-innerhtml-2" {
					a href="#dom-element-innerhtml" {
						- "innerHTML"
					}
				}
				- " will return markup that, if parsed in a different context,\n   would contain a "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-script-element-3" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " node, even though no "
				code id="serialising-html-fragments:the-script-element-4" {
					a href="#the-script-element" {
						- "script"
					}
				}
				- " node existed in the\n   original DOM."
			}
			- "\n\n  "
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		div class="example" {
			- "\n\n   "
			p {
				- "For example, consider the following markup:"
			}
			- "\n\n   "
			pre {
				code class="html" {
					c- p="" {
						- "<"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "form"
					}
					- " "
					c- e="" {
						- "id"
					}
					c- o="" {
						- "="
					}
					c- s="" {
						- "\"outer\""
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "><"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "div"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "></"
					}
					c- f="" {
						- "form"
					}
					c- p="" {
