			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The character reference names originate from "
			cite {
				- "XML Entity Definitions for\n  Characters"
			}
			- ", though only the above is considered normative. "
			a href="#refsXMLENTITY" {
				- "[XMLENTITY]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This list is static and "
			a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/blob/main/FAQ.md#html-should-add-more-named-character-references" {
				- "will\n  not be expanded or changed in the future"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h2 id="the-xhtml-syntax" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "14"
			}
			- " "
			dfn id="xhtml" {
				- "The XML syntax"
			}
			a href="#the-xhtml-syntax" class="self-link"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button onclick="toggleStatus(this)" class="mdn-anno-btn" {
				b title="Support in all current engines." class="all-engines-flag" {
					- "✔"
				}
				span {
					- "MDN"
				}
			}
			div class="feature" {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Guide/HTML/XHTML" title="XHTML is a term that was historically used to describe HTML documents written to conform with XML syntax rules." {
						- "HTML/XHTML"
					}
				}
				p class="all-engines-text" {
					- "Support in all current engines."
				}
				div class="support" {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox"
						}
						span {
							- "2+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari"
						}
						span {
							- "3.1+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge"
						}
						span {
							- "79+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span {
							- "Edge (Legacy)"
						}
						span {
							- "12+"
						}
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span {
							- "Internet Explorer"
						}
						span {
							- "9+"
						}
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Firefox Android"
						}
						span {
							- "4+"
						}
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span {
							- "Safari iOS"
						}
						span {
							- "2+"
						}
					}
					span class="chrome_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Chrome Android"
						}
						span {
							- "18+"
						}
					}
					span class="webview_android yes" {
						span {
							- "WebView Android"
						}
						span {
							- "2+"
						}
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Samsung Internet"
						}
						span {
							- "1.0+"
						}
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span {
							- "Opera Android"
						}
						span {
							- "10.1+"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This section only describes the rules for XML resources. Rules for\n  "
			code id="the-xhtml-syntax:text/html" {
				a href="#text/html" {
					- "text/html"
				}
			}
			- " resources are discussed in the section above entitled \""
			a href="#syntax" id="the-xhtml-syntax:syntax" {
				- "The HTML\n  syntax"
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p id="xml-syntax-not-recommended" class="warning" {
			- "Using the XML syntax is not recommended, for\n  reasons which include the fact that there is no specification which defines the rules for how an\n  XML parser must map a string of bytes or characters into a "
			code id="the-xhtml-syntax:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " object, as well\n  as the fact that the XML syntax is essentially unmaintained — in that, it’s not expected that any\n  further features will ever be added to the XML syntax (even when such features have been added to\n  the "
			a href="#syntax" id="the-xhtml-syntax:syntax-2" {
				- "HTML syntax"
			}
			- ")."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		h3 id="writing-xhtml-documents" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "14.1"
			}
			- " Writing documents in the XML syntax"
			a href="#writing-xhtml-documents" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "The XML syntax for HTML was formerly referred to as \"XHTML\", but this\n  specification does not use that term (among other reasons, because no such term is used for the\n  HTML syntaxes of MathML and SVG)."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The syntax for XML is defined in "
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- " and "
			cite {
				- "Namespaces in XML"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsXML" {
				- "[XML]"
			}
			- "\n  "
			a href="#refsXMLNS" {
				- "[XMLNS]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification does not define any syntax-level requirements beyond those defined for XML\n  proper."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "XML documents may contain a "
			code {
				- "DOCTYPE"
			}
			- " if desired, but this is not required\n  to conform to this specification. This specification does not define a public or system\n  identifier, nor provide a formal DTD."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "According to "
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- ", XML processors are not guaranteed to process\n  the external DTD subset referenced in the DOCTYPE. This means, for example, that using "
			a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#dt-entref" {
				- "entity references"
			}
			- " for characters in XML documents\n  is unsafe if they are defined in an external file (except for "
			code {
				- "&lt;"
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code {
				- "&gt;"
			}
			- ", "
			code {
				- "&amp;"
			}
			- ",\n  "
			code {
				- "&quot;"
			}
			- ", and "
			code {
				- "&apos;"
			}
			- ")."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h3 id="parsing-xhtml-documents" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "14.2"
			}
			- " Parsing XML documents"
			a href="#parsing-xhtml-documents" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This section describes the relationship between XML and the DOM, with a particular emphasis on\n  how this interacts with HTML."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id="xml-parser" data-export="" {
				- "XML parser"
			}
			- ", for the purposes of this specification, is a construct that\n  follows the rules given in "
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- " to map a string of bytes or characters into a\n  "
			code id="parsing-xhtml-documents:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " object."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "At the time of writing, no such rules actually exist."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "An "
			a href="#xml-parser" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:xml-parser" {
				- "XML parser"
			}
			- " is either associated with a "
			code id="parsing-xhtml-documents:document-2" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " object when it is\n  created, or creates one implicitly."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This "
			code id="parsing-xhtml-documents:document-3" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- " must then be populated with DOM nodes that represent the tree\n  structure of the input passed to the parser, as defined by "
			cite {
				- "XML"
			}
			- ", "
			cite {
				- "Namespaces\n  in XML"
			}
			- ", and "
			cite {
				- "DOM"
			}
			- ". When creating DOM nodes representing elements,\n  the "
			a href="#create-an-element-for-the-token" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:create-an-element-for-the-token" {
				- "create an element for a token"
			}
			- " algorithm\n  or some equivalent that operates on appropriate XML data structures must be used, to ensure the\n  proper "
			a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-interface" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:element-interface" data-x-internal="element-interface" {
				- "element interfaces"
			}
			- " are created and that "
			a href="#custom-element" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:custom-element" {
				- "custom elements"
			}
			- " are set up correctly."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the operations that the "
			a href="#xml-parser" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:xml-parser-2" {
				- "XML parser"
			}
			- " performs on the "
			code id="parsing-xhtml-documents:document-4" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- "'s\n  tree, the user agent must act as if elements and attributes were individually appended and set\n  respectively so as to trigger rules in this specification regarding what happens when an element\n  is inserted into a document or has its attributes set, and "
			cite {
				- "DOM"
			}
			- "'s requirements\n  regarding "
			a id="parsing-xhtml-documents:mutation-observers" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#mutation-observers" data-x-internal="mutation-observers" {
				- "mutation observers"
			}
			- " mean that mutation observers "
			em {
				- "are"
			}
			- " fired.\n  "
			a href="#refsXML" {
				- "[XML]"
			}
			- " "
			a href="#refsXMLNS" {
				- "[XMLNS]"
			}
			- " "
			a href="#refsDOM" {
				- "[DOM]"
			}
			- " "
			a href="#refsUIEVENTS" {
				- "[UIEVENTS]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Between the time an element's start tag is parsed and the time either the element's end tag is\n  parsed or the parser detects a well-formedness error, the user agent must act as if the element\n  was in a "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:stack-of-open-elements" {
				- "stack of open elements"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "This is used by various elements to only start certain processes once they are\n  popped off of the "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="parsing-xhtml-documents:stack-of-open-elements-2" {
				- "stack of open elements"
			}
			- "."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This specification provides the following additional information that user agents should use\n  when retrieving an external entity: the public identifiers given in the following list all\n  correspond to "
