				- " right"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " "
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "br[clear=all i], br[clear=both i] "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- " "
				c- k="" {
					- "clear"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " both"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " "
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "For the purposes of the CSS ruby model, runs of children of "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-ruby-element" {
				a href="#the-ruby-element" {
					- "ruby"
				}
			}
			- " elements that are\n  not "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-rt-element" {
				a href="#the-rt-element" {
					- "rt"
				}
			}
			- " or "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-rp-element" {
				a href="#the-rp-element" {
					- "rp"
				}
			}
			- " elements are expected to be wrapped in anonymous boxes\n  whose "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'display'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#display-prop" data-x-internal="'display'" {
				- "'display'"
			}
			- " property has the value "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'ruby-base'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ruby/#valdef-display-ruby-base" data-x-internal="'ruby-base'" {
				- "'ruby-base'"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsCSSRUBY" {
				- "[CSSRUBY]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a particular part of a ruby has more than one annotation, the annotations should be\n  distributed on both sides of the base text so as to minimize the stacking of ruby annotations on\n  one side."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "When it becomes possible to do so, the preceding requirement will be updated to be\n  expressed in terms of CSS ruby. (Currently, CSS ruby does not handle nested "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-ruby-element-2" {
				a href="#the-ruby-element" {
					- "ruby"
				}
			}
			- "\n  elements or multiple sequential "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-rt-element-2" {
				a href="#the-rt-element" {
					- "rt"
				}
			}
			- " elements, which is how this semantic is\n  expressed.)"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents that do not support correct ruby rendering are expected to render parentheses\n  around the text of "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-rt-element-3" {
				a href="#the-rt-element" {
					- "rt"
				}
			}
			- " elements in the absence of "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-rp-element-2" {
				a href="#the-rp-element" {
					- "rp"
				}
			}
			- " elements."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents are expected to support the "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'clear'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#flow-control" data-x-internal="'clear'" {
				- "'clear'"
			}
			- " property on inline elements (in\n  order to render "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:the-br-element" {
				a href="#the-br-element" {
					- "br"
				}
			}
			- " elements with "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:attr-br-clear" {
				a href="#attr-br-clear" {
					- "clear"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attributes) in the manner described in the non-normative note to this effect in "
			cite {
				- "CSS"
			}
			- ".\n  "
		}
		- " \n\n  "
		p {
			- "The initial value for the "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'color'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#the-color-property" data-x-internal="'color'" {
				- "'color'"
			}
			- " property is expected to be black. The initial\n  value for the "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'background-color'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-backgrounds/#propdef-background-color" data-x-internal="'background-color'" {
				- "'background-color'"
			}
			- " property is expected to be 'transparent'. The\n  canvas's background is expected to be white."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:font" {
				a href="#font" {
					- "font"
				}
			}
			- " element has a "
			code {
				- "color"
			}
			- "\n  attribute, its value is expected to be parsed using the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-a-legacy-colour-value" id="phrasing-content-3:rules-for-parsing-a-legacy-colour-value" {
				- "rules for parsing a legacy color\n  value"
			}
			- ", and if that does not return failure, the user agent is expected to treat the\n  attribute as a "
			a href="#presentational-hints" id="phrasing-content-3:presentational-hints-2" {
				- "presentational hint"
			}
			- " setting the\n  element's "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'color'-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#the-color-property" data-x-internal="'color'" {
				- "'color'"
			}
			- " property to the resulting color."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:font-2" {
				a href="#font" {
					- "font"
				}
			}
			- " element has a "
			code {
				- "face"
			}
			- "\n  attribute, the user agent is expected to treat the attribute as a "
			a href="#presentational-hints" id="phrasing-content-3:presentational-hints-3" {
				- "presentational hint"
			}
			- " setting the element's "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'font-family'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-family-prop" data-x-internal="'font-family'" {
				- "'font-family'"
			}
			- " property to the\n  attribute's value."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id="phrasing-content-3:font-3" {
				a href="#font" {
					- "font"
				}
			}
			- " element has a "
			code {
				- "size"
			}
			- "\n  attribute, the user agent is expected to use the following steps, known as the "
			dfn id="rules-for-parsing-a-legacy-font-size" {
				- "rules for\n  parsing a legacy font size"
			}
			- ", to treat the attribute as a "
			a href="#presentational-hints" id="phrasing-content-3:presentational-hints-4" {
				- "presentational hint"
			}
			- " setting the element's "
			a id="phrasing-content-3:'font-size'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-size-prop" data-x-internal="'font-size'" {
				- "'font-size'"
			}
			- " property:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "input"
					}
					- " be the attribute's value."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " be a pointer into "
					var {
						- "input"
					}
					- ", initially pointing at the\n   start of the string."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a id="phrasing-content-3:skip-ascii-whitespace" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#skip-ascii-whitespace" data-x-internal="skip-ascii-whitespace" {
						- "Skip ASCII whitespace"
					}
					- " within "
					var {
						- "input"
					}
					- " given\n   "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " is past the end of "
					var {
						- "input"
					}
					- ", there is no "
					a href="#presentational-hints" id="phrasing-content-3:presentational-hints-5" {
						- "presentational hint"
					}
					- ". Return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the character at "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " is a U+002B PLUS SIGN character (+), then let\n   "
					var {
						- "mode"
					}
					- " be "
					i {
						- "relative-plus"
					}
					- ", and advance "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " to the next character.\n   Otherwise, if the character at "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " is a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-), then\n   let "
					var {
						- "mode"
					}
					- " be "
					i {
						- "relative-minus"
					}
					- ", and advance "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- " to the next\n   character. Otherwise, let "
					var {
						- "mode"
					}
					- " be "
					i {
						- "absolute"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a id="phrasing-content-3:collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" data-x-internal="collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" {
						- "Collect a sequence of code points"
					}
					- " that are "
					a id="phrasing-content-3:ascii-digits" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit" data-x-internal="ascii-digits" {
						- "ASCII digits"
					}
					- " from\n   "
					var {
						- "input"
					}
					- " given "
					var {
						- "position"
					}
					- ", and let the resulting sequence be\n   "
					var {
						- "digits"
					}
					- "."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "digits"
					}
					- " is the empty string, there is no "
					a href="#presentational-hints" id="phrasing-content-3:presentational-hints-6" {
						- "presentational hint"
					}
					- ". Return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Interpret "
					var {
						- "digits"
					}
					- " as a base-ten integer. Let "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " be the resulting\n   number."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    \n\n    "
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "mode"
					}
					- " is "
					i {
						- "relative-plus"
					}
					- ", then increment "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " by 3. If\n    "
					var {
						- "mode"
					}
					- " is "
					i {
						- "relative-minus"
					}
					- ", then let "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " be the result of subtracting\n    "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " from 3."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " is greater than 7, let it be 7."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- " is less than 1, let it be 1."
				}
			}
			li {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Set "
					a id="phrasing-content-3:'font-size'-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-size-prop" data-x-internal="'font-size'" {
						- "'font-size'"
					}
					- " to the keyword corresponding to the value of "
					var {
						- "value"
					}
					- "\n    according to the following table:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				table {
					thead {
						tr {
							th {
								var {
									- "value"
								}
								- "\n       "
							}
							th {
								a id="phrasing-content-3:'font-size'-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-size-prop" data-x-internal="'font-size'" {
									- "'font-size'"
								}
								- " keyword\n     "
							}
						}
					}
					tbody {
						tr {
							td {
								- "1\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'x-small'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "2\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'small'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "3\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'medium'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "4\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'large'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "5\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'x-large'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "6\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'xx-large'\n      "
							}
						}
						tr {
							td {
								- "7\n       "
							}
							td {
								- "'xxx-large'\n    "
							}
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="bidi-rendering" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "15.3.5"
			}
			- " Bidirectional text"
			a href="#bidi-rendering" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="css" {
				c- n="" {
					- "@namespace"
				}
				- " "
				c- s="" {
					- "\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "[dir]:dir(ltr), bdi:dir(ltr), input[type=tel i]:dir(ltr) "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- " "
				c- k="" {
					- "direction"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " ltr"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " "
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "[dir]:dir(rtl), bdi:dir(rtl) "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- " "
				c- k="" {
					- "direction"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " rtl"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " "
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "address, blockquote, center, div, figure, figcaption, footer, form, header, hr,"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "legend, listing, main, p, plaintext, pre, summary, xmp, article, aside, h1, h2,"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "h3, h4, h5, h6, hgroup, nav, section, search, table, caption, colgroup, col,"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "thead, tbody, tfoot, tr, td, th, dir, dd, dl, dt, menu, ol, ul, li, bdi, output,"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "[dir=ltr i], [dir=rtl i], [dir=auto i] "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- "\n  "
				c- k="" {
					- "unicode-bidi"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " isolate"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " \n"
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "bdo, bdo[dir] "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- " "
				c- k="" {
					- "unicode-bidi"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " isolate-override"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- " "
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- " \n\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "input[dir=auto i]:is([type=search i], [type=tel i], [type=url i],"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- f="" {
					- "[type=email i]), textarea[dir=auto i], pre[dir=auto i] "
				}
				c- p="" {
					- "{"
				}
				- "\n  "
				c- k="" {
					- "unicode-bidi"
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ":"
				}
				- " plaintext"
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- p="" {
					- "}"
				}
				- "\n"
				c- c="" {
					- "/* see prose for input elements whose type attribute is in the Text state */"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				c- c="" {
					- "/* the "
				}
				a href="#br-wbr-content" {
					c- c="" {
						- "rules setting the 'content' property"
					}
				}
				c- c="" {
					- " on "
				}
				code id="bidi-rendering:the-br-element" {
					a href="#the-br-element" {
						c- c="" {
							- "br"
						}
					}
				}
				c- c="" {
					- " and "
				}
				code id="bidi-rendering:the-wbr-element" {
					a href="#the-wbr-element" {
						c- c="" {
							- "wbr"
						}
					}
				}
				c- c="" {
					- " elements also has bidi implications */"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="bidi-rendering:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="bidi-rendering:attr-dir" {
				a href="#attr-dir" {
					- "dir"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is in the\n  "
			a href="#attr-dir-auto" id="bidi-rendering:attr-dir-auto" {
				- "auto"
			}
			- " state and its "
			code id="bidi-rendering:attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- "\n  attribute is in the "
			a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" id="bidi-rendering:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" {
				- "Text"
			}
			- " state, then the user agent is\n  expected to act as if it had a user-agent-level style sheet rule setting the\n  "
			a id="bidi-rendering:'unicode-bidi'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes/#unicode-bidi" data-x-internal="'unicode-bidi'" {
				- "'unicode-bidi'"
			}
			- " property to 'plaintext'."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "Input fields (i.e. "
			code id="bidi-rendering:the-textarea-element" {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" {
					- "textarea"
				}
			}
			- " elements, and "
			code id="bidi-rendering:the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " elements when their\n  "
			code id="bidi-rendering:attr-input-type-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attribute is in the "
			a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" id="bidi-rendering:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)-2" {
				- "Text"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" id="bidi-rendering:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)-3" {
				- "Search"
			}
			- ",\n  "
			a href="#telephone-state-(type=tel)" id="bidi-rendering:telephone-state-(type=tel)" {
				- "Telephone"
			}
			- ", "
			a href="#url-state-(type=url)" id="bidi-rendering:url-state-(type=url)" {
				- "URL"
			}
			- ",\n  or "
			a href="#email-state-(type=email)" id="bidi-rendering:email-state-(type=email)" {
				- "Email"
			}
			- " state) are expected to present an editing\n  user interface with a directionality that matches the element's "
			a id="bidi-rendering:'direction'" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes/#direction" data-x-internal="'direction'" {
				- "'direction'"
			}
			- "\n  property."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When the document's character encoding is "
			a id="bidi-rendering:iso-8859-8" href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#iso-8859-8" data-x-internal="iso-8859-8" {
				- "ISO-8859-8"
			}
			- ", the following rules are\n  additionally expected to apply, following those above: "
			a href="#refsENCODING" {
				- "[ENCODING]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="css" {
				c- n="" {
					- "@namespace"
				}
