		- "\n\n\n  "
		h4 id="images-3" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "15.4.2"
			}
			- " Images"
			a href="#images-3" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "User agents are expected to render "
			code id="images-3:the-img-element" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " elements and "
			code id="images-3:the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" {
					- "input"
				}
			}
			- " elements\n  whose "
			code id="images-3:attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" {
					- "type"
				}
			}
			- " attributes are in the "
			a href="#image-button-state-(type=image)" id="images-3:image-button-state-(type=image)" {
				- "Image Button"
			}
			- " state, according to the first applicable rules\n  from the following list:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl class="switch" {
			dt {
				- "If the element "
				a href="#represents" id="images-3:represents" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " an image"
			}
			dd {
				- "The user agent is expected to treat the element as a "
				a id="images-3:replaced-element" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#replaced-element" data-x-internal="replaced-element" {
					- "replaced element"
				}
				- " and\n   render the image according to the rules for doing so defined in CSS."
			}
			dt {
				- "\n\n    If the element does not "
				a href="#represents" id="images-3:represents-2" {
					- "represent"
				}
				- " an image and either:\n\n    "
				ul {
					li {
						- "the user agent has reason to believe that the image will become "
						i id="images-3:img-available" {
							a href="#img-available" {
								- "available"
							}
						}
						- " and be rendered in due\n     course, or\n\n     "
					}
					li {
						- "the element has no "
						code {
							- "alt"
						}
						- " attribute, or\n\n     "
					}
					li {
						- "the "
						code id="images-3:document" {
							a href="#document" {
								- "Document"
							}
						}
						- " is in "
						a id="images-3:quirks-mode" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" data-x-internal="quirks-mode" {
							- "quirks mode"
						}
						- ", and the element already has\n     "
						a id="images-3:natural-dimensions" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions" data-x-internal="natural-dimensions" {
							- "natural dimensions"
						}
						- " (e.g., from the "
						a href="#dimension-attributes" id="images-3:dimension-attributes" {
							- "dimension attributes"
						}
						- " or CSS\n     rules)\n    "
					}
				}
				- "\n\n   "
			}
			dd {
				- "The user agent is expected to treat the element as a "
				a id="images-3:replaced-element-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#replaced-element" data-x-internal="replaced-element" {
					- "replaced element"
				}
				- " whose\n   content is the text that the element represents, if any, optionally alongside an icon indicating\n   that the image is being obtained (if applicable). For "
				code id="images-3:the-input-element-2" {
					a href="#the-input-element" {
						- "input"
					}
				}
				- " elements, the element\n   is expected to appear button-like to indicate that the element is a "
				a href="#concept-button" id="images-3:concept-button" {
					- "button"
				}
				- "."
			}
			dt {
				- "If the element is an "
				code id="images-3:the-img-element-2" {
					a href="#the-img-element" {
						- "img"
					}
				}
				- " element that "
				a href="#represents" id="images-3:represents-3" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " some text and the\n   user agent does not expect this to change"
			}
			dd {
				- "The user agent is expected to treat the element as a non-replaced phrasing element whose\n   content is the text, optionally with an icon indicating that an image is missing, so that the\n   user can request the image be displayed or investigate why it is not rendering. In non-graphical\n   contexts, such an icon should be omitted."
			}
			dt {
				- "If the element is an "
				code id="images-3:the-img-element-3" {
					a href="#the-img-element" {
						- "img"
					}
				}
				- " element that "
				a href="#represents" id="images-3:represents-4" {
					- "represents"
				}
				- " nothing and the\n   user agent does not expect this to change"
			}
			dd {
				- "The user agent is expected to treat the element as a "
				a id="images-3:replaced-element-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#replaced-element" data-x-internal="replaced-element" {
					- "replaced element"
				}
				- " whose\n   "
				a id="images-3:natural-dimensions-2" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions" data-x-internal="natural-dimensions" {
					- "natural dimensions"
				}
				- " are 0. (In the absence of further styles, this will cause the\n   element to essentially not be rendered.)"
			}
			dt {
				- "If the element is an "
				code id="images-3:the-input-element-3" {
					a href="#the-input-element" {
						- "input"
					}
				}
				- " element that does not "
				a href="#represents" id="images-3:represents-5" {
					- "represent"
				}
				- " an image and the user agent does not expect this to change"
			}
			dd {
				- "The user agent is expected to treat the element as a "
				a id="images-3:replaced-element-4" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#replaced-element" data-x-internal="replaced-element" {
					- "replaced element"
				}
				- "\n   consisting of a button whose content is the element's alternative text. The "
				a id="images-3:natural-dimensions-3" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions" data-x-internal="natural-dimensions" {
					- "natural\n   dimensions"
				}
				- " of the button are expected to be about one line in height and whatever width\n   is necessary to render the text on one line."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The icons mentioned above are expected to be relatively small so as not to disrupt most text\n  but be easily clickable. In a visual environment, for instance, icons could be 16 pixels by 16\n  pixels square, or 1em by 1em if the images are scalable. In an audio environment, the icon could\n  be a short bleep. The icons are intended to indicate to the user that they can be used to get to\n  whatever options the UA provides for images, and, where appropriate, are expected to provide\n  access to the context menu that would have come up if the user interacted with the actual\n  image."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "All animated images with the same "
			a id="images-3:absolute-url" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" data-x-internal="absolute-url" {
				- "absolute URL"
			}
			- " and the same image data are\n  expected to be rendered synchronized to the same timeline as a group, with the timeline starting\n  at the time of the least recent addition to the group."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="note" {
			- "In other words, when a second image with the same "
			a id="images-3:absolute-url-2" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" data-x-internal="absolute-url" {
				- "absolute URL"
			}
			- " and\n  animated image data is inserted into a document, it jumps to the point in the animation cycle that\n  is currently being displayed by the first image."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "When a user agent is to "
			dfn id="restart-the-animation" {
				- "restart the animation"
			}
			- " for an "
			code id="images-3:the-img-element-4" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element\n  showing an animated image, all animated images with the same "
			a id="images-3:absolute-url-3" href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" data-x-internal="absolute-url" {
				- "absolute URL"
			}
			- " and the\n  same image data in that "
			code id="images-3:the-img-element-5" {
				a href="#the-img-element" {
					- "img"
				}
			}
			- " element's "
			a id="images-3:node-document" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" data-x-internal="node-document" {
				- "node document"
			}
			- " are expected to restart\n  their animation from the beginning."
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		hr
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following CSS rules are expected to apply:"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		pre {
			code class="css" {
				c- n="" {
					- "@namespace"
				}
				- " "
				c- s="" {
					- "\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\""
				}
				c- p="" {
					- ";"
				}
				- "\n\n"
				span id="img-contain-size" {
					c- f="" {
						- "img:is([sizes=\"auto\" i], [sizes^=\"auto,\" i]) "
					}
					c- p="" {
						- "{"
					}
					- "\n  "
					c- k="" {
						- "contain"
					}
					c- p="" {
						- ":"
					}
					- " size !important;\n  contain-intrinsic-size: 300px 150px;\n}"
				}
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The following CSS rules are expected to apply when the "
			code id="images-3:document-2" {
