				a href="#dom-external-addsearchprovider" id="other-elements,-attributes-and-apis:dom-external-addsearchprovider" {
					c- g="" {
						- "AddSearchProvider"
					}
				}
				- "();\n  "
				c- b="" {
					- "undefined"
				}
				- " "
				a href="#dom-external-issearchproviderinstalled" id="other-elements,-attributes-and-apis:dom-external-issearchproviderinstalled" {
					c- g="" {
						- "IsSearchProviderInstalled"
					}
				}
				- "();\n};"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for="External" id="dom-external-addsearchprovider" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "AddSearchProvider()"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for="External" id="dom-external-issearchproviderinstalled" data-dfn-type="method" {
				code {
					- "IsSearchProviderInstalled()"
				}
			}
			- " methods\n  must do nothing."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n  "
		h2 id="iana" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17"
			}
			- " IANA considerations"
			a href="#iana" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n  "
		h3 id="text/html" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.1"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "text/html"
				}
			}
			a href="#text/html" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "text"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "html"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No required parameters"
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						code {
							- "charset"
						}
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "The "
							code {
								- "charset"
							}
							- " parameter may be provided to specify the\n      "
							a id="text/html:document's-character-encoding" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" data-x-internal="document's-character-encoding" {
								- "document's character encoding"
							}
							- ", overriding any "
							a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="text/html:character-encoding-declaration" {
								- "character encoding declarations"
							}
							- " in the document other than a Byte Order\n      Mark (BOM). The parameter's value must be an "
							a id="text/html:ascii-case-insensitive" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" data-x-internal="ascii-case-insensitive" {
								- "ASCII case-insensitive"
							}
							- " match for the\n      string \""
							code {
								- "utf-8"
							}
							- "\". "
							a href="#refsENCODING" {
								- "[ENCODING]"
							}
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    8bit (see the section on "
				a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id="text/html:character-encoding-declaration-2" {
					- "character encoding\n    declarations"
				}
				- ")\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Entire novels have been written about the security considerations that apply to HTML\n    documents. Many are listed in this document, to which the reader is referred for more details.\n    Some general concerns bear mentioning here, however:"
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "HTML is scripted language, and has a large number of APIs (some of which are described in\n    this document). Script can expose the user to potential risks of information leakage, credential\n    leakage, cross-site scripting attacks, cross-site request forgeries, and a host of other\n    problems. While the designs in this specification are intended to be safe if implemented\n    correctly, a full implementation is a massive undertaking and, as with any software, user agents\n    are likely to have security bugs."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Even without scripting, there are specific features in HTML which, for historical reasons,\n    are required for broad compatibility with legacy content but that expose the user to unfortunate\n    security problems. In particular, the "
					code id="text/html:the-img-element" {
						a href="#the-img-element" {
							- "img"
						}
					}
					- " element can be used in conjunction with\n    some other features as a way to effect a port scan from the user's location on the Internet.\n    This can expose local network topologies that the attacker would otherwise not be able to\n    determine."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "HTML relies on a compartmentalization scheme sometimes known as the "
					i {
						- "same-origin\n    policy"
					}
					- ". An "
					a href="#concept-origin" id="text/html:concept-origin" {
						- "origin"
					}
					- " in most cases consists of all the pages served from the same\n    host, on the same port, using the same protocol."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "It is critical, therefore, to ensure that any untrusted content that forms part of a site be\n    hosted on a different "
					a href="#concept-origin" id="text/html:concept-origin-2" {
						- "origin"
					}
					- " than any sensitive content on that site. Untrusted\n    content can easily spoof any other page on the same origin, read data from that origin, cause\n    scripts in that origin to execute, submit forms to and from that origin even if they are\n    protected from cross-site request forgery attacks by unique tokens, and make use of any\n    third-party resources exposed to or rights granted to that origin."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Rules for processing both conforming and non-conforming content\n    are defined in this specification.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd id="authors-using-html" {
				- "\n    This document is the relevant specification. Labeling a resource\n    with the "
				code id="text/html:text/html" {
					a href="#text/html" {
						- "text/html"
					}
				}
				- " type asserts that the resource is\n    an "
				a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" id="text/html:html-documents" data-x-internal="html-documents" {
					- "HTML document"
				}
				- " using\n    "
				a href="#syntax" id="text/html:syntax" {
					- "the HTML syntax"
				}
				- ".\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Web browsers, tools for processing web content, HTML authoring\n    tools, search engines, validators.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No sequence of bytes can uniquely identify an HTML\n     document. More information on detecting HTML documents is\n     available in "
						cite {
							- "MIME Sniffing"
						}
						- ". "
						a href="#refsMIMESNIFF" {
							- "[MIMESNIFF]"
						}
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "\""
						code {
							- "html"
						}
						- "\" and \""
						code {
							- "htm"
						}
						- "\"\n     are commonly, but certainly not exclusively, used as the\n     extension for HTML documents."
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						code {
							- "TEXT"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No restrictions apply."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="text/html:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " used with "
			code id="text/html:text/html-2" {
				a href="#text/html" {
					- "text/html"
				}
			}
			- " resources\n  either refer to the "
			a href="#the-indicated-part-of-the-document" id="text/html:the-indicated-part-of-the-document" {
				- "indicated part"
			}
			- " of the corresponding "
			code id="text/html:document" {
				a href="#document" {
					- "Document"
				}
			}
			- ", or\n  provide state information for in-page scripts."
		}
		- "\n\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.2"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "multipart/x-mixed-replace"
				}
			}
			a href="#multipart/x-mixed-replace" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "multipart"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "x-mixed-replace"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				ul class="brief" {
					li {
						code {
							- "boundary"
						}
						- " (defined in RFC2046) "
						a href="#refsRFC2046" {
							- "[RFC2046]"
						}
						- "\n    "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No optional parameters."
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "binary"
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Subresources of a "
				code id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
					a href="#multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
						- "multipart/x-mixed-replace"
					}
				}
				- "\n    resource can be of any type, including types with non-trivial\n    security implications such as "
				code id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:text/html" {
					a href="#text/html" {
						- "text/html"
					}
				}
				- ".\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    None.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    This specification describes processing rules for web browsers.\n    Conformance requirements for generating resources with this type are the same as for "
				code id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:multipart/mixed" {
					a href="#multipart/mixed" {
						- "multipart/mixed"
					}
				}
				- ". "
				a href="#refsRFC2046" {
					- "[RFC2046]"
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    This type is intended to be used in resources generated by web servers, for consumption by web browsers.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No sequence of bytes can uniquely identify a "
						code id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:multipart/x-mixed-replace-2" {
							a href="#multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
								- "multipart/x-mixed-replace"
							}
						}
						- " resource."
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific file extensions are recommended for this type."
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific Macintosh file type codes are recommended for this type."
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No restrictions apply."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " used with\n  "
			code id="multipart/x-mixed-replace:multipart/x-mixed-replace-3" {
				a href="#multipart/x-mixed-replace" {
					- "multipart/x-mixed-replace"
				}
			}
			- " resources apply to each body part as defined by the type\n  used by that body part."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="application/xhtml+xml" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.3"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "application/xhtml+xml"
				}
			}
			a href="#application/xhtml+xml" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "application"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "xhtml+xml"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-2" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-3" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-4" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-5" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt id="authors-using-xhtml" {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Labeling a resource with the "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xhtml+xml" {
					a href="#application/xhtml+xml" {
						- "application/xhtml+xml"
					}
				}
				- " type asserts that the\n   resource is an XML document that likely has a "
				a id="application/xhtml+xml:document-element" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" data-x-internal="document-element" {
					- "document element"
				}
				- " from the "
				a id="application/xhtml+xml:html-namespace-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace" data-x-internal="html-namespace-2" {
					- "HTML\n   namespace"
				}
				- ". Thus, the relevant specifications are "
				cite {
					- "XML"
				}
				- ", "
				cite {
					- "Namespaces in\n   XML"
				}
				- ", and this specification. "
				a href="#refsXML" {
					- "[XML]"
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsXMLNS" {
					- "[XMLNS]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-6" {
					a href="#application/xml" {
						- "application/xml"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsRFC7303" {
					- "[RFC7303]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "Same as for "
						code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xml-7" {
							a href="#application/xml" {
								- "application/xml"
							}
						}
						- " "
						a href="#refsRFC7303" {
							- "[RFC7303]"
						}
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "\""
						code {
							- "xhtml"
						}
						- "\" and \""
						code {
							- "xht"
						}
						- "\" are sometimes used as\n     extensions for XML resources that have a "
						a id="application/xhtml+xml:document-element-2" href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" data-x-internal="document-element" {
							- "document element"
						}
						- " from the "
						a id="application/xhtml+xml:html-namespace-2-2" href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace" data-x-internal="html-namespace-2" {
							- "HTML\n     namespace"
						}
						- "."
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						code {
							- "TEXT"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No restrictions apply."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="application/xhtml+xml:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " used with\n  "
			code id="application/xhtml+xml:application/xhtml+xml-2" {
				a href="#application/xhtml+xml" {
					- "application/xhtml+xml"
				}
			}
			- " resources have the same semantics as with any\n  "
			a id="application/xhtml+xml:xml-mime-type" href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-mime-type" data-x-internal="xml-mime-type" {
				- "XML MIME type"
			}
			- ". "
			a href="#refsRFC7303" {
				- "[RFC7303]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="text/ping" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.4"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "text/ping"
				}
			}
			a href="#text/ping" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "text"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "ping"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No parameters"
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						code {
							- "charset"
						}
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "The "
							code {
								- "charset"
							}
							- " parameter may be provided. The parameter's value must be\n      \""
							code {
								- "utf-8"
							}
							- "\". This parameter serves no purpose; it is only allowed for\n      compatibility with legacy servers."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Not applicable."
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "If used exclusively in the fashion described in the context of\n    "
					a href="#hyperlink-auditing" id="text/ping:hyperlink-auditing" {
						- "hyperlink auditing"
					}
					- ", this type introduces no new\n    security concerns."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Rules applicable to this type are defined in this specification.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    This document is the relevant specification.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Web browsers.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						code id="text/ping:text/ping" {
							a href="#text/ping" {
								- "text/ping"
							}
						}
						- " resources always consist of the four\n     bytes 0x50 0x49 0x4E 0x47 (`"
						code {
							- "PING"
						}
						- "`)."
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific file extension is recommended for this type."
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific Macintosh file type codes are recommended for this type."
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Only intended for use with HTTP POST requests generated as part\n   of a web browser's processing of the "
				code id="text/ping:ping" {
					a href="#ping" {
						- "ping"
					}
				}
				- " attribute."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="text/ping:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " have no meaning with\n  "
			code id="text/ping:text/ping-2" {
				a href="#text/ping" {
					- "text/ping"
				}
			}
			- " resources."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="application/microdata+json" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.5"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "application/microdata+json"
				}
			}
			a href="#application/microdata+json" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "application"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "microdata+json"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/microdata+json:application/json" {
					a href="#application/json" {
						- "application/json"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsJSON" {
					- "[JSON]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-2" {
					a href="#application/json" {
						- "application/json"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsJSON" {
					- "[JSON]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "8bit (always UTF-8)"
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-3" {
					a href="#application/json" {
						- "application/json"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsJSON" {
					- "[JSON]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Same as for "
				code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-4" {
					a href="#application/json" {
						- "application/json"
					}
				}
				- " "
				a href="#refsJSON" {
					- "[JSON]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Labeling a resource with the "
				code id="application/microdata+json:application/microdata+json" {
					a href="#application/microdata+json" {
						- "application/microdata+json"
					}
				}
				- " type asserts that the\n    resource is a JSON text that consists of an object with a single entry called \""
				code {
					- "items"
				}
				- "\" consisting of an array of entries, each of which consists of an object\n    with an entry called \""
				code {
					- "id"
				}
				- "\" whose value is a string, an entry called \""
				code {
					- "type"
				}
				- "\" whose value is another string, and an entry called \""
				code {
					- "properties"
				}
				- "\" whose value is an object whose entries each have a value consisting\n    of an array of either objects or strings, the objects being of the same form as the objects in\n    the aforementioned \""
				code {
					- "items"
				}
				- "\" entry. Thus, the relevant specifications are\n    "
				cite {
					- "JSON"
				}
				- " and this specification. "
				a href="#refsJSON" {
					- "[JSON]"
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "Applications that transfer data intended for use with HTML's microdata feature, especially in\n    the context of drag-and-drop, are the primary application class for this type."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "Same as for "
						code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-5" {
							a href="#application/json" {
								- "application/json"
							}
						}
						- " "
						a href="#refsJSON" {
							- "[JSON]"
						}
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "Same as for "
						code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-6" {
							a href="#application/json" {
								- "application/json"
							}
						}
						- " "
						a href="#refsJSON" {
							- "[JSON]"
						}
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "Same as for "
						code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-7" {
							a href="#application/json" {
								- "application/json"
							}
						}
						- " "
						a href="#refsJSON" {
							- "[JSON]"
						}
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No restrictions apply."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="application/microdata+json:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " used with\n  "
			code id="application/microdata+json:application/microdata+json-2" {
				a href="#application/microdata+json" {
					- "application/microdata+json"
				}
			}
			- " resources have the same semantics as when used with\n  "
			code id="application/microdata+json:application/json-8" {
				a href="#application/json" {
					- "application/json"
				}
			}
			- " (namely, at the time of writing, no semantics at all).\n  "
			a href="#refsJSON" {
				- "[JSON]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="text/event-stream" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.6"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "text/event-stream"
				}
			}
			a href="#text/event-stream" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This registration is for community review and will be submitted to the IESG for review,\n  approval, and registration with IANA."
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Type name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "text"
			}
			dt {
				- "Subtype name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "event-stream"
			}
			dt {
				- "Required parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "No parameters"
			}
			dt {
				- "Optional parameters:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						code {
							- "charset"
						}
					}
					dd {
						- "\n      "
						p {
							- "The "
							code {
								- "charset"
							}
							- " parameter may be provided. The parameter's value must be\n      \""
							code {
								- "utf-8"
							}
							- "\". This parameter serves no purpose; it is only allowed for\n      compatibility with legacy servers."
						}
						- "\n     "
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "8bit (always UTF-8)"
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				p {
					- "An event stream from an origin distinct from the origin of the content consuming the event\n    stream can result in information leakage. To avoid this, user agents are required to apply CORS\n    semantics. "
					a href="#refsFETCH" {
						- "[FETCH]"
					}
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Event streams can overwhelm a user agent; a user agent is expected to apply suitable\n    restrictions to avoid depleting local resources because of an overabundance of information from\n    an event stream."
				}
				- "\n\n    "
				p {
					- "Servers can be overwhelmed if a situation develops in which the server is causing clients to\n    reconnect rapidly. Servers should use a 5xx status code to indicate capacity problems, as this\n    will prevent conforming clients from reconnecting automatically."
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Rules for processing both conforming and non-conforming content are defined in this\n    specification.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Published specification:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    This document is the relevant specification.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications that use this media type:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Web browsers and tools using web services.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Additional information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				dl {
					dt {
						- "Magic number(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No sequence of bytes can uniquely identify an event stream."
					}
					dt {
						- "File extension(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific file extensions are recommended for this type."
					}
					dt {
						- "Macintosh file type code(s):"
					}
					dd {
						- "No specific Macintosh file type codes are recommended for this type."
					}
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Person & email address to contact for further information:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Intended usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Common"
			}
			dt {
				- "Restrictions on usage:"
			}
			dd {
				- "This format is only expected to be used by dynamic open-ended streams served using HTTP or a\n   similar protocol. Finite resources are not expected to be labeled with this type."
			}
			dt {
				- "Author:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "W3C"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			a href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id="text/event-stream:concept-url-fragment" data-x-internal="concept-url-fragment" {
				- "Fragments"
			}
			- " have no meaning with\n  "
			code id="text/event-stream:text/event-stream" {
				a href="#text/event-stream" {
					- "text/event-stream"
				}
			}
			- " resources."
		}
		- "\n\n\n  "
		h3 id="web+-scheme-prefix" {
			span class="secno" {
				- "17.7"
			}
			- " "
			dfn {
				code {
					- "web+"
				}
				- " scheme prefix"
			}
			a href="#web+-scheme-prefix" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p {
			- "This section describes a convention for use with the IANA URI scheme registry. It does not\n  itself register a specific scheme. "
			a href="#refsRFC7595" {
				- "[RFC7595]"
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		dl {
			dt {
				- "Scheme name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Schemes starting with the four characters \""
				code {
					- "web+"
				}
				- "\" followed by one or more letters in the range\n    "
				code {
					- "a"
				}
				- "-"
				code {
					- "z"
				}
				- ".\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Status:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Permanent"
			}
			dt {
				- "Scheme syntax:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Scheme-specific."
			}
			dt {
				- "Scheme semantics:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Scheme-specific."
			}
			dt {
				- "Encoding considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "All \""
				code {
					- "web+"
				}
				- "\" schemes should use UTF-8 encodings where relevant."
			}
			dt {
				- "Applications/protocols that use this scheme name:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Scheme-specific."
			}
			dt {
				- "Interoperability considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "The scheme is expected to be used in the context of web applications."
			}
			dt {
				- "Security considerations:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    Any web page is able to register a handler for all \""
				code {
					- "web+"
				}
				- "\" schemes. As\n    such, these schemes must not be used for features intended to be core platform features (e.g.,\n    HTTP). Similarly, such schemes must not store confidential information in their URLs, such as\n    usernames, passwords, personal information, or confidential project names.\n   "
			}
			dt {
				- "Contact:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "Change controller:"
			}
			dd {
				- "Ian Hickson <ian@hixie.ch>"
			}
			dt {
				- "References:"
			}
			dd {
				- "\n    "
				cite {
					- "Custom scheme handlers"
				}
				- ", HTML Living Standard:\n    "
				a href="#custom-handlers" {
					- "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#custom-handlers"
				}
				- "\n   "
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n\n\n  "
		h2 id="index" class="no-num" {
			- "Index"
			a href="#index" class="self-link"
		}
		- "\n\n  \n\n  "
