		- "\n\n  "
		p class="tablenote" {
			small {
				- "An asterisk (*) in a cell indicates that the actual rules are more\n  complicated than indicated in the table above."
			}
		}
		- "\n\n  "
		p class="tablenote" {
			small {
				- "† Categories in the \"Parents\" column refer to parents that list\n  the given categories in their content model, not to elements that themselves are in those\n  categories. For example, the "
				code id="elements-3:the-a-element-2" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element's \"Parents\" column says \"phrasing\", so any\n  element whose content model contains the \"phrasing\" category could be a parent of an\n  "
				code id="elements-3:the-a-element-3" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element. Since the \"flow\" category includes all the \"phrasing\" elements, that means\n  the "
				code id="elements-3:the-th-element-3" {
					a href="#the-th-element" {
						- "th"
					}
				}
				- " element could be a parent to an "
				code id="elements-3:the-a-element-4" {
					a href="#the-a-element" {
						- "a"
					}
				}
				- " element."
			}
		}
